hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"14928","(14922) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī narrated to us: Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Anas ibn Sīrīn, and he mentioned something similar to it, except that he said: \Let him divorce her if he wishes.\"" He said: ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," will that divorce be counted?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"14929","(14923) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to me: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik, from Anas ibn Sīrīn, who said: I asked Ibn ʿUmar about the wife he had divorced. He said: \I divorced her while she was menstruating. That was mentioned to ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — and he mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: 'Tell him to take her back. When she becomes pure"," let him divorce her for her purity.'\"" He said: \""So I took her back"," then I divorced her for her purity.\"" I said: \""Was that divorce — the one you pronounced while she was menstruating — counted?\"" He said: \""Why should I not count it"," even if I was helpless and foolish?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā."""
"14930","(14924) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Ibn Ṭāwūs informed me from his father that he heard Ibn ʿUmar being asked about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: \Do you know ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar?\"" He said: Yes. He said: \""He divorced his wife while she was menstruating"," so ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of the matter"," and he commanded him to take her back.\"" He said: \""I did not hear him add anything beyond that to his father.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"14931","(14925) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Qabīṣah narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr, from Abū Wāʾil, that Ibn ʿUmar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to take her back until she became pure, and when she became pure, he should divorce her. [Ḥasan]"
"14932","(14926) Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq in Baghdād — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sābiq Abū Jaʿfar narrated to us, dictating from his book; Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Firās, from ʿĀmir, who said: Ibn ʿUmar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, one divorce. So ʿUmar went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He commanded him: when she becomes pure, he should take her back, then he should initiate the divorce during her ʿiddah, and the divorce that he issued the first time shall be counted. [Ḥasan]"
"14933","(14927) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAlī ibn Maʿbad narrated to us; Abū al-Malīḥ narrated from Maymūn ibn Mihrān, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he divorced his wife during her menses. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to take her back until she became pure, and when she became pure, if he wished he could divorce her, and if he wished he could retain her, before he touched her. [Ḥasan]"
"14934","(14928) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he made it one divorce.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: And Abū Maʿmar said: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; Ayyūb informed him from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: It was counted against me as one divorce. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14935","(14929) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ayman, the freedman of ʿUrwah, asking Ibn ʿUmar — while Abū al-Zubayr was listening — he said: \What is your opinion regarding a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating?\"" He said: \""ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," divorced his wife while she was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: 'He divorced his wife while she was menstruating.' ʿAbd Allāh said: 'So he returned her to me and did not consider it anything"," and he said: When she becomes pure"," let him divorce or let him retain.'\"" Ibn ʿUmar said: And the Prophet ﷺ recited: {O Prophet"," when you [Muslims] divorce women"," divorce them at [the commencement of] their ʿiddah} — meaning at the beginning of their ʿiddah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. Muslim said: He erred when he said \""ʿUrwah\"" — rather he was the freedman of ʿAzzah. Muslim also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad and Abī ʿĀṣim from Ibn Jurayj"," and in it the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Let him take her back.\"" So he returned her. And in the narration of some of them from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," he said: He said to me: \""Take her back.\"" So he returned her to me and did not consider it anything. [Ṣaḥīḥ"," excluding his statement \""he did not consider it anything\""]"""
"14936","(14930) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; he said: al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The ḥadīth of Abū al-Zubayr is similar to it — meaning what Nāfiʿ narrated from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the command to take her back.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""And Nāfiʿ is more reliable in narration from Ibn ʿUmar than Abū al-Zubayr"," and the more reliable of the two ḥadīths is more deserving to be acted upon when they differ. And Nāfiʿ has been corroborated by others among the people of reliability in the ḥadīth. It was said to him: 'Was the divorce of Ibn ʿUmar during the time of the Prophet ﷺ counted as one divorce?' He said: 'What is the matter with you?' — meaning it was counted. And the Qurʾān indicates that it is counted. Allah"," the Most High"," said: {Divorce is twice; then [after that]"," either keep [her] in good manner or release [her] with good treatment.} He did not specify one divorce to the exclusion of another.\"" Then he continued his speech until he said: \""And it is also possible that it was not counted as anything — a correct action that was an error"," as it is said of a man: 'He erred in his action' and 'He erred in an answer that he gave' — he did not do anything"," meaning he did not do anything correct.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14937","(14931) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd — al-Sijistānī — said: \All the aḥādīth are contrary to what Abū al-Zubayr said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14938","(14932) Abū al-Fawāris — al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris, brother of the Shaykh Abī al-Fatḥ al-Ḥāfiẓ, may Allah have mercy on him — in Baghdād informed us; Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Salm — narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Abū al-Ṣalt Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Umayyah al-Dhāriʿ narrated to us from his memory; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: I heard Muʿādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever gives a divorce in accordance with bidʿah (innovation)"," we shall bind him to his bidʿah.\"""""
"14939","(14933) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Umayyah al-Miṣrī is matrūk al-ḥadīth (abandoned in ḥadīth)."
"14940","(14934) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us. Both said: Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the freedman of the family of Ṭalḥah, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \Command him to take her back"," then let him divorce her when she becomes pure"," or when she is pregnant.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ"," agreed upon]"""
"14941","(14935) And al-Shāfiʿī also cited as evidence what Abū Zakariyyāʾ ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ narrated to us — al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us — Mālik narrated to us — Ibn Shihāb narrated to me — that Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī informed him: that ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī came and mentioned the hadith concerning the liʿān (mutual cursing). Sahl said: \When they had finished their mutual cursing"," ʿUwaymir said: 'I have lied against her"," O Messenger of Allah — if I had kept her"," I would have been lying about her.' So he divorced her three times before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ could give him any command.\"" He said in the book: \""So ʿUwaymir pronounced three divorces before the Prophet ﷺ"," and if that had been forbidden"," he would have prohibited him from it.\"" And he said: \""If the divorce has become binding upon you"," then you are sinful for combining three [at once]; do such-and-such.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And in the narration of Ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," the Prophet ﷺ said to the two who performed the liʿān: \""Your reckoning is with Allah; one of you is a liar. You have no right over her.\"" This is not in the narration of Sahl ibn Saʿd"," nor is the triple divorce in the narration of Ibn ʿUmar.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," also cited as evidence the hadith of Fāṭimah bint Qays: that Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥafs divorced her al-battah (i.e."," irrevocably) — meaning"," and Allah knows best"," three times — and we did not learn that the Prophet ﷺ forbade that. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14942","(14936) And it has been narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him — Abū Ḥāmid al-Sharqī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us — my father narrated to me — Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭaḥmān narrated to us from Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from al-Shaʿbī from Fāṭimah bint Qays, that she said: \My husband divorced me three times"," and that was raised to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," but he did not grant me a residence or maintenance"," and he commanded me to observe my ʿiddah at the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr from Fāṭimah bint Qays"," she said: \""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," my husband has divorced me three times"," and I fear that he may rush [into something harmful].' So he commanded her"," and she moved.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1480]"""
"14943","(14937) And Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Naysābūrī narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn al-Akram narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Yaḥyā narrated to me — ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to me — al-Qāsim narrated from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her: \A man divorced his wife three times"," and another man married her and then divorced her before he had touched her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Is she lawful for the first [husband]?' He said: 'No"," until he tastes her honey as the first one tasted it.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Bundār"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," both of them from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān. Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""And Rukānah divorced his wife al-battah"," which could mean one or three"," and the Prophet ﷺ asked him about his intention and made him swear an oath regarding it. We do not know that he forbade pronouncing al-battah when intending three. And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," may Allah be pleased with him"," divorced his wife three times.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"14944","(14938) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us — Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak from Muḥammad ibn Rāshid — Salamah ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us from his father, that it was mentioned to him that pronouncing three divorces at once is reprehensible, and he said: \Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Mughīrah divorced Fāṭimah bint Qays with a single word — three times — and we did not learn that the Prophet ﷺ censured him for that. And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf divorced his wife three times"," and no one censured him for it.\""\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by Shaybān ibn Farrūkh from Muḥammad ibn Rāshid.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," also cited as evidence in this regard what he narrated through his chain from Ibn ʿAbbās"," Abū Hurayrah"," and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," may Allah be pleased with them"," regarding the one who divorces his wife three times before consummating the marriage — she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. He said: \""Neither Ibn ʿAbbās nor Abū Hurayrah censured him for pronouncing three [at once]"," and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr did not say to him: 'Evil is what you have done by divorcing three times.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Those reports will come after this"," if Allah wills.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14945","(14939) As for the hadith which Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Shuʿayb ibn Ruzayq narrated to us — that ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī narrated to him from al-Ḥasan, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: \He divorced his wife one divorce while she was menstruating"," and then he intended to follow it with two more divorces at the two remaining periods of purity. This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: 'O Ibn ʿUmar"," this is not how Allah commanded you. You have erred from the Sunnah. The Sunnah is that you wait for purity and then divorce for each period of purity.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me"," so I took her back. Then he said: 'When she becomes pure"," then either divorce or keep her.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think if I had divorced her three times — would it be permissible for me to take her back?' He said: 'She would have become irrevocably separated from you"," and it would be a sin.'\""\n\nThese additions brought by ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī are not in the narration of anyone else"," and they have spoken critically of him. It is likely that his words \""and it would be a sin\"" refer back to the act of pronouncing three divorces during the state of menstruation. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14946","(14940) And likewise Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Shādhān and Aḥmad ibn Salamah said — Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: \He divorced his wife while she was menstruating with a single divorce. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to take her back"," then to keep her until she became pure"," then menstruated another menstrual period with him"," then to allow her time until she became pure from her menstruation. Then"," if he wished to divorce her"," he should divorce her when she became pure"," before he touched her. That is the ʿiddah which Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," commanded that women be divorced for.\"" And when Ibn ʿUmar was asked about that"," he would say to any one of them: \""If you divorced her three times"," she has become forbidden for you until she marries a husband other than you"," and you have disobeyed Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," regarding what He commanded you concerning the divorce of your wife.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"14947","Here is the translated text in English:

Ibn Umar said, ""If I were to divorce my wife twice, the Prophet would order me to do this."" 

Abdullah said, ""When I was asked about this, I said, 'I do not have any of them.' Then I said, 'If I were to divorce my wife once, twice, or thrice, the Messenger of Allah would order me to do this. And if I were to divorce her thrice, it would be forbidden for me to marry another woman until I marry a woman other than her, and I would have disobeyed Allah in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce. And I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice. And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce, and I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice.'

He said, ""And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce, and I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice. And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce, and I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice.'

He said, ""And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce, and I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice. And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce, and I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice.'

