He said, ""And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce, and I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice. And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce, and I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice.'

He said, ""And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him in what He has ordered me to do with my wife, which is divorce, and I would not have any return in the third divorce, but only in the first and second divorce, which is in the divorce and the divorce twice. And my saying 'I would have disobeyed Allah' means that I would have disobeyed Him"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'If I had divorced it once or twice"," the Prophet ﷺ would have commanded me with this.'\""\n\nIt was narrated to us by ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Milḥān narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ: \""That ʿAbd Allāh divorced his wife while she was menstruating"," and he mentioned the hadith.\"" He said: \""And ʿAbd Allāh"," when asked about that"," would say to any one of them: 'As for you — if you divorced your wife once or twice"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me with this. But if you divorced her three times"," she has become forbidden for you until she marries a husband other than you"," and you have disobeyed Allah regarding what He commanded you concerning the divorce of your wife'\"" — meaning"," and Allah knows best"," there is no revocation in the three; revocation is only in the one and the two"," i.e."," in the single divorce and the two divorces.\n\nAnd his statement \""and you have disobeyed Allah regarding what He commanded you concerning the divorce of your wife\"" refers to when he divorced her during the state of menstruation. Thus"," his statement here goes back to the original issue. As for the detailed distinction"," it is for the purpose of establishing or negating the right of revocation"," not for attributing sin to one of them rather than the other. And Allah knows best.\n\nAs for his statement in the narration of Nāfiʿ: \""then he should keep her until she becomes pure"," then menstruates another menstrual period with him"," then he should allow her time until she becomes pure from her menstruation\"" — al-Shāfiʿī said: \""It is possible that what he meant by that is the istibrāʾ (waiting to ensure the womb is clear)"," that he should ascertain her state after the menstrual cycle in which he divorced her by means of a complete period of purity and then a complete menstrual cycle"," so that he divorces her while she knows whether her ʿiddah is determined by pregnancy or by menstruation"," and so that he divorces after knowing whether she is pregnant"," without being ignorant of what he has done"," or that he may wish to keep her on account of pregnancy. And if she had asked for a divorce while not being pregnant"," she should refrain from asking while pregnant.\"" Then he continued his discussion until he said: \""Along with the fact that other than Nāfiʿ only narrated from Ibn ʿUmar: 'until she becomes pure from the menstrual cycle in which he divorced her; then if he wishes"," he may keep her"," and if he wishes"," he may divorce.'\""\n\nYūnus ibn Jubayr"," Anas ibn Sīrīn"," Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and others narrated it contrary to the narration of Nāfiʿ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""The narration from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh on this is varied. As for from others"," it is as al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14948","(14942) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī narrated — he said: This hadith was narrated from Ibn ʿUmar by Yūnus ibn Jubayr, Anas ibn Sīrīn, Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, Zayd ibn Aslam, Abū al-Zubayr, and Manṣūr from Abū Wāʾil — all of them with the same meaning: \The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to take her back until she became pure; then if he wished"," he could divorce"," and if he wished"," he could keep her.\""\n\nAnd likewise Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated it from Sālim from Ibn ʿUmar. As for the narration of al-Zuhrī from Sālim from Ibn ʿUmar"," and the narration of Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: \""The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to take her back until she became pure"," then menstruated"," then became pure; then if he wished"," he could divorce"," or if he wished"," he could keep her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14949","(14943) As for the athar which Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Ḥumayd ibn Masʿadah narrated to us — Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Ayyūb narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Kathīr from Mujāhid, who said: \I was with Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," when a man came to him and said: 'He has divorced his wife three times.' He remained silent until we thought that he would return her to him. Then he said: 'One of you goes and commits a foolish act"," then says: \""O Ibn ʿAbbās"," O Ibn ʿAbbās!\"" And Allah"," exalted be His praise"," said: { And whoever fears Allah"," He will make for him a way out } [al-Ṭalāq:2]. But you have not feared Allah"," so I find no way out for you. You have disobeyed your Lord"," and your wife has become irrevocably separated from you. And Allah said: { O Prophet"," when you divorce women"," divorce them } — at the beginning of their ʿiddah — thus in this narration"," three times.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Sijistānī 2197]"""
"14950","(14944) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿAbbās: \He was asked about a man who divorced his wife one hundred times. He said: 'You have disobeyed your Lord"," and your wife has become irrevocably separated from you. You did not fear Allah so that He might make a way out for you.' Then he recited: { O Prophet"," when you divorce women"," divorce them } — at the beginning of their ʿiddah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14951","(14945) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding a man who divorced his wife a thousand times. He said: \As for three"," they render your wife forbidden to you"," and the remainder is a sin upon you"," for you have taken the verses of Allah as a mockery.\""\n\nIn this there is an indication that he considered the sin to lie in what exceeds three"," and Allah knows best.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī narrated it from al-Zanjī from Ibn Jurayḥ from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding one hundred: he said"," \""Ninety-seven — you have taken the verses of Allah as a mockery.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""Ibn ʿAbbās condemned everything that exceeded the number of divorces which Allah had not sanctioned"," and he did not condemn that which Allah had sanctioned"," namely the three.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14952","(14946) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh informed me; Yazīd ibn al-Haytham informed me that Ibrāhīh ibn Abī al-Layth narrated to him; al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us from Sufyān from Abū Isḥāq from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \Whoever wishes to divorce according to the Sunnah"," as Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has commanded"," let him wait until she menstruates"," then becomes pure"," then let her divorce her while she is pure"," without having had intercourse"," and let him have two witnesses. Then let her wait until she menstruates"," then becomes pure. If he wishes"," he may take her back"," and if he wishes"," he may divorce her.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14953","(14947) Al-Aʿmash narrated it from Abū Isḥāq from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \The Sunnah divorce is that he divorce her in each period of purity"," one divorce. When the last of these occurs"," that is the waiting period which Allah has commanded.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn and al-Qāsim"," the two sons of Ismāʿīl al-Maḥāmilī"," both said: Abū al-Sāʾib — Salm ibn Junādah — narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghayāth narrated to us from al-Aʿmash"," and he mentioned it. \""And we consider it recommended to act in this manner.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd that he considered transgression to lie in exceeding three"," and Allah knows best. This is in what Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated from ʿAmr ibn Marzūq from Shuʿbah from al-Aʿmash from Masrūq"," who said: \""A man asked ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: 'A man divorced his wife a hundred times.' He said: 'She is irrevocably separated by three"," and the rest is transgression.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14954","(14948) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me by way of ijāzah; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Ibn Zuhayr narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us from Sufyān from Manṣūr and al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm from ʿAlqamah, who said: \A man came to ʿAbd Allāh and said: 'I have divorced my wife a hundred times.' He said: 'She is separated from you by three"," and the rest is disobedience (maʿṣiyah).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14955","(14949) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us; Ḥumayd ibn Wāqiʿ ibn Saḥbān informed us that a man came to ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was in the mosque and said: \A man divorced his wife three times in a single sitting.\"" He said: \""He has sinned against his Lord"," and his wife has become forbidden to him.\"" The man went and mentioned that to Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with him)"," intending thereby to find fault with ʿImrān. He said: \""Do you not see that ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn said such and such?\"" Abū Mūsā said: \""May Allah increase the likes of Abū Nujayd among us.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14956","(14950) Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Junayd narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ḥumayd ibn Kāsib narrated to us; Yaʿlā ibn Shabīb al-Makkī narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated to us from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \A man used to divorce his wife as much as he wished"," even if he divorced her a hundred times or more"," and if he took her back before her waiting period had expired"," she would be his. A man said to his wife: 'By Allah"," I shall not divorce you so that you become irrevocably separated from me"," nor shall I take you back.' She said: 'How is that?' He said: 'I shall divorce you"," and whenever your waiting period is about to end"," I shall take you back"," then I shall divorce you again"," and I shall keep doing this.' The woman complained of that to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," and ʿĀʾishah mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He remained silent and said nothing"," until the Qurʾān was revealed: {Divorce is twice; then either retain her in kindness or release her with good treatment} [al-Baqarah 229]. Then the people began the divorce anew — whoever wished"," divorced"," and whoever wished"," did not divorce.\""\n\nQutaybah ibn Saʿīd and al-Ḥumaydī also narrated it from Yaʿlā ibn Shabīb"," and Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yāsar said something to the same effect. [Ḥasan]"""
"14957","(14951) The revelation of the verse concerning this was narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father, who said: \When a man divorced his wife and then took her back before her waiting period had expired"," that was valid for him"," even if he had divorced her a thousand times. Then a man set out to his wife and divorced her"," then gave her respite until"," when her waiting period was nearly over"," he took her back and then divorced her"," and said: 'By Allah"," I shall never take you back"," and you shall never be free.' So Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," revealed: {Divorce is twice; then either retain her in kindness or release her with good treatment} [al-Baqarah 229]. Then the people began the divorce anew from that day — those among them who had divorced and those who had not.\""\n\nThis is a mursal narration"," and it is ṣaḥīḥ"," as stated by al-Bukhārī and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14958","(14952) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; al-Zuhrī narrated to me; ʿUrwah narrated from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that he heard her say: \The woman of Rifāʿah al-Quraẓī came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I was with Rifāʿah al-Quraẓī"," and he divorced me irrevocably (battat ṭalāqī). Then I married ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr after him"," but with him he has only something like the fringe of a garment.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled and said: 'Do you wish to return to Rifāʿah? No"," not until you taste his sweetness and he tastes your sweetness.'\""\n\nAbū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and Khālid ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ was at the door"," waiting to be given permission to enter. He called out and said: \""O Abū Bakr"," do you not hear what this woman is openly declaring in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14959","(14953) Abū ʿAmr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb — informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; al-Ḥasan, that is Ibn Sufyān, narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to us; al-Qāsim narrated from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that a man divorced three times, then she married another man who divorced her. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: \Is she lawful for the first husband?\"" He said: \""No"," until she tastes his sweetness"," just as the first tasted hers.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Yaḥyā.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) also used as evidence the ḥadīth of ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī and Fāṭimah bint Qays"," both of which we have mentioned. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"14960","(14954) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed me; Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us from Ayyūb from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: \I remained for twenty years"," being narrated to by people whom I do not suspect"," that Ibn ʿUmar divorced his wife three times while she was menstruating"," and he was commanded to take her back. I did not suspect them"," but I did not know the ḥadīth"," until I met Abū Ghallāb — Yūnus ibn Jubayr — who was a man of reliability. He narrated to me that he asked Ibn ʿUmar"," and he narrated to him that he divorced his wife one divorce while she was menstruating"," and he was commanded to take her back. I said: 'Was it counted against him?' He said: 'What then"," even if he was helpless and foolish?'\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"14961","(14955) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū Umayyah al-Ṭarsūsī narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr al-Rāzī narrated to us; Shuʿayb ibn Ruzayq narrated to us that ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī narrated to them from al-Ḥasan, who narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — divorced his wife once while she was menstruating, and then intended to follow it with two further divorces at the remaining two periods of purity. This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \O Ibn ʿUmar"," this is not how Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," has commanded. You have erred from the Sunnah"," and the Sunnah is that you await the period of purity and then divorce for each period of purity.\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me"," so I took her back. Then he said to me: 'When she becomes pure"," then either divorce at that point or retain her.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what is your view — if I were to divorce her three times"," would it be permissible for me to take her back?' He said: 'No. She would become irrevocably separated from you"," and it would be a sin.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14962","(14956) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: It was read to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz while I was listening: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Tarjamānī — Abū Ibrāhīm — narrated to you; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — that a man came to ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — and said: \I have irrevocably divorced my wife (al-battah) while she was menstruating.\"" He said: \""You have disobeyed your Lord and separated from your wife.\"" The man said: \""Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — when he separated from his wife"," to take her back.\"" So ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — said to him: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to take his wife back because there remained a divorce for him to revoke"," but nothing remains for you by which you may take your wife back.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14963","(14957) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Zayd ibn Wahb, that Bāṭāl was in Madīnah and he divorced his wife a thousand times. This was raised to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — and he said: \I was only playing.\"" So ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — struck him with the whip and said: \""Three should suffice you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14964","(14958) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from Shaqīq, who heard Anas ibn Mālik say: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — said regarding a man who divorced his wife three times before consummating the marriage: \They are three (i.e."," all three take effect). She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband.\"" And whenever such a case was brought to him"," he would punish the man severely. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14965","(14959) Abū ʿAmr al-Razjāhī narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, saying: I read to Abū Muḥammad Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Kūfī; Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us; Ḥasan narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — regarding a man who divorced his wife three times before consummating the marriage. He said: \She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14966","(14960) And Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14967","(14961) And Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Khushaysh al-Muqriʾ in Kūfah informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Azdī, Ibn Abī al-ʿAzāʾim, informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us from al-Aʿmash, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from some of his companions, who said: A man came to ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — and said: \I have divorced my wife a thousand times.\"" He said: \""Three render her unlawful for you"," and distribute the remainder among your wives.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14968","(14962) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: I heard Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn say: ʿAlqamah ibn Qays narrated to me, saying: A man came to Ibn Masʿūd — may Allah be pleased with him — and said: \A man divorced his wife a hundred times last night.\"" He said: \""Did you say it once?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Did you intend thereby that your wife become irrevocably separated from you?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""It is as you said.\"" He said: \""And another man came to him and said: 'A man divorced his wife last night the number of the stars.'\"" He said: \""Did you say it once?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Did you intend thereby that your wife become irrevocably separated?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""It is as you said.\"" Muḥammad said: \""He mentioned something about the women of the people of the earth that I do not remember.\"" He said: \""Allah has made the matter of divorce clear. Whoever divorces as Allah has commanded"," it is clear for him"," and whoever has it made confusing for him"," We have made it confusing for him. By Allah"," you do not confuse matters for yourselves and we bear it on your behalf — it is as you say.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14969","(14963) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from Ayyūb, from Ibn Sīrīn, from ʿAlqamah, who said: \We were with ʿAbd Allāh"," and he mentioned its meaning"," but the wording differs.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14970","(14964) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd informed us; Abū Muslim al-Kajjī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from ʿĀṣim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \A woman divorced three times before consummation is in the same position as the one with whom consummation has taken place.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14971","(14965) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Ibn Qaʿnab and Ibn Bukayr informed us from Mālik — and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us from Ibn Shihāb, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from Muḥammad ibn Iyās ibn al-Bukayr, who said:\n\nA man divorced his wife three times before consummating the marriage. Then he wished to remarry her, so he came to seek a fatwā. I went along with him to ask on his behalf. He asked Abū Hurayrah and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās about it, and they both said: \We do not see that you may marry her until she marries a husband other than you.\"" He said: \""My divorce of her was only one.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""You have sent forth from your hand that which was your prerogative (and cannot be taken back).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14972","(14966) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bukayr — meaning Ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ashajj — who informed him from Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh al-Anṣārī, who said:\n\nI was sitting with ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr and ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them — when Muḥammad ibn Iyās ibn al-Bukayr came to them and said: \A man from the people of the desert divorced his wife three times before consummating the marriage. What do you two say?\"" Ibn al-Zubayr said: \""This is a matter in which we have no ruling. Go to Ibn ʿAbbās and Abū Hurayrah"," for I left them both with ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — so ask them and then come back and inform us.\"" So he went and asked them. Ibn ʿAbbās said to Abū Hurayrah: \""Give him a fatwā"," O Abū Hurayrah"," for a difficult matter has come to you.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""One divorce separates her"," and three divorces make her ḥarām until she marries a husband other than him.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"14973","(14967) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bukayr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ashajj, from al-Nuʿmān ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh al-Anṣārī, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, who said:\n\nA man came to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ to seek a fatwā about a man who had divorced his wife three times before touching her. ʿAṭāʾ said: I said, \The divorce of a virgin is only one.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr said to me: \""You are only a storyteller. One divorce separates her"," and three divorces make her ḥarām until she marries a husband other than him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14974","(14968) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh informed me: Yazīd ibn al-Haytham informed me that Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth informed them from al-Ashjaʿī, from Sufyān, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said:\n\nIf a man divorces his wife three times before consummating the marriage, she is not lawful for him until she marries a husband other than him. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14975","(14969) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: Ibn Numayr informed us from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, that a man asked Ibn ʿUmar:\n\n\I divorced my wife three times while she was menstruating.\"" He said: \""You have disobeyed your Lord and separated from your wife.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14976","(14970) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh informed us: My father informed us: Shuʿbah informed us from Ṭāriq ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: I heard Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim say:\n\nA man asked al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah — and I was present — about a man who had divorced his wife one hundred times. He said: \Three make her ḥarām"," and ninety-seven are an excess.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14977","(14971) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Wāsiṭī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥumayd al-Rāzī informed us: Salamah ibn al-Faḍl informed us from ʿAmr ibn Abī Qays, from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said:\n\nʿĀʾishah al-Khathʿamiyyah was married to al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him. When ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — was killed, she said: \Congratulations on the caliphate!\"" He said: \""You express schadenfreude at the killing of ʿAlī! Go"," you are divorced\"" — meaning three times. He said: She wrapped herself in her garments and sat until she completed her ʿiddah. Then he sent her the remainder of her dowry and ten thousand as charity. When the messenger came to her"," she said: \""A paltry provision from a departing beloved.\"" When her words reached him"," he wept and then said: \""Were it not that I heard my grandfather — or my father informed me that he heard my grandfather — say: 'Any man who divorces his wife three times at one time"," or three times in an ambiguous manner"," she is not lawful for him until she marries a husband other than him' — I would have taken her back.\""\n\nIt is also narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shamir"," from ʿImrān ibn Muslim"," and from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā"," from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14978","(14972) Abū Naṣr al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ informed us — and Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ and Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr informed us. Isḥāq and Isḥāq said: \informed us","\"" and Ibn Rāfiʿ said: \""informed us\"" — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us from Ibn Ṭāwūs"," from his father"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said:\n\nAt the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," Abū Bakr"," and the first two years of the caliphate of ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — three divorces were counted as one. Then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \""People have hastened in a matter in which they had patience. Were we to enforce it upon them"," we would enforce it upon them.\"" So he enforced it upon them.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1472]"""
"14979","(14973) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Ibn Ṭāwūs informed me from his father that Abū al-Ṣahbāʾ said to Ibn ʿAbbās:\n\n\Do you know that three divorces were made to count as one at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — and during three years of the governorship of ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him?\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""Yes.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Rūḥ from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"14980","(14974) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq and Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us. Abū Bakr said: \informed us","\"" and Abū al-Faḍl said: \""informed us\"" — Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us: Ḥammād informed us from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī"," from Ibrāhīm ibn Maysarah"," from Ṭāwūs"," that Abū al-Ṣahbāʾ said to Ibn ʿAbbās:\n\n\""Tell me from your own knowledge: was not the triple divorce at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — counted as one?\"" He said: \""That was so. But then"," during the time of ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — people began to issue divorces in rapid succession"," so he enforced it upon them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. This ḥadīth is one of those over which al-Bukhārī and Muslim differed: Muslim included it"," while al-Bukhārī omitted it. I believe he omitted it because it contradicts the other narrations from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"14981","(14975) Among them is what Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Thābit al-Marwazī narrated to me, that ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated to me from his father, from Yazīd al-Naḥwī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the verse: **{And the divorced women shall wait concerning themselves for three menstrual periods}** up to His words: **{And their husbands have a better right to take them back}** — the verse. And that is: when a man divorced his wife, he had a greater right to take her back, even if he divorced her three times. Then this was abrogated, and He said: **{Divorce is twice}** — the verse. [Weak]"
"14982","(14976) And among them is what Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that al-Rabīʿ informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Muslim and ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʿIkrimah ibn Khālid informed me that Saʿīd ibn Jubayr informed him: that a man came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said: \I have divorced my wife a thousand times.\"" He said: \""Take three and leave nine hundred and ninety-seven.\"" And ʿAmr ibn Murrah narrated it from Saʿid ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," that he said to a man who had divorced his wife three times: \""She has become forbidden for you.\"" [Good]"""
"14983","(14977) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, that al-Rabīʿ informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Muslim ibn Khālid and ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Mujāhid, who said: A man said to Ibn ʿAbbās: \I have divorced my wife a hundred times.\"" He said: \""Take three and leave ninety-seven.\"" [Good. It was narrated before it.]"""
"14984","(14978) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, that my father narrated to us, that Shuʿbah narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ and Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj, from Mujāhid, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about a man who had divorced his wife a hundred times. He said: \You have disobeyed your Lord"," and your wife has become irrevocably separated from you. You did not fear Allah so that He might make a way out for you — **{Whoever fears Allah"," He will make a way out for him}** — **{O Prophet"," when you divorce women"," divorce them}** — at the beginning of their waiting period.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14985","(14979) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, that Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Rāfiʿ, from ʿAṭāʾ: that a man said to Ibn ʿAbbās: \I have divorced my wife a hundred times.\"" He said: \""Take three and leave ninety-seven.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14986","(14980) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, that Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated from Ayyūb, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, that Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about a man who had divorced his wife the number of the stars. He said: \A single pronouncement of divorce is sufficient for you.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14987","(14981) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, that Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Mālik ibn al-Ḥārith, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \A man came to me and said: 'My uncle has divorced his wife three times.' He said: 'Your uncle has disobeyed Allah"," so Allah has caused him to regret it"," and he obeyed Satan"," so He did not make a way out for him.' He said: 'Can no one make her lawful for him (through marriage to another man)?' He said: 'Whoever tries to deceive Allah"," Allah will deceive him.'\"" [Good]"""
"14988","(14982) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, that Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from Muḥammad ibn Iyās ibn al-Bukayr, who said: \A man divorced his wife three times before consummating the marriage with her"," then he wished to marry her. He came to seek a fatwa"," and I went with him to ask on his behalf. He asked Abū Hurayrah and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās about that"," and they said to him: 'We do not think that you should marry her until she has married another husband.' He said: 'My divorce of her was only one.' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'You have sent from your hand that which was your excess (i.e."," you pronounced more than you intended).'\""\n\nThese are the narrations of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ"," Mujāhid"," ʿIkrimah"," ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," Mālik ibn al-Ḥārith"," and Muḥammad ibn Iyās ibn al-Bukayr — and it has been narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī ʿĀyāsh al-Anṣārī — all of them from Ibn ʿAbbās"," that he permitted the triple divorce and upheld it. [Authentic]"""
"14989","(14983) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī said: \If the meaning of Ibn ʿAbbās's statement is that the triple divorce was counted as one during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — meaning by the command of the Prophet ﷺ — then what seems most likely"," and Allah knows best"," is that Ibn ʿAbbās knew that it was something that was then abrogated. If it is said: 'What indicates what you have described?' It is said: 'It is unlikely that Ibn ʿAbbās would narrate something from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then contradict it with something he did not know was from the Prophet ﷺ in which there was a difference of opinion.'\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: The narration of ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās has already been discussed regarding abrogation"," and therein is confirmation of the soundness of this interpretation.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""If it is said: 'Perhaps this is something narrated from ʿUmar"," and Ibn ʿAbbās said in it the statement of ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him","' it is said: 'We know that Ibn ʿAbbās differed with ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," regarding mutʿah marriage"," the selling of a dīnār for two dīnārs"," and the selling of the mothers of children"," and other matters. So how could he agree with him regarding something in which there was a difference of narration from the Prophet ﷺ?' If it is said: 'And this was mentioned during the time of Abū Bakr and the early part of the caliphate of ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him","' it is said: 'Allah knows best"," and the answer when he was asked for a fatwa contrary to that is as I have described.'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""And perhaps Ibn ʿabbās answered that the triple and the single are the same"," since Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has left the number of divorces to the husband"," and he may divorce whenever he wishes — so the triple and the single and more than three are the same in terms of effecting the divorce.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""And it is possible that he expressed 'triple divorce' to mean irrevocable divorce (al-battah)"," as some of them have held.\"" [Authentic. Al-Shāfiʿī said in al-Umm.]"""
"14990","(14984) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us, that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥātim narrated to us, who said: I heard Abū Zurʿah say: \The meaning of this hadith"," in my view"," is that what you (people) today pronounce as three divorces"," they used to pronounce as one during the time of the Prophet ﷺ"," Abū Bakr"," and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with them both.\""\n\nAnd Abū Yaḥyā al-Sājī held that its meaning is: when he says to a virgin: 'You are divorced"," you are divorced"," you are divorced","' it counts as one. Then ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," made it severe upon them and counted it as three.\n\nThe Sheikh said: The narration of Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī indicates the soundness of this interpretation. [Authentic]"""
"14991","(14985) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad ibn Marwān narrated to us; Abū al-Nuʿmān narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from more than one narrator, from Ṭāwūs: that a man known as Abū al-Ṣahbāʾ, who was prolific in questioning Ibn ʿAbbās, said: \Did you know that when a man divorced his wife with three pronouncements before consummating the marriage"," they counted it as one during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," Abū Bakr"," and the early part of ʿUmar's caliphate?\"" Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \""Indeed"," when a man divorced his wife with three pronouncements before consummating the marriage"," they counted it as one during the time of the Prophet ﷺ"," Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and the early part of ʿUmar's caliphate (may Allah be pleased with him). But when ʿUmar saw that people had begun doing it consecutively"," he enforced all three upon them.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: It is as though he intended that if he issued three divorces in succession.\n\nJābir ibn Yazīd narrated from al-Shaʿbī"," from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," regarding a man who divorced his wife with three pronouncements before consummating the marriage: \""It was a bond he held in his hand; he released them all at once. But if they were issued in succession"," they count for nothing.\""\n\nSufyān al-Thawrī said: \""In succession\"" means: \""You are divorced"," you are divorced"," you are divorced.\"" She is irrevocably separated by the first"," and the other two count for nothing.\n\nIt was also narrated from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," to that effect. [Sahih. Previously referenced as no. 14982]"""
"14992","(14986) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; one of the sons of Abū Rāfiʿ, the freedman of the Prophet ﷺ, informed me from ʿIkrimah, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: ʿAbd Yazīd, the father of Rukānah, and his brothers divorced Umm Rukānah, and he married a woman from Muzaynah. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \He is no more use to me than this hair is to a hair he took from her head. Separate between us.\"" The Prophet ﷺ became angry and summoned Rukānah and his brothers. Then he said to his companions: \""Do you see that so-and-so resembles him in such-and-such a way"," and so-and-so resembles him in such-and-such a way?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAbd Yazīd: \""Divorce her.\"" So he did. Then he said: \""Take back your wife"," Umm Rukānah"," and her sisters.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I divorced her three times!\"" He said: \""I know. Take her back.\"" And he recited: {O Prophet"," when you [Muslims] divorce women"," divorce them at [the commencement of] their waiting period.} [Quran 65:1]\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: The ḥadīth of Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjayr and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah"," from his father"," from his grandfather"," that Rukānah divorced his wife with an irrevocable divorce and the Prophet ﷺ took her back"," is more authentic"," because they are the man's children and his family"," and they know best. Indeed"," Rukānah only divorced his wife with an irrevocable divorce"," and the Prophet ﷺ counted it as one. [Hasan]"""
"14993","(14987) The Sheikh said: It has also been narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Rukānah divorced his wife with three pronouncements in a single session. He was so grieved over her that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: \How did you divorce her?\"" He said: \""I divorced her three times.\"" He said: \""In a single session?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""That counts as only one. Take her back if you wish.\"" So he took her back. Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to hold the view that divorce should be pronounced at [the commencement of] each period of purity. That is the Sunnah upon which the people were"," and that which Allah commanded: {Divorce them at [the commencement of] their waiting periods.} [Quran 65:1]\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us; Muslim ibn ʿIṣām narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿd narrated to us; my uncle narrated to us; my father narrated from Ibn Isḥāq; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn narrated to me"," and he mentioned it.\n\nThis chain of narration does not constitute a proof"," given that eight narrators reported from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) a ruling to the contrary"," and given the narration of Rukānah's children that Rukānah's divorce was [counted as] one. And with Allah is success. [Hasan]"""
"14994","(14988) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Hishām narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Salamah al-Labaqī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from al-Aʿmash, who said: There was a sheikh in Kufah who said: \I heard ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) say: 'When a man divorces his wife with three pronouncements in a single session"," it is reduced to one. The people are [like] a single neck; they come to him and listen from him.'\"" He said: \""So I went to him and knocked on his door. An old man came out to me. I said: 'How did you hear ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) say regarding one who divorces his wife with three pronouncements in a single session?' He said: 'I heard ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) say: When a man divorces his wife with three pronouncements in a single session"," it is reduced to one.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'Where did you hear this from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)?' He said: 'I will bring you a book.' He brought it out"," and in it was: 'In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful. This is what I heard ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) say: When a man divorces his wife with three pronouncements in a single session"," she is irrevocably separated from him and is not lawful to her until she marries another husband.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'Woe to you! This is not what you said!' He said: 'The correct version is this"," but those people wanted me to say that.'\"" [Daʿīf]"""
"14995","(14989) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk in Baghdād narrated to us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿImrān ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylá narrated to us; Maslamah ibn Jaʿfar al-Aḥmasī said: I said to Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad: \Some people claim that whoever divorces three times in a state of ignorance is returned to the Sunnah"," making it one"," and they attribute this to you.\"" He said: \""Allah forbid! This is not our position. Whoever divorces three times"," it is as he said.\"" [Daʿīf]"""
"14996","(14990) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Sulaymān al-Kūfī in Baghdād narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Bahrām narrated to us; al-Ashjaʿī narrated from Bussām al-Ṣayrafī, who said: I heard Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad say: \Whoever divorces his wife with three pronouncements"," whether in ignorance or with knowledge"," she is irrevocably separated from him.\"" [Hasan]"""
"14997","(14991) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Fihr al-Miṣrī, resident in Makkah, narrated to us; the Qāḍī Abū al-Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Dhuhlī narrated to us; Idrīs ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm narrated to us; Layth ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Sumayʿ al-Ḥanafī narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: \I hear Allah say: {Divorce is twice.} [Quran 2:229] Where is the third?\"" He said: {Either retain her in kindness or release her with good treatment.} [Quran 2:229] That is the third.\"" This is how it was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him). The correct version is from Ismāʿīl ibn Sumayʿ"," from Abū Ruzayn"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," as a mursal narration. A group of trustworthy narrators reported it from Ismāʿīl in this way. [Daʿīf]"""
"14998","(14992) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh, Ismāʿīl ibn Zakariyyā, and Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Sumayʿ, from Abū Ruzayn, that a man said to the Prophet ﷺ: {Divorce is twice.} Where is the third? He said: {Either retain her in kindness or release her with good treatment.} It was also narrated from Qatādah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), but it is not [a valid narration]. [Daʿīf]"
"14999","(14993) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated from Sulaymān. And Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Mufassir informed us from the original of his hearing; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us in the Sacred Mosque; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to me; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥabīb ibn Arḍak, who heard ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ say: Yūsuf ibn Māhak informed me that he heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say, from the Prophet ﷺ: \Three things are taken seriously whether spoken in earnest or in jest: marriage"," divorce"," and taking back [one's wife].\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ismāʿīl. In the narration of Ibn Wahb"," it says: He heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And he said: from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥabīb"," without mentioning ibn Arḍak. [Daʿīf]"""
"15000","(14994) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ said to us: al-Layth narrated to me; Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq; ʿUmarah ibn ʿAbd Allāh heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib narrate from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Four things are binding: vows"," divorce"," emancipation"," and marriage.\"" [Daʿīf]"""
"15001","(14995) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakkī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that he used to say: \There are three matters in which there is no jesting: marriage (nikāḥ)"," divorce (ṭalāq)"," and manumission (ʿitq).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15002","(14996) By way of evidence, through what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh in Baghdād informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzāz narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Faqīh informed us, Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī informed me that he heard ʿAlqama ibn Waqqāṣ al-Laythī say: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) on the minbar narrating from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Actions are judged only by intentions"," and every person shall have only what he intended. So whoever's migration was for the sake of Allah and His Messenger"," his migration is for the sake of Allah and His Messenger; and whoever's migration was for the sake of worldly gain or a woman he wished to marry"," his migration is for that which he migrated.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr from Yazīd ibn Hārūn"," and from Ibn Abī ʿUmar from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15003","(14997) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us. He said: Abū ʿUbayd said regarding the ḥadīth of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man was brought to him whose wife had said to him: \Give me a simile.\"" He said: \""You are like a gazelle; you are like a dove.\"" She said: \""I will not be pleased until you say: 'Khalīyatun ṭāliqun.'\"" So he said that. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Take her by the hand"," for she is your wife.\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: Hushaym narrated it to us"," Ibn Abī Laylā informed us"," from al-Ḥakam"," from Khaythama ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shihāb al-Khawlānī"," from ʿUmar.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: His statement \""khalīyatun ṭāliqun\"" — he intended a she-camel that is tied with a rope and then released from its tether"," so it is \""khalīyatun\"" (freed) from the rope and \""ṭāliqun\"" (released) because it has been released from it. So the man intended that"," and ʿUmar waived the divorce from him due to his intention. This is the principle for everyone who utters something resembling the wording of divorce while intending something other than it: his word stands between him and Allah (the Most High). In terms of legal ruling"," it is upon the interpretation of the madhhab of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\nThe Sheikh said: The matter is as he explained regarding his statement \""khalīyatun.\"" As for his statement \""ṭāliqun","\"" that is the very expression of divorce itself"," so his claim regarding it is not accepted in legal ruling. However"," it is possible that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) only waived it from him because he said \""khalīyatun ṭāliqun\"" — he did not direct the divorce toward her nor address her with it"," so the divorce did not take effect upon her. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan]"""
"15004","(14998) The Sheikh al-Imām Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us by dictation. Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, my uncle Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Shāfiʿ narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Sāʾib, from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjayr ibn ʿAbd Yazīd, that Rukāna ibn ʿAbd Yazīd divorced his wife Suḥayma al-Muzaniyya al-Batta, then came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I divorced my wife Suḥayma al-Batta"," and by Allah"," I only intended one (divorce).\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Rukāna: \""By Allah"," did you only intend one?\"" Rukāna said: \""By Allah"," I only intended one.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned her to him. Then he divorced her a second time during the era of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and a third time during the era of ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15005","(14999) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yūnus al-Nasāʾī narrated that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr narrated to them, from Muḥammad ibn Idrīs, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī narrated to me, from Ibn al-Sāʾib, from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjayr, from Rukāna ibn ʿAbd Yazīd, from the Prophet (ﷺ), with this ḥadīth.\n\nLikewise, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Madanī narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Sāʾib, in a connected (mawṣūl) chain."
"15006","(15000) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Saʿīd narrated to me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī, from his father, from his grandfather. Abū Dāwūd said: I heard a shaykh in Makkah, and he said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjayr, from Rukāna ibn ʿAbd Yazīd, who said: \I had a woman called Suḥayma. I divorced her al-Batta"," then I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I divorced my wife Suḥayma al-Batta"," and by Allah"," I only intended one.' He said: 'By Allah"," did you only intend one?' I said: 'By Allah"," I only intended one.' So he returned her to me on the basis of one (divorce).\""\n\nThe second ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī is ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Sāʾib"," and the first ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī is Ibn Rukāna ibn ʿAbd Yazīd. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15007","(15001) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us with it. Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālūyah narrated to us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr al-Azdī narrated to us, Muʿāwiya ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, Jarīr narrated, from al-Zubayr ibn Saʿīd al-Hāshimī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn Rukāna, from his father, from his grandfather, that he divorced his wife al-Batta during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ), then came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and informed him, and said: \I did not intend by that except one.\"" He said: \""By Allah?\"" He said: \""By Allah.\"" He said: \""Then it is according to what you intended.\""\n\nLikewise"," Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated it from Shaybān ibn Farrūkh"," from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15008","(15002) It has also been said, regarding him and others: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn Yazīd ibn Rukāna. Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī, Shaybān, and others narrated to us. They said: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Saʿīd, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn Yazīd ibn Rukāna narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that he divorced his wife al-Batta, then came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \What did you intend by it?\"" He said: \""One.\"" He said: \""By Allah?\"" He said: \""By Allah.\"" He said: \""Then it is according to what you intended.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15009","(15003) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustūyah narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Saʿīd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm, Nūḥ ibn al-Haytham, and Ṣafwān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us. They said: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzāʿī narrated. He said: I asked al-Zuhrī: \Which of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) sought refuge from him?\"" He said: ʿUrwa informed me from ʿĀʾisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the daughter of al-Jawn entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he drew close to her"," she said: \""I seek refuge in Allah from you.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""You have sought refuge in the Mighty. Go back to your family.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," from al-Walīd ibn Muslim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15010","(15004) In the narration of Ibn Abī Dhiʾb from al-Zuhrī, he said: \Go back to your family\"" — he made it (count as) one divorce. ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us"," Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us"," Maḥmūd ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī narrated to us"," Ḥāmid ibn Ādam ibn Muslim al-Azdī narrated to us"," Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us"," from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"," from al-Zuhrī"," and he mentioned it as the statement of al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15011","(15005) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, that ʿAbdullāh ibn Kaʿb, the guide of Kaʿb when he became blind, from among his sons, said: \I heard Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrating his ḥadīth regarding when he stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabūk.\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth in its entirety"," and that the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and said: \""Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to separate from your wife.\"" I said: \""Shall I divorce her"," or what shall I do with her?\"" He said: \""No"," rather separate from her and do not approach her.\"" And he sent the same message to my two companions. So I said to your wife: \""Go to your family and remain among them until Allah decrees this matter.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from al-Layth. In this"," along with the first narration"," there is an indication that his statement \""Go to your family\"" is a figurative expression (kināyah): if he intended by it divorce"," it is a divorce"," and if he did not intend it"," it is not a divorce. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15012","(15006) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Faraj Abū ʿUtbah narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated from Abū al-Haytham, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Sawdah bint Zamʿah (may Allah be pleased with her): \Observe your waiting period (ʿiddah).\"" He made it a single divorce"," and he had the most right over her. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15013","(15007) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr, who heard Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Jaʿfar saying: al-Muṭṭalib ibn Ḥanṭab informed me that he divorced his wife irrevocably (al-battah), then he came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him. He said: \What compelled you to do that?\"" He said: \""I have done it.\"" So ʿUmar recited: *\""And had they done that to which they were admonished"," it would have been better for them and more strengthening\""* (al-Nisāʾ"," 4:66). \""What compelled you to do that?\"" He said: \""I have done it.\"" He said: \""Retain your wife"," for indeed the single divorce is irrevocable (tubatt).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15014","(15008) Abū Zakariyyā informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Salamah, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding the twin wife (al-tuʾamah) the same as he said regarding al-Muṭṭalib. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15015","(15009) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us: Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to say regarding *khaliyyah*, *bariyyah*, *battah*, and *bāʾinah*: \It is a single divorce"," and he has the most right over her.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15016","(15010) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us: It reached him that a letter was written to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) from Iraq that a man said to your wife: \Your rope is upon your hump (Ḥabluki ʿalā ghāribuki).\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to his governor: \""Order him to come to me during the season (of Ḥajj).\"" While ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) was performing ṭawāf of the House"," the man met him and greeted him. He said: \""Who are you?\"" He said: \""I am the one you ordered to be brought before you.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by the Lord of this structure"," did you intend divorce by your statement 'Your rope is upon your hump'?\"" The man said: \""Had you adjured me in other than this place"," I would not have told you the truth. I intended separation (al-firāq).\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""It is as you intended.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15017","(15011) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us: Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us: Ghassān ibn Muḍar narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Yazīd narrated from Abū al-Ḥalāl al-ʿAtkī, who said: A man came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: \Indeed"," I said to my wife: 'Your rope is upon your hump (Ḥabluki ʿalā ghāribuki).'\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""Meet us during the season.\"" The man came to him in al-Masjid al-Ḥarām and recounted the story. He said: \""Do you see that bald man performing ṭawāf of the House? Go to him"," ask him"," then come back and inform me of what he tells you.\"" So he went to him"," and behold"," it was ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: \""Who sent you to me?\"" He said: \""The Commander of the Faithful.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," he said to his wife: 'Your rope is upon your hump.'\"" He said: \""Face the House and swear by Allah that you did not intend divorce.\"" The man said: \""I swear by Allah"," I intended nothing but divorce.\"" He said: \""Your wife is irrevocably separated from you.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15018","(15012) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Manṣūr narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rābāḥ, that a man said to his wife: \Your rope is upon your hump (Ḥabluki ʾalā ghāribuki)","\"" and he said it repeatedly. Then he came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he adjured him between the Corner (al-Rukn) and the Station (al-Maqām): \""What did you intend by your statement?\"" He said: \""I intended divorce.\"" So he separated them.\n\nThe Shaykh said: It is as though he only adjured him regarding the intention of emphasis through repetition"," not regarding a new pronouncement"," and it is as though the man confessed and said: \""I intended by each instance the initiation of a divorce.\"" So he separated them. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15019","(15013) al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said in al-Qadīm: Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAṭāʾ that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) was approached regarding a man who said to his wife: \Your rope is upon your hump (Ḥabluki ʿalā ghāribuki).\"" So he said to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): \""Judge between them.\"" He mentioned the meaning of what we narrated"," except that he said: \""So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) carried it out as three.\"" He also narrated from Saʿīd"," from Qatādah"," from al-Ḥasan"," from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) something similar.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: This does not contradict the narration of Mālik"," as though ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) made it one"," as he said regarding al-battah"," and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) made it three. And Allah knows best. And it is possible that both of them made it three due to his repetition of the expression three times to a wife with whom consummation had occurred"," and his intention by each instance to initiate a divorce"," as we stated in the narration of Manṣūr from ʿAṭāʾ. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15020","(15014) Abū al-Fatḥ al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shurayḥī narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Sharīk, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh, and Qays narrated from Abū Ḥuṣayn, from Nuʿaym ibn Dajājah, who said: A man divorced his wife two divorces, then said to her: \You are ḥarām (forbidden) upon me.\"" He went to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him. He said to him: \""Do you consider them (women) the most insignificant to me?\"" Then he separated her from him.\n\nThe Shaykh said: It is as though he informed him of his intention of separation by it. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd we have narrated from Sharīḥ and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rābāḥ regarding al-battah that he is taken at his word (yudayyanu) in it; and from ʿAṭāʾ regarding his statement *khaliyyah*"," *khalawtu minnī*"," *bariyyah*"," *barittu minnī*"," *bāʾinah*"," and *bintu minnī* that he is taken at his word in them; and similarly from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār. [Ḥasan]"""
"15021","(15015) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us, Bisḥr ibn Aḥmad informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, Sufyān informed us, Maʿmar informed us, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, who said: \Whatever is intended as divorce"," it is divorce.\""\n\nAnd similarly it has been narrated to us from Masrūq"," Ibrāhīm"," and others. They intended by this that when a person speaks with words resembling divorce.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15022","(15016) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us, from ʿĀmir, who said: \ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāh ʿanhu) used to regard al-khaliyyah"," al-bariyyah"," al-battah"," and al-ḥarām as three divorces.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15023","(15017) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Kūfī informed us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, Ḥasan narrated to us, from Abī Sahl, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāh ʿanhu), who said: \Al-khaliyyah"," al-bariyyah"," al-battah"," al-bāʾin"," and al-ḥarām — if he intends them"," they are equivalent to three divorces.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: He only made them three divorces in this narration if he intended [divorce]. The first narration is more authentic in its isnād.\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15024","(15018) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bisḥrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr ibn Ḥabīb al-Sahmī narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us, from ʿUmar ibn ʿĀmir, from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from Saʿd ibn Hishām, that Zayd ibn Thābit said regarding al-bariyyah, al-ḥarām, and al-battah: \Three"," three.\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"15025","(15019) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bisḥrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (raḍiya Allāh ʿanhumā), that he used to say regarding al-khaliyyah, al-bariyyah, and al-battah: \Three [divorces]"," she is not lawful for him until she marries a husband other than him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 1174]"""
"15026","(15020) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Abū al-Yamān informed us, Shuʿayb informed us, from al-Zuhrī, who said: I heard Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān say: ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), informed him that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) came to her when Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, commanded him to give his wives the choice. The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) began with me and said: \I am going to mention something to you"," so do not hasten until you consult your parents.\"" And he knew that my parents would not command me to separate from him. Then he said: \""Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: 'O Prophet"," say to your wives' [al-Aḥzāb 28] until the completion of the two verses.\"" I said to him: \""In this matter shall I consult my parents? Indeed"," I desire Allah"," His Messenger"," and the Abode of the Hereafter.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān.\n\nAnd Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yūnus"," from al-Zuhrī"," adding in it that she said: \""Then the wives of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) did as I had done.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"15027","(15021) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us, Yūnus informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāh ʿanhā), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) was commanded to give his wives the choice…\"" and he mentioned its meaning with additional wording.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"15028","(15022) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated to us. And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl, from ʿĀmir, from Masrūq, who said: \I asked ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāh ʿanhā) about the choice"," and she said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) gave us the choice"," and we chose him"," and that was not a divorce.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," from Yaḥyā"," and Muslim narrated it from another chain from Ismāʿīl.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"15029","(15023) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from al-Shaʿbī, from Masrūq, who said: \I do not care whether I give my wife the choice once"," or a hundred times"," or a thousand times"," after she has chosen me. And indeed I asked ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāh ʿanhā)"," and she said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) gave us the choice — was that a divorce?'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"15030","(15024) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Akhr narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah. And from al-Aʿmash, from Muslim, from Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāh ʿanhā), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) gave us the choice"," and we chose him"," and that was not a divorce.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"15031","(15025) Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Abu Bakr al-Isfahani informed us; Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Umar and Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say: \If he gives her the choice and she chooses herself"," then it is one divorce"," and he has greater right over her. And if she chooses her husband"," then there is nothing (incumbent).\"" [Sahih]"""
"15032","(15026) He said: And Sufyan narrated from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he used to say regarding the option of choice (al-takhyir) the same as the statement of Umar and Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with them both. [Da'if]"
"15033","(15027) Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isfahani informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; Abu 'Abbad narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us; 'Isa ibn 'Asim narrated from Zadhan, who said: We were in the presence of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned the option of choice (al-khiyar). He said: \The Commander of the Faithful asked me about the option of choice"," so I said: 'If she chooses herself"," then it is one irrevocable divorce (ba'inah)"," and if she chooses her husband"," then it is one divorce and he has greater right over her.' Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'It is not so. Rather"," if she chooses her husband"," then there is nothing (incumbent)"," and if she chooses herself"," then it is one divorce and he has greater right over her.' I could not do other than follow the Commander of the Faithful"," Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him. When the matter was resolved for me and I knew that I would be questioned about the private parts"," I took what I held as my opinion.\"" They said: \""By Allah"," if you had agreed with the Commander of the Faithful"," Umar"," and abandoned the opinion you held"," it would have been more beloved to us than a matter in which you were singular after him.\"" He (the narrator) said: Then he laughed and said: \""He had already sent to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked Zayd"," and Zayd opposed both me and him. Zayd"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'If she chooses herself"," then it is three divorces"," and if she chooses her husband"," then it is one divorce and he has greater right over her.'\"" [Sahih]"""
"15034","(15028) He said: And al-Za'farani narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated from Jarir, from 'Isa, from Zadhan, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, something similar to it."
"15035","(15029) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us; Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated from 'Amir, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \If a man gives his wife the choice and she chooses her husband"," then it is one divorce and he has greater right over her return (raj'ah). And if she chooses herself"," then it is one irrevocable divorce (ba'inah) and he is a suitor among the suitors.\""\n\nHe said: And Zayd ibn Thabit"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to say: \""If she chooses herself"," then it is three (divorces).\""\n\nHe said: And Abdullah ibn Mas'ud"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to say: \""If a man gives his wife the choice and she chooses her husband"," then there is nothing (incumbent). And if she chooses herself"," then it is one divorce and he has greater right over her return (raj'ah).\"" (Q) The statement of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud"," may Allah be pleased with him"," is in agreement with the statement of Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," regarding the option of choice"," and this is what we hold"," due to its agreement with the established Sunnah from A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the option of choice"," and its agreement with the meaning of the well-known Sunnah from Rukanah from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the irrevocable divorce (al-battah): that it is a revocable divorce (raj'iyyah) when he intends by it one (divorce). As for Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," the narrations from him differ concerning that"," and the most well-known of them is what we have narrated"," and likewise Abu Hassan al-A'raj narrated from Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Sahih]"""
"15036","(15030) Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Bakr and 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' both said: Sa'id narrated from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \If she chooses herself"," then it is one irrevocable divorce (ba'inah)"," and if she chooses her husband"," then it is one divorce and he has greater right over her.\"" This was the position Qatadah held. And it has been narrated from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali"," from Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," two differing narrations"," each of them contradicting what has preceded. [Sahih]"""
"15037","(15031) One of them is what Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Isfahani informed us; Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Mukhawwal, from Abu Ja'far, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: \If she chooses herself"," then it is one irrevocable divorce (ba'inah)"," and if she chooses her husband"," then there is nothing (incumbent).\"" [Da'if]"""
"15038","(15032) And the other is what Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu 'Uthman 'Amr ibn Abdullah al-Basri narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Isma'il — that is, Ibn Abi Khalid — narrated from Abu Ishaq, who said: I and Abu al-Safar went to Abu Ja'far, and I asked him about the option of choice regarding a man who gave his wife the choice and she chose herself. He said: \It is one divorce"," and her husband has greater right over her return (raj'ah).\"" We said: \""If she chooses her husband?\"" He said: \""Then there is nothing (incumbent).\"" We said: \""Some people narrate from Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he said: 'If she chooses her husband"," then it is one divorce and her husband has greater right over her — that is"," over her return (raj'ah) — and if she chooses herself"," then it is one irrevocable divorce (ba'inah) and she has greater right over herself.'\"" He said: \""This is what they found in the written records. As for Abdullah ibn Mas'ud"," the authentic narration from him is what we have narrated.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15039","(15033) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah, who said: \If a man says to your wife: 'Your affair is in your own hands","' or 'Your affair is for you","' or he gives her to her family"," then it is one irrevocable divorce (ba'inah).\"" This is what is in this narration from Abdullah. [Sahih]"""
"15040","(15034) And the authentic view is that this is the statement of Masruq himself. Abu Abdullah informed us; Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to me; my father narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Isra'il narrated from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, who said: \If a man says to your wife: 'Your affair is in your own hands","' or 'Choose","' or he gives her to her family"," then it is one irrevocable divorce (ba'inah).\"" [Sahih]"""
"15041","(15035) He said: And 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: And I asked Sufyan, and he said: It is from Masruq, meaning that he did not say it was from 'Abd Allah. And the correct narration from 'Abd Allah is what has been previously mentioned. And Allah knows best.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Sharik, from Abu Hasin, raised to 'Abd Allah, regarding the gift (of authority): \If she accepts it"," it is one divorce"," and he has greater right over her.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15042","(15036) Abu al-Mihrajan informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakk informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), that she arranged the marriage of Quraybah bint Abi Umayyah to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and they married him to her. Then they reproached 'Abd al-Rahman, saying: \Only 'A'ishah married us (to her).\"" So 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) sent a message to 'Abd al-Rahman and mentioned that to him"," and he placed the matter of Quraybah in her own hands. So she chose her husband"," and that was not a divorce. [Sahih. Narrated by Malik]"""
"15043","(15037) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, al-Rabi' said: al-Shafi'i narrated as a report from Abu Mu'awiya and Ya'la, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, that a woman said to her husband: \If the matter that is in your hand were in my hand"," I would divorce you.\"" He said: \""I have placed the matter in your hand.\"" So she divorced herself three times. So 'Umar asked 'Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) about that. He said: \""It is one divorce"," and he has greater right over her.\"" So 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I also hold that opinion.\""\n\nAnd from al-Shafi'i as a report from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa"," from Ibn Abi Layla"," from Talhah"," from Ibrahim"," from 'Alqamah"," from 'Abd Allah"," who said: \""There is no irrevocable divorce except through khul' or ila'.\"" [Sahih. Previously mentioned under number 15025]"""
"15044","(15038) Abu Bakr al-Ardastani informed us, Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi informed us, Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us, 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali informed us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: Al-Aswad and 'Alqamah narrated to me, they said: A man came to Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: \There was between me and my wife some of what occurs between people.\"" She said: \""If the matter that is in your hand were in my hand"," I would know what to do.\"" He said: \""The matter that is in my hand regarding you is now in your hand.\"" She said: \""Then I have divorced myself three times.\"" 'Abd Allah said: \""I consider it to be one divorce"," and you have greater right over her. I will meet the Commander of the Faithful"," 'Umar"," and ask him about that.\"" So he met him and asked him"," and recounted the story to him. So 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""May Allah do such-and-such to men who take what Allah has placed in their hands and place it in the hands of women—dust in their mouths"," dust in their mouths!\"" He said: \""What did you say?\"" He said: \""I said: 'It is one divorce"," and he has greater right over her.'\"" He said: \""I also hold that opinion. And had you said otherwise"," I would have considered that you were not correct.\"" [Hasan]"""
"15045","(15039) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakk narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us, al-Shafi'i informed us, Malik informed us, from Sa'id ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, who informed him: He was sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) when Muhammad ibn Abi 'Atiq came to him with his eyes weeping. Zayd ibn Thabit said to him: \What is the matter with you?\"" He said: \""I gave my wife authority over her own matter"," and she separated from me.\"" Zayd said to him: \""What compelled you to do that?\"" He said: \""Fate (al-qadar).\"" Zayd said to him: \""Take her back if you wish. It is only one divorce"," and you have greater right over her.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Malik]"""
"15046","(15040) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad 'Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi both informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan, from Aban ibn 'Uthman, that a man placed the matter of his wife in her own hands, and she divorced herself three times. That was referred to Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: \It is one divorce"," and he has greater right over her.\"" [Hasan]"""
"15047","(15041) Through this same chain of narration, from 'Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that a man placed the matter of his wife in her own hands, and she divorced herself a thousand times. That was referred to Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: \It is one divorce"," and he has greater right over her.\"" [Hasan]"""
"15048","(15042) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us, al-Shafi'i informed us, Malik informed us, from Nafi', that Ibn 'Umar used to say: \When a man gives his wife authority over her own matter"," the ruling is whatever she decides"," unless the man disputes it and says: 'I only intended one divorce","' and he swears an oath to that effect. Then he has greater right over her"," so long as she is in her waiting period ('iddah).\"" [Sahih]"""
"15049","(15043) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajan informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Malik informed us, that it reached him from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr and from Abu Hurayrah, that they were asked about a man who gives his wife authority over her own matter, and she returns it to him without deciding anything regarding it. They both said: \That is not a divorce.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15050","(15044) Abu Bakr al-Ardastani informed us, Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi informed us, Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us, 'Ali ibn al-Hasan informed us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \If they accept it"," it is one divorce"," and he has greater right over her. And if they do not accept it"," then there is nothing (binding) upon the man when he gives his wife to her family.\"" [Hasan]"""
"15051","(15045) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ reported, al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy upon him, said, narrating from Sharīk, from Abī Ḥaṣīn, from Yaḥyā ibn Waththāb, from Masrūq, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: When a man says to his wife, \Rejoin your family","\"" or gives her over to her family"," and they accept her"," then it is one divorce"," and he has greater right over her. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15052","(15046) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad informed us, Muṭarrif reported, from al-Ḥakam, from Yaḥyā ibn al-Jazzār, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding a man who gave his wife over to her family: he said, \If they accept her"," then it is an irrevocable divorce (ṭalqah bāʾinah)"," and if they reject her"," then it is one divorce"," and he has greater right of taking her back.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15053","(15047) ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū Saʿīd informed us, al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Shabābah ibn Sawwār informed us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb reported, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: When a man grants his wife authority (mallaka) once, and she decides, then he has no further say in her affair; and if she does not decide, then it is one divorce, and her affair rests with him. Thus I found it, though there is a defect in its chain of narration.\n\nThe statement of ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding al-Takhyīr (granting choice) and al-Tamlīk (granting authority) is agreed upon, as is the statement of ʿUmar and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding both matters. As for Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him, his statement differs regarding both matters, as we have narrated.\n\nAl-Thawrī narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Shaʿbī, regarding \I choose\"" and \""Your affair is in your hand","\"" that it is the same according to the statements of ʿAlī"," Zayd ibn Thābit"," and Ibn Masʿūd"," may Allah be pleased with them"," as though he knew from them another statement in one of the two issues that agrees with their statement in the other issue. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15054","(15048) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd said: I asked Ayyūb, \Do you know anyone who said"," according to the statement of al-Ḥasan"," regarding 'Your affair is in your hand' (amruki biyadiki)"," that it constitutes three divorces?\"" He said: \""No"," except something that Qatādah narrated to us from Kathīr"," the freedman of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah"," from Abī Salamah"," from Abī Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," to that effect.\"" Ayyūb said: \""Then Kathīr came to us"," and I asked him"," and he said"," 'I never narrated it at all.' So I mentioned it to Qatādah"," and he said"," 'Yes"," but he has forgotten.'\""\n\nThis Kathīr — his reliability has not been established to the degree that would necessitate acceptance of his narration"," and the general body of scholars have narrated contrary to his narration. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]\n\n(24) Chapter: The Woman Says"," in the Context of Tamlīk (Granting Authority)"," \""I Have Divorced You","\"" Intending Divorce\n\nThe hadith of al-Aswad and ʿAlqamah has already passed regarding the man who said to his wife"," \""What is in my hand regarding your affair is in your hand.\"" She said"," \""Then I have divorced you three times.\"" He asked ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," and he said"," \""I consider it to be one divorce"," and you have greater right over her.\"" He also asked ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and he said"," \""I also hold that view.\"""""
"15055","(15049) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik reported, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, that a man from Thaqīf granted his wife authority over her own affair. She said, \You are divorced.\"" He remained silent. Then she said"," \""You are divorced.\"" He said"," \""May stones be in your mouth!\"" Then she said"," \""You are divorced.\"" He said"," \""May stones be in your mouth!\"" They both took their dispute to Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam"," and he made him swear that he had only granted her authority once"," and then he returned her to him. Al-Qāsim used to admire that judgment and considered it the best he had heard on the matter. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik]"""
"15056","(15050) It is narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, that he was asked about a man who placed his wife's affair in her own hand, and she said, \You are divorced three times.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said"," \""May Allah make her endeavor go astray! Why did she not divorce herself three times?\"" Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us"," Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us"," ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said"," Abū ʿUbayd said"," Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash"," from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15057","(15051) Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmārah narrated it from al-Ḥakam and Ḥabīb, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, in a more complete form. And al-Ḥasan is abandoned (matrūk). Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us, they said, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Khālid informed us, Aḥmad ibn Khālid informed us, al-Ḥasan narrated from al-Ḥakam and Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a woman said to her husband, \If only the authority I do not possess over my own affair were in my hand"," I would know what to do.\"" He said"," \""Then what I possess of authority over your affair is now in your hand.\"" She said"," \""I have divorced you three times.\"" This was mentioned to Ibn ʿAbbās"," and he said"," \""May Allah make her endeavor go astray! Why did she not divorce herself? Divorce is upon her"," not upon him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"15058","(15052) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī informed us, Jarīr narrated, from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that a woman said to her husband, \If only I had in my hand the authority over divorce that is in your hand"," I would act.\"" He said to her"," \""It is in your hand","\"" or he said"," \""I have placed it in your hand.\"" She said to him"," \""You are divorced three times.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said"," \""May Allah make her endeavor go astray! Why did she not divorce herself?\""\n\nWe have narrated from Manṣūr that he said: I asked Ibrāhīm"," \""It has reached me that Ibn ʿAbbās used to say"," 'May Allah make her endeavor go astray! If only she had said"," \""I have divorced myself.\""'\"" Ibrāhīm said"," \""They are the same — meaning her saying 'I have divorced you' and 'I have divorced myself' are the same.\"" And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]\n\n(25) Chapter: The Man Divorces His Wife in His Heart Without Moving His Tongue with It"""
"15059","(15053) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us, my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī informed us, Abū ʿAwānah narrated, from Qatādah, from Zurārah ibn Awfā, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \Allah has pardoned my ummah for what occurs within themselves"," so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," and al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Qatādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"15060","(15054) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us, Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us, Abū Tawbah informed us — and Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī informed us in Marw, and the wording is his — Abū al-Muwajjah informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Bishr al-Ḥarīrī informed us, they both said, Muʿāwiyah ibn Salām narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, that Yaʿlā ibn Ḥakīm informed him, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, that he heard Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: When a man declares his wife unlawful for himself, it is an oath for which he must give expiation. And he said, \There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern\"" (Qurʾān 33:21).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ from Abū Tawbah"," except that he said in its text: \""When he declares his wife unlawful"," it is nothing","\"" and he said"," \""There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern.\"" And Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Bishr as we have narrated it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"15061","(15055) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Isfahani informed us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Hisham narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Ya'la ibn Hakim from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said regarding al-haram (declaring something forbidden upon oneself): \It is an oath for which expiation must be made.\"" And he recited: \""Indeed"," in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example\"" [al-Ahzab 21].\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Mu'adh ibn Fudalah from Hisham. [Sahih. Preceded before it.]"""
"15062","(15056) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Isfahani informed us, saying: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Ya'qub al-Dawraqi narrated to us; Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us; Hisham al-Dustawa'i said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir wrote to me, narrating from 'Ikramah that 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Al-haram is an oath for which expiation must be made.\""\n\nHisham said: And Yahya ibn Abi Kathir wrote to me from Ya'la ibn Hakim from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas that he used to say regarding al-haram: \""It is an oath for which expiation must be made.\"" And he recited: \""Indeed"," in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example\"" [al-Ahzab 21] — meaning that the Prophet (peace be upon him) had declared a slave-girl forbidden upon himself"," so Allah said: \""Why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you?\"" [al-Tahrim 1] until His words: \""Allah has already ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths\"" [al-Tahrim 2]. So he expiated his oath and al-haram was treated as an oath.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas"," without this addition"," from Zuhayr ibn Harb from Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah. [Sahih. Muslim 1473.]"""
"15063","(15057) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn al-Saffar narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Mihran narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Sufyan narrated — and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Harith al-Isfahani informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Mansur narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Salim al-Aftas from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man came to him and said: \I have declared my wife forbidden upon myself.\"" He said: \""You have lied; she is not forbidden upon you.\"" Then he recited: \""O Prophet"," why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you?\"" [al-Tahrim 1]. \""Upon you is the most severe of expiations: the freeing of a slave.\""\n\nThe wording is that of Rawh's hadith"," and in the hadith of Abu Nu'aym the words \""upon you is the most severe of expiations\"" are not present. And it has been narrated from him that it involves a choice (takhyir)"," and this is what we hold. [Sahih.]"""
"15064","(15058) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed him; Abu al-Hasan al-Tara'ifi narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding His words: \Allah has already ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths\"" [al-Tahrim 2]: Allah commanded the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the believers"," when they declare something forbidden upon themselves that Allah has made lawful"," that they should expiate their oaths by feeding ten poor persons"," or clothing them"," or freeing a slave. And divorce does not enter into this. [Sahih through other chains.]"""
"15065","(15059) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Abu Bishr from Yusuf ibn Mahak that a Bedouin came to Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: \I have declared my wife forbidden upon myself.\"" He said: \""She is not forbidden upon you.\"" He said: \""Have you not heard the words of Allah the Most High: 'All food was lawful to the Children of Israel except what Israel forbade upon himself' [Al 'Imran 93]?\"" Ibn 'Abbas said: \""Israel (Ya'qub) suffered from an ailment"," so he made a vow that if Allah cured him"," he would never eat the sinews of anything — and that was not forbidden.\"" [Sahih.]"""
"15066","(15060) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and 'Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Sa'id narrated from Matar from 'Ata' from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: \Regarding al-haram"," it is an oath.\""\n\nAnd 'Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated it from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Urabah"," and he said: \""It is an oath for which expiation must be made.\"" [Da'if.]"""
"15067","(15061) Al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Abu Yusuf from al-Ash'ath ibn Sawwar from al-Hakam from Ibrahim from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said regarding al-haram: \If he intended it as an oath"," then it is an oath; and if he intended it as a divorce"," then it is a divorce. It is whatever he intended thereby.\"" [Da'if.]"""
"15068","(15062) And al-Thawri narrated from al-Ash'ath ibn Sawwar from al-Hakam from Ibrahim from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to say: \His intention in al-haram is what he intended. If he did not intend a divorce"," then it is an oath.\"" Abu Bakr al-Ardastani informed us; Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Sufyan narrated it. [Da'if.]"""
"15069","(15063) Abu Mansur 'Abd al-Qahir ibn Tahir al-Imam and Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Ali ibn Hamdan informed us, saying: Abu 'Amr ibn Najid informed us; Abu Muslim narrated to us; al-Ansari narrated to us; al-Ash'ath narrated from al-Hasan regarding al-haram: \If he intended an oath"," then it is an oath; and if he intended a divorce"," then it is a divorce.\"" [Da'if.]"""
"15070","(15064) The noble Abu al-Fath al-'Umari informed us; Abu Ahmad al-Shurayhi informed us; Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us; Sharik narrated from Mukhul ibn Rashid from Abu Ja'far regarding al-haram: \If he intended a divorce"," then it is a single divorce"," and he has the right of return (raj'ah); and if he did not intend a divorce"," then it is an oath for which expiation must be made.\"" [Da'if.]"""
"15071","(15065) He said: And Sharik narrated to us, from Mikhawl, from Amir, from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), a similar narration."
"15072","(15066) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Uthman al-Basri informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: \Declaring one's wife unlawful (haram) upon oneself is an oath (yamin).\""\n\nThe narration differs on this matter from the Commander of the Faithful"," 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). [Da'if]"""
"15073","(15067) Abu Bakr al-Isbahani informed us; Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Sufyan narrated, from Jabir, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) used to consider declaring one's wife unlawful (haram) upon oneself as an oath (yamin). [Sahih]"
"15074","(15068) And with his chain of narration, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): that a man came to him who had divorced his wife twice, and said: \You are unlawful (haram) upon me.\"" So 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I will not return her to you.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from 'Ali and Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with them) regarding al-bariyyah"," al-battah"," and al-haram: that they each constitute three divorces. [Da'if]"""
"15075","(15069) Abu al-Qasim — Mujalid ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Mujalid al-Bajali — informed us in Kufa; Muslim ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muslim al-Tamimi narrated to us; al-Hadrami narrated to us; Sa'id ibn 'Amr al-Ash'athi informed us; 'Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated, from Mutarrif, from 'Amir — that is, al-Sha'bi — regarding a man who declares his wife unlawful (haram) upon himself, he said: \They say that 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) considered it three (divorces).\""\n\n'Amir said: \""'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) did not say this. Rather"," he said: 'I neither make her lawful nor make her unlawful.'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated previously from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that it constitutes three (divorces) if he intended so — however"," this is a weak narration"," and Allah knows best. [Sahih]"""
"15076","(15070) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — by recitation — and 'Ubayd ibn Muhammad — verbally — both said: Abu al-'Abbas, that is, al-Asamm, narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Dawud narrated, from 'Amir, from Masruq: that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ila' (abstention) and declared (something) unlawful, so Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \O Prophet"," why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you?\"" He said: \""The unlawful (haram) is lawful.\"" And he said regarding the verse: \""Allah has already ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths.\"" This is a mursal narration. [Da'if]"""
"15077","(15071) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and 'Ubayd ibn Muhammad informed us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas, that is, al-Asamm, narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Sa'id narrated, from Matar, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ila' (abstention) with his wives and declared (something) unlawful"," then he made the unlawful (haram) lawful"," and he made expiation (kaffarah) for the oath.\""\n\nThis strengthens the position of the one who claims that the word al-haram"," when used unconditionally"," does not constitute an oath"," a divorce"," or a declaration of zihar. [Hasan]"""
"15078","(15072) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and 'Ubayd ibn Muhammad informed us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas, that is, al-Asamm, narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Sa'id narrated, from Matar, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, that he said: \I do not care whether I declare her unlawful (haram) upon myself or (drink) pure water.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15079","(15073) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Uthman al-Basri informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Sufyan narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, who said: \I do not care whether I declare her unlawful (haram) or (give) a bowl of tharid.\"" And Allah knows best."""
"15080","(15074) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz — informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Raja' informed us; Isra'il narrated, from Muslim al-A'war, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: \O Prophet"," why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you?\"" He said: \""He declared his concubine (surriyyah) unlawful upon himself.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15081","(15075) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Kāmil al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Saʿd ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAṭiyyah ibn Saʿd informed me: my father informed me: my paternal uncle al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAṭiyyah informed me: my father informed me, from my grandfather ʿAṭiyyah ibn Saʿd, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the verse: {O Prophet, why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you} until His words {and He is the All-Knowing, the All-Wise}. He said: Ḥafṣah and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them both) were deeply devoted to one another, and they were both wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Ḥafṣah went to her father to converse with him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent for his concubine and remained with her in Ḥafṣah's house, and that was the day on which he would normally visit ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). When Ḥafṣah returned and found her in her house, she waited for her departure, and she was seized by intense jealousy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) then sent his concubine away, and Ḥafṣah entered and said: \I have seen who was with you"," and by Allah"," you have displeased me.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""By Allah"," I shall please you"," and I am confiding to you a secret"," so guard it.\"" He said: \""I call you to witness that this concubine of mine is forbidden upon me"," as a means of pleasing you.\"" Ḥafṣah and ʿĀʾishah used to be in alliance against the other wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). So Ḥafṣah went and disclosed to her a secret"," namely: \""Rejoice"," for Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has made his concubine forbidden upon himself.\"" When she disclosed the secret of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," Allah exposed the matter before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and Allah revealed to His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him): {O Prophet"," why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you} to the end of the verse. [Weak]"""
"15082","(15076) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Baṭṭah informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Zakariyyā al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bukayr al-Ḥaḍramī informed us: Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated from Thābit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had a concubine with whom he would be intimate. Ḥafṣah persisted with him until he made her forbidden upon himself. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed this verse: {O Prophet, why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you, seeking the approval of your wives} to the end of the verse. [Authentic]"
"15083","(15077) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍarawī al-Harawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Hushaym informed us: ʿUbaydah narrated from Ibrāhīm and Juwaybir, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk, that Ḥafṣah, Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), visited her father one day, and it was her day. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came and did not find her at home, he sent for his concubine Māriyah al-Qibṭiyyah and was intimate with her in Ḥafṣah's house. Ḥafṣah came upon that situation and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," do you do this in my house and on my day?\"" He said: \""She is forbidden upon me; do not inform anyone of that.\"" So Ḥafṣah went to ʿĀʾishah and informed her of that. Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," then revealed in His Book: {O Prophet"," why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you} until His words {and the righteous of the believers}. He was commanded to expiate his oath and to take back his concubine.\n\nAl-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī narrated something similar in a mursal narration. [Weak]"""
"15084","(15078) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍarawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Hushaym informed us: Dāwūd narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from Masrūq, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) swore an oath to Ḥafṣah that he would not approach his concubine, and he said: \She is forbidden upon me.\"" So the expiation for his oath was revealed"," and he was commanded not to prohibit what Allah had made lawful.\n\nThis is a mursal narration. We have narrated it in connected form earlier in this chapter. [Weak]"""
"15085","(15079) Abū Dāwūd narrated in al-Marāsīl from Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ ibn Sufyān, from Sufyān, from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Qatādah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in Ḥafṣah's house. She entered and saw his concubine with him and said: \In my house and on my day?\"" He said: \""Be quiet. By Allah"," I shall not approach her"," and she is forbidden upon me.\""\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated it. [Weak]"""
"15086","(15080) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Manīʿī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us: Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad said: Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAṭāʾ claimed that he heard ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr narrating, he said: I heard ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to stay with Zaynab bint Jaḥsh (may Allah be pleased with her) and drink honey at her place. So Ḥafṣah and I agreed that whichever of us the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) visited, she should say: \I detect upon you the smell of maghāfīr. Have you eaten maghāfīr?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) visited one of them and she said that to him. He said: \""Rather"," I drank honey at Zaynab's place"," and I shall not return to it.\"" So there was revealed: {Why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you} until {if you two repent to Allah}"," referring to ʿĀʾishah and Ḥafṣah (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," {and when the Prophet confided a matter to one of his wives}"," referring to his words: \""Rather"," I drank honey.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim"," both from Ḥajjāj.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā said"," from Hishām ibn Yūsuf"," from Ibn Jurayj"," from ʿAṭāʾ"," in this hadith: \""And I shall not return to it. I have sworn an oath"," so do not inform anyone of that.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: Likewise"," Muḥammad ibn Thawr narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. And in the hadith of Ibn Abī Mulaykah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding this story: \""By Allah"," I shall not drink it.\"" So he informed that he had sworn an oath"," and it is more likely that the obligation of expiation was connected to the oath"," not to the act of prohibition.\n\n[Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"15087","(15081) ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated from ʿĀʾishah, differing with him in some wordings and not mentioning the revelation of the verse in it, and it is in what Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us in the Fawāʾid of al-Aṣamm, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Khalīl informed us: ʿAlī ibn Mushhir narrated from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to love honey and sweets. When he finished the ʿAṣr prayer, he would enter upon his wives and be close to one of them. He entered upon Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and stayed with her longer than he would normally stay. I became jealous and asked about that. It was said to me: \A woman from her people gave her a skin of honey"," and she gave him a drink from it.\"" I said: \""By Allah"," we shall certainly contrive something for him.\"" I said to Sawdah ibn Zamʿah: \""When he comes near you upon entering"," say to him: 'O Messenger of Allah"," have you eaten maghāfīr?' He will say to you: 'No.' Then say to him: 'What is this smell I detect from you?' He will say to you: 'Ḥafṣah gave me a drink of honey.' Then say to him: 'Its bees must have fed on the ʿurfut plant.' And I shall say the same"," and O Ṣafiyyah"," say that too.\"" Sawdāh said: \""By Allah"," he was only standing at the door when I wanted to call out to him with what you had commanded me"," out of fear of you.\"" When he came near her"," Sawdāh said to him: \""O Messenger of Allah"," have you eaten maghāfīr?\"" He said: \""No.\"" She said: \""What is this smell I detect from you?\"" He said: \""Ḥafṣah gave me a drink of honey.\"" She said: \""Its bees must have fed on the ʿurfut plant.\"" When he came to me"," I said the same to him. When he came to Ṣafiyyah"," she said the same"," meaning when he came to Ḥafṣah"," she said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," shall I not give you some of it to drink?\"" He said: \""I have no need of it.\"" She said — meaning Sawdāh said to her: \""Glory be to Allah! By Allah"," we have made it forbidden for him.\"" I said to her: \""Be quiet.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Farwah ibn Abī al-Maghrāʾ from ʿAlī ibn Mushhir"," and Muslim narrated it from Suwayd ibn Saʿīd from ʿAlī ibn Mushhir."""
"15088","(15082) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Zakariyyā al-ʿAnbarī informed me: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from Abī al-Ḍuḥā, from Masrūq, who said: A udder was brought to ʿAbdullāh, and he said to the people: \Come near and eat from it.\"" They began to eat. One of them was sitting aside. ʿAbdullāh said: \""Come near.\"" He said: \""I do not want it.\"" He said: \""Why?\"" He said: \""Because I have made the udder forbidden upon myself.\"" ʿAbdullāh said: \""This is from the footsteps of Satan.\"" Then ʿAbdullāh said: {O you who believe"," do not prohibit the good things that Allah has made lawful for you"," and do not transgress. Indeed"," Allah does not love the transgressors.} Come near"," eat"," and expiate your oath"," for this is from the footsteps of Satan. And Allah knows best. [Authentic]"""
"15089","(15083) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ and Ibn Yaḥyā — and this is the hadith of Aḥmad — they said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Abī Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from Muḥammad ibn Iyās, that Ibn ʿAbbās, Abū Hurayrah, and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ (may Allah be pleased with them) were asked about a virgin whom her husband divorces three times. They all said: \She is not lawful for him until she marries a husband other than him.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Mālik narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"," from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj"," from Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī ʿAyāsh"," that he witnessed this story. [Authentic]"""
"15090","(15084) That is, as Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd that Bukayr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ashajj informed him from Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī ʿAyāsh al-Anṣārī, that he was sitting with ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr and ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar. He said: Muḥammad ibn Iyās ibn al-Bukayr came to them and said: \A man from the people of the desert divorced his wife three times before consummating the marriage. What do you two think?\"" Ibn al-Zubayr said: \""This is a matter about which we have no opinion. Go to Ibn ʿAbbās and Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," for I left them with ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). Ask them"," then come back and inform us.\"" So he went and asked them. Ibn ʿAbbās said to Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with them both): \""Give him a fatwā"," O Abū Hurayrah"," for a difficult case has come to you.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""One divorce separates her"," and three divorces make her forbidden.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said the same"," adding: \""Until she marries a husband other than him.\""\n\n[Authentic. Mālik narrated it (1206)]"""
"15091","(15085) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī ʿAyāsh, from Ibn Iyās ibn al-Bukayr, that ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar and Ibn al-Zubayr were brought a Bedouin who had divorced his wife three times before consummating the marriage. He mentioned the meaning of the ḥadīth of Mālik, and added: \And ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," concurred with them both.\"" This is the well-known position from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās.\n\nAnd we narrated it in the issue of the triple ṭalāq from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," and Anas ibn Mālik"," may Allah be pleased with them all. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before.]"""
"15092","(15086) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī informed us verbatim, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭā' informed us, Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from ʿIkrimah, from ʿAṭā', from Ṭāwūs, and from Jābir ibn Zayd — all of them narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him — that he said: \It is one irrevocable divorce\"" — meaning regarding a man who divorces his wife three times before consummating the marriage. This may indicate that the intended meaning is when he pronounces them separately"," in which case it would not contradict what preceded it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15093","(15087) And that which indicates this, along with what has preceded, is what Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us, Sufyān narrated from Jābir, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding a man who divorced his wife three times before consummating the marriage. He said: \It was a bond in his hand; he released them all at once. And if he had pronounced them separately"," it would have been nothing.\""\n\nSufyān said: \""Separately\"" — meaning \""You are divorced"," you are divorced"," you are divorced\"" — \""then she is irrevocably separated by the first"," and the second two are nothing.\""\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī narrated in the book *Ikhtilāf al-ʿIrāqiyyīn* — I think it was from Abū Yūsuf — regarding a man who says to his wife"," before consummating the marriage: \""You are divorced"," you are divorced"," you are divorced\"" — the first divorce takes effect and the remaining two do not take effect upon her. This is the position of Abū Ḥanīfah"," as we received it from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," and Zayd ibn Thābit"," may Allah be pleased with them all"," and Ibrāhīm (al-Nakhaʿī) held this view. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15094","(15088) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Fudayk narrated from Ibn Abī Dhi'b, from Ibn Qusayṭ, from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith, that he said regarding a man who said to his wife, before consummating the marriage: \You are divorced"," then you are divorced"," then you are divorced\"" — Abū Bakr said: \""Does he divorce his wife in the middle of the road? She became irrevocable from the moment he pronounced the first divorce.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15095","(15089) The Shaykh said: And the meaning of this is what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated from his brother, from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAtīq and Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sulaymān ibn al-Arqam, who said: al-Ḥasan said: \Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The divorce of a woman with whom marriage has not been consummated is one.'\""\n\nAnd this is a mursal ḥadīth. Its narrator is Sulaymān ibn al-Arqam"," and he is weak. And it is possible"," if it is authentic"," that he intended that her divorce and the divorce of a woman with whom marriage has been consummated are one and the same"," as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd said. And Allah knows best. And the ḥadīth of Abī al-Ṣahbā' regarding the question of Ibn ʿAbbās has already passed"," and the discussion concerning it has already been given. And with Allah lies success. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15096","(15090) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us, Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us, Sufyān narrated from al-Zubayr ibn ʿAdī, from Ibrāhīm, from Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding a man who said to his wife: \If you do such and such"," then you are divorced","\"" and she did it. He said: \""It is one divorce"," and he has more right to take her back.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15097","(15091) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān, from Ibrāhīm, regarding a man who said to his wife: \You are divorced for a year.\"" He said: \""She is his wife; he may enjoy her until a year passes.\"" And something similar was narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," and ʿAṭā' and Jābir ibn Zayd held this view. [Ḥasan]"""
"15098","(15092) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Ḥasan informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, Isrā'īl and Sharīk narrated from Jābir, from al-Shaʿbī, regarding a man who said to his wife: \You are divorced when Ramaḍān comes.\"" He said: \""She remains his wife on the day he divorced her until Ramaḍān arrives.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15099","(15093) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffā' informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us, Ibn Abī Uways informed us, Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: \Any man who says to his wife: 'You are divorced if you go out until nightfall","' and his wife goes out"," or who says that regarding his slave boy and his slave boy goes out before nightfall without his knowledge — his wife is divorced and his slave boy is set free"," because he failed to make the exception; had he wished"," he could have said: 'With my permission.' But he was negligent in making the exception"," so his negligence is held against him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15100","(15094) Abū Dharr ibn Abī al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Qāsim al-Mudhakkir and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī, among others, informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, Bishr ibn Bakr informed us, al-Awzāʿī narrated from ʿAṭā', from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed Allah has pardoned my ummah for their mistakes"," their forgetfulness"," and that which they are coerced into.\""\n\nBishr ibn Bakr refined its chain of narration"," and he is among the trustworthy narrators. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"15101","(15095) Al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Awzāʿī, but he did not mention ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr in its isnād. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿUmar ibn Sinān, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān, and others said: Muḥammad ibn al-Muṣaffā narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, and he mentioned it, saying: from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"15102","(15096) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muṣaffā narrated to us, al-Walīd narrated to us, Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from Mūsā ibn Wardān, who said: I heard ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah has pardoned my Ummah for their mistakes"," their forgetfulness"," and that which they are coerced into.\"" [Ḥasan in virtue of corroborating narrations]"""
"15103","(15097) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū al-Azhar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, saying: I heard Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrating, saying: Thawr ibn Yazīd wrote to me that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to him from ʿAdī ibn ʿAdī that he (ʿAdī) ordered him to go to Ṣafiyyah bint Shaybah and ask her about a hadith that had reached him, which she narrated from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). So I went to her, and she narrated to me that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no divorce and no manumission under compulsion (ighlāq).\""\n\nIbrāhīm ibn Saʿd"," ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr"," and ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān also narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"," and some of them said: \""fī ghlāq\"" instead of \""fī ighlāq.\"" And this Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd is Ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ al-Makkī. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15104","(15098) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Kathīr ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Qazʿah ibn Suwayd narrated from Zakariyyāʾ ibn Isḥāq and Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān collectively, from Ṣafiyyah bint Shaybah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no divorce and no manumission under compulsion (ighlāq).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15105","(15099) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣibghī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us, Ibn Abī Uways informed me, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Qudāmah ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥāṭib al-Jumaḥī narrated from his father that a man was lowering himself down to purchase honey during the time of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). His wife came and stood over the rope and swore that she would cut it or he would divorce her three times. He reminded her of Allah and Islam, but she refused except that. So he divorced her three times. When he came down, he went to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned to him what had transpired between her and him. He said: \Return to your family"," for this is not a divorce.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī also narrated it from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Qudāmah al-Jumaḥī"," from his father"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15106","(15100) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Abī ʿUbayd, who said: Yazīd narrated to me from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Qudāmah al-Jumaḥī, from his father, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), with this same story, except that he said: \It was referred to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he separated her from him.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: A contrary narration has also been reported from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: It has also been narrated from ʿAlī"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," Ibn ʿUmar"," Ibn al-Zubayr"," ʿAṭāʾ"," and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr that they held his divorce to be invalid.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The first narration is more likely. As for the narration from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," then… [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15107","(15101) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: It is narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from Ḥumayd, from al-Ḥasan that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \There is no divorce for the coerced one.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15108","(15102) As for the narration from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both): Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn Rajāʾ informed us, Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Qāriʾ informed us, ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī said: I heard Yaḥyā say: al-Awzāʿī narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr that Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) did not consider the divorce of the coerced person to be valid. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15109","(15103) In the book of Isḥāq, with his isnād, from ʿIkrimah: He was asked about a man whom the thieves coerced until he divorced his wife. He said: Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \It is nothing (i.e."," it is not valid).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15110","(15104) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: The Qāḍī Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣakhr al-Azdī al-Baṣrī, the blind, wrote to us from Makkah (may Allah protect it and be pleased with him), saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Ḥamdān al-Saqaṭī informed us, reciting to him, al-Ḥasan, meaning Ibn al-Muthannā, narrated to us, ʿAffān, meaning ibn Muslim, narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṭalḥah al-Khuzāʿī narrated from Abī Yazīd al-Madanī, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The coerced one has no divorce.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of corroborating narrations]"""
"15111","(15105) As for the narration from Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn al-Zubayr: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Naṣr narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Birtī narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik. And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣighfī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Thābit al-Aḥnaf: that he married the *umm walad* of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. He said: \Then ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān called for me"," so I came to him. I entered upon him and found whips laid out before him"," and a shackle of iron"," and two of his slaves whom he had seated. He said: 'Divorce her"," otherwise"," by the One by Whom oaths are sworn"," I shall do such-and-such to you.' I said: 'She is divorced a thousand times.' I left his presence and encountered Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — on the road to Makkah"," in a ruin. I informed him of what had transpired with me. ʿAbd Allāh became angry and said: 'That is not a divorce. She has not been made unlawful for you. Return to your wife.' He said: 'My soul did not find rest until I came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr — may Allah be pleased with them both — while he was in Makkah that day. I informed him of what had transpired with me and of what Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — had said to me. ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr — may Allah be pleased with them both — said to me: 'She has not been made unlawful for you; return to your wife.' He wrote to Jābir ibn al-Aswad al-Zuhrī"," who was the governor of Madīnah at that time"," commanding him to punish ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and to remove any obstacle between me and my wife. I arrived"," and Ṣafiyyah bint Abī ʿUbayd"," the wife of Ibn ʿUmar"," prepared my wife and delivered her to me with the knowledge of Ibn ʿUmar. Then I invited Ibn ʿUmar on the day of my wedding banquet to my feast"," and he came to me.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Mālik.]"""
"15112","(15106) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated — he said: I heard ʿAmr saying — Thābit al-Aʿraj narrated to me, he said: \I married the *umm walad* of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him. His son called for me and called for two of his slaves. They tied me up and struck me with whips"," and said: 'You must divorce her"," or we shall certainly do such-and-such.' So I divorced her. Then I asked Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn al-Zubayr"," and they did not consider it to be anything [i.e."," a valid divorce].\""\n\nAnd we have narrated this opinion from the Tābiʿīn: from ʿAṭāʾ"," Ṭāwūs"," al-Ḥasan"," ʿIkrimah"," ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported before it.]"""
"15113","(15107) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū Shihāb and Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī, from ʿAlī ibn Ḥanẓalah, from his father, who said: ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \A man is not in control of himself when he is starved"," or bound"," or beaten.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15114","(15108) He said: And Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-Masʿūdī narrated from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Sharīḥ, who said: \Imprisonment is coercion"," beating is coercion"," shackling is coercion"," and threatening is coercion.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15115","(15109) By way of evidence, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ informed us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated from Khālid, from Abū al-Ḍuḥā, from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The pen is lifted from three: the sleeper until he awakens"," the boy until he reaches puberty"," and the insane until he regains his senses.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated it through various chains from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī — may Allah have mercy on him — cited as evidence the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — regarding permission in fighting"," which has passed. [Ḥasan for other reasons.]"""
"15116","(15110) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, al-Aʿmash narrated from Ibrāhīm, from ʿĀbis ibn Rabīʿah, from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \Every divorce is valid except the divorce of the one who is mentally deranged (*al-maʿtūh*).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Shaʿbī"," al-Ḥasan"," and Ibrāhīm that they said: \""The divorce of a minor and his manumission are not valid until he reaches puberty.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Jābir ibn Zayd"," Ibrāhīm"," Abū Qilābah"," and others that they did not consider valid the divorce of one suffering from pleurisy (*al-mubarsim*). And from al-Shaʿbī and Ibrāhīm regarding one who divorces or manumits in a dream"," they said: \""It is nothing.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15117","(15111) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿĀbis ibn Rabīʿah, from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \Every divorce is valid except the divorce of the one who is mentally deranged (*al-maʿtūh*).\""\n\nYaʿqūb said: And Qabīṣah said"," from Sufyān"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿĀbis ibn Rabīʿah"," meaning from his father"," from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — to that effect. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported before it.]"""
"15118","(15112) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated: \It reached him that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Sulaymān ibn Yasār were asked about the divorce of the intoxicated person (*al-sakrān*)"," and they said: 'If the intoxicated person divorces"," his divorce is valid"," and if he kills"," he is killed [in retribution].' Mālik said: 'And that is the ruling according to us.'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Ibrāhīm that he said: \""The divorce and manumission of the intoxicated person are valid.\"" And from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī"," who said: \""The intoxicated person's divorce and manumission are valid"," but his buying and selling are not valid.\"" [Ḥasan. Only from Ibn al-Musayyib.]"""
"15119","(15113) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rūḥ al-Madāʾinī narrated to us, Shabbābah narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: \ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz was brought a man who was intoxicated"," and he said: 'I divorced my wife while I was intoxicated.' ʿUmar's opinion"," along with us"," was that he should be flogged and that separation should be effected between them. But Abān ibn ʿUthmān informed him that ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — said: 'There is no divorce for the insane person or the intoxicated person.' ʿUmar said: 'How can you give me a verdict when this one is narrating to me from ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him?' So he flogged him and returned his wife to him.\""\n\nAl-Zuhrī said: \""That was mentioned to Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah"," and he said: 'ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān read to us the letter of Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān"," in which were the established Sunnahs: that whoever divorced his wife"," it is valid"," except for the insane person.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah have mercy on him — said: \""And it has been narrated from Ṭāwūs that he said: 'How can his divorce be valid when his prayer is not accepted from him?' And from ʿAṭāʾ regarding the divorce of the intoxicated person"," he said: 'It is nothing.' And from Abān ibn ʿUthmān a similar report.\""\n\nAnd there has already passed in the Book of Confession (*al-Iqrār*) the ḥadīth of Sulaymān ibn Buraydah from his father regarding the story of Māʿiz ibn Mālik"," where the Prophet ﷺ said: \""With what should I purify you?\"" He said: \""From zinā (unlawful sexual intercourse).\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Is he insane?\"" He was informed that he was not insane. He said: \""Did you drink wine?\"" A man stood and smelled him"," and found no smell of wine from him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Are you married (*athayyib*)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So the Prophet ﷺ ordered"," and he was stoned. It is evident from this that he intended to nullify his confession by intoxication just as he intended to nullify it by insanity"," thereby indicating that his statement carries no legal weight. Whoever holds the first opinion responds to this by saying that this pertains to the prescribed punishments (*ḥudūd*) of Allah"," Most High"," which are averted by doubts (*shubuhāt*). And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan]"""
"15120","(15114) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us, Nāfiʿ narrated to me that Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — used to say: \Whoever grants his slave permission to marry"," then the divorce is in the slave's hand; no one else has any authority over his divorce.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15121","(15115) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik narrated to us: Abū al-Zinād narrated to us from Sulaymān ibn Yasār that Nufayʿ, a mukātab (slave contracted for manumission) of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ — or he was a slave belonging to her — had a free woman under his marriage contract. He divorced her twice and then wished to take her back. The wives of the Prophet ﷺ instructed him to go to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) and ask him about the matter. He went to him and found him at the stairs, holding the hand of Zayd ibn Thābit. He asked them both, and they both hastened to answer simultaneously: \She has become forbidden for you"," she has become forbidden for you.\"" A musnad hadith has also been narrated on this topic. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15122","(15116) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū ʿUtbah Aḥmad ibn al-Faraj al-Ḥijāzī narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥajjāj al-Mahriyy narrated to us from Mūsā ibn Ayyūb al-Ghāfiqī from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ complaining that his mawlā (master) had married him (to a woman) and now intended to separate him from his wife. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \What is the matter with people who marry their slave men to their slave women and then wish to separate them? Beware"," the one who has authority over divorce is the one who takes hold of the shank (i.e."," the husband).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15123","(15117) Ibn Lahīʿah contradited him, narrating it from Mūsā ibn Ayyūb as a mursal hadith, as Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith both informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Dāwūd narrated to us: Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to us from Mūsā ibn Ayyūb from ʿIkrimah that a slave came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned something similar, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The one who has authority over divorce is the one who took hold of the shank.\""\n\nIbn Lahīʿah did not mention Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both). It has also been narrated from another chain as a marfūʿ hadith"," but it contains weakness. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15124","(15118) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad al-Farrāʾ, al-Ḥasan ibn Hārūn, and Qaṭn ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Walīd narrated to us from Sufyān al-Thawrī, Ḥammād ibn Salamah, and Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When a man takes an oath and says 'In shāʾ Allāh' (if Allah wills)"," he has indeed made an exception.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15125","(15119) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ayyūb from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever swears an oath and says 'In shāʾ Allāh","' then he has the choice: if he wishes"," he may proceed"," and if he wishes"," he may not.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was narrated previously.]"""
"15126","(15120) A weak hadith has been narrated on this topic from Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) as a marfūʿ narration. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated — and Abū Aḥmad said: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm also narrated to us, and the wording is his — al-Ḥasan ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us from Ḥumayd ibn Mālik from Makḥūl from Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \O Muʿādh"," Allah has not created anything on the face of the earth more hateful to Him than divorce"," and Allah has not created anything on the face of the earth more beloved to Him than manumission. So when a man says to his slave: 'You are free"," in shāʾ Allāh","' he is free"," and there is no exception for him. And when he says to his wife: 'You are divorced"," in shāʾ Allāh","' then the exception applies to him"," and no divorce takes effect upon him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15127","(15121) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Abū Khawlah Maymūn ibn Maslamah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Muṣaffá narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us from Ḥumayd ibn Mālak al-Lakhmī: Makḥūl narrated to us from Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who says to his wife: \You are divorced"," in shāʾ Allāh.\"" He said: \""His exception stands.\""\n\nA man then said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what if he says to his slave boy: 'You are free"," in shāʾ Allāh'?\"" He said: \""He is set free"," because Allah wills manumission and does not will divorce.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. It was narrated previously.]"""
"15128","(15122) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn ʿAlī al-Dūlabī narrated to us: Ḥumayd ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us from Ḥumayd ibn Mālik al-Nakhaʿī, and he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Ismāʿīl. Ḥumayd said: Yazīd ibn Hārūn said to me: \What a hadith this would be if only Ḥumayd ibn Mālik al-Lakhmī were known!\"" I said: \""He is my father's grandfather.\"" Yazīd said: \""You have delighted me now; it has become a hadith.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""There is not much cause for delight in it"," for Ḥumayd ibn Rabīʿ ibn Ḥumayd ibn Mālik al-Kūfī al-Khazzāz is very weak — Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and others have accused him of lying. Ḥumayd ibn Mālik is unknown (majhūl)"," and Makḥūl's narration from Muʿādh ibn Jabal is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). It has also been narrated from Ḥumayd from Makḥūl from Khālid ibn Maʿdān from Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and also from him from Makḥūl from Mālik ibn Yukhāmir from Muʿādh — but it is not preserved (maḥfūẓ). And Allah knows best.\"""""
"15129","(15123) A weak hadith has been narrated in opposition to it, one with which it is not permissible to use as evidence. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ghāfiqī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Maʿbad ibn Nūḥ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Maʿbad ibn Shaddād al-Kaʿbī narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rawwād from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever says to his wife: 'You are divorced"," in shāʾ Allāh","' or to his slave: 'You are free"," in shāʾ Allāh","' or 'I will walk to the House of Allah"," in shāʾ Allāh","' then nothing is incumbent upon him.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: \""This hadith"," with its chain"," is munkar (objectionable); none narrates it except Isḥāq al-Kaʿbī.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has also been narrated from al-Jārūd ibn Yazīd from Bahz ibn Ḥakīm from his father from his grandfather as a marfūʿ narration concerning divorce alone"," and it is also weak. And in the hadith of Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) there is sufficiency"," and with Allah lies success. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15130","(15124) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn Abī Rawwād and Muslim ibn Khālid informed me, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Abī Mulaykah informed me that he asked Ibn al-Zubayr about a man who divorces a woman with an irrevocable divorce (yubattuhā) and then dies while she is still in her waiting period. ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr said: \ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) irrevocably divorced Ṭumāḍir bint al-Aṣbaʿ al-Kalbiyyah and then died while she was in her waiting period"," so ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) made her an heir.\"" Ibn al-Zubayr said: \""As for me"," I do not think that a woman irrevocably divorced should inherit.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15131","(15125) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us: Ibn Jurayj reported to us from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: I asked ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr about a man who divorced his wife during his terminal illness and made it irrevocable (battā). He said: As for ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him), he made her an heir; but as for me, I do not consider her an heir merely by virtue of his having spent one night with her."
"15132","(15126) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik reported from Ibn Shihāb, from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwf — who was the most knowledgeable among them regarding this matter — and from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) irrevocably divorced his wife while he was ill, and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) made her his heir after the completion of her waiting period (ʿiddah)."
"15133","(15127) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The ḥadīth of Ibn al-Zubayr is connected (muʾtaṣil), and he states that ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) made her an heir during the waiting period; whereas the ḥadīth of Ibn Shihāb is interrupted (maqṭūʿ). And he said in al-Imlāʾ: ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) made the wife of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf an heir after he had divorced her three times, following the completion of the waiting period. He said: And it seems to me that this narration is more established than the two ḥadīths."
"15134","(15128) The Shaykh said: That which corroborates the narration of Ibn Shihāb from Ṭalḥah and Abū Salamah is what Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Aṣbagh ibn Faraj informed me: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus reported from Ibn Shihāb, who said: I heard Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar speaking to al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd al-Malik at his evening meal while we were between Makkah and Madīnah. He said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, Abān ibn ʿUthmān married the daughter of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān to the detriment of the daughter of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar, when she refused to sell him her inheritance from him during his illness when he was struck by paralysis. He did not stop at that until he divorced Umm Kulthūm, and she became lawful (i.e., her waiting period ended) during his illness. And this al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd ibn Ukht Namir is alive and bears witness to the ruling of ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Tumāḍir bint al-Aṣbagh, whom he made an heir of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) after she had become lawful. And he bears witness to the ruling of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Umm Ḥakīm bint Qāriẓ, whom he made an heir of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mukmil after she had become lawful. So summon him and ask him about his testimony. When al-Walīd concluded his speech, he said: I do not think that ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled by that. Muʿāwiyah said: If al-Sāʾib does not bear witness to that, then I shall nullify his presence and his observation. The Shaykh said: This is a connected chain of narration, and Ibn Akhī Ibn Shihāb followed it up from his uncle."
"15135","(15129) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated that he heard Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān say: It reached me that the wife of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf asked him to divorce her. He said to her: When you have menstruated and then become pure, inform me. She had not yet menstruated when ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) fell ill. When she became pure, she informed him, and he irrevocably divorced her — or a divorce after which he had no further right of divorce over her — and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān was ill at that time. So ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) made her his heir after the completion of her waiting period. Al-Shāfiʿī said: And the position I prefer is that if she inherits after the completion of the waiting period, she inherits so long as she has not remarried. But if she remarries, she does not inherit from him, so that she would inherit from two husbands, as though she had forfeited her right by remarrying."
"15136","(15130) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān reported from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit: A shaykh from Quraysh narrated to me from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said regarding the one who divorces while ill: We continue to make her an heir until he recovers or she remarries, even if he remains ill for a year. Al-Shāfiʿī said: And others said: She inherits him so long as the waiting period has not ended."
"15137","(15131) It was narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) through a chain that is not established among the scholars of ḥadīth — meaning what Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān reported from al-Mughīrah, from Ibrāhīm, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding the one who divorced his wife while ill: She inherits him during the waiting period, and he does not inherit her. This is interrupted (munqaṭiʿ), and al-Mughīrah did not hear it from Ibrāhīm; rather, he said: ʿUbaydah mentioned it from Ibrāhīm from ʿUmar. And ʿUbaydah al-Ḍabbī is weak, and ʿUbaydah did not raise it to ʿUmar in the narration of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān from him; rather, he mentioned it from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī from Sharīḥ, and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) is not in it."
"15138","(15132) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us. Al-Rabīʿ said: He sought guidance from Allah regarding it — meaning al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) — and he said: The irrevocably divorced woman (al-mabtūtah) does not inherit. Al-Rabīʿ said: And this is the position of Ibn al-Zubayr. And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) divorced her on the basis that she would not inherit, if Allah willed, according to his view. And Allah knows best."
"15139","(15133) By way of evidence, from what Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā informed us: Abū Khaythamah narrated to us — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū ʿAmr informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Sufyān reported from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd and ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm, from his uncle ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd: A complaint was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about a man who imagines that he perceives something during the prayer. He said: He should not break off the prayer until he hears a sound or detects an odor. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī and others from Sufyān, and Muslim narrated it from Abū Khaythamah and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah."
"15140","(15134) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us. Abū ʿUbayd said regarding the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) about a man who had four wives and divorced one of them but did not know which one he had divorced: He said: That which affects them regarding divorce is like that which affects them regarding inheritance. Abū ʿUbayd said: Hushaym narrated it to us: Abū Bishr informed us from ʿAmr ibn Ḥarim, from Jābir ibn Zayd, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both). His statement: \That which affects them regarding divorce is like that which affects them regarding inheritance\"" means: If the man dies having divorced one wife without knowing which one"," then the inheritance is shared among all of them — that is"," it is held in suspension until she is specifically identified. Likewise"," if he divorced her and did not know which one she was"," he must abstain from all of them if the divorce was irrevocable (three divorces). And Allah knows best."""
"15141","(15135) He cited as evidence what Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥumayd — who is Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — and ʿUbayd Allāh — who is Ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah — and Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: I asked ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) about a man from the people of al-Baḥrayn who divorced his wife one or two divorces, then she married another husband, and he died or divorced her, after which she returned to the first husband. How many divorces remained for her with him? He said: She is with him based on what remains. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15142","(15136) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: al-Ḥumaydī informed us: Sufyān informed us: al-Zuhrī narrated it with its chain and its meaning, except that he said: Then her waiting period expired, and she married a man other than him. Al-Ḥumaydī said: And Sufyān was asked about Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab being among them, and he said: Al-Zuhrī narrated to us thus — he did not add to these three. When he finished from it, he said: I do not preserve from al-Zuhrī that Saʿīd was in the chain, but Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated it to us from Saʿīd, from Abū Hurayrah, similarly, and that is sufficient for you. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before it.]"
"15143","(15137) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd narrated from al-Ḥakam, from a man from the people of Hajar whose name is Mazyadah, from his father, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: She is with him based on what remains of her divorces. Saʿīd said: And Qatādah used to take this opinion, i.e., regarding the man who divorces one or two divorces, then she marries, then he takes her back. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15144","(15138) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: Abū ʿAbbād informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: al-Ḥakam narrated from Mazyadah ibn Jābir, from his father, that he heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: She is with him based on what remains. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15145","(15139) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Maṭar, from al-Ḥakam, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: She is based on what remains of the divorce — i.e., regarding the man who divorces his wife, so she becomes irrevocably separated from him, then she marries a husband who divorces her, and then the first husband marries her. He said: She is with him based on what remains of her divorces. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15146","(15140) Abū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us: Sufyān informed us: Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated from Ibn Sīrīn, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: She is based on what remains of the divorce.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) something contrary to that. [Ḥasan]"
"15147","(15141) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Wabarah, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: If a man divorces his wife one or two divorces, then another man marries her, and then he (the first husband) marries her after that, she would be upon a fresh divorce (i.e., a new set of three). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15148","(15142) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Mihrajānī al-Faqīh informed us: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najyid informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Umayyah ibn Bisṭām informed us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us: Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the man who divorces two divorces, then another man marries her and divorces her or dies, and then her first husband marries her: He said: She would be upon a fresh divorce of three.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15149","(15143) The Shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Isrāʾīl narrated from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the man who divorces his wife one or two divorces, then she marries and her (second) husband divorces her. He said: If she returns to him after having married, he resumes the divorce (anew), and if he married her during her waiting period, she is with him based on what remains.\n\nThe first narration from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) is more authentic, and the narrations of ʿAbd al-Aʿlā from Ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah are weak according to the people of hadith. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15150","(15144) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Mihrān informed us: Abū al-Ṭāhir informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Ibrāhīm never lied except for three lies — two of them concerning the sake of Allah: his statement \I am sick\"" and his statement \""Rather"," their greatest one did this\"" — and one concerning the matter of Sārah. He arrived in the land of a tyrant"," and Sārah was with him"," and she was the most beautiful of people. He said to her: Indeed"," this tyrant"," if he learns that you are my wife"," he will overpower you. So if he asks you"," inform him that you are my sister"," for you are my sister in Islam"," and I do not know of any Muslim on the earth other than myself and you. When he entered his land"," some of the tyrant's people saw her and came to him"," saying: A woman has now entered your land who should only belong to you. So he sent for her and she was brought to him. Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) stood up for prayer. When she was brought before him"," he could not restrain himself from reaching out his hand toward her"," but his hand was seized with a severe grip. He said to her: Supplicate Allah to release my hand"," and I will not harm you. She did so. He reached out again"," and his hand was seized more severely than the first time. He said to her the same thing. He reached out again"," and his hand was seized more severely than the first two times. He said: Supplicate Allah to release my hand"," and I pledge to Allah that I will not harm you. She did so"," and his hand was released. He called the one who had brought her and said: You have brought me a devil"," not a human being. Expel her from my land"," and give her Hājar. She came walking"," and when Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) saw her"," he turned away and said: What happened? She said: Good — Allah restrained the hand of the wicked man and gave me a servant girl. Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: That is your mother"," O children of the water of the sky. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Tulayd"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Ṭāhir"," both from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15151","(15145) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyūb from Muḥammad from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Ibrāhīm"," peace be upon him"," did not lie except for three lies.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith as a mawqūf narration"," except that he said: \""While he was in the land of a tyrant among the tyrants"," and Sārah was with him"," it was said to that king: 'There is a man here who has with him a woman of the most beautiful of people.' So he sent for Ibrāhīm"," peace be upon him"," and he came to him. He said: 'Who is this woman?' He said: 'My sister.' He said: 'Go and send her to me.' So he came to her and said: 'He has asked me about you"," and I informed him that you are my sister"," so do not contradict me before him"," for there is no Muslim on the earth other than me and you. You are my sister in Islam.' \"" He said: \""So she departed.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated it from Muḥammad from Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," from the Prophet ﷺ with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ; previously cited.]"""
"15152","(15146) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Kāmil narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid and Khālid al-Ṭaḥḥān — meaning al-Maʿnī — all of them narrated from Khālid from Abū Tamīmah al-Hujaymī: that a man said to his wife, \O my little sister (yā ukhayyat)","\"" so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""Is she your sister?\"" He disliked that and forbade it.\n\nʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated it from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from Abū Tamīmah from a man among his people"," that he heard the Prophet ﷺ hear a man say to his wife"," \""O my little sister","\"" so he forbade him from that.\n\nʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Mukhtār narrated it from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from Abū ʿUthmān from Abū Tamīmah from the Prophet ﷺ. And Shuʿbah narrated it from Khālid from a man from Abū Tamīmah from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15153","(15147) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī said regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: \If they wish for reconciliation (in arāḍū iṣlāḥan)\"" — it is said: the reconciliation of divorce is through taking back (al-rajʿah). And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15154","(15148) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His words: \And their husbands have a greater right to take them back in this"," if they wish for reconciliation\"" (Q. 2:228). He says: \""If the man divorces his wife one or two divorces while she is pregnant"," then he has a greater right to take her back"," so long as she has not given birth. And it is not permissible for her to conceal her pregnancy.\"" And this is His words: \""And it is not lawful for them to conceal what Allah has created in their wombs\"" (Q. 2:228). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15155","(15149) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam narrated to us; Warqāʾ narrated to us from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid regarding His words, the Most High: \And their husbands have a greater right to take them back in this\"" — meaning"," during the waiting period (al-ʿiddah). [Ḥasan]"""
"15156","(15150) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Labbād narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to us; Asbāṭ ibn Naṣr narrated to us from al-Suddī from Abī Mālik and Abī Ṣāliḥ from Ibn ʿAbbās, and from Murrah from ʿAbd Allāh, and from people among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — then he mentioned the tafsīr up to His words: \Divorce is twice\"" (al-ṭalāqu marratān). He said: \""It is the appointed time during which taking back (al-rajʿah) is possible. If he divorces once or twice"," then either he retains her in a goodly manner and takes her back"," or he leaves her alone until her waiting period expires"," and then she is more entitled to herself.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15157","(15151) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — informed us; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Ibn Abī ʀāṣim narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; my father narrated to us from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: \A man used to divorce his wife and then take her back before the waiting period expired — there was no fixed limit for divorce — until a man from the Anṣār divorced his wife due to the bad relationship between them. He said"," 'I will leave her neither a widow nor a married woman.' So he kept divorcing her"," and when her waiting period was about to end"," he would take her back. So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed concerning this"," as Hishām ibn ʿUrwah informed me from his father from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her: 'Divorce is twice; then either retain in a goodly manner or release with kindness' (Q. 2:229). So He fixed for them the limit of three divorces — he may take her back after the first and after the second"," but he has no right of taking back after the third. Then Allah"," the Most High"," said: 'And when you divorce women"," divorce them at their prescribed periods"," and count the prescribed periods"," and fear your Allah' (Q. 2:228) up to His words: 'manifest indecency' (Q. 4:19).\"" And the hadith of Rukānah regarding taking back has already been mentioned in the book of divorce. [Ḥasan]"""
"15158","(15152) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — meaning al-Shaybānī — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Naḍr and Aḥmad ibn Sahl narrated to us; Muʾammal ibn Hishām narrated to us; Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Ayyūb from Nāʿif: that Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he commanded him to take her back, then to leave her alone until she menstruated another menstrual period, then to leave her alone until she became pure, then to divorce her before touching her. He said: \That is the waiting period which Allah has commanded that women be divorced in.\"" He said: \""So when Ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," was asked about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating"," he would say: 'As for you"," if you have divorced her once or twice"," then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to take her back"," then to leave her alone until she menstruated another menstrual period"," then to leave her alone until she became pure"," then to divorce her before touching her. But as for you"," if you have divorced her three times"," then you have disobeyed Allah regarding what He has commanded you concerning the divorce of your wife"," and she has become irrevocably separated from you.' \"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15159","(15153) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz — narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Miṣrī narrated to us in Makkah; Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh and ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl said: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Sakan al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; Ḥumayd narrated to us from Anas, who said: \When the Prophet ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah"," he was commanded to take her back"," so he took her back.\""\n\nAnd in the hadith of Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān"," he said from Anas ibn Mālik: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah"," and he was commanded to take her back.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15160","(15154) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī said regarding this verse: \When they are about to reach their appointed term"," either take them back in a goodly manner or let them complete their waiting period in a goodly manner.\"" And He forbade them to retain them harmfully in order to transgress. So it is not permissible to retain them harmfully. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15161","(15155) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us: Ādam informed us: Warqāʾ informed us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding His — the Most High's — words: **\And do not retain them (your wives) to cause harm\""** — he said: *\""The harm (ḍirār) is that a man divorces his wife with one divorce"," then takes her back when only one day remains of her waiting period (ʿiddah)"," then divorces her again"," then takes her back again when only one day remains of her waiting period — he harms her by doing this.\""* [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15162","(15156) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥaḍramī informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us, from Ziyād al-Aʿlam, from al-Ḥasan, regarding this verse: **\And do not retain them to cause harm"," thereby transgressing\""** — he said: *\""It is that a man divorces his wife"," and when she is about to complete her waiting period"," he takes her back (in revocable divorce)"," then divorces her again. And when she is about to complete her waiting period"," he takes her back — intending to prolong (her waiting period) for her.\""* And we have narrated from Masrūq ibn al-Ajdʿ a similar meaning to this. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15163","(15157) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān informed us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the client of the family of Ṭalḥah, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: *\A slave may marry two women and may pronounce two divorces.\""* [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15164","(15158) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Abū al-Zinād, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that Nufayʿ was a mukātab (a slave contracted for manumission) belonging to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ — or he was a slave under whom was a free woman — and he divorced her with two divorces and wished to take her back. The wives of the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to go to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) and ask him about that. So he went and met him at the stairs, holding the hand of Zayd ibn Thābit, and he asked them both. They both rushed to answer and said: *\She has become forbidden for you! She has become forbidden for you!\""* [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik]"""
"15165","(15159) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us. And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that Nufayʿ, a mukātab belonging to Umm Salamah, divorced a free woman with two divorces. He sought a legal ruling from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: *\She has become forbidden for you.\""* [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15166","(15160) Abū Zakariyyā informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad informed us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from ʿAbd Rabbih ibn Saʿīd, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī, that Nufayʿ, a mukātab belonging to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, sought a legal ruling from Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: *\I have divorced a free woman with two divorces.\""* Zayd ibn Thābit said: *\""She has become forbidden for you.\""* [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik]"""
"15167","(15161) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Maʿmar ibn Sulaymān al-Raqqī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishr informed us, from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, that a mukātab had a free woman under him, and he divorced her with two divorces. He came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān and Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with them both) and asked them about that. Each one of them hastened to answer and said to him: *\She has become forbidden for you"," and divorce is the prerogative of men.\""* [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15168","(15162) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Rāzī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ẓāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us: Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad informed us: Hishām informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, who said: Nufayʿ narrated to me that he was a slave and had a free woman under him. He divorced her with two divorces and asked ʿUthmān and Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with them both), and they said: *\Your divorce is the divorce of a slave"," and her waiting period is the waiting period of a free woman.\""* [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15169","(15163) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī al-Khastrawajirdī informed us from his original manuscript: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ghiṭrīf informed us: Abū Khalīfah informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥawḍī informed us: Hammām informed us, from Qatādah, from Abū al-Khalīl, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: *\Divorce is the prerogative of men"," and the waiting period is the prerogative of women.\""* [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15170","(15164) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: *\When a slave divorces his wife with two divorces"," she becomes forbidden for her until she marries a husband other than him — whether she is a free woman or a slave woman. The waiting period of a free woman is three menstrual cycles"," and the waiting period of a slave woman is two menstrual cycles.\""* This is how Mālik narrated it in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15171","(15165) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; they said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Abū al-Azhar narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding a slave woman who is married to a free man: she is separated by two divorces and observes a waiting period of two menstrual cycles. And if a free woman is married to a slave, she is separated by two divorces and observes a waiting period of three menstrual cycles.\n\nSālim likewise narrated this from Ibn ʿUmar. His position in this matter is that whichever of the two is enslaved, the number of divorces is reduced on account of his or her enslavement. This is the position of Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) in this matter."
"15172","(15166) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz and Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; they said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Shabīb al-Musallī narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĪsā from ʿAṭiyyah al-ʿAwfī from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The divorce of a slave woman is two"," and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles.\""\n\nʿUmar ibn Shabīb al-Musallī is alone in narrating it thus as a marfūʿ (elevated) hadith"," and he was weak. The correct narration is what Sālim and Nāfiʿ narrated from Ibn ʿUmar as a mawqūf (stopped) narration"," as mentioned above. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15173","(15167) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; he said: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: The hadith of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĪsā from ʿAṭiyyah from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (ﷺ) is munkar (denounced) and not established, on two grounds. One of them is that ʿAṭiyyah is weak, while Sālim and Nāfiʿ are more reliable and have more authentic narrations. The other ground is that ʿUmar ibn Shabīb is weak, and his narration is not used as evidence. And Allah knows best."
"15174","(15168) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; he said: I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: \ʿUmar ibn Shabīb was nothing [i.e."," of no significance in hadith narration]"," and I have seen him.\"""""
"15175","(15169) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; they said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAmr Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf ibn Khālid narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīm al-Muqawwim narrated to us; Ṣughdī ibn Sinān narrated from Muẓāhir ibn Aslam from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The divorce of a slave is two"," and a woman does not become lawful for him until she marries a husband other than him. The waiting period of a slave woman is two menstrual cycles. A free woman may be married alongside a slave woman"," but a slave woman may not be married alongside a free woman.\"" And he said: \""The divorce of a slave is two.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15176","(15170) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Muẓāhir ibn Aslam from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A slave woman is divorced by two pronouncements"," and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles.\"" Abū ʿĀṣim said: Muẓāhir ibn Aslam narrated it to me. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15177","(15171) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: I heard Ibn Ḥammād say: Al-Bukhārī said: \Muẓāhir ibn Aslam"," from al-Qāsim"," from ʿĀʾishah — Abū ʿĀṣim declared him weak.\"""""
"15178","(15172) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us; Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: Al-Qāsim was asked about the waiting period of a slave woman. He said: \The people say two menstrual cycles"," but we do not know this from the Book of Allah nor from the Sunnah of His Prophet (ﷺ).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī]"""
"15179","(15173) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me; al-Layth narrated to me; Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated to me; Zayd ibn Aslam narrated, who said: Al-Qāsim was asked: \How many times is a slave woman divorced?\"" He said: \""Her divorce is two"," and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles.\"" It was then said to him: \""Has this reached you from the Prophet (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""No.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15180","(15174) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Zakariyyā al-Sājī narrated to us; Bundār narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Ashʿath ibn Sawwār from al-Shaʿbī from Masrūq from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Sunnah regarding women is in matters of divorce and waiting period.\"" Ashʿath ibn Sawwār is not strong. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15181","(15175) And it has been narrated from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Masruq, from 'Abd Allah, though it is not preserved. Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khwarizmi narrated to us; Abu Yazid — Yusuf ibn Yazid ibn Kamil al-Qaratisi — narrated to us; al-'Abbas ibn Talib narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated it. And it has been narrated from him contradicting it."
"15182","(15176) Al-Sharif Abu al-Fath al-'Umari informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shuraih informed us; Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Abd Allah, who said: \Divorce pertains to men"," and the waiting period ('iddah) pertains to women.\"" Thus I found it in his original book"," though it is not preserved. [Da'if]"""
"15183","(15177) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Salam narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us; 'Abbad narrated, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The established practice (sunnah) is that divorce and the waiting period pertain to women.\"" Thus he said. [Sahih]"""
"15184","(15178) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Walid informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us; Waki' narrated, from Hisham al-Dastawa'i, from Qatadah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Divorce pertains to men"," and the waiting period pertains to women.\""\n\nHe said: And Waki' narrated to us"," from Ibrahim ibn Yazid"," from 'Ata'"," from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: \""Divorce"," I think"," pertains to men"," and the waiting period pertains to women.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15185","(15179) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: \Divorce pertains to men"," and the waiting period pertains to women.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated the hadith of 'Ikrimah"," once from Ibn 'Abbas and once as a mursal narration from the Prophet (peace be upon him): \""Divorce is only for the one who takes hold of the shank.\"" And Allah knows best. [Sahih. Narrated by Malik]"""
"15186","(15180) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Muhammad — al-Hasan ibn Hamshadh — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Shaybani al-Nahwi narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Amr ibn Mu'attib, that Abu Hasan, the freedman of Banu Nawfal, informed him that he asked Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) for a legal ruling concerning a male slave who had a female slave as his wife; he divorced her twice, thereby separating her from him, and then both of them were subsequently freed. Is it permissible for the man to propose marriage to her? Ibn 'Abbas said: \Yes"," for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) judged accordingly.\"" And thus Hisham narrated it"," from Yahya"," from 'Amr ibn Mu'attib. And some of the narrators said: 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak"," from Yahya"," from 'Amr ibn Mu'attib. And thus Mu'awiyah ibn Salam narrated it"," from Yahya"," from 'Umar.\n\nAnd Abu Dawud mentioned"," from Ahmad ibn Hanbal"," from 'Abd al-Razzaq"," that Ibn al-Mubarak said to Ma'mar: \""Who is this Abu al-Hasan? He has indeed shouldered a massive rock\"" — meaning by this his rejection of the hadith he had brought. [Da'if]"""
"15187","(15181) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Bara'i narrated to us. He said: 'Ali ibn al-Madini was asked about 'Amr ibn Mu'attib, from whom Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated, from Abu al-Hasan, the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) judged concerning a male slave who had a female slave as his wife.\"" He said: \""He is unknown (majhul); no one other than Yahya narrated from him.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: And the majority of the jurists hold a view contrary to what he narrated. Had it been established"," we would have acted upon it; however"," we do not establish a hadith narrated by one whose integrity is unknown. And with Allah lies the granting of success. And it has been narrated from Ibn Mas'ud and Jabir"," from their own statements"," contradicting that. [Sahih]"""
"15188","(15182) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Walid informed us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, concerning a male slave who divorced his wife twice and she was then freed: \He may not marry her until she marries a husband other than him.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15189","(15183) He said: And Abu Bakr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' narrated, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who said: \If she is freed during her waiting period"," then he may marry her"," and she shall be with him on the basis of one (remaining) divorce.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15190","(15184) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Yazid narrated; Shu'bah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Among the trusts (amanah) is placing confidence in a woman regarding her chastity.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15191","(15185) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us, Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding His — the Most High's — words: **\And it is not lawful for them to conceal what Allah has created in their wombs\""** — he said"," meaning pregnancy. He said: \""A woman must not say"," 'I am with child","' when she is not"," nor must she say"," 'I am not with child","' when she is.\""\n\nAnd Layth ibn Abī Sulaym narrated it from Mujāhid"," concerning both menstruation and pregnancy together. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15192","(15186) Abū Zakariyyāʾ ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — that he divorced his wife while she was in the dwelling of Ḥafṣah — may Allah be pleased with her — and his path to the mosque passed by her, so he took the other path, going behind the houses, out of dislike of asking her permission (to enter), until he took her back.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār that they both said: \Nothing from her is lawful to him until he takes her back.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15193","(15187) Abū Zakariyyāʾ ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Yaḥyī ibn Ḥassān narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, from ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn Mālik al-Jazarī, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib — may Allah be pleased with him — regarding a man who divorces his wife, then calls witnesses to his taking her back, while she is unaware of that. He said: \She is the first man's wife"," whether the other had consummated the marriage with her or not.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15194","(15188) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, who said: Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — divorced his wife Ṣafiyyah bint Abī ʿUbayd with one or two divorces. He would not enter upon her except with her permission. When he took her back, he called witnesses to his taking her back and then entered upon her. [Ḥasan]"
"15195","(15189) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated from Qatādah and Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, and from Ayyūb, from Ibn Sīrīn, that ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn — may Allah be pleased with him — was asked about a man who divorced his wife without calling witnesses, and then took her back without calling witnesses. ʿImrān said: \He divorced contrary to the prescribed waiting period and took her back contrary to the Sunnah. Let him now call witnesses.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15196","(15190) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that he heard her say: \The woman of Rifāʿah al-Quraẓī came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I was with Rifāʿah"," and he divorced me with a final divorce. Then I married ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr"," but with him there is only something like the fringe of a garment.' The Prophet ﷺ smiled and said: 'Do you wish to return to Rifāʿah? No"," not until you taste his ʿusaylah and he tastes your ʿusaylah.'\"" She said: \""And Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — was with the Prophet ﷺ"," and Khālid ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ was at the door"," waiting to be given permission"," so he called out: 'O Abū Bakr"," do you not hear what this woman is openly declaring in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?'\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Shāfiʿī. In the narration of al-Zaʿfarānī from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — it is: \""The woman of Rifāʿah al-Quraẓī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","\"" then he mentioned the similar hadith up to his words: \""…not until he tastes your ʿusaylah and you taste his ʿusaylah.\"" He did not mention what came after that.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," all of them from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"15197","(15191) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyāʾ ibn Abī Isḥāq all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who informed him that Rifāʿah al-Quraẓī divorced his wife with a final divorce. After him, she married ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \She was under Rifāʿah"," and he divorced her with the last of three divorces. Then she married ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr after him. And by Allah"," with him there is only something like this fringe.\"" She took hold of the fringe of her garment. He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled"," laughing"," and said: 'Perhaps you wish to return to Rifāʿah? No"," not until you taste his ʿusaylah and he tastes your ʿusaylah.'\"" She said: \""And Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and Khālid ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ was sitting at the door of the chamber"," not having been given permission. So Khālid began calling out to Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him: 'Will you not restrain this woman from what she is openly declaring in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah"," from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"15198","(15192) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Hishām narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — that a woman from Banī Qurayẓah was married to a man from among them, and he divorced her. Then another man married her. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," with him there is only something like this fringe.\"" He said: \""No"," not until he tastes your ʿusaylah and you taste his ʿusaylah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"15199","(15193) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — that she was asked about a man who marries a woman and then divorces her three times. She said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'She is not lawful for the first (husband) until the other tastes her ʿusaylah and she tastes his ʿusaylah.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"15200","(15194) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — who said: \A man divorced his wife"," and she married another husband. He consummated the marriage with her"," but with him there was only something like the fringe of a garment"," and he did not attain from her what he desired. So he did not delay in divorcing her. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about that. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," my husband divorced me"," and I married another husband. He consummated the marriage with me"," but with him there was only something like the fringe of a garment. He only approached me once and did not attain from me what I desired. Am I lawful for my first husband?' He said: 'You are not lawful for your first husband until the other tastes your ʿusaylah and you taste his ʿusaylah.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad"," from Abū Muʿāwiyah"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Kurayb"," from Abū Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"15201","(15195) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us; Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna both said: Yahya narrated from 'Ubaydullah; al-Qasim narrated from 'A'isha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a man divorced his wife with three divorces. She married another husband, but he divorced her before consummating the marriage. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: \Is she lawful for the first husband?\"" He said: \""No"," until he (the second husband) tastes her 'usaylah (i.e."," consummates the marriage) as the first one tasted it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Bashshar"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna. It was also narrated by al-Aswad ibn Yazid from 'A'isha (may Allah be pleased with her)"," both as a marfu' (elevated) and mawquf (stopped) narration. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"15202","(15196) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami all said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Malik ibn Anas informed us from al-Miswar ibn Rifa'ah al-Qurazi from al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr from his father, that Rifa'ah divorced his wife Tamimah bint Wahb with three divorces during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr then married her, but he was impotent and could not consummate the marriage, so he divorced her without having touched her. Rifa'ah then wished to remarry her — she being the wife whom he had divorced before 'Abd al-Rahman — and he mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He forbade him from marrying her and said: \She is not lawful for you until she tastes the 'usaylah (i.e."," until the second husband consummates the marriage).\"" [Sahih]"""
"15203","(15197) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Malik informed us from al-Miswar ibn Rifa'ah al-Qurazi from al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr, that Rifa'ah divorced his wife Tamimah bint Wahb, and he mentioned the hadith with the same meaning.\n\nYahya ibn Bukayr also narrated it from Malik, but he did not mention \from his father","\"" and he said: \""Tamimah bint Wahb","\"" and he mentioned the hadith with the same meaning. [Sahih — as previously cited]"""
"15204","(15198) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us; Abu 'Ubayd narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman narrated from Sufyan from 'Alqamah from Razin al-Ahmari from Ibn 'Umar.\n\n(Additionally) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Kathir al-'Abdi informed us; Sufyan narrated from 'Alqamah ibn Murthad from Sulayman ibn Razin from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked while he was on the minbar about a man who divorced his wife with three divorces, and another man married her, closed the door, drew the curtain, and lifted the veil, then separated from her. He said: \She is not lawful for the first husband until the other one tastes her 'usaylah (i.e."," consummates the marriage).\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of al-'Abdi. Al-'Abdi also said in his isnad what Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri said. The correct narration is that of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi"," for Waki' narrated it once from Sufyan and said: from 'Alqamah from Razin ibn Sulayman al-Ahmari. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15205","(15199) Shu'bah contradicted him in the isnad, for he narrated it from 'Alqamah ibn Murthad from Salim ibn Razin from Salim ibn 'Abdullah from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAbu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan both informed us of it; they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; Khalaf and Yahya ibn Ma'in both said: Ghundar narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated, and he mentioned it.\n\nIt has reached me from Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari that he weakened the hadith of both Shu'bah and Sufyan, and from Abu Zur'ah that he said: \The hadith of Sufyan is more authentic.\"""""
"15206","(15200) The Shaykh said: The narration of Waki' and 'Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan is more authentic, for Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated it and said: 'Alqamah ibn Murthad narrated to us from Razin al-Ahmari, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked on the minbar about a man who divorced his wife and she became irrevocably separated from him, and he mentioned the hadith.\n\nAbu Muhammad Janah ibn Nadhir al-Muharibi in Kufah informed us; Abu Ja'far ibn Duhaym informed us; Ahmad ibn Hazim informed us; Malik ibn Isma'il informed us; Qays narrated it, and he mentioned it.\n\nShu'bah used to say: \Sufyan is more precise (ahfaz) than me.\"" And Yahya al-Qattan said: \""When they (Sufyan and Shu'bah) differ"," I take the statement of Sufyan.\"" [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15207","(15201) It has also been narrated concerning this from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (ﷺ). Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Halali informed us; Yahya ibn Hammad informed us; Muhammad ibn Dinari narrated from Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i, who said: Anas ibn Malik was asked about a man who married a woman whose husband had divorced her — I think he said three times — but the second husband had not yet consummated the marriage. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked, and he said: \She is not lawful for him until he tastes her 'usaylah and she tastes his 'usaylah (i.e."," until the marriage is consummated).\"" [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15208","(15202) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzzi informed us; Abu al-Hasan al-Tarifi informed us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Salih informed us; Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) regarding the words of the Most High: {But if he has divorced her, then she is not lawful to him until she marries a husband other than him} (al-Baqarah 230). He said: If he divorces her with three divorces, she is not lawful to him until she marries a husband other than him. Then He said: {Then if he divorces her, there is no blame on them if they return to each other} (al-Baqarah 230). He said: If she marries after the first husband and the other one consummates the marriage, there is no sin on the first husband to marry her if the other one divorces her or dies.\n\nIt has also been narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad regarding the death of the second husband before consummating the marriage: it is not lawful for her first husband to marry her. [Da'if (Weak)]"
"15209","(15203) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Zahiri informed us; Muhammad ibn Maslamah informed us; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; Shu'bah narrated from Ibn 'Awn from Abu Salih, meaning al-Hanafi, who said: Ibn al-Kawa' asked 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) about a slave woman who is under a man and he divorces her twice, then he purchases her. He said: \She is not lawful for him.\""\n\nYahya al-Qattan also narrated it from Shu'bah. [Sahih]"""
"15210","(15204) Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihranjani informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzzi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-BushanjI informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Malik narrated from Ibn Shihab from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he used to say regarding a man who divorces a slave woman three times and then purchases her: \She is not lawful for her until she marries a husband other than him.\"" He said: \""And I heard Malik say: 'More than one of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) said that.'\"" [Sahih]"""
"15211","(15205) Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Raffāʾ informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashr informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us; Ibn Abī Uways informed us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of Madīnah, regarding a man who married a slave woman and she was irrevocably divorced from him (bi-l-battah), then her master took her back into concubinage (istasarrahā), and then her husband purchased her after that — she does not become lawful for him by virtue of her master's taking her into concubinage, nor does she become lawful for him by virtue of his ownership (milk yamīnihi) until she marries a husband other than him. [Weak]"
"15212","(15206) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mātī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated from Sufyān, from Shuʿbah, from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUbaydah al-Salmānī, who said: \She does not become lawful for him except through the same means by which she was made unlawful to him\"" — referring to a man who married a slave woman and divorced her with two divorces"," then purchased her. He said: \""When a slave woman is under a man and he divorces her with two divorces"," and then her master has sexual intercourse with her"," the master does not make her lawful for her husband unless he is a husband.\"" [Weak]"""
"15213","(15207) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, who said: \I came upon thirteen of the Companions — that is"," of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — all of them saying: 'The one who makes an oath of abstinence (al-mawlā) shall be made to stand (before the judge).'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The minimum of 'thirteen' is thirteen"," and they say: 'They were from the Anṣār.'\"" [Sound]"""
"15214","(15208) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl informed me; al-Uwaysī informed me; Sulaymān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAbd Rabbihi ibn Saʿīd, from Thābit ibn ʿUbayd, a freedman of Zayd ibn Thābit, from twelve of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ): \The oath of abstinence (al-īlāʾ) is not a divorce until the one who swore it is made to stand (before the judge).\"" [Fair]"""
"15215","(15209) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us; Ibn Abī Maryam informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, who said: \I asked twelve of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the man who makes an oath of abstinence (yuʾlī). They said: 'Nothing is incumbent upon him until four months pass. Then he shall be made to stand (before the judge); if he returns (to his wife)"," then so be it"," otherwise he must divorce.'\"" [Fair]"""
"15216","(15210) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated from Miʿsar, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from Ṭāwūs, that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) used to make the one who made an oath of abstinence (al-muʾlī) stand (before the judge). [Sound]"
"15217","(15211) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; they said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us; ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us; Manṣūr ibn Salamah informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from ʿUmar ibn Ḥusayn, from al-Qāsim, that ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) did not consider the oath of abstinence (al-īlāʾ) to be anything, even if the four months elapsed, until the one who swore it was made to stand (before the judge). [Weak]"
"15218","(15212) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from al-Shaybānī, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAmr ibn Salamah, who said: \I witnessed ʿAlī making the one who made an oath of abstinence (al-muʾlī) stand (before the judge).\"" [Fair through other chains]"""
"15219","(15213) Abū Zakariyyā informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Layth, from Mujāhid, from Marwān al-Ḥakam, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) made the one who made an oath of abstinence (al-muʾlī) stand (before the judge). [Fair through other chains]"
"15220","(15214) Abū Zakariyyā informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to make the one who made an oath of abstinence (al-muʾlī) stand (before the judge). [Fair through other chains]"
"15221","(15215) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) used to say regarding the oath of Īlāʾ (abstention): \When four months have passed and he is not made to stand (for judgment)"," then that is not a divorce"," and even if a year were to pass"," no divorce would be incumbent upon him until he is made to stand (and given the choice).\"" [Weak]"""
"15222","(15216) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Shaybānī, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: \He (the one who swore the oath of Īlāʾ) shall be made to stand (for judgment) after the four months; either he returns to his wife (reconciles) or he divorces her.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15223","(15217) Abū al-Fatḥ al-Faqīh narrated to us: al-Shurayḥī narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Shaybānī, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said: \I witnessed ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) make a man stand at the end of four months. He stood him in the open space and said: 'Either you return to your wife or you divorce her.'\""\n\nThis is a sound"," connected chain of narration. It is also narrated from Abū al-Bakhtarī"," from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him)"," who said: \""When a man swears an oath of Īlāʾ against his wife"," he shall be made to stand upon the completion of four months"," and it shall be said to him: 'Either return to your wife or resolve upon divorce.' And he shall be compelled to do so.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15224","(15218) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Mazzī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him), that he used to say: \Any man who swears an oath of Īlāʾ against his wife — when four months have passed"," he shall be made to stand (for judgment) until he either divorces or returns to her. No divorce shall befall her when the four months have passed until he is made to stand (and given the choice).\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," from Mālik. [Authentic]"""
"15225","(15219) Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, who said: \ʿĀʾishah (may Allāh be pleased with her)"," when a man was mentioned to her who had sworn an oath not to approach his wife"," and he left her for five months"," she did not consider that to be anything (i.e."," not a divorce) until he was made to stand (for judgment). And she would say: 'How (beautifully) did Allāh"," the Mighty and Majestic"," say: {Either retention with kindness or release with good conduct} (Qurʾān 2:229).'\"" [Weak]"""
"15226","(15220) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn al-Rabīʿ ibn Ṭāriq narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed me: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar informed me, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), that she said regarding the oath of Īlāʾ: \There is nothing (incumbent)"," even if a year were to pass. Either he returns to his wife or he divorces her.\"" [Weak]"""
"15227","(15221) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī narrated to us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated to us, from Qatādah, that Abū Dharr and ʿĀʾishah (may Allāh be pleased with them both) said: \The one who swore the oath of Īlāʾ shall be made to stand (for judgment) after the expiry of the period; either he returns to his wife or he divorces her.\"" [Weak]"""
"15228","(15222) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Rāzī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Zāhir ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: al-Sulamī, meaning Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf, narrated to us: Ḥajjāj narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib (may Allāh, the Most High, have mercy on him), that Abū al-Dardāʾ said regarding the oath of Īlāʾ: \He shall be made to stand (for judgment) upon the expiry of four months; either he divorces or he returns to his wife. And Allāh knows best.\"" [Weak]"""
"15229","(15223) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Abū al-Azhar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Isḥāq: Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihāb narrated to me, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) used to say: \When four months have passed"," it is one divorce"," and the husband has greater right to take her back as long as she is in her waiting period (ʿiddah).\""\n\nThis is how Muḥammad ibn Isḥāh ibn Ysār narrated it from al-Zuhrī. However"," Mālik ibn Anas"," the Imām (may Allāh have mercy on him)"," contradicted him"," narrating it from al-Zuhrī"," from Saʿīd and Abū Bakr"," as their own statement (mawqūf)"," not raised to ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him). [Good]"""
"15230","(15224) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that they both used to say regarding a man who swears an oath of Īlāʾ against his wife: \When the four months have passed"," it is one divorce"," and her husband has the right of return (rajʿah) over her as long as she is in her waiting period (ʿiddah).\""\n\nMālik (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: \""And this was the opinion of Ibn Shihāb (al-Zuhrī).\"" This narration is more authentic than the first narration. [Authentic]"""
"15231","(15225) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar reported from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī, who said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyab about the oath of ilāʾ (abstention from one's wife). Then I passed by Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and he said: \What did you ask him about?\"" I said: \""About ilāʾ.\"" He said: \""Shall I not inform you of what ʿUthmān and Zayd — may Allah be pleased with them both — used to say?\"" They used to say: \""When the four months have passed"," it constitutes one divorce.\"" Al-Awzāʿī likewise narrated this from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī"," but it is not preserved (as authentic). And ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī is not strong (in narration). The well-known narration from ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — contradicts it. [Ḥasan]"""
"15232","(15226) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; al-Maymūnī narrated to us, saying: I mentioned to Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — may Allah have mercy on him — the ḥadīth of ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī from Abū Salamah from ʿUthmān, and he said: \I do not know what this is. The opposite of it has been narrated from ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him.\"" It was said to him: \""Who narrated it?\"" He said: \""Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from Ṭāwūs from ʿUthmān: he is to be stopped (i.e."," his narration is not to be accepted as definitive).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15233","(15227) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAttāb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī al-ʿAwwām al-Rayāḥī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Sufyān ibn Saʿīd reported from ʿAlī ibn Bādhimah from Abī ʿUbaydah from Masrūq from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \When a man takes an oath of ilāʾ (abstention) from his wife and the four months pass"," it constitutes one divorce. He may propose to her during her waiting period"," and no one else may propose to her. And the waiting period is three menstrual cycles.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15234","(15228) Abū Saʿīd narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ reported that al-Shāfiʿī — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \As for what has been narrated from Ibn Masʿūd — may Allah be pleased with him — regarding this"," it is mursal (disconnected). And the ḥadīth of ʿAlī ibn Bādhimah — I do not know anyone else who narrates it with a complete chain (i.e."," no one else connects it).\"" He said: \""And even if this were established"," I would consider it defective. Are the words of more than ten of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more deserving of being followed"," or the words of one or two?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15235","(15229) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Shuʿbah reported from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Najīḥ from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — who said: \When four months have passed"," it is one irrevocable divorce.\"" Yazīd said: \""He means regarding ilāʾ.\"" And likewise it was narrated by Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15236","(15230) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed us; al-Ḥakam informed me, saying: I heard Miqsam say: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — say: \The decisive intent of divorce is the expiry of the four months. And al-fayʾ (return) means sexual intercourse.\"" This is what is authentic from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — although the opposite of it has also been narrated from him. [Ḥasan]"""
"15237","(15231) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ reported from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — regarding the verse of ilāʾ, who said: \A man swears by Allah that he will not approach his wife. She waits four months. If he then approaches her"," he must expiate his oath by feeding ten poor persons"," or clothing them"," or freeing a slave. Whoever cannot find the means must fast three days. And if the four months pass before he approaches her"," the authority (sulṭān) gives him the choice: either he returns (to her) and takes her back"," or he resolves (to divorce) and divorces her"," as Allah — Glorified and Exalted is He — said.\"" [Ḍaʿīf] (13131) ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah reports from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with him — regarding ilāʾ"," that a man takes an oath that he will not have intercourse with his wife. The women wait four months. If the husband has intercourse with his wife"," it is valid; otherwise he must give expiation for his oath"," which is feeding ten poor persons"," clothing them"," or freeing a slave. Whoever cannot find the means must fast three days. If the four months pass before intercourse"," the ruler gives him the choice: if he wishes to return"," he returns"," or if he intends divorce"," he divorces"," as Allah has commanded."""
"15238","(15232) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Labbād narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to us; Asbāṭ reported from al-Suddī regarding the verse of ilāʾ, who said: \ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — used to say: When a man takes an oath of ilāʾ from his wife and four months pass"," he is made to stand (before the authority) and it is said to him: 'Do you retain (your wife) or divorce?' If he retains her"," she is his wife. If he divorces"," she is an irrevocably divorced woman.' Ibn Masʿūd and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with them both — used to say: 'When the four months pass"," she is irrevocably divorced and she is more entitled to herself (i.e."," she is free to remarry).'\"" Al-Shāfiʿī — may Allah have mercy on him — said regarding their citing the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās as evidence: \""We said: As for Ibn ʿAbbās"," you yourself contradict him regarding ilāʾ.\"" He said: \""In what way?\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15239","(15233) He mentioned what Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah reported from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Abī Yaḥyā from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with him — that he said: \Al-muʾlī (the one who takes the oath of abstention) is the one who swears that he will never approach his wife.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15240","(15234) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yazīd — that is, ibn Hārūn — and Abū al-Naḍr both narrated. Yazīd said: Shuʿbah informed us from al-Ḥakam from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — who said: \Al-fayʾ (return) means sexual intercourse.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in its meaning"," though not as a direct statement of the Prophet ﷺ]"""
"15241","(15235) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ṣaydalānī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Asbāṭ narrated from Muṭarrif, from ʿĀmir, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: \Al-Fa'i' (return) means sexual intercourse.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: And Masrūq"," Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," al-Shaʿbī"," and others among the exegetes said the same. And al-Ḥasan said: \""Al-Fa'i' means sexual intercourse. If there is an excuse"," such as illness or imprisonment"," then it suffices for him to return (fa'a) with his tongue.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ by other than him]"""
"15242","(15236) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī narrated to us; al-Uwaysī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Ḥumayd, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) swore an oath of abstinence (īlā') from his wives"," and his foot had become dislocated"," so he stayed in his upper chamber for twenty-nine nights"," then he came down. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," you swore an oath for a month.' He said: 'Indeed"," the month can be twenty-nine nights.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Uwaysī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1911]"""
"15243","(15237) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿĀmir narrated from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabaḥ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them).\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAmrūyah al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUbayd, Abū Qudāmah, narrated to us; ʿĀmir al-Aḥwal narrated to me; ʬāʾ narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: \The oath of abstinence (īlā') of the people of the Jāhiliyyah used to be for a year"," two years"," or more than that. So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," fixed for them a period of four months. If his oath of abstinence is...\"" And in the narration of Yūnus: \""Whoever's oath of abstinence is less than four months"," then it is not an oath of abstinence.\""\n\nHe said: And ʬāʾ said: \""If he swears an oath of abstinence from her while she is still in her family's house before he has cohabited with her"," then it is not an oath of abstinence.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15244","(15238) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, regarding the oath of abstinence (īlā'): \That he swear that he will never touch her"," or for six months"," or more"," or whatever exceeds four months"," or something of that nature.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15245","(15239) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Razjāhī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Kūfī informed us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; al-Masʿūdī narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: \Every oath that prevents sexual intercourse is an oath of abstinence (īlā').\"" And we also narrated it from al-Shaʿbī and al-Nakhaʿī (may Allah have mercy on both of them). [Ḥasan]"""
"15246","(15240) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū al-Ashʿath narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, al-Thaqafī, narrated from Dāwūd, Ibn Abī Hind, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from a man from Banī ʿIjl, from Abū ʬiyyah, that his brother died and left behind a nursing infant. Abū ʬiyyah said to his wife: \Nurse him.\"" She said: \""I fear that you may impregnate me.\"" So he swore that he not approach her until she weaned him. He did so until she weaned him. He said: \""I mentioned that to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'You only intended good"," and the oath of abstinence (īlā') is only in anger.'\""\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated it from Hushaym"," from Dāwūd"," from Simāk ibn Ḥarb"," from Abū ʬiyyah al-Asadī"," that he married his brother's wife while she was nursing his brother's son"," and he mentioned it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15247","(15241) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Simāk, from ʬiyyah ibn Jubayr, who said: \My mother was nursing a boy"," and one of our children had died. My father swore that he would not approach her until she weaned the boy. When four months had passed"," it was said to him: 'She has been irrevocably separated from you.' So he went to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'If you swore the oath out of harm (to her)"," then she is your wife; otherwise"," she has been irrevocably separated from you.'\"" This is what Shuʿbah said from Simāk ibn Ḥarb.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī said in al-Qadīm: \""Whoever says this statement should also say: Similarly"," if she has an ailment that makes sexual intercourse harmful to her"," and the oath was sworn without the intention of harming her"," then it is not an oath of abstinence. And for this statement there is a good basis"," and Allah knows best.\""\n\nAnd others said: \""He is one who has sworn an oath of abstinence (mu'lin)"," and every oath that prevents sexual intercourse is an oath of abstinence.\"" And al-Shāfiʿī affirmed this position in al-Jadīd"," and he argued that Allah"," the Most High"," revealed the ruling on īlā' in absolute terms"," without mentioning anger or pleasure therein. And Allah knows best."""
"15248","(15242) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Tamīm ibn Salamah, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \All praise is due to Allah"," whose hearing encompasses all voices. The woman who came to plead her case came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and I was in a corner of the house"," not hearing what she was saying. Then Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: 'Indeed"," Allah has heard the statement of the woman who disputes with you concerning her husband.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""And al-Aʿmash said from Tamīm"," and he mentioned it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15249","(15243) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; the Sheikh Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us; Abū Kurayb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿUbaydah ibn Maʿn al-Masʿūdī narrated to me; my father narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Tamīm ibn Salamah, from ʿUrwah. He said: ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \Blessed is Allah whose hearing encompasses everything. Indeed"," I can hear the speech of Khawlah bint Thaʿlabah"," and some of it is hidden from me"," while she is complaining to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about her husband"," saying: 'O Messenger of Allah"," he consumed my youth and I bore him children"," but when I grew old and my childbearing ceased"," he declared ẓihār from me. O Allah"," I complain to You.'\"" ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""She did not leave until Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came down with these verses: 'Indeed"," Allah has heard the statement of the woman who disputes with you concerning her husband.'\""\n\nHe said: And her husband was Aws ibn al-Ṣāmit. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15250","(15244) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī informed us; Abū al-Nuʿmān Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that Jamīlah was the wife of Aws ibn al-Ṣāmit, and Aws was a man afflicted with intermittent fits of madness. When his madness intensified, he would declare ẓihār from his wife. So Allah, the Blessed and Most High, revealed the expiation for ẓihār.\n\nAnd Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated it from Ḥammād, and he sent it as a mursal narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15251","(15245) And Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad — informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā — informed us: Abū Ḥamzah al-Thumālī — from ʿIkrimah — from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When a man would say to his wife in the Jāhiliyyah: \You are to me like the back of my mother","\"" she became forbidden upon him in Islam. He said: The first person to practice Ẓihār in Islam was Aws"," and under his marriage was his cousin's daughter"," Khuwaylah bint Khuwaylid. He pronounced Ẓihār upon her"," and it fell from his hand"," and he said: \""I see nothing but that you have become forbidden upon me.\"" She said the like of that to him. He said: \""Go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him.\"" So she came to the Prophet ﷺ and found at his side a hairdresser combing his head. She informed him"," and he said: \""O Khuwaylah"," we have not been commanded anything regarding your matter.\"" Then revelation descended upon the Prophet ﷺ"," and he said: \""O Khuwaylah"," receive glad tidings.\"" She said: \""Good?\"" He said: \""Good.\"" Then he recited upon her the words of the Most High: **\""Allah has indeed heard the statement of the one who disputes with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah…\""** [Sūrah al-Mujādilah"," 58:1]. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15252","(15246) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq — informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī — informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd — informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ — from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ — from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālah — from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: No divorce occurs through Ẓihār — meaning by Ẓihār. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15253","(15247) And Abū ʿAbd Allāl-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Kaʿbī — informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah — informed us: Yazīd ibn Ṣāliḥ — informed us: Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf — from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān, who said: Ẓihār and Īlāʾ were considered divorce in the era of the Jāhiliyyah. So Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, fixed a period of four months for Īlāʾ and prescribed expiation (Kaffārah) for Ẓihār. [Ḥasan]"
"15254","(15248) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us: Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Shādhān — informed us: Muʿlā ibn Manṣūr — informed us: Ibn Lahīʿah — from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb — from his father — from his grandfather, who said: There is no Ẓihār from a slave woman. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15255","(15249) And he said: Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to us — from Aṭāʾ — from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: There is no Ẓihār from a slave woman. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15256","(15250) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr — both said: ʿAlī — informed us: Yūsuf ibn Isḥāq ibn Bahlūl — informed us: my grandfather — informed us: my father — informed us: Abū Juzayy Naṣr ibn Ṭarīf — from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī — from Ibn Abī Mūlaykah — from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Whoever wishes, I shall invoke the curse of Allah upon him — that there is no Ẓihār from a slave woman. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15257","(15251) And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah — informed us: Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Khamīrūyah — informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah — informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — informed us: Sufyān — from Ibn ʿAjlān — from ʿIkrimah — from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Ẓihār and divorce before ownership (i.e., before marriage) amount to nothing.\n\nAnd it has been reported in the Book of Ṭalāq from the Prophet ﷺ, then from ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them: \There is no divorce before marriage","\"" and Ẓihār carries the same meaning. [Ḥasan]"""
"15258","(15252) And it has been reported from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, to the contrary, with a mursal chain of narration.\n\nAbū Aḥmad al-Mihrānīyy — informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī — informed us: Ibn Bukayr — informed us: Mālik — from Saʿīd ibn ʿAmr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqī — that he asked al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad about a man who divorced a woman if he married her. He said: al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad said: A man declared his wife to be like the back of his mother if he married her, so ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, commanded him to marry her and not approach her until he expiated the expiation of the one who pronounces Ẓihār.\n\nThis is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). Al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad did not reach ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15259","(15253) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh — informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān — informed us: Abū al-Azhar — informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd — informed us: Isrāʾīl — from Manṣūr — from Mujāhid — from Ibn ʿAbbās — from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding a man who pronounced Ẓihār upon four women with a single word: \A single expiation (Kaffārah).\"" And similarly it was reported from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḥasan]"""
"15260","(15254) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinīyy — informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdīyy — informed us: al-Sājīyy — informed us: Ibn al-Muthannā — informed us: Abū Dāwūd — informed us: Shuʿbah — from Maṭar al-Warrāq and ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥakam — both of whom heard ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb — from Ibn al-Musayyib — that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said regarding a man who pronounced Ẓihār upon three women: \Upon him is a single expiation.\"" And ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"," al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī"," and Rabiʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said the same. Mālik said: \""That is the matter according to us.\"" And al-Shāfiʿī said it in the old opinion"," and in the new opinion he said: \""Upon him is an expiation for each one of them","\"" and that is the narration of Qatādah from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī. And al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah said the same. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15261","(15255) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī said: What I have preserved from what I heard regarding the verse {They return to what they said} [al-Mujādilah 58:3] is that the one who performs ẓihār declares his wife forbidden upon him by virtue of the ẓihār. Then, when a period of time elapses after the utterance of ẓihār, she is not rendered forbidden to him by a divorce through which she would become prohibited, nor by anything else that would provide him a means of exit from her being forbidden to him. Thus, the expiation (kaffārah) of ẓihār becomes obligatory upon him, as though they hold the view that when he refrains from that which he has declared forbidden upon himself—though it is in fact lawful—and then returns to what he said by way of contradiction, he has thereby made lawful what he had made forbidden. He said: And I know no meaning more appropriate for it than this.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: I know of no one who disagrees that the expiation of ẓihār is obligatory upon him, even if he does not repeat the ẓihār. It is not permissible to say, \I know of no one who disagrees that it is not the meaning of the verse.\"""""
"15262","(15256) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibnbishrān informed us in Baghdād, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us, Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated to me, Abū al-ʿĀliyah al-Riyāḥī said: Khawlah bint Dulayj was married to a man from the Anṣār who was ill-tempered, blind, and poor. During the Jāhiliyyah, when a man wished to separate from his wife, he would say to her: \You are to me like the back of my mother.\"" She quarreled with him over something"," and he said: \""You are to me like the back of my mother.\"" He had one or two children. When she heard him say what he said"," she took her children and set out running to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She found him at the house of ʿĀʾishah"," Mother of the Believers"," may Allah be pleased with her"," and ʿĀʾishah was washing one side of the head of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She stood before him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," my husband is poor"," blind"," and ill-tempered. I quarreled with him over something"," and he said: 'You are to me like the back of my mother","' but he did not intend divorce.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) raised his head and said: \""I do not know except that you have become forbidden to him.\"" He said: She became subdued and said: \""I complain to Allah of what has befallen me and my children.\"" He said: ʿĀʾishah turned to wash the other side of his head"," and she turned with her. She said the same thing. She said: \""I have from him one or two children.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) raised his head toward her and said: \""I do not know except that you have become forbidden to him.\"" She wept and said: \""I complain to Allah of what has befallen me and my children.\"" The face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) changed. ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""Move behind me","\"" so she moved back. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained as long as Allah willed"," then the revelation ceased. He said: \""O ʿĀʾishah"," where is the woman?\"" She said: \""Here she is.\"" He said: \""Call her.\"" So she called her. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Go and bring your husband.\"" He said: She set out running and did not delay before she came with him. She brought him before the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he was as she had described—blind"," poor"," and ill-tempered. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""I seek refuge in the All-Hearing"," the All-Knowing"," from the accursed Satan. In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful: {Indeed"," Allah has heard the statement of the woman who disputes with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah} [al-Mujādilah 58:1] to the end of the verse.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \""Can you free a slave?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Can you fast two consecutive months?\"" He said: \""By the One who sent you with the truth"," if I do not eat once"," twice"," or three times a day"," my eyesight will nearly fail.\"" He said: \""Can you feed sixty poor persons?\"" He said: \""No"," unless you assist me therein.\"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for him and he expiated his oath. This is a mursal narration"," but it have supporting evidences"," and Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"15263","(15257) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ from Sulaymān ibn Yasārah from Salamah ibn Ṣakhr al-Bayāḍī, who said: I was a man who had a great desire for women; I did not see any man who indulged in that as much as I did. When Ramaḍān entered, I performed ẓihār from my wife until Ramaḍān ended. One night, while she was conversing with me, something of her was exposed, so I leapt upon her and had intercourse with her. When morning came, I went to my people and informed them of my affair. I said to them: \Ask the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on my behalf.\"" They said: \""We would not do that"," lest a revelation from Allah descend concerning us"," or a statement be made by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that would leave a disgrace upon us. Rather"," we will hand you over for your crime. Go yourself and present your matter to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" So I set out until I came to him and informed him of the matter. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Is it you who did this?\"" I said: \""It is I who did this"," and here I am"," O Messenger of Allah"," patient for the decree of Allah upon me.\"" He said: \""Then free a slave.\"" I said: \""By the One who sent you with the truth"," I do not own anything except this neck of mine.\"" He said: \""Then fast two consecutive months.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," has not the affliction that befell me come except through fasting?\"" He said: \""Then give charity—feed sixty poor persons.\"" I said: \""By the One who sent you with the truth"," we spent this night without any supper.\"" He said: \""Then go to the custodian of the charity of Banī Zuraq and tell him to give it to you. Feed sixty poor persons and avail yourself of the remainder.\"" [Weak]"""
"15264","(15258) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Bahlūl narrated to us, Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ from Sulaymān ibn Yasārah from Salamah ibn Ṣakhr, from the Prophet (ﷺ), regarding the one who performs ẓihār and then has intercourse before expiating: \It is one expiation.\"" [Weak]"""
"15265","(15259) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī in Marw narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl al-Balkhī narrated to us, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar al-ʿAdanī narrated to us, al-Ḥakam ibn Abān narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) after having performed ẓihār from his wife and then had intercourse with her. He said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I performed ẓihār from my wife and then had intercourse with her before I expiated.\"" He said: \""What compelled you to do that"," may Allah have mercy on you?\"" He said: \""I saw her anklets in the moonlight.\"" He said: \""Then do not approach her until you do what Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has commanded.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15266","(15260) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd said: Al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥārith wrote to me, informing me that al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us from Maʿmar, from al-Ḥakam ibn Abān, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (ﷺ), with the meaning of this. And with its meaning, Saʿīd ibn Kulayb, the judge of ʿAdan, narrated from al-Ḥakam, connected (mawṣūlan)."
"15267","(15261) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṭālaqānī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn Abān, from ʿIkrimah, that a man performed ẓihār from his wife and then had intercourse with her before expiating. He came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and informed him. He said: \What compelled you to do what you did?\"" He said: \""I saw the whiteness of her shin in the moonlight.\"" He said: \""Then keep away from her until you expiate on your behalf.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been narrated before it.]"""
"15268","(15262) He said: Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Ismāʿīl narrated to us, al-Ḥakam ibn Abān narrated from ʿIkrimah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), similarly, without mentioning the shin. And likewise, Maʿmar ibn Sulaymān narrated it from al-Ḥakam, as a mursal narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been narrated before it.]"
"15269","(15263) And likewise it was narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿIkrimah, as a mursal narration. Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us, Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿIkrimah, who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \I performed ẓihār from my wife and had intercourse with her before I expiated.\"" He said: \""What compelled you to do that?\"" He said: \""The moon revealed her anklets to me"," so I had intercourse with her before I expiated.\"" He said: \""Refrain from her until you expiate.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been narrated before.]"""
"15270","(15264) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Hishām al-Warrāq al-Aḥmarī al-Kūfī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣīnī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Hāshim narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I performed ẓihār from my wife"," and I saw the whiteness of her anklets in the moon"," and it pleased me"," so I had intercourse with her.\"" He said: \""Has Allah not said: {Before they touch each other} [al-Mujādilah 58:3]?\"" He said: \""I have done so"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Then refrain from her until you expiate.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain.]"""
"15271","(15265) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us that ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashr narrated to us that Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us that Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: Whoever performs ẓihār against his wife and then divorces her before expiating, and then marries her thereafter, he shall not touch her until he expiates the expiation of ẓihār. [Weak]"
"15272","(15266) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik narrated from Hilāl ibn Usāmah from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from ʿUmar ibn al-Ḥakam that he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had a slave-girl who used to tend my sheep. I came to her and she had lost one of the sheep, so I asked her about it. She said: A wolf ate it. I became upset with her — and I am of the children of Ādam — so I struck her face. I have an obligation to free a slave. Shall I free her? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: Where is Allah? She said: In the heavens. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Then free her. ʿUmar ibn al-Ḥakam said: O Messenger of Allah, there were things we used to do in the Jāhiliyyah — we used to consult the soothsayers. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not go to the soothsayers. ʿUmar said: And we used to practice omens (ṭiyarah). He said: That is merely something one of you finds in his soul; let it not harm you.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The man's name is Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam. Thus narrated al-Zuhrī and Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Thus a group narrated it from Mālik ibn Anas (may Allah have mercy on him). [Authentic]"
"15273","(15267) Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated it from Mālik in a refined version, saying from Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam. At the end of it he said: He said: Free her, for she is a believer. Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī narrated it to us that Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾīnī narrated to us that Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik from Hilāl ibn Usāmah from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam, and he mentioned it. And Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated it from Hilāl ibn Abī Maymūnah from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam al-Sulamī regarding soothsayers and omens. And al-Zuhrī narrated it from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam regarding soothsayers and omens. [Authentic. It was mentioned before.]"
"15274","(15268) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Yaʿqūb al-Jawzajānī narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that al-Masʿūdī narrated from ʿAwn ibn ʿAbd Allāh from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah from Abū Hurayrah that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with a black slave-girl and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am obligated to free a believing slave. He said to her: Where is Allah? She pointed to the heavens with her finger. He said: Then who am I? She pointed to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and to the heavens, meaning: You are the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Free her, for she is a believer. [Authentic]"
"15275","(15269) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Zuhayr narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥārithī narrated to us that Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us that Abū Maʿdān al-Minqarī — meaning ʿĀmir ibn Masʿūd — narrated to us that ʿAwn ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with a black slave-girl and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am obligated to free a believing slave. Will this one suffice me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Who is your Lord? She said: Allah is my Lord. He said: What is your religion? She said: Islam. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you pray the five prayers and affirm what I have brought from Allah? She said: Yes. He (peace and blessings be upon him) struck her back and said: Free her. [Weak]"
"15276","(15270) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us that my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah al-Ḍabbī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — that is, ibn Muḥammad — narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from his father from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no deity but Allah. When they testify that there is no deity but Allah, and believe in me and in what I have brought, they have protected their blood from me, except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah. [Authentic. Bukhārī 2946]"
"15277","(15271) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Mālik ibn Anas informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd that a man from the Anṣār came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with his black slave-girl and said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, I am obligated to free a believing slave. Shall I free this one? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: Do you testify that there is no deity but Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you testify that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you believe in the resurrection after death? She said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then free her.\n\nThis is a mursal narration, and it has been narrated in connected form with part of its meaning. [Weak]"
"15278","(15272) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Ḥamzah ibn al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḍubaʿī narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr from Abū Salamah from al-Sharīd ibn Suwayd al-Thaqafī, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother bequeathed to me that I free a slave on her behalf, and I have a black Nubian slave-girl. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Bring her. He said: Who is your Lord? She said: Allah. He said: Who am I? She said: The Messenger of Allah. He said: Free her, for she is a believer. [Weak]"
"15279","(15273) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik informed us: It reached him that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar was asked about the obligatory slave to be freed, and it was said to him: May one purchase with a condition? He said: No. [Weak]"
"15280","(15274) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Sahl and al-Walīd both said: Abū Masʿūd informed us that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Maʿmar ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥanẓalah from Yūsuf ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām, who said: Khuwaylah bint Thaʿlabah, who was married to Aws ibn al-Ṣāmit, the brother of ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit, narrated to me. She said: He came to me and spoke to me about something in which he was irritated, and I responded to him. He became angry and said: You are to me like the back of my mother. Then he went out to the gathering of his people, then returned to me and tried to compel myself upon him, but I refused. He overpowered me, and I resisted him, and I overpowered him as a woman overpowers a weak man. She said: I said: By Him in whose hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you shall not reach me until Allah judges between me and you. I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and complained to him of what I had suffered. He said: Your husband is your cousin. Fear Allah and treat him well. She said: I had not yet left when Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {Allah has indeed heard the statement of the woman who disputes with you concerning her husband} (al-Mujādalah: 1) up to the expiation. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Tell him to free a slave. She said: By Allah, he does not possess a slave to free. He said: Then let him fast two consecutive months. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man; he has no strength for fasting. He said: Then let him feed sixty poor persons. I said: O Prophet of Allah, he has nothing with which to feed. He said: Indeed, we shall assist him with a ʿaraq. The ʿaraq is a basket containing thirty ṣāʿ of dates. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall assist him with another ʿaraq. He said: You have done well. Tell him to give charity. And Allah knows best. [Hasan through other chains]"
"15281","(15275) Al-Sharīf Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us, Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb ibn Shihāb said: The Sunnah regarding one who begins fasting the two months and then becomes wealthy is that he should complete them. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15282","(15276) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū al-Rabīʿ informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥarmalah narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār that Khuwaylah bint Thaʿlabah was married to Aws ibn al-Ṣāmit, and he performed ẓihār upon her. He suffered from a form of mental affliction. She came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \Indeed"," Aws has performed ẓihār upon me.\"" She mentioned his affliction and said: \""By the One who sent you with the truth"," I have only come out of mercy for him"," for he has rights over me.\"" Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed the Qurʾān concerning them both. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Tell him to free a slave.\"" She said: \""By the One who sent you with the truth"," he does not possess a slave"," nor can he afford one.\"" He said: \""Tell him to fast two consecutive months.\"" She said: \""By the One who sent you with the truth"," if you were to burden him with even three days"," he would not be able to bear it"," and it was the heat.\"" He said: \""Tell him to feed sixty poor persons.\"" She said: \""By the One who sent you with the truth"," he is not able to do that.\"" He said: \""Tell him to go to Fulān ibn Fulān"," for he has informed me that he possesses a ṣaʿ of dates given as charity. Let him take it as charity upon himself and then give it in charity to sixty poor persons.\""\n\nThis is a mursal narration"," and it serves as a corroborating witness for the connected narration before it. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15283","(15277) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Yazīd al-Riyāḥī informed us, Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān and Abū Salamah, that Salamah ibn Ṣakhr al-Bayāḍī declared his wife to be unto him as the back of his mother if he were to approach her until Ramadan had passed. When half of Ramadan had elapsed, the woman became plump and attractive, and she pleased him, so he approached her one night. He then came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. He said: \Free a slave.\"" He said: \""I do not have one.\"" He said: \""Fast two consecutive months.\"" He said: \""I am not able.\"" He said: \""Feed sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""I do not have the means.\"" He said: \""Then the Prophet (ﷺ) was brought a ʿaraq containing fifteen or sixteen ṣāʿ of dates.\"" He said: \""Give this in charity to sixty poor persons.\""\n\nLikewise"," Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī narrated it from Abū ʿĀmir. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15284","(15278) Shaybān al-Naḥwī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Salamah ibn Ṣakhr, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave him a miktal containing fifteen ṣāʿ and said: \Feed sixty poor persons with it"," and that shall be one mudd for each poor person.\""\n\nAbū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal informed us of it"," Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī informed us"," Mūsā ibn Hārūn informed us"," Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh informed us"," al-Walīd ibn Muslim informed us"," and Shaybān al-Naḥwī narrated it.\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15285","(15279) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Abān informed us, Yaḥyā narrated from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that he said: \The ʿaraq is a large basket that holds fifteen ṣāʿ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15286","(15280) It was narrated from al-Awzāʿī, from Yaḥyā, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah that Sulaymān ibn Ṣakhr al-Bayāḍī declared his wife to be unto him as the back of his mother until Ramadan had passed. He mentioned the hadith up to the point where he said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was brought a miktal containing fifteen ṣāʿ of dates"," and he gave it to him and said: 'Go and feed this to sixty poor persons.'\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us of it"," Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī informed us"," Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Shabīb informed us"," Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān al-Ḥarbī informed us"," al-Hiql ibn Ziyād narrated from al-Awzāʿī"," and he mentioned it. However"," this is an error"," for the well-known narration from Yaḥyā is mursal"," without the mention of Abū Hurayrah in it. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15287","(15281) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-ʿAdl informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed me, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Salamah ibn Ṣakhr al-Anṣārī, who said: \I was a man who had been given more intimacy with women than anyone else had been given. When Ramadan entered"," I performed ẓihār upon my wife"," fearing that I might approach her during some part of the night"," and I continued in that state"," unable to restrain myself until the morning overtook me. One night"," while she was beside me"," something of her became exposed"," and I leapt upon her. In the morning"," I went to my people and informed them of my affair. I said: 'Come with me to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' They said: 'No"," by Allah"," we will not go with you. We fear that something of the Qurʾān may be revealed concerning us"," or that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) may say something about us whose disgrace would remain upon us. Go yourself and do as you see fit.' So I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and informed him of my affair. He said: 'Is that you?' I said: 'I am he. Pass upon me the judgment of Allah"," for I am patient and seeking reward.' He said: 'Free a slave.' I struck the side of my own neck with my hand and said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth"," I do not possess other than this.' He said: 'Fast two consecutive months.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," has not that which afflicted me only occurred during fasting?' He said: 'Feed sixty poor persons.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," by the One who sent you with the truth"," we spent this night hungry"," finding no supper.' He said: 'Go to the custodian of the charity of Banī Zuraq"," and let him give you a wasq of dates. Feed sixty poor persons from it"," and use the remainder to support your family.' I came to my people and said: 'I have found with you hardship.'\""\n\nIt has been narrated from this chain from Sulaymān ibn Yasār in this manner. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15288","(15282) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed me through ijāzah that Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣabīḥ informed them, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shīrūyah informed us, Isḥāq al-Ḥanẓalī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs informed us, and Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated it with its chain similarly, and said at its end: \Go to the custodian of the charity of Banī Zuraq"," and let him give you a wasq of dates. Feed sixty poor persons with it"," and you and your family may eat the remainder.\"" This indicates that he gave from the wasq to sixty poor persons and then ate the remainder of the wasq. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15289","(15283) It is further corroborated by what Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Ibn al-Sarḥ informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Ibn Lahīʿah and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, with this report, that he said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was brought dates"," approximately fifteen ṣāʿ"," and he gave them to him and said: 'Give this in charity.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," upon one poorer than me and my family?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'You and your family may eat.'\"" This narration from Sulaymān is in agreement with the narration of Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Ibn Thawbān regarding the story of Salamah ibn Ṣakhr"," and it is more appropriate. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15290","(15284) As for the hadith of Aws ibn al-Ṣāmit, the narrations differ concerning it. It has been narrated as Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, Ibn Idrīs narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Maʿmar ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥanẓalah, from Yūsuf ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām, from Khuwaylah bint Mālik ibn Thaʿlabah, who said: \My husband"," Aws ibn al-Ṣāmit"," performed ẓihār upon me"," so I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to complain to him about him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) argued with me concerning him and said: 'Fear Allah"," for he is your husband and your cousin.' I did not cease until the Qurʾān was revealed: 'Indeed"," Allah has heard the statement of the one who disputes with you concerning her husband' (Qurʾān 58:1). He said: 'Let him free a slave.' She said: 'He does not have one.' He said: 'Then let him fast two consecutive months.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," he is an old man; he has no strength for fasting.' He said: 'Then let him feed sixty poor persons.' She said: 'He has nothing with which to give charity.' He said: 'Then I shall assist him with an ʿaraq of dates.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I shall assist him with another ʿaraq.' He said: 'You have done well. Go and feed with them sixty poor persons on his behalf"," and return to your cousin.'\"" He said: \""And the ʿaraq was sixty ṣāʿ.\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. It has been previously mentioned.]"""
"15291","(15285) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ibn Isḥāq through this chain of narration, similarly, except that he said: \And al-ʿaraq is a large basket containing thirty ṣāʿ.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: \""And this is more authentic than the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Ādam.\"" [Ḥasan due to corroborating narrations]"""
"15292","(15286) Abū ʿAlī informed us that Abū Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd said: \I read before Ibn Wazīr al-Miṣrī: 'Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us that al-Awzāʿī narrated to us that ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us from Aws"," the brother of ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit"," that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him fifteen ṣāʿ of barley as food for sixty poor persons.'\"" Abū Dāwūd said: \""ʿAṭāʾ did not meet Aws"," and Aws was among the people of Badr and died early. The ḥadīth is mursal.\"" [Ḥasan due to corroborating narrations]"""
"15293","(15287) Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī — informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Abū Ḥamzah al-Thumālī narrated to us from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he mentioned the story of the ẓihār of Aws, until he said: \Then came the verse: {So the freeing of a slave} [Al-Mujādilah:3].\"" Khuwaylah said: \""I said: 'And which slave do we have? By Allah"," there is no one who serves him other than me.'\"" He said: \""{And whoever does not find one"," then fasting for two consecutive months} [Al-Mujādilah:4].\"" She said: \""By Allah"," were it not that he eats and drinks three times a day"," his eyesight would be gone.\"" He said: \""{And whoever is not able"," then feeding sixty poor persons} [Al-Mujādilah:4].\"" She said: \""From where would we have food for another like it?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called for half a wasq"," which is thirty ṣāʿ"," and said: \""Let him feed sixty poor persons and let him return to you.\"" This is how Abū Ḥamzah al-Thumālī narrated it"," and he is weak. Al-Ḥakam ibn Abān narrated it from ʿIkrimah without mentioning Ibn ʿAbbās in it"," and he said at its end: \""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: 'Then feed sixty poor persons.' He said: 'I do not have it.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was brought something of dates — it is said fifteen ṣāʿ"," and it is said twenty ṣāʿ — and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: 'Take this and distribute it.' The man said: 'There is no one between its two sides [i.e."," within the city] poorer than me.' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Then you and your family eat it.'\"" [Weak. Previously mentioned under no. 15245]"""
"15294","(15288) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ghujdawānī in Bukhārā informed us that Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān and Muḥammad ibn Bikkār ibn al-Rayyān both said: \Ḥudayj ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Juʿfī"," the brother of Zuhayr"," narrated to us that Abū Isḥāq al-Hamdānī narrated to us.\""\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Ḥāmid ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Bikkār narrated to us that Ḥudayj narrated from Abū Isḥāq"," from Yazīd ibn Zayd"," from Khuwaylah"," that her husband called her while she was praying"," and she delayed in coming to him. So he said: \""You are to me like the back of my mother; if I were to lie with you…\"" She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and complained to him about that"," but nothing had yet reached the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding that matter. Then she came to him a second time"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Free a slave.\"" He said: \""I do not have that"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Fast for two consecutive months.\"" He said: \""I am not able to do that.\"" He said: \""Then feed sixty poor persons — thirty ṣāʿ.\"" He said: \""I do not possess that"," O Messenger of Allah"," unless you help me.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) helped him with fifteen ṣāʿ"," and the people helped him until it reached thirty ṣāʿ. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \""Feed sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," there is no one in greater need of it than me and my household.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \""Take it — you and your family.\"" So he took it. This is how Ḥudayj ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated it from Abū Isḥāq. Isrāʾīl narrated it from Abū Isḥāq"," but he did not say \""from Khuwaylah\"" and did not mention \""thirty ṣāʿ\"" in the ḥadīth. He said: \""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) helped him with fifteen ṣāʿ","\"" and did not add more. Then he mentioned his poverty and that he was commanded to eat it. We have narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) helped him with fifteen ṣāʿ of barley. And ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī said likewise. And Abū Yazīd al-Madanī said: \""A woman came with half a wasq of barley"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him two mudd of barley in place of one mudd of wheat.\"" These are differing narrations"," most of which are mursal. We have narrated in the Book of Fasting"," in the ḥadīth of the one who has intercourse [during Ramadan]"," from strong routes"," that which indicates what we have stated. [Ḥasan due to corroborating narrations]"""
"15295","(15289) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Rūḥ al-Dimashqī narrated to them that al-Qāsim ibn ʿUthmān al-Jūʿī narrated to us that Masrūq ibn Ṣadaqah narrated to us from al-Awzāʿī, from al-Zuhrī, that Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am ruined!\"" He said: \""Woe to you! What is that?\"" He said: \""I lay with my wife on a day in the month of Ramadan.\"" He said: \""Free a slave.\"" He said: \""I do not find one.\"" He said: \""Then fast for two consecutive months.\"" He said: \""I am not able.\"" He said: \""Then feed sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""I do not find [the means].\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was brought an ʿaraq containing fifteen ṣāʿ of dates. He said: \""Take it and give it in charity.\"" He said: \""To someone poorer than my family? By Allah"," there is no one between the two sides of Madīnah more in need than my family.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) laughed until his back teeth became visible. He said: \""Take it"," seek forgiveness from Allah"," and feed it to your family.\"" Likewise narrated by Ḍuḥaym from al-Walīd ibn Muslim from al-Awzāʿī"," and likewise narrated by al-Hiql ibn Ziyād from al-Awzāʿī. [Ḥasan due to corroborating narrations]"""
"15296","(15290) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us from al-Aʿmash, from Ṭalq ibn Ḥabīb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \I have lain with my wife during Ramadan.\"" He said: \""Free a slave.\"" He said: \""I do not find one.\"" He said: \""Fast for two consecutive months.\"" He said: \""I am not able.\"" He said: \""Then give charity to sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""I do not find [the means].\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was brought a miktal containing fifteen ṣāʿ of dates"," which is sixty rubʿ"," and he gave it to him and said: \""Feed sixty poor persons with this.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," there is no household between its two sides more in need than us.\"" He said to him: \""Go and feed it to your family.\"" In this mursal narration there is corroboration for the connected narration"," and this is preferable to the narration of ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī from Ibn al-Musayyab with doubt regarding \""fifteen or twenty.\"" Likewise"," it was narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿĀmir from Ibn al-Musayyab: \""fifteen\"" without doubt. And it will be narrated"," if Allah the Most High wills"," in the Book of Oaths"," the narrations from the Companions regarding the permissibility of giving charity of one mudd to each poor person. And Allah is the One who grants success. [Ḥasan due to corroborating narrations]"""
"15297","(15291) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, and al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā, ʿImrān ibn Mūsā, and Ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Warrāq informed us, all saying: \Bundār ibn Bashshār narrated to us that Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated to us that Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us that ʿIkrimah narrated to us from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both): Hilāl ibn Umayyah accused his wife of adultery with Sharīk ibn Saḥmāʾ. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: '[Bring] proof"," or there will be a ḥadd punishment on your back.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," if one of us sees a man with his wife"," should he seek proof?' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) kept saying: 'Proof"," or there will be a ḥadd punishment on your back.' Hilāl said: 'By Allah"," Who sent you with the truth"," I am indeed truthful"," and Allah will surely reveal regarding my affair that which will free my back from the ḥadd punishment.' Then Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came down"," and the verse was revealed: {And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves} [Al-Nūr:6]"," until He said: {And the fifth [testimony will be] that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is among the truthful} [Al-Nūr:9]. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) departed and sent for them both. They came"," and Hilāl ibn Umayyah stood and testified"," while the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Allah knows that one of you is a liar. Is there any one of you who will repent?' Then she stood and testified. When it came to the fifth [testimony] — {that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is among the truthful} — they said to her: 'Indeed"," it is decisive [i.e."," it brings about the punishment].' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'She hesitated"," and we thought she would retract. Then she said: \""I will not disgrace my people for the rest of the day.\"" So she proceeded [with the testimony].' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Observe her. If she gives birth to one with dark eyes"," wide buttocks"," and thick shins"," then it belongs to Sharīk ibn Saḥmāʾ.' She gave birth to such a child. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Were it not for what has already been revealed in the Book of Allah the Most High"," I would have had a matter with her.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 4747]"""
"15298","(15292) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us that ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that ʿIkrimah narrated to us from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: When this verse was revealed: {And those who accuse chaste women and then do not produce four witnesses} [Al-Nūr:4] to the end of the verse, Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah said: \Is it thus that it was revealed? If I were to find a man with my licentious wife"," I would not move him nor stir him until I bring four witnesses. By Allah"," I would not bring four witnesses until he has fulfilled his need.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""O company of the Anṣār! Do you not hear what your leader is saying?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," do not blame him"," for he is a jealous man. By Allah"," he has never married among us except a virgin"," and he has never divorced a woman of his such that any one of us would dare to marry her"," due to the intensity of his jealousy.\"" Saʿd said: \""By Allah"," I know"," O Messenger of Allah"," that it is the truth and that it is from Allah"," but I was astonished. While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in that state"," Hilāl ibn Umayyah al-Wāqifī came — and he was one of the three upon whom Allah accepted repentance. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I came last night at the time of ʿishāʾ from my garden in which I was"," and I saw a man with my wife. I saw with my own eyes and heard with my own ears.'\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked what he came with"," and it was said: \""Will Hilāl be flogged and his testimony be invalidated among the Muslims?\"" Hilāl said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," by Allah"," I see in your face that you dislike what I have come with"," and I hope that Allah will grant me a way out.\"" While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in that state"," revelation came down upon him. When revelation came down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," his cheeks and face would change color"," and his Companions would refrain from speaking"," and none of them would speak. When the revelation was lifted"," he said: \""Rejoice"," O Hilāl!\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Call her.\"" So she was called. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," knows that one of you is a liar. Is there any one of you who will repent?\"" Hilāl (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""By Allah"," O Messenger of Allah"," I have spoken nothing but the truth"," and I have been truthful.\"" She then said at that point: \""He has lied.\"" It was said to Hilāl: \""Testify four testimonies by Allah that you are among the truthful.\"" And it was said to him at the fifth: \""O Hilāl"," fear Allah"," for the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter"," and indeed this [fifth testimony] is the one that obligates the punishment upon you.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," Allah will never punish me"," just as He did not have me flogged for it.\"" So he testified the fifth [testimony]: \""That the curse of Allah be upon him if he is among the liars.\"" Then it was said: \""Testify four testimonies by Allah that he is among the liars.\"" And it was said to her at the fifth: \""O woman"," fear Allah"," for the punishment of Allah is more severe than the punishment of people"," and indeed this [fifth testimony] is the one that obligates the punishment upon you.\"" She remained silent for a while"," then said: \""By Allah"," I will not disgrace my people.\"" So she testified the fifth [testimony]: \""That the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is among the truthful.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed that she would not be accused"," nor would her child be accused. And whoever accused her or her child would receive the ḥadd punishment. And he would not be obligated to provide her with sustenance or lodging"," because they are separating without divorce or death. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Observe her. If she gives birth to one with thick shins"," wide buttocks"," dark-eyed"," with thick thighs"," then it belongs to Hilāl ibn Umayyah. And if she gives birth to one with thick shins"," wide buttocks"," brown-skinned"," with curly hair"," of handsome build"," then it belongs to her companion [i.e."," the one she was accused with].\"" She gave birth to one brown-skinned"," with curly hair"," of handsome build"," with thick shins and wide buttocks. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Were it not for the oaths"," there would have been a matter between me and her.\"" ʿAbbād said: \""I heard ʿIkrimah say: 'I saw him as the governor of one of the cities"," and it was not known who his father was.' And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15299","(15293) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us that ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr narrated to us from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \Hilāl ibn Umayyah came and mentioned the story of the liʿān in its entirety"," and at its end he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Were it not for the oaths"," there would have been a matter between me and her.'\"" Imām Aḥmad said: \""He named the liʿān an oath [yamīn].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"15300","(15294) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil ibn Khalaf al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us that Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī narrated to us that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: When Hilāl ibn Umayyah accused his wife, it was said to him: \By Allah"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) will surely have you flogged eighty lashes.\"" He said: \""Allah is more just than that — that He should strike me eighty lashes"," when He knows that I saw until I was certain and heard until I understood clearly. By Allah"," He will never strike me.\"" Then the verse of al-mulāʿanah was revealed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called them both when the verse was revealed and said: \""Allah knows that one of you is a liar. Is there any one of you who will repent?\"" Hilāl said: \""By Allah"," I am truthful.\"" He said to him: \""Swear by Allah"," besides whom there is no deity"," that I am truthful — say this four times. And if I am a liar"," then upon me be the curse of Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Stop him at the fifth"," for it is decisive.\"" So he swore. Then she said four times: \""By Allah"," besides whom there is no deity"," he is among the liars. And if he is truthful"," then upon her be the wrath of Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Stop her at the fifth"," for it is decisive.\"" She hesitated and was about to confess. Then she said: \""I will not disgrace my people.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""If she gives birth to one with dark eyes"," wide buttocks"," thick thighs"," and thick shins"," then it belongs to the one with whom she was accused. And if she gives birth to one who is yellow"," slender"," and smooth-haired"," then it belongs to Hilāl ibn Umayyah.\"" She gave birth to one with the characteristics of the adulterer. Ayyūb said — and Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn said: \""The man with whom he accused his wife was Sharīk ibn Saḥmāʾ"," and he was the brother of al-Barāʾ ibn Mālik"," the brother of Anas ibn Mālik through his mother. His mother was Sawdāʾ. And Sharīk used to stay at Hilāl's house and be present with him.\"" The Shaykh said: \""He named the word of liʿān an oath [ḥalf].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"15301","(15295) Abu al-'Adib 'Amr narrated to us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to me — Abu Ya'la and al-Hasan, who is Ibn Sufyan, both narrated to us — 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Asma' narrated to us — Juwayriyah narrated from Nafi' — from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, separated a man and a woman from the Ansar when the man accused his wife of adultery. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, made them both swear oaths, and then he separated them. Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Musa b. Isma'il from Juwayriyah.\n\nAnd it has been related to us from Yunus from al-Hasan al-Basri, who said: \Each couple may invoke the curse (li'an).\""\n\n[Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqq 'alayh)]"""
"15302","(15296) And in what Abu 'Abd Allah permitted me to narrate from him, from Abu al-'Abbas: al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: al-Shafi'i said: \They claimed that 'Amr b. Shu'ayb narrated from 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," from the Prophet"," peace be upon him"," that he said: 'Four types (of women) between whom and their husbands there is no li'an: the Christian woman under a Muslim"," the Jewish woman under a Muslim"," the free woman under a slave"," and the slave woman under a free man"," and the Christian woman under a Christian man.'\"" We said to them: \""You have related this from an unknown man and from a man who made an error"," and 'Amr b. Shu'ayb from 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr is munqati' (disconnected). The two who narrate it — one of them attributes it to the Prophet"," peace be upon him"," and the other stops it at 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr. Thus"," it is not established from 'Amr"," nor from 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr"," nor does it reach the Prophet"," peace be upon him"," except through a man who made an error.\"" He said: \""'Amr b. Shu'ayb has narrated to us from the Prophet"," peace be upon him"," rulings that agree with our positions and contradict your positions"," which trustworthy narrators transmit from him"," and he ascribes them to the Prophet"," peace be upon him. Yet you reject them from us and reject his narration and attribute it to error. If his hadith were established through those narrations of his with which we agree and you disagree — approximately thirty rulings from the Prophet"," peace be upon him"," most of which you have opposed — then you would be unjust if you cite his narration as proof while he is someone whose narration we do not establish"," and then you use from it that which"," even if it were established from him — and he is someone whose hadith is established — we would not establish it"," because it is munqati' between him and 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr.\""\n\n[Sahih]"""
"15303","(15297) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr b. al-Harith al-Faqih both informed us — they said: 'Ali b. 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us — Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Yazid al-Za'farani narrated to us — 'Ali b. Sa'id b. Qutaybah al-Ramli narrated to us — Damrah b. Rabi'ah narrated from Ibn Ata' — from his father — from 'Amr b. Shu'ayb — from his father — from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: \Four types of women between whom there is no li'an: the Christian woman under a Muslim"," the Jewish woman under a Muslim"," the slave woman under a free man"," and the free woman under a slave.\"" Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni"," the Hafiz"," said: \""This is 'Uthman b. Ata' al-Khurasani"," and he is extremely weak (da'if jiddan) in hadith.\"" Ibn Bazay' al-Ramli followed him in this from Ata' al-Khurasani"," and he is also weak.\n\n[Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15304","(15298) Abu Bakr b. al-Harith informed us — Abu Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us — Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. 'Ali b. Bahr narrated to us — Abu Musa narrated to us — Abu al-Walid narrated to us — Yazid b. Bazay' al-Ramli narrated from Ata' al-Khurasani — from 'Amr b. Shu'ayb — from his father — from his grandfather — from the Prophet, peace be upon him, something similar to it. The Shaykh said: \And Ata' al-Khurasani is also not strong (ghayr qawiyy).\""\n\n[Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15305","(15299) And Abu Bakr informed us: Ahmad b. Muhammad b. al-Harith al-Isbahani informed us — 'Ali b. 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu Salih 'Abd al-Rahman b. Sa'id b. Harun informed us — Muhammad b. al-Hajjaj b. Yazid, Abu al-Fadl, narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahim b. Sulayman narrated from 'Uthman b. 'Abd al-Rahman — from al-Zuhri — from 'Amr b. Shu'ayb — from his father — from his grandfather, 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: \Four types between whom there is no li'an: there is no li'an between a free man and a slave woman; there is no li'an between a free woman and a slave; there is no li'an between a Muslim and a Jewish woman; and there is no li'an between a Muslim and a Christian woman.\"" Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni"," the Hafiz"," said: \""'Uthman b. 'Abd al-Rahman is al-Waqqasi"," and he is matruk al-hadith (abandoned in hadith).\""\n\n[Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15306","(15300) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad b. Ya'qub narrated to us — al-'Abbas b. Muhammad al-Dawri said: I heard Yahya b. Ma'in saying: \Al-Waqqasi — his name is 'Uthman b. 'Abd al-Rahman — and he is weak (da'if).\""\n\n[Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15307","(15301) And Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr b. al-Harith al-Faqih both informed us — they said: 'Ali b. 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us — al-Ru'habi, al-Hasan b. Ahmad b. Sa'id, narrated to us — Muhammad b. Abi Farwah narrated to us — my father narrated to us — 'Ammar b. Matar narrated to us — Hammad b. 'Amr narrated from Zayd b. Rufay' — from 'Amr b. Shu'ayb — from his father — from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, sent 'Attab b. Usayd and mentioned something similar to it. 'Ali, may Allah have mercy on him, said: \Hammad b. 'Amr"," 'Ammar b. Matar"," and Zayd b. Rufay' are weak (du'afa').\"" And it has been related to us from Yahya b. Ma'in and from al-Bukhari regarding Hammad b. 'Amr.\n\n[Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15308","(15302) And al-Daraqutni said: It has been narrated from Ibn Jurayj and al-Awza'i — both of whom are imams — from 'Amr b. Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, as his own statement (mawquf), and they did not raise it to the Prophet, peace be upon him. Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr b. al-Harith both informed us — they said: 'Ali b. 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us — Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Muhammad al-Muqri' narrated to us — Ahmad b. al-'Abbas al-Tabari narrated to us — Isma'il b. Sa'id al-Kinani narrated to us — 'Umar b. Harun narrated from Ibn Jurayj and al-Awza'i — from 'Amr b. Shu'ayb — from his father — from his grandfather, who said: \Four types between whom and their husbands there is no li'an: the Jewish woman under a Muslim"," the Christian woman under a Muslim"," the free woman under a slave"," and the slave woman under a free man.\"" And thus did Yahya b. Abi Unaysah narrate it from 'Amr.\n\n[Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15309","(15303) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad 'Ubayd b. Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Mahdi al-Saydalani both informed us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad b. Ya'qub narrated to us — Yahya b. Abi Talib informed us — 'Abd al-Wahhab informed me — Yahya b. Abi Unaysah narrated from 'Amr b. Shu'ayb — from his father — from his grandfather, who said: 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say: \Four types of women between whom and their husbands there is no li'an: the Christian woman under a Muslim"," the slave woman under a slave"," the slave woman under a free man"," and the free woman under a slave.\"" The Shaykh said: \""In the establishment of this narration as mawquf (stopped) as well"," there is room for consideration. The first narrator is 'Umar b. Harun"," who is not strong"," and the second narrator is Yahya b. Abi Unaysah"," who is matruk (abandoned). As for what al-Shafi'i said — that it is munqati' (disconnected) — perhaps it was conveyed to al-Shafi'i as 'Amr b. Shu'ayb narrated from 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr"," and that is munqati' without any doubt. But whoever narrated it marfu' (elevated) or mawquf (stopped)"," he only narrated it from 'Amr"," from his father"," from his grandfather"," and that is mawsul (connected) according to the scholars of hadith. Some of them have named his grandfather in this"," saying 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr"," and the hearing of Shu'ayb b. Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah from his grandfather 'Abd Allah is sound. However"," the chain of narration to 'Amr must be sound"," and the chains of this hadith to 'Amr are not sound. And Allah knows best.\""\n\n[Da'if (Weak)]"""
"15310","(15304) And Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad b. 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us — al-Qasim b. 'Ali al-Jawhari narrated to us — Yahya b. 'Uthman b. Salih narrated to us — Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to me — Yahya b. Salih al-Ayli narrated from Isma'il b. Umayyah — from Ata' — from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: \O 'Attab b. Usayd"," I have sent you to the people of Makkah"," so forbid them from such and such.\"" And he mentioned the hadith"," and in it: \""Four types between whom there is no li'an: the Jewish woman under a Muslim"," the Christian woman under a Muslim"," a slave woman when her husband is a free man"," and a free man when his wife is a slave woman.\""\n\nAnd this hadith with this chain of narration is batil (false). Yahya b. Salih al-Ayli — his ahadith are not preserved (ghayr mahfuzah). And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best.\n\n[Batil (False)]"""
"15311","(15305) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Ibn Jurayj informed me that Ibn Shihāb, concerning the two who mutually invoke curses (al-mutaʿāliyan), narrated from the Ḥadīth of Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, one of Banū Sāʿidah, that a man from the Anṣār said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think if a man finds another man with his wife—what should he do with him?\"" Then the verse of mutual cursing (āyat al-liʿān) was revealed concerning him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Allah has decreed judgment concerning you and your wife.\"" He said: \""So they performed the mutual cursing in the mosque"," and I was a witness","\"" and he mentioned the rest of the Ḥadīth. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. And in the narration of Mālik"," Yūnus ibn Yazīd"," and Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān"," from Ibn Shihāb"," from Sahl"," in this Ḥadīth"," he said: \""So they performed the mutual cursing while I was among the people with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" And it is narrated from Ibn Wahb"," from Yūnus"," from Ibn Shihāb or another: \""That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the husband and the woman to swear after ʿAṣr near the pulpit.\"" This narration is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)"," and it has reached us in a connected form only through Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Wāqidī"," and he is weak (ḍaʿīf). [Ṣaḥīh — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"15312","(15306) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Mūsā ibn ʿĪsā al-Qāriʾ informed us that Qaʿnab ibn Muḥarrar Abū ʿAmr informed us that al-Wāqidī informed us that al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān informed us from ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas, who said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar say: \I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he conducted the mutual cursing between ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī and his wife"," upon the return of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Tabūk. He (ʿUwaymir) denied the pregnancy she was carrying in her womb"," saying: 'It is from Ibn al-Saḥmāʾ.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Bring your wife"," for the Qurʾān has been revealed concerning you both.' So the mutual cursing was performed between them after ʿAṣr near the pulpit"," concerning the pregnancy.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15313","(15307) Abū Bakr informed us that ʿAlī informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Khawwāṣ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Saʿd al-ʿAwfī informed us that al-Wāqidī narrated with this chain of narration something similar to it."
"15314","(15308) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that Mālik informed us from Hāshim ibn Hāshim ibn ʿUtbah ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Nisṭās, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Sulamī, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever swears a sinful oath upon this pulpit of mine"," let him take his seat in the Fire.\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"15315","(15309) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Nāfiʿ ibn Isḥāq al-Khuzāʿī in Makkah informed us that al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Muḥammad al-Janadī informed us that al-Zubayr ibn Abī Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us that Abū Ḍamrah informed us that Hāshim ibn Hāshim ibn Abī Waqqāṣ al-Zuhrī informed us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Nisṭās, who said: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \No man shall swear a sinful oath near this pulpit of mine except that he shall take his seat in the Fire"," even if it be concerning a green tooth-stick (siwāk).\"" [Ṣaḥīh — as previously mentioned]"""
"15316","(15310) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and others said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed us that Ibn Shihāb informed him that Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī informed him that ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī came to ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī al-Anṣārī and said to him: \O ʿĀṣim"," what do you think—if a man finds another man with his wife"," should he kill him"," and then you would kill him"," or what should he do? Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf about that.\"" So ʿĀṣim asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that"," but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the questions and found fault with them"," until what he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weighed heavily upon ʿĀṣim. When ʿĀṣim returned to his family"," ʿUwaymir came to him and said: \""O ʿĀṣim"," what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?\"" ʿĀṣim said to ʿUwaymir: \""You have not brought any good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the question you asked me about.\"" ʿUwaymir said: \""By Allah"," I will not cease until I ask him about it.\"" So ʿUwaymir went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was among the people and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think—if a man finds another man with his wife"," should he kill him"," and then you would kill him"," or what should he do?\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Allah has revealed concerning you and your companion (your wife). Go and bring her.\"" Sahl ibn Saʿd said: \""So they performed the mutual cursing in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and I was among the people. When they had finished"," ʿUwaymir said: 'I have lied against her"," O Messenger of Allah"," if I keep her.' So he divorced her with three pronouncements before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ could command him.\"" Ibn Shihāb said: \""That became the established practice (sunnah) for those who perform mutual cursing.\"" [Ṣaḥīh — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"15317","(15311) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr, and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, saying: I read to Mālik from Ibn Shihāb, and he mentioned the Ḥadīth in a similar manner. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf and Ibn Abī Uways, from Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā."
"15318","(15312) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us from Ibn Shihāb, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, who informed him, saying: \ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī came to ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī and said: 'O ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī"," ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf about a man who finds another man with his wife—if he kills him"," will he be killed in retaliation"," or what should he do?' So ʿĀṣim asked the Prophet ﷺ"," and the Prophet ﷺ found fault with the questions. ʿUwaymir met him and said: 'What did you do?' He said: 'I have not done anything good for you. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he found fault with the questions.' ʿUwaymir said: 'By Allah"," I will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him.' So he went to him and found that the Qurʾān had been revealed concerning them both. He called them both"," and they performed the mutual cursing. Then ʿUwaymir said: 'If I take her back"," it is as though I have lied against her.' So he separated from her before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ could command him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Observe her. If she gives birth to a child that is very black"," with large buttocks and prominent eyes"," then I think he has told the truth. And if she gives birth to a child that is reddish"," like a lizard (waḥrah)"," then I think he is a liar.' She gave birth to the child with the disliked characteristics.\"" Ibn Shihāb said: \""That became the established practice (sunnah) for those who perform mutual cursing.\"" [Ṣaḥīh — as previously mentioned]"""
"15319","(15313) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ informed us from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, that ʿUwaymir came to ʿĀṣim and said: \What is your opinion regarding a man who finds another man with his wife and kills him—would you kill him in retaliation? Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf"," O ʿĀṣim.\"" So he asked the Prophet ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the questions and found fault with them. ʿĀṣim returned to ʿUwaymir and informed him that the Prophet ﷺ had disliked the questions and found fault with them. ʿUwaymir said: \""By Allah"," I will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" So he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Qurʾān had been revealed contrary to what ʿĀṣim had reported. He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," who said: \""The Qurʾān has been revealed concerning you both. Come forward"," and they performed the mutual cursing.\"" Then he said: \""I have lied against her if I keep her.\"" So he separated from her"," and the Prophet ﷺ had not yet commanded him. Thus the practice (sunnah) for those who perform mutual cursing was established. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Observe her. If she gives birth to a child that is red"," short"," like a lizard (waḥrah)"," then I do not think he has lied against her. And if she gives birth to a child that is very black"," with large eyes and prominent buttocks"," then I do not think he has lied against her.\"" She gave birth to the child with the disliked characteristics. [Ṣaḥīh — as previously mentioned]"""
"15320","(15314) Abū Bakr, Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Zakariyyā said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, the brother of Banū Sāʿidah, that a man from the Anṣār came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think—if a man finds another man with his wife"," should he kill him"," and then you would kill him"," or what should he do?\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed concerning his affair what was mentioned in the Qurʾān regarding the matter of those who perform mutual cursing. The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Judgment has been decreed concerning you and your wife.\"" He said: \""So they performed the mutual cursing"," and I was a witness. Then he separated from her in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ"," and it became the established practice after them that separation be enacted between those who perform mutual cursing. She was pregnant"," and he denied her pregnancy. Her child was attributed to his mother.\"" [Ṣaḥīh — as previously mentioned]"""
"15321","(15315) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī said: In the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Dhiʾb there is evidence that Sahl ibn Saʿd said: \It was the established practice (sunnah) regarding the two who mutually invoke curses (al-mutaʿāliyan).\"" And in the ḥadīth of Mālik and Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd"," it is as though it were the statement of Ibn Shihāb. And this may not be a matter of contradiction; Ibn Shihāb would state it on one occasion without mentioning Sahl"," and on another occasion he would state it and mention Sahl. And Ibn Abī Dhiʾb agreed with Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd regarding what was added at the end of the ḥadīth beyond the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"15322","(15316) As for the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Dhiʾb: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Aḥmad al-Thaqafī narrated to me: ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Sadūsī narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, that ʿUwaymir came to ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī and mentioned the ḥadīth with the same meaning as the narration of ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"
"15323","(15317) As for the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah and ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad — and this is the ḥadīth of Aḥmad — both said: Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us from Ibn Shihāb regarding the two who mutually invoke curses (al-mutaʿāliyan) and the established practice (sunnah) concerning them, from the ḥadīth of Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, one of the Banī Sāʿidah: \A man from the Anṣār came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what do you say about a man who finds another man with his wife — should he kill him"," or what should he do?' So Allah revealed concerning his affair what was mentioned in the Qurʾān regarding the two who mutually invoke curses. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Allah has decreed concerning you and your wife.' He said: 'So we performed the mutual invocation of curses (liʿān) in the mosque while I was present. When they had finished"," he said: \""I have lied against her"," O Messenger of Allah"," if I keep her.\"" So he divorced her three times before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to do so when they had finished the mutual invocation of curses. He separated from her in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ"," and he said: \""That is the separation between every two who mutually invoke curses.\""' Ibn Jurayj said: Ibn Shihāb said: \""The established practice (sunnah) after them was that the two who mutually invoke curses are separated. She was pregnant"," and her son was attributed to his mother. Then the established practice (sunnah) was set regarding inheritance: that she inherits from him and he inherits from her what Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," decreed for them.\"" Ibn Jurayj said: Ibn Shihāb said"," from Sahl ibn Saʿd"," in this ḥadīth: \""The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If she gives birth to him red-haired"," short-statured"," and knock-kneed"," I do not think she has spoken the truth and he has lied against her. And if she gives birth to him black"," with large eyes"," with heavy buttocks"," I do not think he has lied against her.' So she gave birth to him with the characteristics that indicated his truthfulness.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"," both from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. And a group other than them narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," among them al-Awzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15324","(15318) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Fāryābī narrated to us: al-Awzāʿī narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Sahl ibn Saʿd: \ʿUwaymir came to ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī"," and he was the chief of the Banī al-ʿAjlān. He said: 'What do you say about a man who finds another man with his wife — should he kill him so that you kill him"," or what should he do? Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that for me.' He said: So ʿĀṣim came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," a man finds another man with his wife — should he kill him so that you kill him"," or what should he do?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the question. ʿUwaymir asked him"," and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the question and condemned it.' ʿUwaymir said: 'By Allah"," I will not cease until I ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that.' He said: So ʿUwaymir came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," a man finds another man with his wife — should he kill him so that you kill him"," or what should he do?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah has revealed the Qurʾān concerning you and your wife.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them with the mutual invocation of curses (liʿān) as Allah had named it in His Book. He said: So he invoked the curse upon her"," then he said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," if I keep her"," I have wronged her.' So he divorced her"," and that became the established practice (sunnah) for those who came after them among those who mutually invoke curses. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Look — if she gives birth to him black"," with dark eyes"," with heavy buttocks"," and thick calves"," I do not think ʿUwaymir has lied against her. And if she gives birth to him reddish"," like a lizard (waḥrah)"," I do not think ʿUwaymir has spoken the truth against her.' He said: So she gave birth to him with the description that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had given indicating ʿUwaymir's truthfulness. He said: So after that"," the child was attributed to his mother.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq"," from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf.\n\nAnd al-Awzāʿī narrated from al-Zubaydī"," from al-Zuhrī"," from Sahl ibn Saʿd"," and he mentioned in it: \""So they performed the mutual invocation of curses"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated between them and said: 'They shall never be reunited.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15325","(15319) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Ḥassān — from the original of his book — and he is Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ḥassān, narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: al-Walīd — he is Ibn Muslim — and ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid both said: al-Awzāʿī narrated from al-Zubaydī, from al-Zuhrī, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, and he mentioned it, but did not mention in it the story of the divorce."
"15326","(15320) And among them is Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī. Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Tājir informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb: Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Anṣārī informed me: \ʿUwaymir al-Anṣārī"," from the Banī al-ʿAjlān"," came to ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī and mentioned the ḥadīth with the same meaning as the ḥadīth of Mālik"," except that he said: 'When they finished their mutual invocation of curses"," he said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have lied against her if I keep her.\"" So he divorced her three times before the Prophet ﷺ commanded him. His separation from her afterwards became the established practice (sunnah) for those who mutually invoke curses.' Sahl said: 'She was pregnant"," and her son was attributed to his mother. Then the established practice (sunnah) was set that he inherits from her and she inherits from him what Allah decreed for her.'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"15327","(15321) And among them is Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh Abū ʿAmr al-Basṭāmī informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū Muḥammad Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥammādī, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān al-Nasawī, Abū Yaʿlā al-Mawṣilī, Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed me, and Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us, and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Salām al-Sulamī al-Baṣrī informed me. They all said: Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us: Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Sahl ibn Saʿd: \A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what do you say about a man who finds another man with his wife — should he kill him so that you kill him"," or what should he do?' So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed concerning them what was mentioned in the Qurʾān regarding the two who mutually invoke curses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah has decreed concerning you and your wife.' He said: 'So we performed the mutual invocation of curses while I was present before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'If I keep her"," I have lied against her.' So he separated from her"," and the established practice (sunnah) between them was that the two who mutually invoke curses are separated. She was pregnant"," and he denied her pregnancy. Her son was attributed to her. Then the established practice (sunnah) was set regarding inheritance: that he inherits from her and she inherits from him what Allah decreed for her.\"" Abū Yaʿlā said: \""He said: 'It has been decreed concerning you.'\"" He and al-Ḥasan said: \""He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," if I keep her…'\"" And their ḥadīth is otherwise the same. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"15328","(15322) And among them is ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Fihrī. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Sarḥ narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated from ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Fihrī and others, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, in this report. He said: \So he divorced her three divorces in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enforced it"," and what was done in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became the established practice (sunnah).\"" Sahl said: \""And I was present before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then the established practice (sunnah) was set after that for those who mutually invoke curses: that they are separated and never reunited.\"""""
"15329","(15323) And among them is Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, except that he did not narrate it with the precision of those [narrators], and he added in it: \So he separated between them.\"" Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī"," who heard Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Saʿdī say: \""I witnessed the two who mutually invoke curses during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he separated between them. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I have lied against her if I keep her.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī"," from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"15330","(15324) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us. He said: Abū Dāwūd said: \No one followed Ibn ʿUyaynah in [the narration] that he separated between the two who mutually invoke curses.\"" The Shaykh said: He meant by that in the ḥadīth of al-Zuhrī from Sahl ibn Saʿd"," except what we have narrated from al-Zubaydī from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"15331","As for the hadith of Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him): Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān informed us from Ayyūb from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) separated between the two brothers of Banī ʿAjlan.\""\n\nAnd he said"," gesturing with his index finger and his middle finger"," joining the middle finger with the one next to it"," meaning the index finger"," and said: \""Indeed"," Allah knows that one of you is a lie. Is there either of you who will repent?\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Sufyān.\n\n(T) And with the same meaning"," Ḥammād ibn Zayd and Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated it from Ayyūb"," and ʿAzrah narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) separated between the two who performed liʿān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15332","Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār.\n\n(H) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, saying: I heard Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah say: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed us from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the two who performed liʿān: \Your account is upon Allah; one of you is a liar. You have no claim over her.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what about my wealth?\"" He said: \""You have no wealth. If you spoke truthfully about her"," then it is in exchange for what you made lawful of her private parts. And if you lied about her"," then that is even further from her for you\"" — or \""from him.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and a group"," all of them from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15333","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār informed us, Muʿādh ibn Hishām informed us, my father informed me from Qatādah from ʿAzrah from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: \Al-Muṣʿab did not separate between the two who performed liʿān.\"" Saʿīd said: \""This was mentioned to Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did separate between the two who performed liʿān.'\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as mentioned before]"""
"15334","Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us orally, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sharqī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed us from Mālik ibn Anas from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man performed liʿān with his wife and disowned her child. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) separated between them and attributed the child to the woman. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Mālik.\n\n(Sh) Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: His divorce of three may be interpreted — meaning in the hadith of Sahl — as referring to what he found within himself, knowing his own truthfulness and her falsehood, and her audacity in defying the prohibition, so he divorced her three times, being unaware that liʿān itself constitutes a separation. Thus it is like one upon whom a divorce is pronounced without his having issued it, or like one who stipulates a condition in a sale or a guarantee in a salam contract, when it is binding upon him whether he stipulates it or not.\n\nHe (al-Shāfiʿī) said: And Ibn ʿUmar added from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he separated between the two who performed liʿān. The separation by the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is not the same as the husband's separation; rather it is a separation by judicial ruling.\n\n(T) The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And we have narrated in the hadith of ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) in the story of Hilāl ibn Umayyah, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed that she should not be accused, nor should her child be accused. And whoever accuses her or her child shall be flogged the ḥadd punishment. And he shall have no obligation to provide her with maintenance or lodging, because they are separated without divorce and without the husband's death. This narration confirms what al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"15335","Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥām al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān informed us from Ibn Shihāb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab or Abū Salamah — the doubt being from Sufyān — from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The child belongs to the bed"," and the adulterer gets the stone.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15336","And Abū Zakariyyā informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd from his father, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) sent for an elderly man from Banī Zuhrah who lived in our house. I went with him to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he asked about a child born in the Jāhiliyyah. He said: \As for the bed"," it belongs to so-and-so"," and as for the semen"," it belongs to so-and-so.\"" ʿUmar said: \""You have spoken the truth"," but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged according to the bed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15337","Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Mahdī ibn Maymūn Abū Yaḥyā informed us.\n\n(H) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ informed us, Mahdī ibn Maymūn informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Yaʿqūb informed us from al-Ḥasan ibn Saʿd from Rabbāḥ, who said: \My family married me to a Roman slave-girl of theirs. I had intercourse with her and she bore me a black boy like myself"," so I named him ʿAbd Allāh. Then I had intercourse with her again and she bore me a black boy like myself"," so I named him ʿUbayd Allāh. Then a slave-boy of my family"," called Yuḥannis"," became intimate with her and spoke to her in his language"," and she bore a boy that looked like a lizard. I said to her: 'What is this?' She said: 'It is the son of Yuḥannis.' The matter was raised to the Commander of the Faithful"," ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" He said — I think he said — \""He asked her and she confessed.\"" ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Are you both content that I judge between you according to the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged that the child belongs to the bed.\"" Mahdī said — and I think he said — \""He flogged her and flogged him"," and they were both slaves.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of al-Muqrī. In the narration of al-Rūdhbārī"," it is \""Yuḥannah.\"" He said — I think Mahdī said — \""He asked them and they both confessed.\"" And at the end he said: \""He flogged her and flogged him\"" — and I think he said — \""and they were both slaves.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15338","And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim and Mahdī ibn Maymūn informed us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Yaʿqūb from Rabbāḥ, and he mentioned it with the same meaning. And at the end he said: \Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged that the child belongs to the bed"," and the adulterer gets the stone. He is your son; he inherits from you and you inherit from him.\"" I said: \""Glory be to Allah!\"" He said: \""That is how it is.\"" So I would place him between these two — these two are black and this one is white. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15339","Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad informed us from Yazīd ibn al-Hād from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūnus, who heard al-Maqburī narrating to al-Qurazī. Al-Maqburī said: Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say when the āyah of liʿān was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Any woman who brings to a people one who is not from them"," she has nothing to do with Allah"," and Allah will not admit her into His Paradise. And any man who denies his child while looking at him"," Allah will veil Himself from him and expose him before the eyes of all creation"," the first and the last.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15340","And Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Baghdādī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me from Ibn al-Hād from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūnus from Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say — and he mentioned it with the same meaning, as a marfūʿ narration.\n\nʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūnus said: Then Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb al-Qurazī said, while Saʿīd al-Maqburī was narrating this hadith, he said: \This has reached me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"""""
"15341","(15335) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, Abū Maʿmar al-Naḍrawī, narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah from Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmur from Abī al-Aswad al-Duʾilī from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever claims lineage to other than his father"," knowing that he is not his father"," has indeed committed disbelief. And whoever claims what does not belong to him is not of us"," and let him take his seat in the Fire. And whoever accuses a man of disbelief or calls him the enemy of Allah"," when he is not so"," it shall rebound upon the accuser if he is not as described.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Maʿmar"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from ʿAbd al-Wārith. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15342","(15336) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥammāmī al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAlī al-Khuṭabī informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Khālid narrated to us that Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ narrated to us from Abū ʿUthmān from Saʿd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever claims lineage to other than his father"," knowing that he is not his father"," Paradise is forbidden for him.\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: I mentioned that to Abū Bakrah"," and he said: \""My ears heard it and my heart retained it.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15343","(15337) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Muʾammal ibn Ḥasan ibn ʪsā narrated to us that al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn Musayyib al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us that Hushaym narrated to us from Khālid from Abū ʿUthmān who said: \When Muʿāwiyah claimed Ziyād (as his son)"," I met Abū Bakrah and said: 'What is this that you have done? Indeed"," I heard Saʿd saying: \""My ears heard it and my heart retained it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," who said: 'Whoever claims a father in Islam"," knowing that he is not his father"," Paradise is forbidden for him.'\""\n\nAbū Bakrah said: \""And I heard it from him.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr al-Nāqid from Hushaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15344","(15338) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Sufyān narrated to us from Ibn Shihāb from Sahl ibn Saʿd who said: \I witnessed the two who performed the mutual imprecation (al-mutaʿāniʿayn) before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while I was fifteen years of age","\"" then he proceeded with the hadith. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15345","(15339) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us by dictation that Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us that al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us that Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār who said: I heard Saʿīd ibn Jubayr say: I heard Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say to the two who performed the mutual imprecation: \Your account is upon Allah; one of you is a liar. You (the husband) have no claim over her.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," my wealth! My wealth!\"" He said: \""There is no wealth for you. If you have spoken truthfully"," it is in exchange for what you have made lawful of her private parts"," and if you have lied against her"," it is even further removed from you in that regard.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ as it has preceded. And the story of the two who performed the mutual imprecation has also been narrated by ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās"," and Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with them all)"," and in that is evidence that they witnessed the mutual imprecation along with others. And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15346","(15340) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that al-Firyābī narrated to us that al-Awzāʿī narrated to us that al-Zuhrī narrated to us from Sahl ibn Saʿd in the story of ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Allah has revealed the Qurʾān concerning you and your wife.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them to perform the mutual imprecation (liʿān) as Allah"," the Most High"," named it in His Book. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq from al-Firyābī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15347","(15341) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Maʿqil narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to me that Muqaddam ibn Muḥammad narrated to me that my uncle al-Qāsim ibn Yaḥyā narrated to me from ʿUbayd Allāh — and he had heard from him — from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man accused his wife and disavowed her child during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them, so they performed the mutual imprecation (liʿān) as Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, had said. Then he judged that the child belong to the woman, and he separated the two who had performed the mutual imprecation. Al-Bukhārī narrated it thus. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"15348","(15342) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr who said: \I was asked about the two who performed the mutual imprecation during the time of Muṣʿab ibn al-Zubayr — whether they should be separated — and I did not know what to say. So I rose and went to the house of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and sought permission to enter. It was said: 'He is sleeping.' But he heard my voice and said: 'Ibn Jubayr — give him permission.' So I entered upon him and he said: 'What brings you at this hour except some need?' He was lying on the saddle-cloth of his mount"," resting his head on a pillow stuffed with palm fibre — he meant the fibre of the palm-tree. I said: 'O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," should the two who performed the mutual imprecation be separated?' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! Yes. Indeed"," the first one to ask about this was so-and-so"," son of so-and-so. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think if one of us sees a man with his wife — what should he do? If he speaks"," he speaks of a grave matter"," and if he remains silent"," he remains silent upon the like of that.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not answer him. Then after that"," he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," that which I asked you about — I have been afflicted with it.\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed the verses in Sūrat al-Nūr: \""And those who accuse their wives...\"" (al-Nūr: 6) to the end of the verses. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called the man and recited them to him"," admonished him"," and informed him that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. He said: \""By the One Who sent you with the truth"," I have not lied against her.\"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called the woman and recited them to her"," admonished her"," reminded her"," and informed her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. She said: 'No"," by the One Who sent you with the truth"," he has not spoken the truth — he has lied.' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) began with the man"," and he testified four testimonies by Allah that he was among the truthful"," and in the fifth: 'That the curse of Allah be upon him if he is among the liars.' Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned to the woman"," and she testified four testimonies by Allah that he was among the liars"," and in the fifth: 'That the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is among the truthful.' Then he separated the two of them.'\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15349","(15343) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī said: \I only commanded that they be stopped and reminded because Sufyān informed us from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb from his father from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded a man who was overseeing the mutual imprecation between the two who performed it to place his hand over the man's mouth at the fifth testimony and say: 'Indeed"," it is the one that necessitates (punishment).'\"" And Allah"," Glorified and Most High"," knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15350","(15344) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to me that Abū Yaʿlā Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muthannā al-Mawṣilī narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us that Fulayḥ narrated to us from al-Zuhrī from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think of a man who sees a man with his wife — should he kill him so that you kill him"," or what should he do?\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed what was mentioned in the Qurʾān regarding the mutual imprecation (liʿān). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \""It has been decreed concerning you and your wife.\"" He said: \""So they performed the mutual imprecation while I was a witness before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," if I keep her"," I have lied against her.\"" So he separated her from him"," and it became a Sunnah thereafter that the two who performed the mutual imprecation be separated. She was pregnant"," and he denied her pregnancy. Her child was attributed to her. Then the Sunnah came into effect regarding inheritance: that the child inherits from her and she inherits from him what Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has ordained for them. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ. And we have narrated his statement \""and she was pregnant\"" in the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj and Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī from al-Zuhrī in the story of ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15351","(15345) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Jarīr narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Jarīr informed.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me, and the wording is his: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Jarīr narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbdillāh, who said:\n\nWe were in the mosque on Friday night when a man from the Anṣār entered and said: \If a man finds another man with his wife"," and he speaks"," you will flog him; and if he kills"," you will kill him; and if he remains silent"," he remains silent out of rage. By Allah"," I will certainly ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it.\"" When the next day came"," he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him"," saying: \""If a man finds another man with his wife"," and he speaks"," you will flog him; or if he kills"," you will kill him; or if he remains silent"," he remains silent out of rage.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""O Allah"," make it clear","\"" and he began to supplicate. Then the verses of al-Liʿān were revealed: {And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves} [Sūrah al-Nūr"," 6–9]. The man was tested with this among the people. He and his wife came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and they performed the mutual imprecation (liʿān). The man testified four times by Allah that he was among the truthful"," and on the fifth occasion he invoked the curse of Allah upon himself if he was among the liars. Then the woman went to invoke the curse"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Stop.\"" She then performed the liʿān. When they departed"," he said: \""Perhaps she will bring forth a black child with curly hair.\"" And she brought forth a black child with curly hair.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm"," Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," and ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1495]"""
"15352","(15346) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAmr — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us; ʿAbadah narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbdillāh, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ performed the liʿān on the basis of pregnancy. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15353","(15347) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī al-Wazīr al-Tājir — informed me; Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Rāzī narrated to us; al-Anṣārī narrated to me; Hishāb ibn Ḥassān narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Faḍl informed us, and the wording is his; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated. He said: Hishām ibn Ḥassān was asked about a man who accuses his wife. Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us from Muḥammad, who said: I asked Anas ibn Mālik about that, and I believed he had knowledge of it. He said: Hilāl ibn Umayyah accused his wife with Sharīk ibn Saḥmāʾ, and he was the brother of al-Barāʾ ibn Mālik through his mother, and he was the first person to perform the liʿān. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the liʿān between them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Observe her. If she brings forth a white"," lank-haired"," large-eyed child"," then he belongs to Hilāl ibn Umayyah. And if she brings forth a black"," curly-haired"," thin-shanked child"," then he belongs to Sharīk ibn Saḥmāʾ.\"" He said: I was informed that she brought forth a black"," curly-haired"," thin-shanked child.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā.\n\n(T) And we have narrated it in the ḥadīth of Hishām ibn Ḥassān from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās"," more complete than that"," and in it the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Were it not for what has already passed from the Book of Allah"," I would have had a matter concerning her.\""\n\n(Q) And in all of that there is an indication that he performed the liʿān between them on the basis of the pregnancy. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15354","(15348) As for the ḥadīth, Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿAbbās al-Asfaṭī and Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh — in Baghdād narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated. They both said: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim narrated, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said:\n\nThe two who performed the liʿān were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī said something about it. He departed, and a man from his people came to him and mentioned that he had found another man with his wife. ʿĀṣim said: \I have not been tested with this except because of my statement.\"" He brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what he had found his wife to be upon. That man was yellowish"," lean"," with lank hair"," and the one who claimed he had found him with his family was brown-skinned"," fleshy"," with tightly curled"," jet-black hair. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Allah"," make it clear.\"" She gave birth to a child resembling the one her husband claimed he had found with her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the liʿān between them. A man in the assembly said to Ibn ʿAbbās: \""Is this the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence"," I would stone this one'?\"" Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," said: \""No"," that was a woman who used to manifest evil in Islam.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim narrated it from Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf from Ibn Abī Uways.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: This narration creates the illusion that he performed the liʿān between them after the delivery. It is also possible that some of its narrators placed the account of the delivery before the account of the liʿān in the narration. This is the story of ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī. We have narrated from al-Zuhrī from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī in the story of ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī that the Prophet ﷺ performed the liʿān between him and his wife while she was pregnant. And Ibn Jurayj narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿid this story"," placing the narration of the liʿān before the account of the delivery"," similar to the narration of the group"," except that he omitted ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim from its chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15355","(15349) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Sālim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to him, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," by Allah"," I have not been intimate with my family since the pollination of the palm trees.\"" He said: \""And their pollination is that when they are pollinated"," they are left for forty days without being watered after the pollination.\"" He said: \""I found another man with my wife.\"" He said: \""Her husband was yellowish"," thin-shanked"," with lank hair"," and the one she was accused with was brownish-black"," with tightly curled"," jet-black hair.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Allah"," make it clear.\"" Then he performed the liʿān between them"," and she brought forth a child resembling the man she was accused with.\n\nAbū al-Zinād narrated it from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform the liʿān between al-ʿAjlānī and his wife while she was pregnant"," and the one she was accused with was Ibn al-Saḥmāʾ.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"15356","(15350) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed me by way of ijāzah that Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdillāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Sammīdhī informed him, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah; Bindār narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us; al-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform the liʿān between al-ʿAjlānī and his wife while she was pregnant. Her husband said: \By Allah"," I have not been intimate with her since we pollinated.\"" He said: \""And al-ʿAfr is that the palm tree is watered after being left unwatered for two months after pollination.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Allah"," make it clear.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned the woman's husband — he was thin-armed and thin-shanked"," with reddish-brown hair — and the one she was accused with was Ibn al-Saḥmāʾ. She brought forth a black child"," with dark eyes"," curly hair"," thick arms"," and fleshy shins.\n\nAl-Qāsim said: Ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād said to Ibn ʿAbbās: \""Is this the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence"," I would stone her'?\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""No"," that was a woman who manifested evil in Islam.\""\n\nIbn Abī al-Zinād narrated it from his father with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the liʿān between al-ʿAjlānī and his wife while she was pregnant"," and her husband said: \""By Allah"," I have not been intimate with her since we pollinated the palm trees","\"" and he mentioned the explanation of al-ʿAfr. He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah"," make it clear.'\"" And they claimed that the woman's husband was thin-armed"," and he described him similarly"," except that he said \""prominent-eyed\"" instead of \""dark-eyed","\"" and he added \""jet-black.\"" Muḥammad ibn Khuzaymah said: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Ibn Abī al-Zinād informed me from his father; al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad narrated to me"," from ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"15357","(15351) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me; Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf narrated, from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān, regarding His statement: {And those who accuse the chaste women, then do not bring four witnesses, flog them eighty lashes} [Sūrah al-Nūr, 4], he said:\n\nʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī stood and mentioned the story of his question regarding a man who sees another man upon his wife's belly committing zinā with her, and the revelation of the verses of al-Liʿān, and that Hilāl ibn Umayyah — his cousin — accused his wife with his cousin Sharīk ibn Saḥmāʾ, and she was pregnant. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for the lover, the woman, and the husband, and they gathered before him. The Prophet ﷺ said to her husband Hilāl: \Woe to you! What do you say about your cousin's daughter"," your cousin"," and your close friend"," that you accuse her with a false charge?\"" The husband said: \""I swear by Allah"," O Messenger of Allah"," I saw him with her upon her belly"," and she is pregnant from him"," and I have not been intimate with her for four months.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said to the woman: \""Woe to you! What does your husband say?\"" She said: \""I swear by Allah"," he is a liar"," and he has not seen anything from me that would arouse suspicion.\"" And he mentioned a lengthy statement of denial. The Prophet ﷺ said to the lover: \""Woe to you! What does your cousin say?\"" He said: \""I swear by Allah"," he has not seen what he says"," and he is among the liars.\"" And he mentioned a lengthy statement of denial. He said: The Prophet ﷺ said to the woman and the husband: \""Stand and swear by Allah.\"" They stood near the minbar after the ʿAṣr prayer. Her husband Hilāl ibn Umayyah swore and said: \""I bear witness by Allah that I am among the truthful.\"" He mentioned his liʿān and the description of her liʿān. And he mentioned in the husband's liʿān that she is pregnant from other than me"," and that I am among the truthful. Then he did not mention that he made Sharīk swear. He only mentioned the statement of the Prophet ﷺ: \""When she gives birth"," bring him to me.\"" She gave birth to a black child"," curly-haired"," as if he were from the Ḥabashah. When he looked and saw his resemblance to Sharīk — and he was the son of a Ḥabashī woman — he said: \""Were it not for the oaths that have already passed"," I would have had a matter concerning her","\"" meaning stoning.\n\n(Q) The statement of al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," that the Prophet ﷺ asked Sharīk and he denied"," but he did not make him swear — it is possible that he took it from the people of tafsīr"," for it was heard from him"," and I have not found it in the connected narrations. What al-Shāfiʿī said in the book Aḥkām al-Qurʾān — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not summon the one accused with the woman — he said it only in the story of ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī. The one accused with the woman was not named in the story of al-ʿAjlānī in the narrations we have"," except that the statement of the Prophet ﷺ \""If she brings forth such and such\"" in that story also indicates that he accused her with a specific man. It is not narrated in it that he summoned him. Al-Shāfiʿī said in al-Imlāʾ: \""I think the man al-ʿAjlānī accused his wife with his cousin"," and his cousin was Sharīk ibn al-Saḥmāʾ.\"" Then he continued the speech until he said: \""And al-ʿAjlānī performed the liʿān"," and the Prophet ﷺ did not punish Sharīk with the liʿān.\"" What is in the narrations we have is that the one who accused his wife with Sharīk ibn Saḥmāʾ was Hilāl ibn Umayyah al-Wāqifī"," from Banī al-Wāqif. And I do not know anyone who named"," in the story of ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī"," that he accused his wife with Sharīk ibn Saḥmāʾ"," except from the direction of Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Wāqidī with a chain he mentioned"," which we have mentioned previously. And it is also in the narration of Abū al-Zinād from al-Qāsim from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," as it preceded in the well-known narrations. It was only named in the story of Hilāl ibn Umayyah. It is likely that the two stories are one"," and the narrators differed regarding the name of the accuser. Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," in one of the two narrations"," and Anas ibn Mālik"," may Allah be pleased with him"," name him Hilāl ibn Umayyah"," and Sahl ibn Saʿd names him ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī. And Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," in the narration of Ibn Abī al-Zinād from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from him"," says: \""He performed the liʿān between al-ʿAjlānī and his wife.\"" And Ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," says: \""He separated between the two brothers of Banī al-ʿAjlān.\"" And Ibn Masʿūd"," may Allah be pleased with him"," says: \""A man from the Anṣār.\"" So his statement in al-Imlāʾ departs from some of what has been narrated of the difference regarding the name of the man. Or it is possible that they are two separate stories"," and when ʿĀṣim asked about it"," he asked only on behalf of ʿUwaymir al-ʿAjlānī"," and Hilāl ibn Umayyah was also tested with it. The verse was revealed"," and when each of them came"," he performed the liʿān between him and his wife"," and the revelation of the verse was attributed to him. According to this"," what occurred in al-Imlāʾ is likely to be a scribal error or a following of what was narrated in the ḥadīth of Abū al-Zinād and the ḥadīth of al-Wāqidī. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15358","(15352) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Mālik narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdillāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānjānī informed us, and the wording is his; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that a man performed the liʿān with his wife during the time of the Prophet ﷺ and denied paternity of her child. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated between them and attributed the child to the woman. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"
"15359","(15353) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated; they both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated. He said: I said to Mālik: Did Nāfiʿ narrate to you from Ibn ʿUmar that a man performed the liʿān with his wife during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated between them and attributed the child to the mother? He said: \Yes.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"15360","(15354) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us; ʿAbdillāh ibn Numayr narrated; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the two who performed the liʿān: \Your account is with Allah. One of you is a liar. You have no claim over her.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," my property"," my property!\"" He said: \""If you spoke truthfully about her"," then it is in exchange for what you made lawful of her private parts. And if you lied about her"," then it is even more remote from you.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān as it preceded. And we have narrated from Muḥammad ibn Zayd"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: \""The two who performed the liʿān"," when they separate"," they will never be reunited.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"15361","(15355) Abū ʿAlī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr informed us from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbāṣ (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the story of Hilāl ibn Umayyah and his wife: that the Prophet (ﷺ) carried out the procedure of *liʿān* (mutual imprecation) between them. The wife testified, after the husband's *liʿān*, four testimonies by Allah that he was indeed among the liars. When the fifth testimony came, it was said to her: \Fear Allah"," for the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter"," and this is the one that will bring upon you the punishment.\"" She remained silent for a while"," then said: \""By Allah"," I shall not disgrace my people.\"" So she testified in the fifth instance that the wrath of Allah would be upon her if he was among the truthful. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) separated them and decreed that the child would not be attributed to any father"," and she would not be accused of adultery"," nor would her child be accused. Whoever accused her or her child would be subject to the prescribed punishment (*ḥadd*). He also decreed that the husband would have no obligation to provide her with housing or sustenance"," because the two of them had separated without a divorce or a death."""
"15362","(15356) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me that ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbd Allāh and others informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, in the hadith of the two who performed *liʿān*, he said: \The established practice (*sunnah*) thereafter regarding the two who perform *liʿān* is that they are separated and shall never be reunited.\"""""
"15363","(15357) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us that Ibn Abī Ḥassān narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that al-Walīd and ʿAmr narrated to us that al-Awzāʿī narrated from al-Zubaydī, from al-Zuhrī, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, regarding the story of the two who performed *liʿān*, he said: \They performed *liʿān* in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) separated them and said: 'They shall never be reunited.'\"""""
"15364","(15358) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd ibn Muslim narrated to us that al-Haytham ibn Jamīl narrated to us that Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated from ʢĀṣim, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbd Allāh; and Qays narrated from ʢĀṣim, from Zirr, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), they both said: \The established practice (*sunnah*) regarding the two who perform *liʿān* is that they shall never be reunited.\"""""
"15365","(15359) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding the two who perform *liʿān*: \When they perform *liʿān*"," they are separated and shall never be reunited.\"""""
"15366","(15360) He said: And Sufyān narrated to us from Abū Hāshim al-Wāsiṭī, from Jahm ibn Dīnār, from Ibrāhīm, who said: \If a man recants after the *liʿān*"," he is subjected to the prescribed punishment (*ḥadd*)"," the child is attributed to him"," and they shall never be reunited. And Allah knows best.\"""""
"15367","(15361) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Ibn Numayr narrated to us that ʿAbdah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \We were in the mosque one Friday night when a man said: 'If a man finds another man with his wife and kills him"," will you kill him? And if he merely speaks"," will you flog him? I shall mention this to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' So he mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and Allah"," the Most High"," revealed the verses of *liʿān*. Then the man came and accused his wife of adultery"," so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) carried out the *liʿān* between them and said: 'Perhaps she will give birth to a black"," curly-haired boy.' She then gave birth to a black"," curly-haired boy.\"" Muslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān."""
"15368","(15362) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Barzah informed us in Hamadhān that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Ḥammād ibn Zayd al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us that Mālik narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that a Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah!\"" — and in the narration of al-Shāfiʿī: \""A man from the people of the desert came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said to him: 'My wife has given birth to a black boy.'\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \""Do you have camels?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""What are their colours?\"" He said: \""Red.\"" He said: \""Is there among them a grey one?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""How do you think that came to be?\"" He said: \""Perhaps a vein (ancestral trait) drew it out.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Perhaps this one too was drawn out by a vein (ancestral trait).\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways."""
"15369","(15363) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Shādhān narrated to us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Sufyān narrated, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that a Bedouin from Banī Fazārah came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \My wife has given birth to a black boy.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \""Do you have camels?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""What are their colours?\"" He said: \""Red.\"" He said: \""Is there among them a grey one?\"" He said: \""There are indeed grey ones among them.\"" He said: \""How did that come to be?\"" He said: \""Perhaps a vein (ancestral trait) drew it out.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""And this one too — perhaps a vein (ancestral trait) drew it out.\"" This is the wording of al-Shāfiʿī's narration. In the narration of Qutaybah: \""A man from Banī Fazārah came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'Perhaps a vein (ancestral trait) drew it out.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Qutaybah and a group of narrators."""
"15370","(15364) Maʿmar narrated it from al-Zuhrī, and he said in the hadith: \A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," my wife has given birth to a black boy","' and he was at that time hinting at disowning the child.\"" Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith with the same meaning. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it; he said: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm."""
"15371","(15365) It was narrated by Ibn Abi Dhi'b from az-Zuhri, with the same meaning as the hadith of Ibn 'Uyyaynah, and he added at the end of the hadith: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not permit him to deny paternity of the child.\"" Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yunus ibn Habib informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated from az-Zuhri"," and he mentioned it. [Sahih. Preceded it.]"""
"15372","(15366) It was narrated by Yunus ibn Yazid from Ibn Shahab from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \My wife has given birth to a black boy"," and I have denied him.\"" Then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Sufyan. Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Isma'il ibn Ahmad al-Jurjani informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us; Harmalah informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yunus ibn Yazid narrated"," and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Harmalah"," may Allah have mercy on him. [Sahih. Preceded it.]"""
"15373","(15367) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Muhammad ibn Sa'id informed us; Sa'd ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us; Qudamah ibn Muhammad informed us; Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated from his father, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shahab claim that Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb used to narrate from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that he passed judgment regarding a man who denied the child of his wife while she was pregnant, then acknowledged it while she was still pregnant, but when the child was born, he denied it. So 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, ordered that he be given eighty lashes for his slander against her, and then the child was attributed to him. [Da'if]"
"15374","(15368) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl informed us in Baghdad; Isma'il ibn Muhammad as-Saffar informed us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr informed us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from Mujalid ibn Sa'id from ash-Sha'bi from Shurayh from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \If a man acknowledges his child even for the blink of an eye"," he has no right to deny paternity of it. And Allah knows best.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15375","(15369) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us; Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us; Sufyan narrated from az-Zuhri from Sa'id from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The child belongs to the owner of the bed"," and the adulterer gets the stone.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Sa'id ibn Mansur. [Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"15376","(15370) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yunus ibn Habib informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Shu'bah narrated from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \The child belongs to the owner of the bed"," and the adulterer gets the stone.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Adam from Shu'bah. [Sahih. Preceded it.]"""
"15377","(15371) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; ar-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; ash-Shafi'i informed us; Sufyan narrated from az-Zuhri from 'Urwah from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that 'Abd ibn Zam'ah and Sa'd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disputing over the son of the slave girl of Zam'ah. Sa'd said: \O Messenger of Allah"," my brother instructed me"," when I came to Makkah"," to look at the son of the slave girl of Zam'ah and take him"," for he is my son.\"" 'Abd ibn Zam'ah said: \""He is my brother and the son of my father's slave girl"," born on my father's bed.\"" The Prophet ﷺ saw a clear resemblance to 'Utbah and said: \""He is yours"," O 'Abd ibn Zam'ah. The child belongs to the owner of the bed. And veil yourself from him"," O Sawdah.\"" Both al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in their Sahih from the hadith of Sufyan ibn 'Uyyaynah. [Sahih. Preceded it.]"""
"15378","(15372) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us; al-Asfati informed us; Isma'il narrated from Malik. (H) And Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated from Malik from Ibn Shahab from 'Urwah from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \'Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas had made a promise to his brother Sa'd that the son of the slave girl of Zam'ah was from me"," so take him with you. In the year of the Conquest"," Sa'd took him and said: 'He is my brother; he had made a promise to me regarding him.' 'Abd ibn Zam'ah stood up and said: 'He is my brother"," born on my father's bed.' They both went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Sa'd said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," my brother had made a promise to me regarding him.' 'Abd ibn Zam'ah said: 'He is my brother and the son of my father's slave girl.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He is yours"," O 'Abd ibn Zam'ah. The child belongs to the owner of the bed"," and the adulterer gets the stone.' Then he said to Sawdah bint Zam'ah"," may Allah be pleased with her: 'Veil yourself from him.' Due to the resemblance she saw to 'Utbah"," she never saw him until she met Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\"" The wording is from the hadith of Abu 'Abdullah. Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi and Isma'il ibn Abi Uways. [Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"15379","(15373) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq as-Saghani informed us; 'Uthman ibn Salih informed us; Ibn Lahi'ah narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Habib and 'Uqayl ibn Khalid from Ibn Shahab from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that when Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ, was born from Mariyah, his slave girl, something almost entered the heart of the Prophet ﷺ regarding him, until Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: \Peace be upon you"," O father of Ibrahim.\"" In this"," if it is established"," there is evidence for the establishment of lineage to the bed of the slave woman. [Da'if]"""
"15380","(15374) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzzi informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us; ar-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; ash-Shafi'i informed us; Malik narrated from Ibn Shahab from Salim ibn 'Abdullah from his father that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \What is the matter with men who have intercourse with their slave girls and then practice coitus interruptus with them? No slave woman should come to me whose master acknowledges that he has had intercourse with her"," except that I will attribute the child to him. Then practice coitus interruptus afterwards"," or leave it.\""\n\nHe said: And Malik informed us from Nafi' from Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd from 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," regarding the sending of slave women for intercourse"," with a meaning similar to the hadith of Ibn Shahab from Salim. [Sahih]"""
"15381","(15375) It was narrated to us by Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani, who was informed by Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, who narrated to us Ibn Bukayr, who narrated to us Malik, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \What is the matter with men who cohabit with their slave-girls and then let them go free? No slave-girl should come to me whose master acknowledges that he has had intercourse with her"," except that I would attach her child to him. So either set them free or keep them.\"""""
"15382","(15376) It was narrated to us by Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr, who narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm, who informed us al-Rabi', who said: I said to al-Shafi'i, may Allah be pleased with him: \Has anyone other than us opposed you in this matter?\"" He said: \""Yes"," some of the people of the East.\"" I said: \""What was their evidence?\"" He said: \""Their evidence was that Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," denied the child of his slave-girl"," and Zayd ibn Thabit"," may Allah be pleased with him"," denied the child of his slave-girl"," and Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," denied the child of his slave-girl.\"" I said: \""What was your argument against them"," i.e."," your response?\"" He said: \""As for Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," it is narrated from him that he denied the pregnancy of his slave-girl who had confessed to a reprehensible act. As for Zayd ibn Thabit and Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," they denied — if they indeed did so — the child of two slave-girls whom they recognized were not from either of them. And likewise"," the husband of a free woman"," if he knows that she has conceived from adultery"," may repudiate her child and not attach it to his lineage"," for it is not from him"," between him and Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic. And he spoke at length on this matter"," which is too lengthy to mention here.\"""""
"15383","(15377) It was narrated to us by Abu Hazim al-Hafiz, who informed us Abu al-Hasan ibn Hamzah al-Harawi, who informed us Ahmad ibn Najdah, who narrated to us Sa'id ibn Mansur, who narrated to us Hushaym, from al-Shaybani, who informed me 'Imran ibn Kathir al-Nakha'i: that 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hur married a slave-girl from his people called al-Dardā', and her father had married her to him. Then 'Ubayd Allah departed and joined Mu'awiya, remaining absent from his wife for a long time. The father of the slave-girl died, and her family married her to a man among them called 'Ikrimah. When this reached 'Ubayd Allah, he came and contested the matter before 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. 'Ali returned the woman to him, and she was pregnant from 'Ikrimah. He placed her in the custody of a trustworthy person. The woman said to 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: \Am I more entitled to my property"," or is 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hur?\"" He said: \""You are more entitled to it.\"" She said: \""Then I bear witness to you that whatever was owed to me by 'Ikrimah from any part of my dowry is his.\"" When she delivered what was in her womb"," he returned her to 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hur and attached the child to his father. And Allah knows best."""
"15384","(15378) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari, who informed us Abu Bakr ibn Dasah, who narrated to us Abu Dawud, who narrated to us Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Bahrani, who narrated to us Yahya ibn Salih, who narrated to us Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, who narrated to me 'Umar ibn Muhajir, from his father, from Asma' bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan al-Ansariyyah: that she was divorced during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and there was no prescribed waiting period (‘iddah) for the divorced woman. So Allah, exalted be His praise, revealed the ‘iddah for divorce at the time Asma' was divorced. She was the first person regarding whom the ‘iddah for divorce was revealed."
"15385","(15379) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sadiq Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fawaris al-'Attar, who both said: narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who narrated to us al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan, who narrated to us Asbat, from Mutarrif, from Abu 'Uthman, who said: When the ‘iddah of women was revealed in Surah al-Baqarah regarding the divorced woman and the woman whose husband has died, Abu 'Uthman said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: \O Messenger of Allah"," some of the people of Madinah say that there remain categories of women regarding whom nothing has been mentioned.\"" He said: \""What are they?\"" He said: \""The young girls"," the elderly women"," and those who are pregnant.\"" He said: Then the verse was revealed: {And those who have despaired of menstruation among your women"," if you doubt"," their ‘iddah is three months"," and for those who have not yet menstruated. And for those who are pregnant"," their term is until they deliver their burden.}"""
"15386","(15380) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, who narrated to us Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam, who narrated to us Yahya ibn Yahya, who said: I recited to Malik:\n\n(And it was narrated to us by Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari, who informed us Abu Bakr ibn Dasah, who narrated to us Abu Dawud, who narrated to us al-Qa'nabi, from Malik, from Nafi', from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar: that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. So 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, about that. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Command him to take her back"," then let her remain until she becomes pure"," then menstruates"," then becomes pure again. Then if he wishes"," he may keep her after that"," and if he wishes"," he may divorce her before touching her. That is the ‘iddah which Allah has commanded for women to be divorced.\"")\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ibn Abi Uways from Malik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya."""
"15387","(15381) It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, who narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who narrated to us Hajjaj, who said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayman asking Ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, while Abu al-Zubayr was listening. He said: \What is your opinion regarding a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating?\"" He said: \""Ibn 'Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him. So 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," asked the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar has divorced his wife while she was menstruating.' The Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'Let him take her back.' So he returned her to me and said: 'When she becomes pure"," let him either divorce her or keep her.'\"" Ibn 'Umar said: The Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," recited: {O Prophet"," when you divorce women"," divorce them} at the beginning of their ‘iddah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Harun ibn 'Abd Allah from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad."""
"15388","(15382) It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, who both said: narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who narrated to us al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman, who informed us al-Shafi'i, who informed us Malik:\n\n(And it was narrated to us by Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajani al-'Adl, who informed us Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanji, who narrated to us Ibn Bukayr, who narrated to us Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: that Hafsah bint 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq moved to a separate place when she entered the bleeding of the third menstruation. Ibn Shihab said: I mentioned that to 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, and she said: \'Urwah has spoken the truth. People argued with her about that and said: 'Indeed Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," says: {Three quru'}.'\"" 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""Do you know what al-aqra' (the quru') are? Al-aqra' are the periods of purity (at-har).\"")\n\nThey both said: And Malik informed us from Ibn Shihab that he said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman say: \""I did not meet any of our jurists except that he would say this"," meaning what 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said.\"" The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Bukayr. And in the narration of al-Shafi'i"," 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""You have spoken the truth. Do you know what al-aqra' are? Al-aqra' are the periods of purity.\"""""
"15389","(15383) It was narrated to us by Abu Tahir al-Faqih, who informed us Abu Hamid ibn Bilal, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi, who narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \Al-aqra' (the quru') are the periods of purity (at-har).\"""""
"15390","(15384) And it was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, who narrated to us Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who narrated to us Ahmad ibn Shayban, who narrated to us Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \When the divorced woman enters the third menstruation"," she has become free from him.\"""""
"15391","(15385) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan — and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ and Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that al-Aḥwaṣ died in Shām when his wife had entered the bleeding of the third menstrual cycle, and he had already divorced her. Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān wrote to Zayd ibn Thābit asking him about that, and Zayd wrote to him: \When she enters the bleeding of the third menstrual cycle"," she is freed from him and he is freed from her"," and she does not inherit from him nor does he inherit from her.\"" In the narration of al-Shāfiʿī there is the addition: \""And he had divorced her","\"" and the remainder is the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it.]"""
"15392","(15386) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Shaybān narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, who said: Muʿāwiyah wrote to Zayd, and Zayd wrote: \When the divorced woman enters the third menstrual cycle"," she has become free from him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15393","(15387) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that he used to say: \When a man divorces his wife and she enters the bleeding of the third menstrual cycle"," she is freed from him and he is freed from her"," and she does not inherit from him nor does he inherit from her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15394","(15388) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad — ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Ṣaydalānī — narrated to us, word for word, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: \When she enters the third menstrual cycle"," there is no taking back (rajʿah) for him over her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15395","(15389) Abū al-Ḥasan — Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Isfarāʾīnī — narrated to us therein: Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Khayyāṭ narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Junayd al-Dāmaghānī narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated from Hishām ibn Ḥassān, from Qays ibn Saʿd, from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, who said: Zayd ibn Thābit said: \When a drop of blood falls from the divorced woman in the third menstrual cycle"," her waiting period (ʿiddah) has expired.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15396","(15390) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from al-Fuḍayl ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh, the client of al-Mahriyy, that he asked al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad and Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh about the woman who is divorced and then enters the bleeding of the third menstrual cycle, and they both said: \She has become irrevocably separated (bānat) from him and has become lawful (i.e."," her waiting period has ended).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15397","(15391) He said: And Mālik narrated to us that it reached him from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Sulaymān ibn Yasār, and Ibn Shihāb that they used to say that: \When the divorced woman enters the bleeding of the third menstrual cycle"," she has become irrevocably separated from her husband"," there is no inheritance between them"," and there is no taking back for him over her.\"" Mālik"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""And that is the matter upon which I found the people of knowledge in our city"," and Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15398","(15392) Abū Bakr — Aḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: My grandfather narrated to us: Ismāʿīl — that is, Ibn ʿUlayyah — narrated from Ayyūb, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh experienced istiḥāḍah (irregular bleeding), so she asked the Prophet ﷺ — or the Prophet ﷺ was asked on her behalf — and he commanded her to abandon the prayer during the days of her aqrāʾ (menstrual periods) and to perform ghusl for what is beyond that, to fasten a cloth (istidhfār), and to pray. It was said to Sulaymān: \May her husband approach her?\"" He said: \""We only say what we have heard.\"" ʿAbd al-Wārith and Ḥammād ibn Zayd likewise narrated it from Ayyūb"," except that they both mentioned that Umm Salamah sought the fatwā on her behalf. Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah used this narration as evidence and claimed that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from Ayyūb in this manner. Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""Sufyān never narrated this. Rather"," Sufyān said"," from Ayyūb"," from Sulaymān ibn Yasār"," from Umm Salamah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'She should abandon the prayer for the number of nights and days during which she used to menstruate' — or he said"," 'the days of her aqrāʾ' — the doubt being from Ayyūb — 'it is not known which of the two he said.' He made one of them to mean what he intended"," and this is not truthful.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15399","(15393) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Bishshār narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Umm Salamah, that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh, may Allah be pleased with her, experienced istiḥāḍah, so Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on her behalf, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \It is not menstruation; it is only a vein (ʿirq).\"" So he commanded her to abandon the prayer during the days of her aqrāʾ and the days of her menstruation"," then to perform ghusl and to pray. If the blood overpowered her"," she should fasten a cloth (istidhfār) — \""thus I found it"," and the correct wording is 'the days of her aqrāʾ or the days of her menstruation","' with doubt.\"" Wuhayb likewise narrated it from Ayyūb. And Abū ʿUbayd Allāh al-Makhzūmī narrated it from Sufyān"," and he said: \""Let her look at the number of nights and days during which she used to menstruate and their measure in the month"," and let her abandon the prayer.\"" Similarly"," Nāfiʿ narrated it from Sulaymān ibn Yasār. Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""Nāfiʿ is more precise in his narration from Sulaymān than Ayyūb"," and he conveys one of the two meanings that Ayyūb narrated.\"" The Sheikh said: \""This wording"," which they used as evidence"," has also been narrated in ḥadīths we have mentioned in the book of Ḥayḍ"," and those ḥadīths themselves differ among the narrators. Some of them said in them 'the days of her aqrāʾ' and some of them said 'the days of her menstruation' or something to that effect. All of that"," from the perspective of the narrators"," is each one of them expressing what occurred to him. The authentic ḥadīths are agreed upon in expressing it as 'the days of menstruation' rather than the wording of al-aqrāʾ. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15400","(15394) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkariyy — narrated to us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: al-Thawrī narrated from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, that a woman came to ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \My husband divorced me and then left me until I returned to my door"," set down my water"," and removed my garments"," and then he said: 'I have taken you back"," I have taken you back.'\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to Ibn Masʿūd"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who was beside him: \""What do you say about her?\"" He said: \""I see that he has more right to her until she performs ghusl from the third menstrual cycle and prayer becomes lawful for her.\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""I also see the same.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15401","(15395) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Amm informed us; al-Rabi' informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \When a man divorces his wife"," he has greater right over her until she performs the ghusl of the third menstrual period"," in the case of one or two divorces.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15402","(15396) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar informed us in Baghdad; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us; Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Rufay', from Abu Ubaydah, who said: \'Uthman"," may Allah be pleased with him"," sent to Ubayy"," may Allah be pleased with him"," asking him about a man who divorced his wife and then took her back when she had entered the third menstrual period.\"" He said: \""I consider that he has greater right over her as long as she has not performed the ghusl of the third menstrual period and as long as prayer has not become permissible for her.\"" He said: \""I do not know that 'Uthman"," may Allah be pleased with him"," acted upon anything other than this.\"" [Hasan]"""
"15403","(15397) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Munadi informed us; Wahb, meaning Ibn Jarir, informed us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from 'Umar, 'Abdullah, and Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with them, regarding a man who divorces his wife and she menstruates three menstrual periods, then he takes her back before she performs the ghusl: \He has greater right over her as long as she has not performed the ghusl of the third menstrual period.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15404","(15398) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; Hajjaj said: Ibn Jurayj said: \Three qurū' (readings/periods).\"" Ibn Jurayj narrated from 'Ata' al-Khurasani"," from Ibn 'Abbas"," who said: \""Three menstrual periods.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15405","(15399) Abu Muhammad al-Sukkari informed us in Baghdad; Isma'il al-Saffar informed us; Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, who said: \The qurū' (plural of qur') are the menstrual periods"," according to the Companions of Muhammad"," peace and blessings be upon him. As for the statement of Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," he took it from Zayd ibn Thabit"," may Allah be pleased with him.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15406","(15400) He said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', that Ibn 'Umar used to say the same as Zayd and 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with them both. [Sahih]"
"15407","(15401) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us; Abu al-Hasan al-Karizi informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us; he said: Abu 'Ubayd said: al-Asma'i and others said: \It is said 'aqra'at al-mar'ah' when her menstrual period draws near"," and 'aqra'at' when her purity draws near.\"" He said: Abu 'Ubayd said: \""The origin of al-aqrā' (plural of qur') is the time of a thing when it arrives.\"" Al-A'sha praised a man for a military expedition he undertook:\n\n \""Mūrithatin mālan wa fī al-dhikri rif'atan limmā ā fīhā min qurū'in nisā'ikā\""\n\n Here"," al-qurū' means the periods of purity (at-hār)"," because women are only intimate during those periods."""
"15408","(15402) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri informed us; Yahya ibn Ma'in informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: \If he divorced her while she was menstruating"," she would not count that menstrual period (toward her 'iddah).\"" Yahya said: \""This is gharib (uncommon); no one narrates it except 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi.\"" The Shaykh said: \""Its meaning has been narrated by Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Misri from 'Ubaydullah"," and we have narrated from Zayd ibn Thabit that he said: 'If a man divorces his wife while she is in a state of nifas (postnatal bleeding)"," her nifas blood shall not be counted in her 'iddah.'\"" [Sahih]"""
"15409","(15403) Abu al-Hasan al-Raffa' informed us; 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Bishr informed us; Isma'il al-Qadi informed us; Ibn Abi Uways informed us; Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madinah: \They used to say: Whoever divorces his wife while she is menstruating or while she is in a state of nifas"," she must observe three menstrual periods"," apart from the blood in which she was when the divorce was given.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15410","(15404) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah informed us; Abu Mansur al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Nadrawi informed us; Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us; Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us; Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: \Among the trusts (amānāt) is that the woman has been entrusted with her private part.\"" And al-Shafi'i narrated from Sufyan"," from 'Amr ibn Dinar"," from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr"," who said: \""The woman has been entrusted with her private part.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15411","(15405) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Abū Shihāb narrated, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khāld, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: A man came to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, and said, \I divorced my wife.\"" She came after two months and said"," \""My ʿiddah has expired.\"" Shuraḥīl (Shurayḥ) was present with ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him. He (Shurayḥ) said"," \""Give your ruling concerning her.\"" The man said"," \""Are you a witness"," O Amīr al-Muʾminīn?\"" ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said"," \""Yes.\"" He (Shurayḥ) said"," \""If she comes with a witness from her family among the upright ones"," testifying that she has had three menstrual cycles"," then (her ʿiddah is complete); otherwise"," she is a liar.\"" ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Qālūn\"" in Roman"," meaning"," \""You have spoken correctly.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15412","(15406) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — recitation — Abū al-Walīd informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Ḥumayd ibn Masʿadah narrated to us; Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from ʿAzrah, from al-Ḥasan al-ʿUranī, that a woman was brought before Shurayḥ whose husband had divorced her. She menstruated within thirty-five nights — three menstrual cycles. He mentioned something similar to the ḥadīth of al-Shaʿbī. Shurayḥ then referred the matter to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him. ʿAlī said, \Ask her neighbors about her. If her menstruation is such-and-such"," then her ʿiddah has expired.\"" And he mentioned the ḥadīth. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15413","(15407) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Mukharramī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; Ḥafṣ narrated, from Ashʿath, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15414","(15408) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Abū Ibrāhīm al-Zāhidī narrated to us; al-Nufaylī narrated, saying: I read to Maʿqil ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rābāḥ, who said: \The minimum duration of menstruation is one day.\"" Abū Ibrāhīm said: \""It was to these two ḥadīths that the Imām of piety"," Imām Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," may Allah the Most High have mercy upon him"," adhered.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15415","(15409) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, who said: There were two wives of his grandfather Ḥabbān — one a Hāshimī woman and the other an Anṣārī woman. He divorced the Anṣārī woman while she was nursing. A year passed, and she did not menstruate. She said, \I inherit from him"," for I have not menstruated.\"" They disputed the matter before ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him. ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," ruled that both of them should inherit. The Hāshimī woman reproached ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him. ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Your cousin's son pointed us to this\"" — meaning ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15416","(15410) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Sālim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr, who was informed: A man from the Anṣār, called Ḥabbān ibn Munqidh, divorced his wife while he was in good health and she was nursing his daughter. She remained for seventeen months without menstruating, as nursing prevented her from menstruating. Then Ḥabbān fell ill after divorcing her, seven or eight months later. He was told, \Your wife wishes to inherit from him.\"" He said to his family"," \""Carry me to ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him.\"" So they carried him to him"," and he mentioned to ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," the matter of his wife. ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and Zayd ibn Thābit"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," were present with him. ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to them both"," \""What do you two see?\"" They both said"," \""We see that she inherits from him if he dies"," and he inherits from her if she dies. She is not among the post-menopausal women who have despaired of menstruation"," nor is she among the virgins who have not yet reached menstruation. Rather"," she remains upon her ʿiddah of menstruation"," whether little or much.\"" Ḥabbān returned to his family and took his daughter (from her). When she lost the nursing"," she menstruated once"," then she menstruated a second time. Then ḿabbān died before she could menstruate a third time. So she observed the ʿiddah of a woman whose husband has died"," and she inherited from him. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15417","(15411) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us; Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated, from Ḥammād, al-Aʿmash, and Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah ibn Qays, that he divorced his wife one or two divorces. She then menstruated one or two cycles. Then her menstruation ceased for seventeen or eighteen months. Then she died. He came to Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him. He said, \Allah has withheld her inheritance from you","\"" and he made him her heir. [Ḥasan]"""
"15418","(15412) As for the ḥadīth: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd and Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qusayṭ, from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Any woman who is divorced and menstruates one or two cycles"," and then her menstruation ceases"," she shall wait nine months. If pregnancy becomes apparent"," then that is it. Otherwise"," she observes an ʿiddah of three months after the nine months"," and then she is lawful (to remarry).\"" Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," adhered to the apparent meaning of this in his earlier position"," but then retracted from it in his later position and adopted the view of Ibn Masʿūd"," may Allah be pleased with him. He interpreted the statement of ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in light of the statement of ʿAbd Allāh (ibn Masʿūd)"," saying: \""It is possible that ʿUmar's statement"," may Allah be pleased with him"," refers to a woman who has reached the age at which women of her kind despair of menstruation"," so that it would not contradict the statement of Ibn Masʿūd"," may Allah be pleased with him. And that is a valid interpretation"," and Allah knows best.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15419","(15413) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Jarīr narrated, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, regarding His statement, \And it is not lawful for them to conceal what Allah has created in their wombs\"" (al-Baqarah 2:228). He said: \""What is most intended by it is menstruation.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15420","(15414) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us; Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated, from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ, from ʿIkrimah, who said: \Menstruation.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15421","(15415) Mujahid reported: That a woman says, \I am menstruating","\"" when she is not menstruating"," or says"," \""I am not menstruating","\"" when she is menstruating"," or says"," \""I am pregnant","\"" when she is not pregnant"," or says"," \""I am not pregnant","\"" when she is pregnant — all of that is indicative of the woman's aversion toward her husband and his love for her. [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15422","(15416) Abu 'Abd al-Hakim al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Muhammad al-'Anbari informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam narrated to us; Ishaq informed us; Jarir narrated from Mutarrif ibn Tarif from 'Amr ibn Salim from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When this verse was revealed in Surah al-Baqarah concerning some of the waiting periods of women, they said, \There remain some waiting periods of women that have not been mentioned — the young girls and the elderly women from whom menstruation has ceased"," and the pregnant women.\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed the verse in Surah al-Nisa': {And those of your women who have despaired of menstruation"," if you are in doubt"," their waiting period is three months"," and for those who have not yet menstruated. And for the pregnant women"," their term is until they deliver their burdens} [al-Talaq: 4]. Imam al-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: His statement {if you are in doubt} means: if you do not know what the women of menstrual cycles should count. [Da'if]"""
"15423","(15417) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us, saying: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Mahmud al-Naysaburi narrated to us; 'Umayr ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Musa al-Dabbi narrated to us; 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, saying: I came across among us — meaning the Mahalibah — a woman who became a grandmother at the age of eighteen. She gave birth to a daughter at the age of nine, and her daughter gave birth at the age of nine, so she became a grandmother at the age of eighteen. [Da'if]"
"15424","(15418) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us; Ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us; 'Abd al-Malik ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us; my father narrated to me; al-Layth narrated that Abu Salih narrated to him from a man who informed him: that his daughter became pregnant and she was ten years old. [Sahih]"
"15425","(15419) Abu Sa'd informed us; Abu Ahmad informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mada'ini narrated to us; Yahya ibn 'Uthman narrated to us; Bakr ibn Sa'd Abu Sa'id al-Ahdab al-Khawlani narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to me; al-Layth narrated to me; my scribe 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to me: that a woman among their neighbors became pregnant and she was nine years old. And we have mentioned all the other narrations on this subject in the Kitab al-Hayd. [Sahih]"
"15426","(15420) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me; 'Ali ibn Hamshadh informed me; Yazid ibn al-Haytham informed me that Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to them; 'Ubayd Allah al-Ashja'i narrated from Sufyan from 'Amr ibn Maymun from his father from Umm Kulthum ibn 'Uqbah: that she was married to al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him. She came to him while he was performing ablution and said, \I would like to free myself with a divorce.\"" So he did so"," and she was pregnant. He went to the mosque"," and when he returned"," she had already delivered what was in her womb. He came to the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and mentioned to him what had transpired. He said"," \""The Book has reached its term\"" — meaning her waiting period had ended. He said"," \""She deceived me; may Allah deceive her.\"" And this was narrated from Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Qasim from Umm Kulthum"," and something to the same effect was narrated through another chain from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. [Da'if]"""
"15427","(15421) 'Abd Allah narrated that the truthful and confirmed Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The creation of each one of you is gathered in the womb of his mother for forty days"," then it becomes a clot for a similar period"," then it becomes a lump of flesh for a similar period. Then Allah sends an angel who breathes the spirit into it"," and he is commanded with four words: to write his provision"," his deeds"," his lifespan"," and whether he is wretched or blessed. By the One besides whom there is no deity"," indeed one of you may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire until there remains between him and it only a cubit"," and the decree overtakes him"," and he is sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise"," so he enters it. And indeed one of you may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise until there remains between him and it only a cubit"," and the decree overtakes him"," and he is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire"," so he enters it.\"" Imam Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Abu Mu'awiya"," and al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it through other chains from al-A'mash. [Sahih]"""
"15428","(15422) Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Allah has appointed an angel over the womb. The angel says"," 'O Lord"," a drop of fluid. O Lord"," a clot. O Lord"," a lump of flesh.' When Allah wills to decree its creation"," the angel says"," 'O Lord"," male or female? Wretched or blessed? What is the provision? What is the lifespan?' And thus it is written while it is in the womb of its mother.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu al-Nu'man"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Kamil from Hammad. [Sahih]"""
"15429","(15423) Abu al-Tufayl narrated from Hudhayfah ibn al-Asid, tracing it back to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \The angel is appointed over the drop of fluid after it settles in the womb for forty days"," or forty-five nights. The angel says"," 'O Lord"," what is it — wretched or blessed?' Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," decrees"," and the two are written. Then the angel says"," 'O Lord"," male or female?' Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," decrees"," and the two are written. His deeds"," his lifespan"," his provision"," and his traces are written. Then the scrolls are raised"," and nothing is added to them nor taken away from them.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb and others from Sufyan. [Sahih]"""
"15430","(15424) Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki reported that 'Amir ibn Wasilah narrated to him that he heard 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud say: \The wretched one is he who is made wretched in the womb of his mother"," and the blessed one is he who takes admonition from others.\"" A man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," called Hudhayfah ibn al-Asid al-Ghifari"," came and narrated this statement of Ibn Mas'ud to him and said"," \""How can a man be made wretched without any deed?\"" The man said"," \""Are you astonished by that? I heard the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," say: 'When the drop of fluid passes forty-two nights"," Allah sends an angel to it who shapes it and creates its hearing"," its sight"," its skin"," its flesh"," and its bones. Then the angel says"," \""O Lord"," male or female?\"" Your Lord decrees as He wills"," and the angel writes. The angel says"," \""O Lord"," his lifespan?\"" Your Lord says as He wills"," and the angel writes. The angel says"," \""O Lord"," his provision?\"" Your Lord decrees as He wills"," and the angel writes. Then the angel departs with the scroll in his hand"," and nothing is added to its command nor taken away from it.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu al-Tahir. [Sahih]"""
"15431","(15425) It is narrated from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \The term of every pregnant woman is that she delivers what is in her womb.\"" Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Razzāz reported it to us in Baghdad; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī reported to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Jahm narrated to us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from ʿĀmir from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\n[Weak]"""
"15432","(15426) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Umayyah: that a woman's husband died, and a man proposed marriage to her, intending to marry her after she became lawful (i.e., after her waiting period ended). When she became lawful, he married her. She remained with him for four and a half months, then she gave birth. The matter reached ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), so he sent for the woman and asked her. She said: \By Allah"," it is his child.\"" ʿUmar asked about the woman"," and nothing but good was reported about her. Then he sent for the women of the Jāhiliyyah"," gathered them"," and asked them about her matter and her condition. One of them said to her: \""Did you have a menstrual period?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""When was the last time you were with your husband?\"" She said: \""Before he died.\"" She said: \""I will inform you of the matter of this woman. She became pregnant by her husband"," and she was experiencing bleeding over him (i.e."," during the pregnancy). Her child withered due to the bleeding. When she married and the fluid of her new husband reached her"," the child revived and began to move at that point. The blood then ceased from her. So when she gave birth"," she gave birth to a child of a full six months.\"" The women said: \""She has spoken the truth; this is her matter.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) separated the two.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15433","(15427) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad informed us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Muḥtasib narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Sulaymān ibn Khuzaymah al-Bukhārī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Abū ʿUbaydah Maʿmar ibn al-Muthannā al-Taymī narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \I was sitting spinning"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was mending his sandal. His forehead began to perspire"," and his perspiration was generating light. I was astonished. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at me and said: 'What is the matter with you"," O ʿĀʾishah? Why are you astonished?' I said: 'Your forehead is perspiring"," and your perspiration is generating light. Were Abū Kabīr al-Hudhalī to see you"," he would know that you are more deserving of his verse.' He said: 'What does Abū Kabīr say?' She said: I said: He says:\n\n'Free from every impurity of menstruation"," and the corruption of a nursing woman"," and the disease of a fatal illness.\n\nWhen you look at the radiance of his face"," it flashes like the lightning of a pouring cloud.'\n\nShe said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) then came to me"," kissed between my eyes"," and said: 'May Allah reward you well on my behalf"," O ʿĀʾishah. You have not been pleased with me except as I have been pleased with you.' In this is an indication that the beginning of pregnancy may occur during menstruation"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not deny it.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"15434","(15428) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Lahīʿah and al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed you from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Umm ʿAlqamah from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): that she was asked about a pregnant woman who sees blood — does she pray? She said: \No"," until the blood ceases from her.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"15435","(15429) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; he said: Isḥāq narrated from Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from ʿAmrah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \When the pregnant woman sees blood"," she refrains from prayer.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"15436","(15430) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Ibrāhīm al-Ḥarbī informed us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us. And Ibrāhīm informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who said: \There is no difference of opinion among us from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that when a pregnant woman sees blood"," she withholds from prayer until she becomes pure.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15437","(15431) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Ibrāhīm al-Ḥarbī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated from Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid from Abī ʿIqāl from Anas: He was asked about the pregnant woman — does she abandon prayer when she sees blood? He said: \Yes.\"" And similarly"," Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ.\n\n[Weak]"""
"15438","(15432) As for the hadith: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Abū Maʿmar narrated to us; and Hammām narrated; Maṭar narrated from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said regarding the pregnant woman when she sees blood: \She should perform ghusl and pray.\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than this chain]"""
"15439","(15433) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥalīm informed us; Abū al-Muwajjih informed us; ʿAbdān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ narrated from Maṭar from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): that a woman came to her and said: \I am menstruating and I am pregnant.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Perform ghusl and pray"," for the pregnant woman does not menstruate.\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than this chain]"""
"15440","(15434) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī informed us; Abū Nuʿaym and al-Ḥawḍī both said: Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Mūsā narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The pregnant woman does not menstruate. When she sees blood"," let her perform ghusl and pray.\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"15441","(15435) Thus did Matar al-Warraq and Sulayman ibn Musa narrate it from 'Ata' from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). And the scholars of hadith have deemed these two narrations from 'Ata' to be weak.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us — Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Muttariz narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us — Hajjaj narrated from Hammad — from Matar — from 'Ata' — from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her).\n\nHammad said: I mentioned this hadith to Yahya ibn Sa'id, and he rejected it. [Sahih]"
"15442","(15436) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us — Ibn Abi 'Ismah narrated to us — Abu Talib: Ahmad ibn Humayd said: I asked Ahmad ibn Hanbal regarding the hadith of Hammad from Matar from 'Ata' from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The pregnant woman"," when she sees blood"," is not menstruating; she prays.\"" He (Ahmad) said: \""Yahya — meaning al-Qattan — used to weaken Abu Layla and Matar from 'Ata'; that is"," he used to weaken their two narrations from 'Ata'.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15443","(15437) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, saying: I heard Abu Sa'd al-Mu'adhdhin saying: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq saying: I heard 'Ubaydah ibn al-Tayyib saying: I heard Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali saying: Ahmad ibn Hanbal said to me: \What do you say regarding the pregnant woman who sees blood?\"" I said: \""She prays","\"" and I cited as evidence the report of 'Ata' from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). He said: Then Ahmad said to me: \""Where are you from the report of the Medinans — the report of Umm 'Alqamah from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) — for it is more authentic?\"" Ishaq said: I then returned to the statement of Ahmad. The Shaykh said: As for the narration of Sulayman ibn Musa from 'Ata'"," Muhammad ibn Rashid is singular in transmitting it from him"," and Muhammad ibn Rashid is weak. And Ibn Jurayj narrated from 'Ata' regarding the pregnant woman who sees blood"," saying: \""She is in the position of the mustahadah (woman experiencing prolonged bleeding).\"" And Hajjaj narrated from 'Ata'"," saying: \""When the pregnant woman sees blood"," she performs wudu' and prays"," and she does not take a bath (ghusl).\"" This contradicts the narration of those who reported from him regarding ghusl from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""
"15444","(15438) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'd ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us — Hafs ibn Ghayath narrated from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym — from Abu 'Umar al-'Abdi — from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding a man who divorces his wife while she is carrying two children, and she gives birth to one and the other remains: He said: \He has greater right to take her back"," so long as she has not delivered the other one.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15445","(15439) He said: And Ahmad narrated to us — Hafs narrated from Ibn Jurayj — from Maysarah — from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) — with the like of it. [Da'if]"
"15446","(15440) He said: And Ahmad narrated to us — Hafs narrated from al-Sha'bi — the like of it. [Da'if]"
"15447","(15441) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us — Ahmad narrated to us — Hafs narrated from Ibn Jurayj — from 'Ata' — the like of it. [Da'if]"
"15448","(15442) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Husayn narrated from his father — from Yazid al-Nahwi — from 'Ikrimah — from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) regarding the statement of Allah, the Most High: **{And the divorced women shall wait for three menstrual periods}** [al-Baqarah 228]: He said: **{And those of your women who have despaired of menstruation, if you are in doubt, their waiting period shall be three months, and also those who have not yet menstruated}** [al-Talaq 4] — so He abrogated that and said: **{And if you divorce them before you have touched them, there is no waiting period for you to count regarding them}** [al-Ahzab 49]. [Da'if]"
"15449","(15443) Abu Sa'd ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Muslim ibn Khalid narrated from Ibn Jurayj — from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym — from Tawus — from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them): \She is entitled to only half the dower"," and there is no waiting period ('iddah) upon her.\"" Al-Shafi'i said: \""And Shurayh says the same"," and that is the apparent meaning of the Book.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15450","(15444) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us — Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Abu Bishr narrated from Sa'id ibn Jubayr — from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: \Al-lams (touching)"," al-mass (feeling)"," and al-mubasharah (intimacy) short of intercourse — that is what is meant — but Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," spoke of it by way of allusion (kinayah).\"" [Sahih]"""
"15451","(15445) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: The divorced woman and the woman whose husband has died begin counting their ʿiddah from the day she was divorced or from the day her husband died. [Ḥasan]"
"15452","(15446) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Aswad, Masrūq, and ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The ʿiddah of the divorced woman is from the moment she is divorced, and the ʿiddah of the woman whose husband has died is from the moment he dies. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15453","(15447) And it has been narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir ibn Zayd, who attributed it to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: From the day he dies. And this is what Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me from Abū al-Walīd: Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Zurārah narrated to us: Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ayyūb, from ʿAmr, and he mentioned it. And in the book of Ibn al-Mundhir, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: She counts her ʿiddah from the day he divorced her or died. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15454","(15448) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, and Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that they said: From the day he died or divorced. The Shaykh said: And this is the view of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rābāḥ, Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī, al-Zuhrī, and others. [Ḥasan]"
"15455","(15449) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah, from Abū Ṣādiq, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: She counts from the day the news reaches her. This is the well-known narration from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). And likewise, al-Shaʿbī narrated it from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15456","(15450) And al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in the book of ʿAlī and ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with both of them) as a balāgh from Hushaym, from al-Ashʿath, from al-Ḥakam, from Abū Ṣādiq, from Rābiʿah ibn Nājid, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The ʿiddah is from the day he divorces or dies.\n\nAbū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, and he mentioned it. The first narration from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) is more well-known, and we only present the statement of others over his statement by way of deduction from the Book (of Allah). And with Allah lies success. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15457","(15451) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the mawlā of the family of Ṭalḥah, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: A slave may marry two women and may issue two divorces, and a slave woman observes an ʿiddah of two menstrual cycles. If she does not menstruate, then two months or one and a half months. Sufyān said: And he was trustworthy (thiqah). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15458","(15452) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Baghdādī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to me: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The ʿiddah of a slave woman, if she does not menstruate, is two months, and if she menstruates, it is two menstrual cycles. And it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The ʿiddah of a slave woman is two menstrual cycles, and if she does not menstruate, then one and a half months. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15459","(15453) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿAmr ibn Aws al-Thaqafī, from a man from Thaqīf, that he heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: If only I could make the ʿiddah of a slave woman one and a half menstrual cycles! A man said: Then make it one and a half months.\n\nSo ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) fell silent. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15460","(15454) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khamīruwayh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿAmr ibn Aws, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If only I could make the ʿiddah of a slave woman one and a half menstrual cycles, I would do so. A man said: O Commander of the Faithful, then make it one and a half months. He said: So he fell silent. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15461","(15455) ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: \The ʿiddah of a free woman is three menstrual cycles"," and the ʿiddah of a slave woman is two menstrual cycles.\"" The Shaykh said: Others have narrated it as a marfūʿ hadith from Ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," but it is not authentic. [Weak]"""
"15462","(15456) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Ḥātim ibn Yūnus al-Jurjānī narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Mūsā al-Kūfī narrated to us; al-Muẓāhir ibn Aslam narrated from al-Qāsim from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The slave woman is divorced with two pronouncements"," and her ʿiddah is two menstrual cycles.\"" [Weak]"""
"15463","(15457) He said: And Ḥātim narrated to us; Mūsā ibn al-Sindī narrated to us; al-Ḍaḥḥākh ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; al-Muẓāhir narrated to us; al-Qāsim narrated from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet ﷺ, a similar hadith.\n\nAl-Ḍaḥḥākh said: \I met al-Muẓāhir and asked him"," and he narrated to me from al-Qāsim from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\"" The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""This is a hadith that al-Muẓāhir ibn Aslam is alone in narrating"," and he is an unknown man known only by this hadith. The authentic narration from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad is that he was asked about the ʿiddah of a slave woman and he said: 'The people say two menstrual cycles.'\"" [Weak]"""
"15464","(15458) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Mazzakī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated that it reached him that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Sulaymān ibn Yasār used to say: \The ʿiddah of a slave woman"," when her husband dies"," is two months and five nights.\"" [Weak]"""
"15465","(15459) He said: And Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb likewise. And we have narrated it through another chain from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, al-Ḥasan, and al-Shaʿbī, may Allah have mercy on them. And Allah knows best."
"15466","(15460) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr, who said: I said—\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Umayyah ibn Bisṭām narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated from Ḥabīb from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: I said to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him: \{And those who die among you and leave wives behind}\"" — this verse has been abrogated by the other verse. So why do you write it"," or why do you leave it? He said: \""O son of my brother"," I do not change anything from its place.\"" And in the narration of ʿAlī: \""Why do you write it when it has been abrogated by the other verse: '{And those who die among you and leave wives behind shall wait by themselves for four months and ten [days]}'?\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Umayyah ibn Bisṭām. [Authentic]"""
"15467","(15461) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī informed me; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated from his father; Yazīd al-Naḥwī narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding the verse: \{And those who die among you and leave wives — an inheritance for their wives"," provision for a year without turning [them] out}\"" — this was abrogated by the verses of inheritance: what was prescribed for them of one-quarter or one-eighth. And the term of one year was abrogated by making her term four months and ten days. [Weak]"""
"15468","(15462) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding this verse: \When a man died and left his wife"," she would observe the ʿiddah of one year in his house"," and he would spend on her from his wealth. Then Allah revealed after that: '{And those who die among you and leave wives shall wait by themselves for four months and ten [days]}' — so this is the ʿiddah of the woman whose husband has died"," unless she is pregnant"," in which case her ʿiddah is until she delivers what is in her womb.\"" And he said regarding her inheritance: \""{For them is one-quarter of what you leave"," if you leave no child; but if you leave a child"," then for them is one-eighth}\"" — so Allah clarified the inheritance of the woman and left aside the bequest and the maintenance. [Weak]"""
"15469","(15463) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-ʿAdl informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl, who is Ibn ʿUlayyah, narrated from Yūnus from Ibn Sīrīn from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both: that he stood and addressed the people here, and recited Sūrat al-Baqarah to them and explained it to them. When he came to this verse: \{If he leaves wealth"," the bequest for parents and near relatives}","\"" he said: \""This verse has been abrogated.\"" Then he continued reciting until he came to this verse: \""{And those who die among you and leave wives}\"" up to His words: \""{without turning [them] out}.\"" And he said: \""This verse has also been abrogated.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15470","(15464) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawyah al-ʿAskarī informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī informed us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us; Ḥumayd ibn Nāfiʿ narrated from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah from her mother: that a woman's husband died and her eyes became inflamed, and they feared for her eyesight. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked his permission regarding kohl. The Prophet ﷺ said to them: \She should not apply kohl. One of you used to remain in the worst of her dwellings or in the worst of her rooms"," and when a year had passed"," if a dog passed by"," she would throw a piece of dung at it. No — until four months and ten days have elapsed.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"15471","(15465) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed me that Ḥumayd ibn Nāfiʿ informed him from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah that she heard Umm Salamah and Umm Ḥabībah mentioning that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that her daughter's husband had died and that her eye was causing her trouble — should she apply kohl to it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \One of you used to throw a piece of dung at the end of the year. It is only four months and ten days.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Yazīd ibn Hārūn. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15472","(15466) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Ḥumayd ibn Nāfiʿ from the Anṣār, and he mentioned the hadith with its meaning and added therein: Ḥumayd said: \I said to Zaynab"," may Allah be pleased with her: 'What is the head of the year?' Zaynab said: 'A woman in the Jāhiliyyah"," when her husband died"," would go to the worst house she had and sit therein until a year had passed over her. Then she would come out and throw a piece of dung.' And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15473","(15467) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Hishām — (ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah: \Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth a few nights after the death of her husband. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked his permission to remarry"," and he gave her permission.\"" In the narration of Jaʿfar"," he said: \""The husband of Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah died"," and she did not remain but a few nights before she gave birth. When she recovered from her postpartum bleeding"," she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he gave her permission for it"," so she married.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Qazaʿah from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15474","(15468) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Ḥasan, that is Ibn Sufyān, informed us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb — (ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn Sahl and Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl said: Abū al-Ṭāhir informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus from Ibn Shihāb informed me: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh informed me that his father ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah wrote to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Arqam al-Zuhrī, commanding him to go to Subayʿah bint al-Ḥārith al-Aslamiyyah and ask her about her hadith and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her when she sought his legal opinion. ʿUmar ibn ʿAbdillāh wrote to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah, informing him that Subayʿah informed him: \She was married to Saʿd ibn Khawlā"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who was from Banū ʿĀmir ibn Luʾayy and was among those who witnessed Badr. He died during the Farewell Pilgrimage while she was pregnant. It was not long before she delivered her child after his death. When she recovered from her postpartum bleeding"," she adorned herself for suitors. Abū al-Sanābil ibn Baʿkkak"," a man from Banū ʿAbd al-Dār"," entered upon her and said: 'What is this I see of you adorned? Perhaps you wish to remarry. By Allah"," you cannot marry until four months and ten days have passed.' Subayʿah said: 'When he said that to me"," I gathered my garments when evening came and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. He gave me a legal opinion that I had become lawful when I delivered my child"," and he commanded me to marry if I wished.'\""\n\nAbū ʿAmr added in his narration: Ibn Shihāb said: \""I see no harm in her marrying when she has delivered"," even if she is still in her bleeding"," provided that her husband does not approach her until she becomes pure.\"" The wording is from the hadith of Ḥarmalah. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah. al-Bukhārī narrated it from the hadith of al-Layth ibn Saʿd from Yūnus"," then he said: \""And Ibn Wahb corroborated it from Yūnus.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15475","(15469) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us: al-Layth from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb that Ibn Shihāb wrote to him, mentioning that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah informed him from his father that he wrote to Ibn al-Arqam: \Ask Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a legal opinion when her husband died.\"" She said: \""He gave me a legal opinion that I may marry when I have delivered.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15476","(15470) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī — (ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from al-Zuhrī — (ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās, who is al-Aṣamm, informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah from his father: \Subayʿah bint al-Ḥārith al-Aslamiyyah gave birth a few nights after the death of her husband. Abū al-Sanābil ibn Baʿkkak passed by her and said: 'You have adorned yourself for marriage. It is four months and ten days.' Subayʿah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Abū al-Sanābil has spoken falsely' — or 'It is not as Abū al-Sanābil says. You have become lawful"," so marry.'\"" This is the wording of the hadith of al-Shāfiʿī. The hadith of Saʿdān is abridged: \""Subayʿah bint al-Ḥārith gave birth after the death of her husband in a month or less"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to marry.\"" This narration is mursal"," and the connected narrations before it are sufficient. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15477","(15471) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Sulmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh in Baghdād informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn — (ḥ) He said: And Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from Abī Salamah said: \I"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," and Abū Hurayrah were discussing a man who dies leaving behind a wife who gives birth shortly after his death. I said: 'When she has given birth"," she has become lawful.' Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," said: 'Her term is the latter of the two terms.' They kept referring the matter back and forth between them. Abū Hurayrah said: 'I am with my nephew' — meaning Abū Salamah. So they sent Kurayb"," the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās"," to Umm Salamah"," may Allah be pleased with her. She said: 'Subayʿah gave birth forty nights after the death of her husband"," and a man from Banū ʿAbd al-Dār"," known as Abū al-Sanābil"," proposed to her and informed her that she had become lawful. She wished to marry someone else. Abū al-Sanābil said to her: \""You have not yet become lawful.\""' Subayʿah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he commanded her to marry.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Umm Salamah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15478","(15472) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed me: al-Layth informed me: Jaʿfar from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj informed us: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah informed him from her mother Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: \A woman called Subayʿah was married to her husband when he died while she was pregnant. Abū al-Sanābil ibn Baʿkkak proposed to her"," but she refused to marry. He said: 'By Allah"," it is not proper for you to marry until you have observed the latter of the two terms.' She remained for approximately twenty nights"," then she gave birth. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: 'Marry.'\"" Fāṭimah ibn Qays used to narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that when she was irrevocably divorced"," he commanded her to move to Ibn Umm Maktūm"," for he was blind"," so she could leave her garments with her before her waiting period ended. Muḥammad ibn Usāmah ibn Zayd said: \""Usāmah ibn Zayd"," whenever Fāṭimah mentioned anything of that"," would throw at her whatever was in his hand.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15479","(15473) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us: Ḥammād from Ayyūb from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn said: \I was sitting with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā and his companions"," who were venerating him as though he were a commander. They mentioned 'the latter of the two terms.' I mentioned the hadith of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah regarding Subayʿah bint al-Ḥārith. One of his companions nudged me"," so I understood and said: 'I am eager to lie — if I were to lie upon ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah while he is in the region of Kūfah.' He felt shy and said: 'But his uncle did not say that.' He said: 'I had not heard anything about it from ʿAbdullāh.' He said: 'So I stood up and met Abū ʿAṭiyyah Mālik ibn al-Ḥārith and asked him. He began narrating to me the hadith of Subayʿah. I said: 'I am not asking you about this"," but have you heard anything from ʿAbdullāh about it?' He said: 'Yes"," we were with ʿAbdullāh and we asked him about her. He said: 'What do you think if she gives birth before the four months and ten days?' We said: 'Not until they have passed.' He said: 'What do you think if the four months and ten days pass before she gives birth?' We said: 'Not until she gives birth.' He said: 'You are imposing strictness upon her and not granting her the concession. Sūrat al-Nisāʾ al-Ṣughrā was revealed after al-Ṭūlā: {And for pregnant women"," their term is until they deliver their burden.}'\"" al-Bukhārī extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ and said: \""And Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and Abū al-Nuʿmān mentioned it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ"," 4910]"""
"15480","(15474) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkari in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah from al-Aʿmash from Muslim from Masrūq said: ʿAbdullāh said: \By Allah"," whoever wishes"," I will declare it: Sūrat al-Nisāʾ al-Ṣughrā was revealed after 'four months and ten days.'\"" And from Muslim Abī al-Ḍuḥā"," who said: ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to say: \""The latter of the two terms.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15481","(15475) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad, that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed us, that Saʿīd al-Ḥakam ibn Abī Maryam informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Kathīr informed us, that Ibn Shubrumah al-Kūfī informed us, on the authority of Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī, on the authority of ʿAlqamah ibn Qays, that Ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whoever wishes"," I shall declare it to him.\"" He said: \""The verse {And for those who are pregnant"," their term is until they deliver their burdens} was not revealed except after the verse concerning the woman whose husband has passed away — that when the woman whose husband has passed away gives birth"," she has become lawful (i.e."," her waiting period has ended).\"" He meant by the verse concerning the woman whose husband has passed away: {And those who are taken in death among you and leave behind wives — the wives shall wait concerning themselves for four months and ten days.} [Hasan]"""
"15482","(15476) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Mālik informed us, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, on the authority of Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), that he was asked about a woman whose husband had passed away while she was pregnant. Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When she gives birth to her child"," she has become lawful (i.e."," her waiting period has ended).\"" A man from the Anṣār then informed him that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) had said: \""Even if she gives birth while her husband is still on the bier"," not yet buried"," she has become lawful (i.e."," her waiting period has ended).\"" And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15483","(15477) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that ʿAbd al-Majīd informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abū al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jābir, that he said: \The woman whose husband has passed away is not entitled to maintenance; her inheritance is sufficient for her.\"" This is the preserved version"," and it is mawqūf (a statement stopping at the Companion). It was also narrated by Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Raqāshī"," who said: Ḥarb ibn Abī al-ʿĀliyah informed us"," on the authority of Abū al-Zubayr"," on the authority of Jābir"," on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," that he said regarding the pregnant woman whose husband has passed away: \""She is not entitled to maintenance.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15484","(15478) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī informed us — word for word — that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Ṣubayḥ informed us, on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, that Ibn al-Zubayr used to give her (the pregnant woman whose husband had passed away) maintenance, until it reached him that Ibn ʿAbbās had said: \She is not entitled to maintenance.\"" So he retracted that statement — meaning regarding the maintenance of the pregnant woman whose husband has passed away. It was also narrated by ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ"," on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: \""She is not entitled to maintenance; the inheritance has become obligatory.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15485","(15479) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, that ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq informed us, on the authority of Abū Isḥāq, on the authority of al-Shaʿbī, on the authority of Fāṭimah bint Qays, who said: \My husband divorced me with three divorces. I intended to move (from my house)"," so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and he said: 'Move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm.'\"" Isḥāq said: \""When al-Shaʿbī narrated this"," al-Aswad pelted him with pebbles and said: 'Woe to you! Do you narrate or give fatwā with something like this? She came to ʿUmar"," and he said: \""If you bring two witnesses who testify that they heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," otherwise we will not abandon the Book of Allah for the statement of a woman\"" — and it is the word of Allah: {And do not turn them out of their houses"," nor should they leave"," except that they commit a clear immorality.} [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15486","(15480) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, that al-Rabīʿ informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Mālik informed us, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, that the daughter of Saʿīd ibn Zayd was married to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān. He divorced her irrevocably (al-battah), and she left (the house). Ibn ʿUmar disapproved of that on her part. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15487","(15481) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Walīd informed us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, that Kāmil ibn Ṭalḥah informed us, that Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us, that Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed us, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, on the authority of Ibn ʿUmar, regarding the verse {except that they commit a clear immorality}, he said: \Her leaving her house is a clear immorality.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15488","(15482) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us, that Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us, that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us, that Sufyān informed us, on the authority of al-Aʿmash, on the authority of Ibrāhīm, on the authority of Masrūq, on the authority of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man came to him and said: \I have divorced my wife with three divorces"," and she wants to leave (the house).\"" He said: \""Detain her.\"" He said: \""I cannot.\"" He said: \""Then restrain her (by force).\"" He said: \""I cannot — she has brothers with thick necks (i.e."," powerful brothers).\"" He said: \""Then seek the help of the governor against them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15489","(15483) And with his chain of narration, Sufyān informed us, that Ashʿath informed us, on the authority of al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd, who said: A man came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," what do you think of a woman who was divorced and then went to her family in the morning?\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""By Allah"," I would not love that her religion (i.e."," her integrity) be worth a single date for me.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15490","(15484) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, that Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, that Sufyān informed us, on the authority of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad, on the authority of Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAlqamah, on the authority of Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the words of the Most High {except that they commit a clear immorality}, he said: \That she be immodest toward her family. When she is immodest toward them"," it becomes lawful for them to expel her.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15491","(15485) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from 'Amr, the mawla of al-Muttalib, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he was asked regarding this verse: \Do not turn them out of their houses"," nor should they leave unless they commit a clear immorality (fāḥisha mubayyina).\"" Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," said: \""The clear immorality is that a woman should act indecently toward the man's household and cause them harm.\"" Al-Shāfi'ī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""The sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the hadith of Fāṭimah bint Qays indicates that what Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," interpreted regarding the statement of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic — 'unless they commit a clear immorality' — is indecent speech toward her husband's family"," as he interpreted"," if Allah the Most High wills.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15492","(15486) Abu Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shāfi'ī informed us: Mālik informed us from 'Abd Allah ibn Yazīd, the mawla of al-Aswad ibn Sufyān, from Abū Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān, from Fāṭimah bint Qays, that Abū 'Amr ibn Ḥafṣ divorced her irrevocably (al-battah) while he was absent in Shām. He sent his agent with barley, and she was displeased with it. He said: \By Allah"," you have nothing from us.\"" She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: \""You are not entitled to maintenance from him.\"" He commanded her to observe her waiting period in the house of Umm Sharīk. Then he said: \""That is a woman whom my companions frequent. Observe your waiting period at Ibn Umm Maktūm's"," for he is a blind man — you may remove your garments.\"" Muslim narrated this in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ — 1480]"""
"15493","(15487) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Sa'd narrated to us: my father narrated to me from Ṣāliḥ, from Ibn Shihāb, that Abū Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān informed him that Fāṭimah bint Qays informed him: she was with Abū 'Amr ibn Ḥafṣ ibn al-Mughīrah, and he divorced her with the final of three divorces. She claimed that she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when she was leaving his house, and he commanded her to move to Ibn Umm Maktūm, the blind man. Marwān refused to believe Fāṭimah regarding the divorced woman's leaving her house. And 'Urwah said that 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, disapproved of that regarding Fāṭimah bint Qays. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥulwānī and 'Abd ibn Ḥumayd, from Ya'qub. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15494","(15488) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: 'Ubayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Yaḥyā, that is ibn Bukayr, narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us from 'Uqayl ibn Khālid, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān, from Fāṭimah bint Qays, that she informed him: she was married to Abū 'Amr ibn Ḥafṣ ibn al-Mughīrah, and he divorced her with the final of three divorces. She claimed that she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sought his ruling regarding her leaving his house, and he commanded her to move to Ibn Umm Maktūm, the blind man. Marwān refused to accept Fāṭimah's hadith regarding the divorced woman's leaving. And 'Urwah said: 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, disapproved of that regarding Fāṭimah bint Qays. Muslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15495","(15489) Abu al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Abu al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Kaysān narrated to us: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us — and in another narration: Sulaymān informed us: Mu'ādh ibn al-Muthannā and Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated to us, they said: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us, they said: Sufyān narrated to us from 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that he said to 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: \Do you not see regarding Fulānah bint al-Ḥakam"," who was irrevocably divorced and then left?\"" She said: \""Evil is what she did.\"" I said: \""Do you not consider the statement of Fāṭimah bint Qays?\"" She said: \""There is no good for her in mentioning that.\"" al-Bukhārī and Muslim both extracted it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq 'alayh]"""
"15496","(15490) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Alī ibn 'Īsā ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah and 'Abd Allah ibn Muḥammad ibn Shirawayh narrated to us, they said: Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated to us from Hishām, who said: my father narrated to me: Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd ibn al-'Āṣ married the daughter of 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥakam and then divorced her and turned her out. 'Urwān criticized them for that and said: \Indeed"," Fāṭimah left.\"" 'Urwān said: \""So I went to 'Ā'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," and informed her of that.\"" She said: \""There is no good for Fāṭimah bint Qays in mentioning this hadith.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15497","(15491) Abu Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abu al-'Abbas informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shāfi'ī informed us: Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd, from al-Qāsim and Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that he heard them both mentioning that Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd ibn al-'Āṣ irrevocably divorced the daughter of 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥakam, and 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥakam moved her. 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, sent to Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam, who was the governor of al-Madinah, and said: \Fear Allah"," O Marwān"," and return the woman to her house.\"" Marwān said — in the hadith of Sulaymān — \""'Abd al-Raḥmān overpowered me.\"" And Marwān said in the hadith of al-Qāsim: \""Has the matter of Fāṭimah bint Qays not reached you?\"" 'Ā'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""It is not upon you that you do not mention anything regarding Fāṭimah.\"" He said: \""If the evil is only in you"," then sufficient is the evil between these two.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways"," from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15498","(15492) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfi'ī informed me: 'Abd al-'Azīz narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn 'Amr, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm, that 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, used to say: \Fear Allah"," O Fāṭimah"," for you know in what state that was.\"""""
"15499","(15493) Abu al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us: Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Sa'dān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated to us from 'Amr ibn Maymūn, from his father, who said: I said to Sa'īd ibn al-Musayyib, \Where does the thrice-divorced woman observe her waiting period?\"" He said: \""She observes it in her house.\"" I said: \""Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not command Fāṭimah bint Qays to observe her waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm?\"" He said: \""That is the woman who caused tribulation among the people — she overstepped against her in-laws with her tongue. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to observe her waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm"," and he was a blind man.\"" Al-Shāfi'ī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""'Ā'ishah"," Marwān"," and Ibn al-Musayyib knew that the hadith of Fāṭimah — that the Prophet ﷺ commanded her to observe her waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm — was as she narrated"," but they held that that was only due to some evil. Ibn al-Musayyib added clarification regarding her overstepping against her in-laws"," and Ibn al-Musayyib and others disliked that she omitted in her hadith the reason for which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to observe her waiting period other than in her husband's house"," out of fear that anyone who heard it might conclude that the irrevocably divorced woman may observe her waiting period wherever she wishes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15500","(15494) Abu 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Zayd narrated to us: my father narrated to me from Sufyān, from Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, regarding Fāṭimah's leaving, he said: \That was only on account of bad character.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15501","(15495) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād informed us on the authority of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, on the authority of his father, who said: ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, criticised that — meaning the ḥadīth of Fāṭimah bint Qays — with the severest criticism, and she said: \Indeed"," Fāṭimah was in a desolate place"," and her safety was feared for; therefore the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted her dispensation.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""And Ibn Abī al-Zinād said"," on the authority of Hishām.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15502","(15496) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad both said: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us that Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us that Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Fāṭimah bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," my husband has divorced me with three divorces"," and I fear that he may assault me.' So he commanded her"," and she moved away.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. The Shaykh said: \""The reason for her narration of both of these (reports) may be that she found her in-laws burdensome"," so each one of the two narrators limited himself to transmitting one of them to the exclusion of the other"," since the ruling was attached to each one of them independently.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""The Prophet ﷺ did not say to her"," 'Observe your ʿiddah wherever you wish'; rather"," he secured her in a place that was suitable"," since her husband was absent and had no agent to provide her accommodation. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15503","(15497) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that Mālik narrated to us, on the authority of Saʿd ibn Isḥāq ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, on the authority of his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Kaʿb, that Furayʿah bint Mālik ibn Sinān informed her: \She came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him to permit her to return to her family in Banī Khudrah"," and that her husband had gone out in search of some of his runaway slaves"," and when they reached the edge of al-Qadūm"," he caught up with them"," and they killed him. She said: 'I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether I could return to my family"," for my husband had not left me in a dwelling that he owned.' She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes.' So she departed"," and when she was in the chamber or in the mosque"," he called for me or commanded that I be summoned"," so I was called to him. He said: 'What did you say?' I repeated to him the account I had mentioned regarding my husband's affair. He said: 'Remain in your house until the prescribed term is fulfilled.' She said: So I observed my ʿiddah therein for four months and ten days. When ʿUthmān became caliph"," he sent to me and asked me about that"," so I informed him"," and he followed it and judged accordingly.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15504","(15498) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us that Saʿd ibn Isḥāq ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah informed him that his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Kaʿb informed him that she heard Furayʿah bint Mālik — the sister of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī — mention: \Her husband was killed during the time of the Prophet ﷺ"," and she wished to move from her husband's house to her family. She mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted her permission to move"," but when she turned to leave"," he called her back and said to her: 'Remain in your house until the prescribed term is fulfilled.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15505","(15499) He said: And Yazīd informed us that Yaḥyā informed us that Saʿd ibn Isḥāq informed him that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, was reminded of the ḥadīth of Furayʿah, so he sent for her until she came to him, and he asked her about the ḥadīth, and she narrated it to him. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15506","(15500) The Shaykh said: And Shuʿbah narrated it on the authority of Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, then he met Saʿd ibn Isḥāq and narrated it to him; he (Yaḥyā) informed him of it. Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us from the original of his book that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that al-Naḍr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to me, on the authority of Saʿd ibn Isḥāq, on the authority of Ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, that he heard his paternal aunt narrate, on the authority of Furayʿah, the sister of Abū Saʿīd: \She was with her husband in one of the villages of Madīnah. He went out in pursuit of some of his slaves"," and they killed him. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained of the loneliness of her dwelling"," and mentioned that she was in a house that did not belong to her"," and she sought permission to go to her brother's dwelling in Madīnah. He permitted her"," then he called for her or she was called to him"," and he said: 'Dwell in the house in which the news of your husband's death reached you"," until the prescribed term is fulfilled.' He (Shuʿbah) said: 'Then I met Saʿd ibn Isḥāq myself"," and he narrated it to me.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15507","(15501) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn al-Ḥammāmī al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us, on the authority of Saʿd ibn Isḥāq, who said: \I heard my paternal aunt Zaynab bint Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah narrate"," on the authority of Furayʿah bint Mālik: 'She was with her husband","' and he mentioned the ḥadīth in a similar manner.\"" And likewise it was narrated by Sufyān al-Thawrī"," Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār"," and Abū Baḥr al-Bakrāwī"," on the authority of Saʿd ibn Isḥāq ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah. And Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it"," on the authority of Isḥāq ibn Saʿd ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah"," on the authority of Zaynab bint Kaʿb"," and it was said on the authority of Ḥammād"," on the authority of Saʿd ibn Isḥāq. And Isḥāq is the more well-known narrator from Ḥammād"," and Saʿd is the more well-known narrator from others besides him. And Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhalī claimed"," in his view"," that they were two separate individuals. And Allah knows best.\n\n(15502) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us the ḥadīth of Ḥammād: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs informed us that Abū al-Nuʿmān Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Saʿd ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah narrated to us that Zaynab bint Kaʿb narrated to me"," on the authority of Furayʿah bint Mālik: \""Her husband went out in search of some of his slaves and was killed at the edge of al-Qadūm.\"" Ḥammād said: \""It is a water place.\"" She said: \""I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned my situation to him and mentioned moving to my sister's house. He granted me permission. When I had gone beyond"," he called me and said: 'Remain in your house until the prescribed term is fulfilled.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15508","(15502) Furayʿah bint Mālik narrated that her husband went out in search of his slaves and was killed at one side of al-Qadūm. Ḥammād said: \It is a place of water.\"" She said: \""I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned my condition to him and mentioned moving to my sister's house. She said: Permission was granted to me. When I had departed"," I was called"," and he said: 'Remain in your house until the prescribed term is fulfilled.'\"""""
"15509","(15503) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Saʿd ibn Isḥāq ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, and he mentioned the ḥadīth in a similar manner. \If they are not two separate individuals"," then this is more in agreement with the rest of the narrators from Saʿd.\""\n\n(T) And al-Zuhrī narrated it from Saʿd. In one narration he said: \""On the authority of Ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah.\"" In another narration he said: \""It reached me from Saʿd"," on the authority of his paternal aunt.\"" And in another narration he said: \""A man from the people of Madīnah"," called Mālik ibn Anas"," narrated to me"," on the authority of Saʿd ibn Isḥāq ibn ʿUjrah","\"" and he mentioned it in a manner similar to the narration of the group from Mālik. And the ḥadīth is well-known through Saʿd ibn Isḥāq; a number of the Imams have narrated it from him. And Allah knows best.\n\n(15504) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānjānī informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated to us"," on the authority of Ḥumayd ibn Qays"," on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"," on the authority of Saʿid ibn al-Musayyab: \""That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to turn back the women whose husbands had died from al-Baydāʾ"," preventing them from performing Ḥajj.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15510","(15504) Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab narrated that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, used to turn back the women whose husbands had died from al-Baydāʾ, preventing them from performing Ḥajj."
"15511","He said: And Malik narrated to us from Nafi' from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The woman whose husband has died and the woman who has been irrevocably divorced shall not spend the night except in her own house. And Allah knows best. [Sahih]"
"15512","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Ya'qub al-Thaqafi narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Muthanna al-'Anbari narrated to us — Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us — Shibl ibn 'Abbad narrated to us — from Ibn Abi Najih, who said: 'Ata' said: Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: This verse abrogated her waiting period ('iddah) at her family's home — so she observes the 'iddah wherever she wishes. And that is the statement of Allah, the Blessed and Most Exalted: {without expelling them} [al-Baqarah 240]. 'Ata' said: If she wishes, she may observe the 'iddah at her family's home, or she may reside in the house bequeathed to her; and if she wishes, she may go out, by virtue of the statement of Allah, the Most High: {And if they leave, there is no blame on you for what they do with themselves} [al-Baqarah 240]. 'Ata' said: Then the inheritance came and abrogated the right of residence — so she observes the 'iddah wherever she wishes. [Hasan]"
"15513","And Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us — Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Rawh al-Mada'ini narrated to us — Shababah narrated to us — Warqa' narrated to us — from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding the verse: {And those of you who die and leave wives behind — the wives shall wait by themselves for four months and ten days} [al-Baqarah 234]: He said: This 'iddah required her to observe the waiting period at her husband's family's home, and that was obligatory upon her. Then Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, revealed: {And those of you who die and leave wives behind — a bequest to their wives of provision for a year, without expelling them. And if they leave, there is no blame on you for what they do with themselves in a reasonable manner} [al-Baqarah 240]. He said: Allah made for her nine months and twenty nights as a bequest — if she wishes, she may reside in the house bequeathed to her, and if she wishes, she may go out. And that is the statement of Allah, the Almighty and Majestic: {without expelling them; and if they leave, there is no blame on you for what they do} — regarding the 'iddah, which remains obligatory upon her. Mujahid held this view.\n\nAnd 'Ata' said, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Then this verse abrogated her 'iddah at her family's home — so she observes the 'iddah wherever she wishes. And that is the statement of Allah, the Almighty and Majestic: {without expelling them}. 'Ata' said: If she wishes, she may observe the 'iddah at her family's home, or she may reside in the house bequeathed to her; and if she wishes, she may go out, by virtue of the statement of Allah, the Almighty and Majestic: {And if they leave, there is no blame on you for what they do with themselves}. 'Ata' said: Then the inheritance came and abrogated the right of residence — so she observes the 'iddah wherever she wishes, and she has no right of residence. Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq, from Rawh, from Shibl, and from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from Warqa'. [Sahih — 5344]"
"15514","Abu Sa'd ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — he said: Al-Shafi'i said, relating from Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, that 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to send the woman whose husband had died on her way and would not wait with her.\n\nAnd from Ibn Mahdi, from Sufyan, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) moved Umm Kulthum seven nights after the killing of 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). And Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it in his Jami' and said: That was because she was in the house of the caliphate. [Da'if]"
"15515","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us — Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us — Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us — 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us — Sufyan narrated to us — from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ata', that 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) performed the Hajj for her sister during her 'iddah.\n\nAnd he said: And Sufyan narrated to me — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim informed us — from al-Qasim, who said: There was the fitnah and fear thereof — meaning when 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) performed the Hajj for her sister during her 'iddah. [Da'if]"
"15516","And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us — Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us — Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us — from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) used to send a woman out during her 'iddah following the death of her husband. He said: The people refused to accept that except in opposition to her view. So we do not take her statement and abandon the statement of the people. And Allah knows best. [Sahih]"
"15517","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us — Abu al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ayyub said — Musaddad narrated to us — Yahya narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj narrated to us — from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: My maternal aunt was divorced with three divorces, and she went out to tend the palm trees. A man met her and forbade her. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Go out and tend the palm trees, perhaps you will give charity or do a righteous deed.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim, from Yahya ibn Sa'id.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The palm trees of the Ansar were near their homes, and the harvesting was done only during the day. [Sahih — 1483]"
"15518","And in what Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz permitted to me to narrate from him — from Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm, who informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — 'Abd al-Majid informed us — from Ibn Jurayj — Isma'il ibn Kathir informed me — from Mujahid, who said: Men were martyred on the day of Uhud, and their wives were left behind, and they were neighbors living in a single house. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we feel lonely at night, so we spend the night at one of our homes, and when morning comes we hasten back to our own houses. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Sit together at one of your homes as much as you wish, but when you desire sleep, let every woman among you return to her own house. [Da'if]"
"15519","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — 'Abd al-Majid informed us — from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah, from 'Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him), who used to say: It is not permissible for a woman to spend even a single night outside her own house when she is in the 'iddah of death or divorce. [Sahih]"
"15520","And Abu Bakr al-Ardashtani informed us — Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us — Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us — 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us — Sufyan narrated to me — Ibn Jurayj and Ibn Abi Dhubyan narrated to us — from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The divorced woman and the woman whose husband has died may go out during the day, but they shall not spend a full night anywhere other than their own houses.\n\nAnd from Sufyan, who said: Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to me — from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The irrevocably divorced woman may visit during the day, but she shall not spend the night anywhere other than her own house.\n\nAnd from Sufyan, from Mansur and al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah: Women from Hamdan were informed of the deaths of their husbands, so they asked Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him). They said: We feel lonely. He commanded them to gather during the day, and when night fell, each woman should return to her own house.\n\nAnd from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from a man from Aslam: A woman asked Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) — her husband had died and she wished to nurse her father who was ill. Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Be at one end of the night in your house. [Hasan]"
"15521","(15515) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd that he said: It reached me that al-Sāʾib ibn Khabbāb passed away, and that his wife came to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — and mentioned to him the death of her husband. She also mentioned to him their farmland at Qanāṭ, and asked him whether it was permissible for her to spend the night there. He forbade her from doing so. Thus she used to leave Madīnah at the time of saḥar and spend the day at their farmland, remaining there throughout the day. Then, when evening approached, she would enter Madīnah and spend the night in her house. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"15522","(15516) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us — and Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from Ḥumayd, from Nāfiʿ, from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah, that she informed him of these three hadiths. Zaynab said: I visited Umm Ḥabībah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when Abū Sufyān passed away. Umm Ḥabībah — may Allah be pleased with her — called for a perfume containing a yellowish substance, khalūq or something else, and applied it to a slave-girl, then touched her cheeks with it. Then she said: By Allah, I have no need for perfume, except that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say — Ibn Bukayr said: from the minbar, and they both agreed — \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three nights"," except for a husband"," for whom she mourns four months and ten days.\""\n\nZaynab said: I visited Zaynab bint Jaḥsh — may Allah be pleased with her — when her brother ʿAbdullāh — may Allah be pleased with him — passed away. She called for perfume and applied some of it"," then said: I have no need for perfume"," except that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say from the minbar: \""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three nights"," except for a husband"," for whom she mourns four months and ten days.\""\n\nZaynab said: And I heard my mother"," Umm Salamah — may Allah be pleased with her — say: A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah"," my daughter's husband has passed away"," and her eye is ailing; may we apply kohl to it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""No.\"" She asked twice or three times"," and each time he said: \""No.\"" Then he said: \""It is only four months and ten days. One of you in the Jāhiliyyah would throw a dung pellet at the end of the year.\""\n\nḤumayd said: I asked Zaynab — may Allah be pleased with her — \""What is 'throwing a dung pellet at the end of the year'?\"" Zaynab said: When a woman's husband died in the Jāhiliyyah"," she would enter a small tent"," wear her worst garments"," and not touch any perfume until a year had passed. Then she would be brought a donkey"," a sheep"," or a bird"," and she would rub herself against it. Rarely would she rub against anything without it dying.\n\nIn the narration of al-Shāfiʿī: She would rub against it"," then go out"," be given a dung pellet"," and throw it. After that"," she could return to using perfume or anything else as she wished. [Sound. Agreed upon]"""
"15523","(15517) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; he said: I read to Mālik from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr, and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā."
"15524","(15518) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us orally, Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah, Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Ghālib informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from Ḥumayd ibn Nāfiʿ, from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah, who said: When the news of Abū Sufyān's death arrived, Umm Ḥabībah — may Allah be pleased with her — called for a yellowish substance and applied it to her cheeks and forearms on the third day, and she said: I would have been free of the need for this, had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three days"," except for a husband"," for whom she mourns four months and ten days.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿUmar"," both from Sufyān. [Sound]"""
"15525","(15519) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us, Shabābah informed us, Shuʿbah informed us, Ḥumayd ibn Nāfiʿ informed me; he said: I heard Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrating from Umm Ḥabībah — may Allah be pleased with her — that when a close relative of hers died, she took a yellowish substance and applied it to her forearms, and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for a Muslim woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three days"," except a woman for her husband"," for whom she mourns four months and ten days.\""\n\nShuʿbah said: And Ḥumayd ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to me from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah"," from her mother"," and from one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ"," something similar to it. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Shuʿbah. [Sound. Agreed upon]"""
"15526","(15520) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us, al-Layth informed us — and Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us, al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ that Ṣafiyyah bint Abī ʿUbayd narrated to him from Ḥafṣah, or from ʿĀʾishah, or from both of them, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day"," or who believes in Allah and His Messenger"," to mourn a deceased person for more than three days"," except for her husband.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and others.\n\nAnd ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār similarly reported it from Nāfiʿ. [Sound. 1490]"""
"15527","(15521) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr al-Rāzī informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī informed us; and he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad al-Nasawī informed me, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; he said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd say: I heard Nāfiʿ narrating from Ṣafiyyah bint Abī ʿUbayd that she heard Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with both of them — narrating from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three days"," except for a husband"," for whom she mourns four months and ten days.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Sound]"""
"15528","(15522) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three days"," except for a husband.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated something similar from Umm ʿAṭiyyah — may Allah be pleased with her — from the Prophet ﷺ"," and that will be mentioned"," Allah willing. [Sound]"""
"15529","(15523) As for the hadith: Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān al-Naysābūrī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī informed us, Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād, from Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays, who said: When Jaʿfar — may Allah be pleased with him — was killed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me, saying: \Mourn for three days"," then do as you wish.\""\n\nHowever"," the hearing of ʿAbdullāh from Asmāʾ is not established. It has also been narrated from Asmāʾ directly"," making it mursal. And Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah is not strong. The hadiths before it are more established"," and recourse to them is more appropriate. And with Allah lies success. [Weak]"""
"15530","(15524) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us — and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from the original of his hearing, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr informed us — both saying: Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj informed us; Ḥumayd ibn Nāfiʿ informed me; he said: I heard Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrating from her mother: A woman's husband passed away, and her eye became ailing. They feared for her eye, and the Prophet ﷺ was asked about it. He said: \One of you would remain in the worst of her garments in her house until the year's end. A dog would pass by"," and she would throw a dung pellet at it. Then she would go out — only four months and ten days.\""\n\nThis is the wording of Yaḥyā's hadith. In the narration of Abū Dāwūd: \""The Prophet ﷺ was asked: 'May she apply kohl?' He said: 'No.'\"" And he said at the end of it: \""Not until four months and ten days have passed.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Shuʿbah. [Sound. Agreed upon]"""
"15531","(15525) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri narrated to us — al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us — 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb al-Mula'i narrated from Hisham, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm 'Atyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three days"," except for her husband. She shall not apply kohl"," nor comb her hair"," nor apply perfume"," except at the time of her closest period of purity"," and she shall not wear a dyed garment"," except a garment of 'asb cloth.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it from al-Fadl ibn Dukayn in an abridged form"," and then he said: \""And al-Ansari said: Hisham narrated to us.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15532","(15526) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, informed us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us — Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us — al-Ansari narrated to us — Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us — Hafsah bint Sirin narrated to me, saying: Umm 'Atyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a woman from mourning more than three days upon a deceased person, except for her husband — she shall mourn him for four months and ten days — and she shall not wear a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb cloth, and she shall not apply kohl, nor touch perfume, except at the time of her closest purity, when she has purified herself with a small amount of qust (costus) or azhar (cypress leaves).\ [Sahih]"""
"15533","(15527) Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Faqih al-Shirazi informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ibrahim narrated to us — Yazid narrated to us — Hisham narrated from Hafsah, from Umm 'Atyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three days"," except for her husband — she shall mourn him for four months and ten days — and she shall not wear a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb cloth"," and she shall not apply kohl"," nor touch perfume"," except at the time of her closest purity"," when she has bathed from her menses with a small amount of qust (costus) or azhar (cypress leaves).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Amr al-Naqid from Yazid ibn Harun. And similarly"," 'Abd Allah ibn Idris and 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated it from Hisham. And Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it from Hisham ibn Hassan with its meaning"," and he added: \""And she shall not apply henna (dye).\"" [Sahih]"""
"15534","(15528) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed him — Abu Bakr al-Qattan narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me — Hisham ibn Hassan narrated it. [Sahih]"
"15535","(15529) Ya'qub al-Dawraqi narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, and he said in place of \'asb\"": \""except a washed garment.\"" Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated it.\n\nAnd Yazid ibn Zura' narrated it from Hisham ibn Hassan. [Sahih]"""
"15536","(15530) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us through dictation — Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us — Yazid ibn Zura' narrated to us — Hisham ibn Hassan narrated from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm 'Atyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn one who has perished for more than three days"," except for her husband — she shall mourn him for four months and ten days — and she shall not wear a dyed garment"," nor a garment of 'asb cloth"," and she shall not apply kohl with antimony (ithmid)"," nor apply henna (dye)"," nor touch perfume"," except at the time of her closest purity"," when she has purified herself from her menses with a small amount of qust (costus) or azhar (cypress leaves).\""\n\nThus he said: \""nor a garment of 'asb cloth.\"" And it has reached me that Ishaq ibn Yunus narrated it from Hisham ibn Hassan likewise"," whereas the narration of the majority (al-jama'ah) differs from that. [Sahih]"""
"15537","(15531) Al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated from Yazid ibn Zura' in accordance with the narration of the majority. Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed me — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us — Yazid ibn Zura' narrated to me — Hisham ibn Hassan narrated it in accordance with the narration of the majority, and he said: \except a garment of 'asb cloth.\"" And he did not mention henna (dye). [Sahih]"""
"15538","(15532) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ahmad ibn al-Nadr ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us — Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us — Hammad narrated to us — Ayyub narrated from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm 'Atyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \We were forbidden to mourn a deceased person for more than three days"," except for her husband — four months and ten days — and we were not to apply kohl"," nor perfume"," nor wear a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb cloth. And concession was granted to her at the time of her purity"," when one of us bathed from her menses"," with a small amount of qust (costus) or azhar (cypress leaves).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu al-Rabi'"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from 'Abd Allah al-Hajabi from Hammad ibn Zayd. [Sahih]"""
"15539","(15533) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us. (H) And Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us through dictation — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Baghdadi narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us — Badyl ibn Maysarah narrated to me — al-Hasan ibn Muslim narrated — from Safiyyah bint Shaybah — from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \A woman whose husband has died shall not wear saffron-dyed garments"," nor garments dyed with wars (a yellow dye)"," nor jewelry"," nor shall she apply henna (dye)"," nor shall she apply kohl.\""\n\nThese are the words of the hadith of Ibrahim ibn al-Harith. And al-Saghani added in his narration: \""And Badyl ibn Maysarah narrated to me that al-Hasan ibn Muslim said: 'I did not see them (the women) consider the application of sabir (a medicinal paste) to be objectionable.'\"" [Sahih]"""
"15540","(15534) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar informed us — Isma'il al-Saffar narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar narrated — from Badyl al-'Uqayli — from al-Hasan ibn Muslim — from Safiyyah bint Shaybah — from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \A woman whose husband has died shall not wear anything of dyed garments"," nor apply kohl"," nor adorn herself"," nor wear jewelry"," nor apply henna (dye)"," nor perfume herself.\"" And this is a mawquf (stopping at the Companion) narration. [Sahih]"""
"15541","(15535) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāʿif, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: A woman whose husband has passed away should not apply kohl, nor perfume, nor henna, nor wear dyed garments except black *muʿaṣṣab* cloth, and she should not spend the night in a house other than her own, though she may go out during the day for visiting. [Ḥasan]"
"15542","(15536) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated that it reached him that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said to a woman who was observing mourning for her husband and had complained of an ailment in her eyes, which had reached her [attention]: \Apply kohl of *al-jilāʾ* at night and wipe it off during the day.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15543","(15537) And with the same chain of narration, Mālik narrated that it reached him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm Salamah—may Allah be pleased with her—while she was observing mourning for Abū Salamah, and she had applied *ṣabr* [aloe] to her eyes. He said: \What is this"," O Umm Salamah?\"" She said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," it is only *ṣabr*.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Apply it at night and wipe it off during the day.\""\n\nThese two narrations are *munqaṭiʿ* [disconnected]"," though they have also been narrated with a connected chain. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15544","(15538) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Makhramah narrated from his father, who said: I heard al-Mughīra ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk say: Umm Ḥakīm bint Asīd informed me from her mother that her husband had passed away and she was suffering from an ailment in her eye, so she applied kohl of *al-jilāʾ*. Aḥmad said: The correct wording is \kohl of *al-ḥilāʾ*.\"" She sent her freedwoman to Umm Salamah to ask her about kohl of *al-jilāʾ*. She said: \""Do not apply it except for a matter of necessity that is severe upon you; then apply it at night and wipe it off during the day.\"" Then Umm Salamah—may Allah be pleased with her—said at that time: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me when Abū Salamah had passed away"," and I had applied *ṣabr* to my eyes. He said: 'What is this"," O Umm Salamah?' I said: 'It is only *ṣabr*"," O Messenger of Allah; there is no perfume in it.' He said: 'It brightens the face"," so do not apply it except at night"," and remove it during the day. Do not comb your hair with perfume or with *ḥinnāʾ* [henna]"," for it is a dye.'\"" She said: \""I said: 'With what shall I comb my hair"," O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'With *sidr* [lote tree leaves]"," and cover your head with it.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15545","(15539) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us. And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that Ṭalḥah was married to Rushayd al-Thaqafī, who divorced her irrevocably [*al-batta*]. She then married during her waiting period. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb—may Allah be pleased with him—struck her and struck her husband with a whip several times, and he separated them. Then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb—may Allah be pleased with him—said: \Any woman who marries during her waiting period—if the husband who married her has not consummated the marriage with her"," they shall be separated"," and she shall complete the remainder of her waiting period from her first husband"," and he shall be considered one of the suitors. But if he has consummated the marriage with her"," they shall be separated"," and she shall complete the remainder of her waiting period from her first husband"," then observe a waiting period from the other"," and he shall never marry her again.\""\n\nSaʿīd said: \""She is entitled to her dowry for what he made lawful of her private part.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15546","(15540) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān narrated from Jarīr, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Zādhān Abī ʿUmar, from ʿAlī—may Allah be pleased with him—that he ruled regarding a woman who married during her waiting period: \They shall be separated"," and she is entitled to the dowry for what he made lawful of her private part"," and she shall complete the remainder of her first waiting period"," then observe a waiting period from the other.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15547","(15541) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Darābjirdī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from ʿAlī—may Allah be pleased with him—regarding a woman who married during her waiting period. He said: \She shall complete the remainder of her first waiting period"," then observe a new waiting period from the other. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15548","(15542) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Ismāʿīl, from al-Shaʿbī, from Masrūq, who said: ʿUmar—may Allah be pleased with him—said regarding a woman who married during her waiting period: \The marriage is unlawful"," and the dowry is unlawful.\"" He ordered the dowry to be placed in the public treasury and said: \""They shall never be together as long as they live.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15549","(15543) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī—verbatim—both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from ʿĀmir, from ʿUbayd ibn Naḍlah—or he said Nuḍaylah; Dāwūd was uncertain—who said: A woman who had married during her waiting period was brought before ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb—may Allah be pleased with him. He said to her: \Did you know that you married during the waiting period?\"" She said: \""No.\"" He said to her husband: \""Did you know?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Had I known"," I would have stoned you both.\"" He then flogged them both with lashes"," took the dowry"," and gave it in charity in the cause of Allah. He said: \""I do not permit a dowry whose marriage I do not permit.\"" And he said: \""She shall never be lawful for you.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15550","(15544) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamzah al-Harawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Hushaym informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sālim narrated from al-Shaʿbī that ʿAlī—may Allah be pleased with him—separated them and assigned her the dowry for what he had made lawful of her private part, and said: \When her waiting period ends"," if she wishes"," she may marry him.\""\n\nOthers also narrated this from al-Shaʿbī. Al-Shāfiʿī—may Allah have mercy upon him—said: \""We follow the statement of ʿAlī—may Allah be pleased with him.\""\n\nThe Shaykh [al-Bayhaqī] said: And ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb—may Allah be pleased with him—retracted his first statement and permitted her dowry and allowed them to be together. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15551","(15545) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf — informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us; Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad — narrated to us; Ashʿath — from al-Shaʿbī, who said:\n\nʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) was brought a woman who had married during her waiting period (ʿiddah). He took her mahr and placed it in the Bayt al-Māl (public treasury), separated the two of them, and said: \They shall never be reunited","\"" and he punished them both.\n\nAl-Shaʿbī said: ʿAlī (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) said: \""It is not like that. Rather"," this is ignorance (jāhiliyyah) on the part of the people. They shall be separated"," and then she shall complete the remainder of the ʿiddah from the first husband"," and then she shall begin a new ʿiddah.\"" And ʿAlī (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) assigned her the mahr on account of what he had made lawful of her private part.\n\nAl-Shaʿbī said: ʿUmar (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) then praised Allah and commended ʿAlī"," and said: \""O people"," return matters of ignorance to the Sunnah.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"15552","(15546) Abū Ḥāziṃ al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥamzah al-Harawī — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us; Hushaym — narrated to us; Ashʿath ibn Sawwār — from al-Shaʿbī — from Masrūq:\n\nThat ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) retracted his position regarding the mahr and assigned it to her on account of what he had made lawful of her private part.\n\n[Weak]"
"15553","(15547) And al-Thawrī narrated it from Ashʿath with his chain of narration: that ʿUmar (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) retracted that and assigned her her mahr and permitted the two of them to be reunited.\n\nAbū Bakr al-Ardistānī — informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī — narrated to us; Sufyān al-Jawharī — narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan — narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd — narrated to us; Sufyān — and he mentioned it.\n\n[Weak]"
"15554","(15548) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah — informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us; Hushaym — informed us; Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind — from ʿIkrimah — from Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhumā):\n\nHe used to say: \If a woman gives birth after nine months"," then twenty-one months of nursing are sufficient for her. And if she gives birth after seven months"," then twenty-three months of nursing are sufficient for her. And if she gives birth after six months"," then twenty-four months of nursing are sufficient for her"," as Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said\"" — meaning His statement: {And his gestation and weaning are thirty months} [al-Aḥqāf 15].\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15555","(15549) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib — narrated to us; Abū Badr Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah — from Dāwūd ibn Abī al-Qaṣṣāf — from Abī Ḥarb ibn Abī al-Aswad al-Dīlī:\n\nThat ʿUmar (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) was brought a woman who had given birth after six months, and he intended to stone her. This reached ʿAlī (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu), who said: \There is no stoning upon her.\"" This reached ʿUmar (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu)"," so he sent for him and asked him. ʿAlī said: {And mothers shall suckle their children for two whole years"," for whoever wishes to complete the nursing period} [al-Baqarah 233]"," and He said: {And his gestation and weaning are thirty months} [al-Aḥqāf 15]. So six months is the period of gestation and two years is the period of weaning. There is no ḥadd upon her — or he said: \""There is no stoning upon her.\"" So ʿUmar (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) released her"," and then she gave birth.\n\n[Weak]"""
"15556","(15550) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās — narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bashīr — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah — from Qatādah — from Dāwūd ibn Abī al-Qaṣṣāf — from Abī Ḥarb ibn Abī al-Aswad al-Dīlī:\n\nThat ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) was presented with a woman, and he mentioned it.\n\nThus it is in this narration: ʿUmar. And similarly it was narrated from al-Ḥasan in a mursal form.\n\n[Weak]"
"15557","(15551) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī — narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr — narrated to us; Mālik — that it reached him:\n\nThat ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) was brought a woman who had given birth in six months, and he ordered that she be stoned. ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhu) said: \That is not upon her.\"" Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," said: {And his gestation and weaning are thirty months} [al-Aḥqāf 15]"," and He said: {And his weaning is in two years} [Luqmān 14]"," and He said: {And mothers shall suckle their children for two whole years} [al-Baqarah 233]. So the nursing period is twenty-four months and the gestation period is six months. ʿUthmān ordered that she be returned"," but she was found to have already been stoned. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Weak]"""
"15558","(15552) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah — informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — from Ibn Jurayj — from Jamīlah ibn Saʿd — from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhā), who said:\n\n\A woman does not exceed two years in pregnancy"," not even by the amount of the shadow of a spindle.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"15559","(15553) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Makhlad — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Bakr ibn Khālid — narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Rashīd — narrated to us. He said: I heard al-Walīd ibn Muslim saying:\n\nI said to Mālik ibn Anas: \I have been narrated from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiy Allāhu ʿanhā) that she said: 'A woman does not exceed two years in pregnancy"," not even by the amount of the shadow of a spindle.'\"" He said: \""Subḥān Allāh! Who says this? This is our neighbor"," the wife of Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlan — a truthful woman"," and her husband is a truthful man. She carried three pregnancies in twelve years"," each pregnancy lasting four years.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15560","(15554) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī — informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd — narrated to us; Ibn Abī Khaythamah — narrated to us; Ibn Abī Rizmah — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī narrated to us — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Makhlad — narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Shaddād ibn Dāwūd al-Makhrāmī — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rizmah — narrated to us; my father — narrated to us; al-Mubārak ibn Mujāhid — who said:\n\n\It is well known among us that the wife of Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlan carries and delivers in four years"," and she was called Ḥāmilat al-Fīl (the Elephant-Pregnant Woman).\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"15561","(15555) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Makhlad ibn Ja'far informed us: Muhammad ibn Jarir informed us: al-Harith ibn Muhammad informed us: Muhammad ibn Sa'd informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Umar, that is, al-Waqidi, who said: I heard Malik ibn Anas saying: Pregnancy may last for two years, and I know of one whose mother carried him for more than two years — meaning himself. [Hasan]"
"15562","(15556) And Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah ibn al-Batta' al-Asbahani informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Dabbi informed us: Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Waqid, in the mention of Malik ibn Anas, that his mother carried him in her womb for three years — this is the meaning of his statement. [Hasan]"
"15563","(15557) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed me: 'Ali ibn 'Umar, the hafiz, informed us: Muhammad ibn Makhlad informed us: Abu Shu'ayb, that is, Salih ibn 'Imran al-Da''a', informed me: Ahmad ibn Ghassan informed us: Hashim ibn Yahya al-Farra' al-Mujashi' said: One day, while Malik ibn Dinari was sitting, a man came to him and said: \O Abu Yahya"," pray for a woman who has been pregnant for four years and has fallen into severe distress.\"" Malik became angry and closed the Mushaf"," then said: \""These people think nothing less than that we are prophets.\"" Then he prayed and said: \""O Allah"," if there is wind in her belly"," expel it from her this very hour"," and if there is a female child in her belly"," replace it with a male child"," for indeed You erase what You will and You establish what You will"," and with You is the Mother of the Book.\"" Then Malik raised his hand"," and the people raised their hands. The messenger came to the man and said: \""Go to your wife.\"" The man left"," and Malik had not yet lowered his hand when the man appeared at the mosque gate"," carrying on his shoulders a curly-haired"," short-haired boy of four years whose teeth had come in evenly and whose umbilical cord had not yet been cut. [Da'if]"""
"15564","(15558) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih al-Asbahani informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar, the hafiz, informed us: Muhammad ibn Nuh al-Jundaysaburi informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us: Ibn Numayr informed us: al-A'mash informed us, from Abu Sufyan, who informed me: Sheikhs from among us said: A man came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," I was absent from my wife for two years"," and I returned to find her pregnant.\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," consulted people regarding her stoning. Mu'adh ibn Jabal"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," if you have a case against her"," you have no case against what is in her womb. Leave her until she delivers.\"" So he left her"," and she gave birth to a boy whose two front teeth had emerged. The man recognized the resemblance in him and said: \""My son"," by the Lord of the Ka'bah!\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Women have been incapable of giving birth to the like of Mu'adh. Were it not for Mu'adh"," 'Umar would have been destroyed.\"" And if this is established"," it serves as evidence that pregnancy may remain for more than two years. And the statement of 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," regarding the wife of the missing man — that she should wait four years — resembles the possibility that he said it due to the pregnancy lasting four years. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""
"15565","(15559) Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajani informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanji informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Malik informed us, from Yazid ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hadi, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayyah: A woman's husband died, so she observed the waiting period of four months and ten days, then married again when she became lawful. She remained with her husband for four months and a half, and then gave birth to a complete child. Her husband came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and mentioned that to him. 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, called some women from the early Jahiliyyah and asked them about it. One of them said: \I will inform you about this woman. Her husband died while she was pregnant"," and her blood flowed"," causing the child in her womb to shrivel. Then the husband she married came to her"," and the child received moisture"," so the child moved in her womb and grew.\"" 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," believed her and separated them. 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""No good has reached me about you both","\"" and he attributed the child to the first husband. [Da'if]"""
"15566","(15560) Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us: Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us: Hisham ibn 'Urwah informed us, from his father, who said: A man would divorce his wife and then take her back, and there was no limit to which he could go back to her. A man from the Ansar said to his wife: \By Allah"," I will never shelter you to myself"," nor will you become lawful for anyone other than me.\"" She said: \""How is that?\"" He said: \""I will divorce you"," and when your term approaches"," I will take you back.\"" She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," complaining. So Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," revealed: \""Divorce is twice. Then either retain her in a good manner or release her with good treatment\"" [al-Baqarah 229]. So the people approached it as something new — those who had divorced and those who had not. And we have narrated this previously in a connected chain"," and in it is the indication that she would observe a waiting period counting from the last divorce. This is the statement of Abu al-Sha'tha'"," Tawus"," 'Amr ibn Dinar"," and others. [Sahih]"""
"15567","(15561) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Yahya ibn Hassan informed us, from Abu 'Awanah, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah al-Asadi, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said regarding the wife of the missing man: \She shall not marry.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15568","(15562) And Abu Zakariyya informed us: Abu al-'Abbas informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Yahya ibn Hassan informed us, from Hushaym ibn Bashir, from Sayyar, that is, Abu al-Hakam, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding the wife of the missing man: \If he arrives and his wife has married"," she is his wife — if he wishes"," he may divorce her"," and if he wishes"," she shall not be given a choice.\"" And Abu 'Ubayd narrated it from Hushaym"," from Sayyar"," from al-Sha'bi"," from 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him."""
"15569","(15563) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan informed us: Abu Usamah informed us: Zaydah ibn Qudamah informed us: Simak informed us, from Hanash, who said: 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \What 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said amounts to nothing\"" — meaning regarding the wife of the missing man: \""She is the wife of the absent one until there comes to her certain knowledge of his death or his divorce"," and she is entitled to her dower from this"," by virtue of what he made lawful of her private parts"," and his marriage is void.\"" And it has been narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Jubayr"," from 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who said: \""She is the wife of the first"," whether the other had intercourse with her or not.\"" And this is the statement of al-Nakha'i and al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah and others. [Da'if]"""
"15570","(15564) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-'Abbas, that is, al-Asamm, informed us: al-'Abbas, that is, al-Duri, said: I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in say: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, from Mansur ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Shubrumah, who said: 'Abd al-'Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, wrote regarding the wife of the missing man: \She should take her time and be patient.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15571","(15565) It is narrated in it a musnad hadith, in whose chain of narration there is one whose hadith is not used as a proof. Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir al-Saqaṭī informed us, Ṣāliḥ ibn Mālik informed us, Sawwār ibn Muṣʿab informed us, Muḥammad ibn Shurayḥīl al-Hamdānī narrated on the authority of al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The wife of the missing person remains his wife until clear evidence comes to her.\""\n\nZakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā al-Wāsiṭī likewise narrated it from Sawwār ibn Muṣʿab"," and Sawwār is weak (ḍaʿīf)."""
"15572","(15566) Abū Saʿid ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us on the authority of Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Any woman whose husband goes missing and she does not know where he is"," she shall wait four years"," then she shall wait four months and ten days.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15573","(15567) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik informed us, and he mentioned it with the same wording, adding: \Then she becomes lawful (to marry).\""\n\nYūnus ibn Yazīd narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," adding therein: \""And ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān ruled likewise after ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both).\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd narrated it in his book from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," from al-Awzāʿī"," from al-Zuhrī"," from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," that ʿUmar and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \""The wife of the missing person shall wait four years"," then she shall observe the waiting period of four months and ten days"," then she may marry.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15574","(15568) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Sulaymān al-Taymī informed us on the authority of Abī ʿAmr al-Shaybānī that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) set the term for the wife of the missing person at four years. [Ḥasan]"
"15575","(15569) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār informed us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Shuʿbah said: I heard Manṣūr narrate from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled regarding the missing person that his wife shall wait four years, then the guardian of her husband shall divorce her, then she shall wait after that four months and ten days, then she may marry.\n\nʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal narrated it from Abī ʿUthmān, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), with the like of that regarding the divorce by the guardian.\n\nLikewise, Mujāhid narrated it from the missing one over whom the jinn had taken control, from the ruling of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding that.\n\nKhilās ibn ʿAmr and Abū al-Malīḥ narrated it from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) with the like of that. The narration of Khilās from ʿAlī is weak (ḍaʿīfah), and the narration of Abū al-Malīḥ from ʿAlī is mursal. The well-known narration from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) is contrary to this.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd narrated in his book from Yazīd, from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ḥayshah, from ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from Jābir ibn Zayd, that he witnessed Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) discussing the wife of the missing person, and they both said: \She shall wait by herself four years"," then she shall observe the waiting period of death.\"" Then they mentioned the maintenance. Ibn ʿUmar said: \""She is entitled to maintenance because she has confined herself for his sake.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""If that is imposed"," it will harm the heirs. Rather"," let her spend from her own resources. If her husband returns"," she may take it from his wealth"," and if he does not return"," she shall have nothing.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15576","(15570) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī — in wording — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, Saʿīd informed us, from Qatādah, from Abī Naḍrah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, that a man from his people among the Anṣār went out to pray ʿIshāʾ with his people, and the jinn seized him, so he was missing. His wife went to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and recounted the story to him. ʿUmar asked his people about him, and they said: \Yes"," he went out to pray ʿIshāʾ and was missing.\"" So he commanded her to wait four years. When the four years had passed"," she came to him and informed him"," and he asked her people"," and they said: \""Yes.\"" So he commanded her to marry"," and she married. Then her husband came and brought a dispute regarding that to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""One of you disappears for a long time while his family does not know whether he is alive.\"" The man said to him: \""I have an excuse"," O Commander of the Faithful.\"" He said: \""What is your excuse?\"" He said: \""I went out to pray ʿIshāʾ and the jinn seized me"," and I remained among them for a long time. Then believing jinn — or he said Muslim jinn; Saʿīd was unsure — waged war against them"," fought them"," and overpowered them. They took captives from among them"," and they took me as a captive among those they captured. They said: 'We see you to be a Muslim man"," and it is not lawful for us to take you captive.' So they gave me the choice between staying and returning to my family"," and I chose to return to my family. They accompanied me. As for the night"," they did not speak to me"," and as for the daytime"," it was a gust of wind that I followed.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""What was your food among them?\"" He said: \""Beans and that over which the name of Allah was not mentioned.\"" He said: \""What was your drink among them?\"" He said: \""Al-jadf.\"" Qatādah said: \""Al-jadf is that drink which has not been fermented.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave him the choice between the dowry (ṣadāq) and his wife.\n\nSaʿīd said: And Maṭar narrated to me from Abī Naḍrah"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," the same hadith as that of Qatādah"," except that Maṭar added in it: He commanded her to wait four years and four months and ten days. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15577","(15571) He said: And ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Abū Masʿūd al-Jurayrī informed us, from Abī Naḍrah, from ʿAbd al-R-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), the same as what Qatādah narrated from Abī Naḍrah.\n\nThābit al-Bunānī narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā in abbreviated form, adding therein: \So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave him the choice between the dowry and his wife"," and he chose the dowry.\"" Ḥammād said: \""I think he said: So he gave him the dowry from the public treasury (bayt al-māl).\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us"," Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us"," Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī informed us"," ʿAffān informed us"," Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us"," Thābit informed us"," and he mentioned it.\n\nMujāhid narrated it from the missing one over whom the jinn had taken control"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\nIn the narration of Yūnus ibn Yazīd from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī"," from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," regarding the wife of the missing person"," he said: \""If her husband returns and she has already married"," he shall be given the choice between his wife and her dowry. If he chooses the dowry"," it shall be upon her other husband"," and if he chooses his wife"," she shall observe the waiting period until she becomes lawful"," then she shall return to her first husband"," and she shall be entitled to her dowry from her second husband for that by which he made her private parts lawful.\""\n\nIbn Shihāb said: \""And ʿUthmān ruled likewise after ʿUmar (may Allah"," the Most High"," be pleased with them both).\"" And Mālik ibn Anas used to reject the narration of those who narrated from ʿUmar regarding the choice (takhyīr). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15578","(15572) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik informed us, and he said: \I found the people rejecting what some people said on the authority of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"," that he said: 'Her husband shall be given the choice"," when he returns and she has married"," between her dowry and the woman.'\""\n\nMālik said: \""If she marries after the completion of the waiting period"," whether he has consummated the marriage with her or not"," then her first husband has no claim over her"," and that is the matter according to us.\"" Mālik (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""If her husband returns before her waiting period has ended"," then he has the greater right to her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15579","(15573) Abū Saʿid ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, and he said: I said to al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah be pleased with him): \Our companion said: 'I found those who reject what some people said on the authority of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).'\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""We have seen those who reject the entire ruling of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the missing person"," and they say: 'This does not resemble anything that could be from the ruling of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).' Is the proof against him anything other than the fact that trustworthy narrators"," when they transmitted it from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," were not accused? Likewise the proof is against you. And how is it permissible for trustworthy narrators to narrate a single hadith from ʿUmar and we take part of it and leave part of it?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15580","(15574) Abū Saʿid informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, al-Thaqafī informed us, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from al-Shaʿbī, from Masrūq — or he said: \I think it is from Masrūq\"" — who said: \""Were it not that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the missing person the choice between his wife and the dowry"," I would have considered that he has the greater right to her when he returns.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding the wife of the missing person: \""She is a woman who has been afflicted; let her be patient and not marry until she receives certainty of his death.\"" He said: \""And this is what we hold.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Qatādah narrated from Khilās ibn ʿAmr and from Abū al-Malīḥ"," from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: \""When the first husband returns"," he shall be given the choice between the latter dowry and his wife.\""\n\nThe narration of Khilās from ʿAlī is weak (ḍaʿīfah)"," and Abū al-Malīḥ did not hear it from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15581","(15575) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Ṣaydalānī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, saying: Abū Naṣr — meaning ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ — said: I asked Saʿīd about the missing person (al-mafqūd), and he informed us from Qatādah, from Abū al-Malīḥ al-Hudhalī, that he said: al-Ḥakam ibn Ayyūb sent me to Sahīmah bint ʿUmayr al-Shaybāniyyah to ask her, and she narrated to me that her husband Ṣayfī ibn Qatīl was announced dead to her from Qandābīl, so she married after him al-ʿAbbās ibn Ṭarīf al-Qaysī. Then her first husband arrived, and we came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān — may Allah be pleased with him — while he was besieged. He looked down upon us and said: \How shall I judge between you while I am in this state?\"" We said: \""We are pleased with your ruling.\"" So he ruled that the first husband be given the choice between the dowry (al-ṣadāq) and his wife. Then ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — was killed"," and we came to ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — and he ruled according to what ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — had said. He said: \""The first husband was given the choice between his wife and the dowry"," and he chose the dowry.\"" So he took from me two thousand and from my husband two thousand"," which was the dowry he had given to the woman. He said: She had been an umm walad (a slave woman who bore her master a child) who had married after him and borne children to her (new) husband. He (the first husband) restored her to him (the second husband) along with her children"," and he gave their father the right to ransom them.\n\nʿAbd al-Wahhāb said: Saʿīd said"," and Ayyūb narrated to us from Abū al-Malīḥ a similar hadith"," except that Ayyūb said: \""He made her children for their father.\"" Qatādah used to say: \""He takes the latter dowry.\"" And from Qatādah"," from al-Ḥasan"," that he said: \""He takes the first dowry.\"" This woman is not one whose narration establishes the proof for this report. Even if it is established"," it weakens the narration of Abū al-Malīḥ from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — as a mursal narration regarding the missing person. For this narration concerns a woman whose husband was announced dead to her"," whereas the well-known position from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — is what we have previously mentioned. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"15582","(15576) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — that he said regarding the umm walad whose master dies: \She observes an ʿidda of one menstrual cycle.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15583","(15577) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \The ʿidda of the umm walad is one menstrual cycle.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15584","(15578) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd that he said: I heard al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad saying: \Indeed Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-Malik separated between men and their wives who were the mothers of the children of men who had perished. They (the women) had married after one or two menstrual cycles"," so he separated between them until they observed an ʿidda of four months and ten days.\""\n\nAl-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad said: \""Glory be to Allah! Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," says in His Book: {And those who are taken in death among you and leave wives behind} (2:234) — they are not"," for them"," wives.\"" And from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad that he used to say: \""The ʿidda of the umm walad"," when her master dies"," is one menstrual cycle.\"" Mālik — may Allah have mercy on him — said: \""And that is the established practice (al-amr) with us.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15585","(15579) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Baghdādī al-Raffāʾ narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: \The ʿidda of the umm walad — whether her master frees her or dies — is one menstrual cycle.\"" [Weak]"""
"15586","(15580) As for the hadith which Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us of — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah. He said: And Yūsuf narrated, and Abū al-Khaṭṭāb narrated to us; Abū Baḥr al-Bakrāwī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah. He said: And Maṭar narrated from Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah from Qabīṣah ibn Dhūʾayb from ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \Do not obscure for us the Sunnah of our Prophet ﷺ. Her ʿidda is the ʿidda of a woman whose husband has died: four months and ten days.\"" In the narration of Yazīd: \""The ʿidda of the umm walad is four months and ten days.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us"," saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \""Qabīṣah did not hear from ʿAmr"," and the correct wording is: 'Do not obscure for us our religion' — and it is mawqūf (stopped at the Companion).\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15587","(15581) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to me; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā from Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah from Qabīṣah ibn Dhūʾayb from ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: \The ʿidda of the umm walad is the ʿidda of a free woman.\"" My father said: \""This is a munkar (objectionable) hadith.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"15588","(15582) He said: And al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī and Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from al-Zuhrī from Qabīṣah ibn Dhūʾayb from ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \The ʿidda of the umm walad is the ʿidda of a free woman.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15589","(15583) The Shaykh said: And Abū Maʿbad Ḥafṣ ibn Ghaylān narrated it from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā with his chain of narration up to ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: \The ʿidda of the umm walad"," when her master dies"," is four months and ten days"," and if she is freed"," her ʿidda is three menstrual cycles.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us"," saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Yaqṭīnī narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd al-Khallāl al-Dimashqī narrated to us; Zayd ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Abū Maʿbad narrated it.\n\nʿAlī said: \""It is mawqūf"," and that is the correct view"," and it is mursal (incomplete in the chain)"," because Qabīṣah did not hear from ʿAmr.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15590","(15584) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Abū Tawbah narrated from Suwayd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz from ʬAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rābāḥ that Māriyah observed an ʿidda of three menstrual cycles after the Prophet ﷺ — meaning Umm Ibrāhīm. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected in the chain). Suwayd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz is weak (ḍaʿīf), and the narration of the group from ʬAṭāʾ represents his madhhab over this narration. [Weak]"
"15591","(15585) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us, Ismā'īl ibn Zurārah narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Qurashī narrated to us, al-'Umarī narrated from Nāfi', who said: Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the 'iddah of an umm al-walad, and he said: \One menstrual cycle.\"" A man said: \""Indeed"," 'Uthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say three menstrual cycles.\"" He said: \""'Uthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) is the best of us and the most knowledgeable of us.\""\n\nThere is weakness in this chain of narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15592","(15586) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Walīd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us, Wakī' narrated from Ibn Abī 'Arūbah, from Qatādah, from Khilās ibn 'Amr, from 'Alī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The 'iddah of an umm al-walad is four months and ten days.\"" Wakī' said: \""This means when her husband dies after her master (owner).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The narrations of Khilās from 'Alī (may Allah be pleased with him) are not considered strong among the scholars of hadith; they say it is extremely weak. [Ḍa'īf]"""
"15593","(15587) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Awn informed us, Sharīk narrated from Qays ibn Wahb, from Abū al-Wadāk, from Abū Sa'īd al-Khudrī, who attributed it (marfū'an), saying that he said regarding the female captives of Awṭās: \A pregnant woman shall not be approached until she gives birth"," and one who is not pregnant shall not be approached until she has one menstrual cycle.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by al-Sha'bī from the Prophet (peace be upon him) in a mursal form. [Ḍa'īf]"""
"15594","(15588) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq — and Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, al-Nufaylī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated to me, from Abū Marzūq, from Ḥanash al-Ṣan'ānī, from Ruwayfi' ibn Thābith al-Anṣārī, who said: A preacher stood among us and said: \Indeed"," I say to you only what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say on the day of Ḥunayn.\"" He said: \""It is not permissible for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to water his crop with the water of another\"" — meaning"," to approach pregnant women — \""and it is not permissible for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to lie with a woman from the captives until he has ascertained her purity (istibrā')"," and it is not permissible for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to sell from the war spoils until they have been divided.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Salamah. In the narration of Ibn Bukayr"," it says: \""We went on campaign with Abū Ruwayfi' al-Anṣārī"," and he mentioned it"," and said: 'On the day of Khaybar","'\"" and he added: \""to approach a thayyib woman from the captions.\""\n\nThe authentic narration is that of Muḥammad ibn Salamah. [Ḥasan]"""
"15595","(15589) Abū 'Alī informed us, Abū Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Sa'īd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated from Ibn Isḥāq this hadith, saying: \Until he has ascertained her purity by means of a menstrual cycle.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \""The menstrual cycle is not preserved (as a reliable addition).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Meaning"," in the hadith of Ruwayfi'. [Ḥasan"," excluding the words \""by means of a menstrual cycle\""]"""
"15596","(15590) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us, 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated from Yazīd ibn Khumayr, who said: I heard 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr narrating from his father, from Abū al-Dardā' (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saw a pregnant woman near the entrance of a tent — or he said, a pavilion — and said: \Perhaps the owner of this (tent) approaches her. I have resolved to curse him with a curse that will enter the grave with him. How can he inherit from her when it is not lawful for him"," and how can he treat her as a slave when it is not lawful for him?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār"," from Abū Dāwūd. The mujihḥ is a pregnant woman near term"," and this is because he may see her as being pregnant when she is not"," so he approaches her and she becomes pregnant from him"," and he sees her as a slave when she is not a slave. What is intended by this is that he (peace be upon him) prohibited the approaching of female captives before ascertaining purity (istibrā'). [Ṣaḥīḥ 1441]"""
"15597","(15591) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Alī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Wazīr al-Dimashqī narrated to us, Marwān ibn Muḥammad narrated — and Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣā'id narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn 'Atīq al-'Absī narrated to us in Damascus, Marwān al-Dimashqī narrated to us — Ismā'īl ibn 'Ayyāsh narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace be upon him) ascertained the purity (istibrā') of Ṣafiyyah by means of a menstrual cycle.\n\nThere is weakness in its chain of narration. [Ḍa'īf]"
"15598","(15592) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad al-Fārisī al-Mashshāṭ informed us, Abū 'Amr ibn Maṭar informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ma'īn narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated from 'Ubayd Allāh, from Nāfi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \The 'iddah of an umm al-walad when her master dies"," and of a slave woman when she is emancipated or given as a gift"," is one menstrual cycle.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn Mas'ūd that he said: \""A slave woman is to be given istibrā' by means of one menstrual cycle.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥasan"," 'Aṭā'"," Ibn Sīrīn"," and 'Ikrimah that they said: \""He should ascertain her purity (istibrā') even if she is a virgin.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15599","(15593) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated from Khālid, from Abū Qilābah and Ibn Sīrīn, regarding a man who performs istibrā' with a slave woman who does not menstruate: \They both did not consider that this could be ascertained except by three months.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15600","(15594) He said, and Abū Bakr narrated to us from Ibn 'Ulayyah, from Layth, from Ṭāwūs and 'Aṭā', who said: \And if she does not menstruate"," then (the period is) three months.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""
"15601","(15595) He said: And Abū Bakr narrated to us from Muʿtamir from Ṣadaqah ibn Yasār from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, who said: \Three months.\""\n\nAnd it has also been narrated to us from Mujāhid and Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15602","(15596) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: \The ʿiddah of the woman who seeks khulʿ is the ʿiddah of the divorced woman.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And this is the view of Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," Sulaymān ibn Yasār"," al-Zuhrī"," al-Shaʿbī"," and the majority. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15603","(15597) As for the ḥadīth which Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī al-Bazzāz narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿUthmān al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Baḥr ibn Barrī narrated to us; Hishām ibn Yūsuf narrated from Maʿmar from ʿAmr ibn Muslim from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both: \That the wife of Thābit ibn Qays"," may Allah be pleased with him"," sought khulʿ from him"," so the Prophet ﷺ made her ʿiddah one menstrual cycle.\""\n\nThus narrated it ʿAlī ibn Baḥr and Ismāʿīl ibn Yazīd al-Baṣrī and others from Hishām from Maʿmar"," as a connected (mawṣūl) narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15604","(15598) And ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it from Maʿmar but sent it as a mursal narration. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us from Maʿmar from ʿAmr ibn Muslim from ʿIkrimah: \That the wife of Thābit ibn Qays sought khulʿ from him"," so the Prophet ﷺ made her ʿiddah one menstrual cycle.\"" And that has been narrated from two other weak chains"," and it is not permissible to use such as evidence. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15605","(15599) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb narrated to us; al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh, may Allah be pleased with her: \That she sought khulʿ during the time of the Prophet ﷺ"," so the Prophet ﷺ commanded her — or she was commanded — to observe an ʿiddah of one menstrual cycle.\"""""
"15606","(15600) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUlayl al-ʿAnazī narrated to us; Abū Kurayb narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the mawlā of the family of Ṭalḥah, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ: \That she sought khulʿ from her husband"," so she was commanded to observe an ʿiddah of one menstrual cycle.\""\n\nThis is more authentic"," and in it there is no mention of who commanded her"," nor the phrase \""during the time of the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated in the Kitāb al-Khulʿ that she sought khulʿ from her husband during the time of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15607","(15601) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Sharīk narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us; Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Nāfiʿ that Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him: \That al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ sought khulʿ from her husband during the time of ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him. Her paternal uncle"," Muʿādh ibn ʿAfrāʾ"," went to ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and said: 'The daughter of Muʿawwidh has sought khulʿ from her husband today — should she move?' ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'She may move"," and there is no ʿiddah upon her; she shall not remarry until she has experienced one menstrual cycle.'\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""ʿUthmān is the eldest among us and the most knowledgeable among us.\""\n\nThis narration makes explicit that it was ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who commanded her to do so. And the apparent meaning of the Book regarding the ʿiddah of divorced women encompasses the woman who seeks khulʿ and others; that is more appropriate. And success is through Allah"," and Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15608","(15602) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd ibn Ṣakhr al-Dārimī narrated to us; Ḥabbān ibn Hilāl narrated to us; Hammām said: I heard Qatādah narrating from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both: \That ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," purchased Barīrah and emancipated her"," stipulating the walāʾ (right of clientage). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed that walāʾ belongs to the one who emancipates"," and he gave her the choice"," so she chose herself (her freedom). He separated them and imposed upon her the ʿiddah of a free woman.\""\n\nAbū Bakr said: \""Ḥabbān excelled in his wording 'the ʿiddah of a free woman","' because ʿAffān ibn Muslim and ʿAmr ibn ʿĀṣim both narrated it and said: 'He commanded her to observe an ʿiddah","' without mentioning 'the ʿiddah of a free woman.'\""\n\nImām Aḥmad"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""And likewise Ḥudbah narrated it from Hammām: 'He commanded her to observe the ʿiddah of a free woman.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15609","(15603) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād al-Dabbāgh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jāmiʿ narrated to us; al-Muʿtamir narrated from al-Ḥajjāj al-Bāhilī from Qatādah from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, and he mentioned the story of Barīrah. He said: And Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, narrated that Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated: \That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made her ʿiddah the ʿiddah of a free woman.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15610","(15604) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us; Abū Maʿshar informed us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her: \That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the ʿiddah of Barīrah the ʿiddah of a divorced woman when she separated from her husband.\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated it from Abū Maʿshar and said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to observe the ʿiddah of a free woman.\"" And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15611","(15605) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us (ḥ). And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣighghī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād al-Surrī narrated us: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to me: Mālik informed me (ḥ). And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik, from ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Bakr, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she informed her that the Prophet (ﷺ) was with her, and she heard the voice of a man seeking permission to enter the house of Ḥafṣah. ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I said, \O Messenger of Allah"," this man is seeking permission to enter your house.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""I think it is so-and-so","\"" referring to the foster paternal uncle of Ḥafṣah. I said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," if so-and-so"," her foster paternal uncle"," were alive"," would he be permitted to enter upon me?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Yes"," indeed"," fosterage prohibits what birth prohibits.\""\n\nThis is the wording of al-Shāfiʿī's hadith. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15612","(15606) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Hāshim ibn al-Burayd narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \What is prohibited by fosterage is what is prohibited by birth.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Maʿmar al-Hudhalī"," from ʿAlī ibn Hāshim. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15613","(15607) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ibn Milḥān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said:\n\n(ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me (ḥ), and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān informed me: Shuʿayb narrated to me, from al-Zuhrī: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Aflaḥ, the brother of Abī al-Quʿays, sought permission to enter upon me after the Ḥijāb had been revealed. I said to him, \I will not grant you permission until I seek the permission of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," for the brother of Abī al-Quʿays did not nurse me; rather"," the wife of Abī al-Quʿays nursed me.\"" She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me"," and I said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," Aflaḥ"," the brother of Abī al-Quʿays"," sought permission to enter upon me"," and I refused to grant him permission until I sought your permission in that regard.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me"," \""What prevents you from granting permission to your paternal uncle?\"" I said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," the man did not nurse me; rather"," his wife nursed me.\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Grant him permission"," for he is your paternal uncle — may your right hand be dusty.\""\n\nʿUrwah said: Because of this"," ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) used to say"," \""Prohibit through fosterage what you prohibit through lineage.\""\n\nThis is the wording of Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah. And in the narration of ʿUqayl: \""After the Ḥijāb was revealed"," I said"," 'By Allah"," I will not grant him permission until I seek the permission of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)","'\"" and the remainder is similar. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr and from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15614","(15608) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbdillāh ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, with this hadith. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah, from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15615","(15609) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Hishām informed us, from his father, who said: ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) informed me that her paternal uncle, the brother of Abī al-Quʿays, came seeking permission to enter upon her after the Ḥijāb had been enjoined. She refused to grant him permission until she could come to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and seek his permission. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came, she mentioned that to him and said, \My paternal uncle"," the brother of Abī al-Quʿays"," came"," and I turned him away until I could seek your permission.\"" He said"," \""Is he not your paternal uncle?\"" She said"," \""It was the woman who nursed me"," not the man.\"" He said"," \""He is your paternal uncle"," so let him enter upon you.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) used to prohibit through fosterage what she prohibited through birth.\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15616","(15610) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: al-Ḥakam narrated to us, from ʿIrāk ibn Mālik, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Aflaḥ, the brother of Abī al-Quʿays, sought permission to enter upon me, and I did not grant him permission. He said, \Do you observe ḥijāb from me when I am your paternal uncle?\"" She said: I said"," \""How is that?\"" He said"," \""The wife of my brother nursed you with my brother's milk.\"" She said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he said"," \""Aflaḥ has spoken the truth"," so grant him permission.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15617","(15611) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbdillāh ibn Wahb informed me: al-Layth informed me.\n\n(ḥ) He said: And Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — and the wording is his —: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿIrāk ibn Mālik, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she informed him that her foster paternal uncle, named Aflaḥ, sought permission to enter upon her, and she observed ḥijāb from him. She informed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he said to her, \Do not observe ḥijāb"," for what is prohibited by fosterage is what is prohibited by lineage.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15618","(15612) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAnbar informed us: Hudbah ibn Khālid narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us: Qatādah narrated to us (ḥ). And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī ibn Mukram in Baghdād narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Jābir ibn Zayd, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (ﷺ) was proposed to regarding the daughter of Ḥamzah. He said, \She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my foster brother. Indeed"," Allah has prohibited through fosterage what He has prohibited through lineage.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Hudbah: \""She is not suitable for me; she is the daughter of my foster brother. And what is prohibited by fosterage is what is prohibited by lineage.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm"," and Muslim narrated it from Hudbah ibn Khālid. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15619","(15613) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Shaybānī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, from Sufyān, from al-Aʿmash, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I said, \O Messenger of Allah"," why is it that I see you showing preference to Quraysh and leaving us?\"" He said"," \""Do you have someone?\"" I said"," \""Yes"," the daughter of Ḥamzah.\"" He said"," \""She is the daughter of my foster brother.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — 1446]"""
"15620","(15614) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Makhramah informed me, from his father, who said: I heard ʿAbdillāh ibn Muslim say: I heard Muḥammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhrī say: I heard Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān say: I heard Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), say: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), \What is your opinion regarding the daughter of Ḥamzah?\"" — or it was said"," \""Why do you not propose to the daughter of Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib?\"" He said"," \""Indeed"," Ḥamzah is my foster brother.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn al-Aylī and others"," from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15621","(15615) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; al-Humaydi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), that she said: \O Messenger of Allah"," do you have any interest in Durrah"," the daughter of Abu Sufyan?\"" He said: \""What should I do?\"" She said: \""I said: 'Marry her.'\"" He said: \""Would you like that?\"" I said: \""I am not one to leave you free [to choose without consultation]"," and I would love for my sister to share in any good that comes to me.\"" He said: \""She is not lawful for me.\"" I said: \""It has reached me that you have sent a proposal of marriage to Zaynab bint Abi Salamah.\"" He said: \""The daughter of Umm Salamah?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," were she not my foster-daughter under my care"," she would have been lawful for me. Indeed"," Thuwaybah suckled me and her father. So do not offer your daughters or your sisters to me [in marriage].\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from al-Humaydi"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Hisham. They said therein"," from Hisham: \""Durrah bint Abi Salamah.\"" And al-Zuhri said it from 'Urwah"," and said: \""Marry my sister 'Azzah.\"" And some of them reported from al-Zuhri: \""Thuwaybah suckled me and Abu Salamah.\"" [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"15622","(15616) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us; Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi narrated to us; my uncle Iyas ibn 'Amir narrated to me, he said: \Do not marry the one whom your father's wife suckled"," nor the one whom your son's wife suckled"," nor the one whom your brother's wife suckled.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15623","(15617) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Malik narrated to us — and Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Ibn Qa'nab, Ibn Bukayr, and Abu al-Walid narrated from Malik — from Ibn Shihab, from 'Amr ibn al-Sharid, that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked about a man who had two wives, one of whom suckled a boy and the other suckled a girl. It was said: \Can the boy marry the girl?\"" He said: \""No. The milk relationship (al-lahā') is one [i.e."," they share the same father].\"" [Sahih]"""
"15624","(15618) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Mu'alla narrated to us; Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to me; Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated from Muhammad, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: \That which is prohibited through suckling is that which is prohibited through lineage (nasab).\""\n\nAnd this position has been narrated from the Successors from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad"," Jabir ibn Zayd Abu al-Sha'tha'"," 'Ata'"," Tawus"," Mujahid"," and al-Zuhri. [Sahih]"""
"15625","(15619) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzzi narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Malik narrated to us — and Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz in Naysabur, Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran, and Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ishaq al-Bazzaz in Baghdad informed us; Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Fakihi narrated to us; Abu Yahya ibn Abi Masarrat narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Azraq narrated to us; Malik ibn Anas narrated to us — and Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Malik narrated to us — and Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Hajjaj and Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam narrated to us; they said: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; he said: I read to Malik — from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said: \There was revealed in the Qur'an ten known sucklings that prohibit [marriage]"," then they were abrogated by five known sucklings. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed away while it was still being recited in the Qur'an.\"" In the narration of Ibn Yusuf: \""five known sucklings that prohibit [marriage].\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih — 1452]"""
"15626","(15620) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; he said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \There was revealed in the Qur'an ten known sucklings"," then they were subsequently replaced by five"," or by five known sucklings.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna. [Sahih]"""
"15627","(15621) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzzi narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she used to say: \There was revealed in the Qur'an ten known sucklings that prohibit [marriage]"," then they were reduced to five that prohibit [marriage]"," and no one would enter upon 'A'ishah except one who had completed five sucklings.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15628","(15622) Abu Tahir al-Faqih, Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us; Anas ibn Iyyad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, who related that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \One suckling does not prohibit [marriage]"," nor do two sucklings.\"" [Sahih — 1450]"""
"15629","(15623) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed me; Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Anas ibn Iyyad narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Rabi' said: I said to al-Shafi'i (may Allah be pleased with him): \Did Ibn al-Zubayr hear from the Prophet (peace be upon him)?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and he memorized from him. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed away"," he was nine years old.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It is as al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said"," except that Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) took this hadith from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," from the Prophet (peace be upon him). [Sahih]"""
"15630","(15624) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas, who is al-Asamm, narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Abu 'Ubayd narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Prophet (peace be upon him), the same [hadith]. [Sahih]"
"15631","(15625) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us: al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: al-Nufaylī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \One suckling or two sucklings do not establish prohibition (of marriage).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others"," from Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUlayyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15632","(15626) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Hāshimī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\nAnd Ayyūb narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). One of them said: \One suckling or two sucklings do not establish prohibition.\"" And the other said: \""One imlājah or two imlājahs do not establish prohibition.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15633","(15627) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated from Abī al-Khalīl, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith, from Umm al-Faḍl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in my house when a Bedouin came to him and said: \I had a woman (wife)"," and I married another woman upon her. My first wife claims that she suckled my new wife once or twice"," or gave her one imlājah or two imlājahs.\"" He said: \""One imlājah or two imlājahs do not establish prohibition.\"" Or he said: \""One suckling or two sucklings do not establish prohibition.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ"," 1451]"""
"15634","(15628) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated from Abī al-Khalīl, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith, from Umm al-Faḍl, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was in my house and said: \O Prophet of Allah"," I had a woman (wife)"," and I married another upon her. My first wife claims that she suckled my new wife once or twice.\"" The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""One imlājah or two imlājahs do not establish prohibition.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15635","(15629) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Abū al-Bakhtarī ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us: Qatādah narrated from Abī al-Khalīl, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith, from Umm al-Faḍl (may Allah be pleased with her), who reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \One suckling or two sucklings"," or one nursing or two nursings"," do not establish prohibition.\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī ʿArūbah and Ḥammād ibn Salamah"," from Qatādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15636","(15630) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Tamtām narrated to us: Abū Salamah narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us: Qatādah narrated from Abī al-Khalīl. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Qabbānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Muthannā narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to me: My father narrated to us: Qatādah narrated from Ṣāliḥ Abī al-Khalīl, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith, from Umm al-Faḍl, that a man from Banī ʿĀmir ibn Ṣaʿṣaʿah said: \O Prophet of Allah"," does one suckling establish prohibition?\"" He said: \""No.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Hishām. And in the narration of Hammām it is: \""A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about one suckling: does it establish prohibition?\"" He said: \""No.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muthannā"," and he extracted it through another chain from Hammām. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15637","(15631) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered the wife of Abī Ḥudhayfah to give Sālim five nursings so that he would become prohibited (in marriage) through her milk. She did so, and she used to regard him as a son.\n\nThis story was narrated by Yūnus ibn Yazīd from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah and Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with both of them). And it was narrated by Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah and ʿUqayl ibn Khālid from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15638","(15632) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \Fewer than five known nursings do not establish prohibition.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ"," Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15639","(15633) Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-ʿAṭṭār al-Naysābūrī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn al-Akhr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm said: Musaddad narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us: Ashʿath ibn Sulaym narrated from his father, from Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered upon me while a man was sitting with me. This upset him greatly, and I saw anger on his face. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," he is my foster brother.\"" He said: \""Consider who your foster brothers are"," for foster relationship is established by that which satisfies hunger (i.e."," full suckling that nourishes).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hannād ibn al-Sarī"," from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ"," and both of them extracted it from the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī and Shuʿbah"," from Ashʿath. [Ṣaḥīḥ"," Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15640","(15634) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj—I think—from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Nothing establishes prohibition through suckling except that which opens the intestines (i.e."," substantial nourishment).\""\n\nAnd similarly al-Zuhrī narrated it from ʿUrwah"," from al-Ḥajjāj al-Aslamī"," from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," as a mawqūf narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15641","(15635) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Jarīr narrated — and ʿAlī said: Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Karkhī narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Jarīr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr used to narrate from al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A single suckling or two sucklings do not establish prohibition (through breastfeeding). Nothing establishes prohibition except that which opens the intestines.\""\n\nAnd ʿUthmān said: \""Nothing establishes prohibition except milk which opens the intestines.\""\n\nAnd al-Zuhrī and Hishām narrated it from ʿUrwah as a mawqūf narration from Abū Hurayrah with part of its meaning. [Weak]"""
"15642","(15636) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Mu'mmal informed us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Marwān narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated to us from Qays from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Al-Fiqah does not establish prohibition.\"" We said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is al-Fiqah?\"" He said: \""A woman gives birth and the milk collects in her breasts"," and she lets her neighbour suckle once or twice.\"" [Denounced (Munkar)]"""
"15643","(15637) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Baghdādī narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb and ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ ibn Ḍamrah said: We read to Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī from Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān, who said: Sālim was asked about breastfeeding that establishes prohibition. He narrated to us: Zayd ibn Thābit informed us that a single breastfeeding, two breastfeedings, and three do not establish prohibition. [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ), except his words \and three do not establish prohibition\""]"""
"15644","(15638) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us from Nāfiʿ that Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh informed him that ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), sent him while he was being breastfed to her sister Umm Kulthūm, and she breastfed him three times. Then she fell ill and did not breastfeed him other than three times. So I would not enter upon ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) because Umm Kulthūm had not completed ten breastfeedings for me. [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"
"15645","(15639) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us, who said: al-Shāfiʿī said: ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) ordered that he be breastfed ten times, because that was the greater number of breastfeedings, and five had not been completed for him. So he would not enter upon her. And perhaps Sālim may have referred to the statement of ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding the ten breastfeedings, that they were abrogated by five known ones. [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"
"15646","(15640) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us from Nāfiʿ from Ṣafiyyah bint Abī ʿUbayd, who informed him that Ḥafṣah Umm al-Mu'minīn (may Allah be pleased with her) sent ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿd to her sister Fāṭimah bint ʿUmar to breastfeed him ten breastfeedings so that he could enter upon her while he was a small child being breastfed. She did so, and he used to enter upon her. [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"
"15647","(15641) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ narrated to us from Saʿīd from Qatādah, who said: We wrote to Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd — Saʿīd said: We were uncertain whether he was al-Nakhaʿī or al-Taymī — Maṭar said: He is al-Nakhaʿī — regarding breastfeeding. And he wrote to us that Sharīḥ narrated that ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \Breastfeeding establishes prohibition"," whether little or much.\"" And he said: \""And in his letter was that Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ al-Muḥāribī narrated that ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: 'A single hurried suckling and two hurried sucklings do not establish prohibition.'\"" [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"15648","(15642) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, who said: Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a matter concerning breastfeeding. He said: \I do not know except that Allah has prohibited the sister through breastfeeding.\"" I said: \""Indeed"," Amīr al-Mu'minīn Ibn al-Zubayr says: 'A single breastfeeding"," two breastfeedings"," a single suckling"," and two sucklings do not establish prohibition.'\"" Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""The decree of Allah is better than your decree and the decree of Amīr al-Mu'minīn along with you.\"" [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"15649","(15643) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, who heard a man say to Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both): \Indeed"," Amīr al-Mu'minīn Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: 'A single breastfeeding and two breastfeedings do not establish prohibition.'\"" Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""The Book of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," is more truthful than Amīr al-Mu'minīn.\"" He then recited: \""Forbidden to you are your mothers"," your daughters"," your sisters…\"" until he reached: \""…and your mothers who breastfed you and your sisters through breastfeeding.\"" [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"15650","(15644) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us; Abū Khaythamah narrated to us; Abū al-Zubayr narrated to us, who said: ʬAṭāʾ sent me and a man with me to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), and we asked him about a woman who breastfeeds a baby boy in the cradle or a young girl a single breastfeeding. He said: \She is forbidden to him.\"" I said: \""Indeed"," ʿĀ'ishah and Ibn al-Zubayr claim that a single breastfeeding"," two"," or three do not establish prohibition.\"" He said: \""The Book of Allah is more truthful than their statement","\"" and he recited the verse of breastfeeding. [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"15651","(15645) Abū al-Qāsim — ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī al-Mu'adhdhin — informed us; Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl — narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān — narrated to me; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways — narrated to me, from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās used to say: \A little breastfeeding and much of it both establish prohibition (taḥrīm) during the nursing period.\"" Ibn Shihāb said: \""There is no breastfeeding after two complete years.\""\n\nSuch is the narration of Ibn ʿAbbās in this report. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15652","(15646) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us; Wuhaib narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us, that he asked ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr about one suckling and two sucklings. He said: \ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," did not consider one suckling or two sucklings to establish prohibition; she did not consider prohibition to be established except by ten or more.\""\n\nHe said: \""So I went to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and asked him about one breastfeeding and two breastfeedings. He said: 'Indeed"," I do not say about it what Ibn al-Zubayr and Ibn ʿAbbāsh"," may Allah be pleased with them"," said.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'How did they both say?' He said: 'They both used to say: One suckling and two sucklings do not establish prohibition"," and prohibition is not established by less than ten breastfeedings or more.'\"" And ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated it from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah.\n\nAnd the narration of al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah is more authentic regarding the view of ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," and the narration of ʿUrwah from Ibn ʿAbbāsh"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," is more authentic regarding his view. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15653","(15647) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — informed us; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī — in Makkah — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀ'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \Sahlāh bint Suhayl ibn ʿAmr came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I see in the face of Abū Ḥudhayfah the displeasure caused by Sālim's entering upon me.' He said: 'Breastfeed him.' She said: 'But he is a grown man.' He smiled and said: 'Do I not know that he is a grown man?'\"" She said: \""She came to him afterwards and said: 'I did not see anything in the face of Abū Ḥudhayfah after that which I disliked.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr al-Nāqid and Ibn Abī ʿAmr"," from Ibn ʿUyaynah.\n\nAnd the fuqahā' are of the opinion that what is meant by breastfeeding here is that Sahlāh bint Suhayl should express her milk into a vessel and send it to Sālim to drink"," and that this be repeated five times"," and by that she becomes prohibited for him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15654","(15648) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibn Milḥān — who is Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me"," from ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," that Abū Ḥudhayfah ibn ʿUtbah ibn Rabīʿah ibn ʿAbd Shams"," may Allah be pleased with him — and he was among those who witnessed Badr with the Prophet ﷺ — adopted Sālim and married him to his brother's daughter Hind bint al-Walīd ibn ʿUtbah ibn Rabīʿah"," who was a freedwoman of a woman of the Anṣār"," just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ adopted Zayd ibn Ḥārithah. And whoever adopted a man in the Jāhiliyyah"," the people would call him his son and he would inherit from his estate"," until Allah revealed regarding that: 'Call them by [the names of] their fathers; it is more just in the sight of Allah. And if you do not know their fathers — then they are your brothers in religion and your freedmen.' [Al-Aḥzāb 33:5] So they were returned to their fathers. Whoever's father was not known became a freedman and a brother in religion. Then Sahlāh bint Suhayl ibn ʿAmr al-Qurashī"," then al-ʿĀmirī — and she was the wife of Abū Ḥudhayfah"," may Allah be pleased with them both — came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we used to consider Sālim a son"," and he used to live with me and Abū Ḥudhayfah in one house and he would see me in a state of undress. And Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has revealed regarding them what You know. What do You think about him"," O Messenger of Allah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Breastfeed him.' So she breastfed him five times"," and he became in the position of her son through breastfeeding. Because of this"," ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," used to command her brothers' daughters to breastfeed whomever ʿĀ'ishah wished to see and to enter upon her — five breastfeedings — so that he could enter upon her. And Umm Salamah and the other wives of the Prophet ﷺ refused to allow anyone among the people to enter upon them on the basis of that breastfeeding"," even if they were nursed in the cradle. They said to ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her: 'By Allah"," we think this was a concession (rukhṣah) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted specifically to Sālim"," not to other people.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15655","(15649) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsá narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed me; Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated to me, from al-Zuhrī, who said: \ʿUrwah informed me"," from ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her","\"" and he mentioned the hadith in its full length"," similar to it"," except that he said: \""Because of this"," ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," used to command her brothers' daughters and her sisters' daughters.\"" And he said: \""Umm Salamah and the other wives of the Prophet ﷺ refused to allow anyone among the people to enter upon them on the basis of that breastfeeding.\"" And the rest is the same.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr and from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15656","(15650) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to me; Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to me; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to me; my father narrated to me, from my grandfather; ʿUqayl ibn Khālid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \Abū ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zamʿah informed me that his mother Zaynab bint Abī Salamah informed him that her mother Umm Salamah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," used to say: 'The rest of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ refused to allow anyone to enter upon them on the basis of that breastfeeding. And they said to ʿĀ'ishah: \""By Allah"," we think this was a concession that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted specifically to Sālim. So no one enters upon us on the basis of this breastfeeding"," nor does anyone see us.\""'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ thus.\n\nal-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""If this was specific to Sālim"," then the specific (khāṣṣ) can only be an exception from the general ruling"," and it is not permissible except that the breastfeeding of an adult does not establish prohibition.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15657","(15651) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Muḥammad ibn Rāshid al-Tammār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthā', from his father, from Masrūq, from ʿĀ'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while a man was with me. He said: 'O ʿĀ'ishah"," who is this?' I said: 'My brother through breastfeeding.' He said: 'O ʿĀ'ishah"," look at who your brothers are"," for breastfeeding is only that which satisfies hunger (al-majāʿah).'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," and Muslim narrated it from two other routes from Sufyān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15658","(15652) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd, Bishr ibn ʿUmar, and Wahb ibn Jarīr said: Shuʿbah informed us, from al-Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthā', from his father, who said: \I heard Masrūq say: 'I heard ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," say: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while a man was with me"," and I saw displeasure on his face. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," he is my brother through breastfeeding.' She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Look at whom you breastfeed"," for breastfeeding is only that which satisfies hunger.'\"" And Bishr said in his hadith: 'Look at who your brothers are.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15659","(15653) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Khallād ibn Aslam narrated to us; al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us; Abū Mūsá narrated to us, from his father, from a son of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, that a man was with his wife on a journey and she gave birth. The infant could not suck, so her husband took to sucking her milk and spitting it out until he found the taste of her milk in his throat. He came to Abū Mūsá and mentioned that to him. He said: \Your wife has become prohibited for you.\"" He then came to Ibn Masʿūd"," who said: \""Are you the one who issues such-and-such a fatwa"," when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no breastfeeding except that which strengthens the bone and causes the flesh to grow'?\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15660","(15654) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Muṭahhar narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to them, from Abū Mūsá, from his father, from a son of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \There is no breastfeeding except that which strengthens the bone and causes the flesh to grow.\"" Abū Mūsá said: \""Do not ask us while this scholar (al-ḥabr) is among you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15661","(15655) Abū Dāwūd said: And Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Anbārī narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated to us, from Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah, from Abū Mūsā al-Hilālī, from his father, from Ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace be upon him), with the same meaning, and he said: \He raised the bone.\"" [Weak]"""
"15662","(15656) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Abū Hishām al-Rifāʿī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, Abū Ḥuṣayn narrated to us, from Abū ʿAṭiyyah, who said: A man came to Abū Mūsā and said, \My wife's breast became swollen"," so I sucked it"," and something entered my throat that overtook me.\"" Abū Mūsā was strict about it"," so he went to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿud and said"," \""Did you ask anyone other than me?\"" He said"," \""Yes"," Abū Mūsā"," and he was strict with me.\"" So he went to Abū Mūsā and said"," \""Is this one a nursling?\"" Abū Mūsā said"," \""Do not ask me as long as this scholar is among you","\"" or he said"," \""as long as he is in your midst.\""\n\nAl-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Ḥuṣayn and added therein"," from ʿAbdullāh: \""Indeed"," nursing is only that which builds flesh and blood.\"" [Good]"""
"15663","(15657) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Saʿīd, from Juwaybir, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Muzāḥim, from al-Nazzāl ibn Sabrah and Masrūq ibn al-Ajdaʿ, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \There is no nursing after weaning.\""\n\nThis is a mauqūf narration"," and it has also been narrated as marfūʿ. [Weak]"""
"15664","(15658) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed him, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Abū Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī narrated to us, Ibn Abī al-Sarī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar informed us, from Juwaybir, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk, from al-Nazzāl ibn Sabrah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \There is no divorce except after marriage"," and no emancipation before ownership"," and no nursing after weaning"," and no waṣāl in fasting"," and no silence for a day until night.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Razzāq said: Sufyān said to Maʿmar"," \""Indeed"," Juwaybir narrated this ḥadīth to us but did not raise it.\"" Maʿmar said"," \""He narrated it to us repeatedly and raised it.\"" [Weak]"""
"15665","(15659) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, who said: A man came to Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) while I was with him at the house of judgment, asking him about the nursing of an adult. Ibn ʿUmar said: A man came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, \I had a slave girl with whom I had intercourse. My wife went to her and nursed her. Then I went to her"," and she said"," 'Keep away! By Allah"," I have indeed nursed her.'\"" ʿUmar said"," \""Punish her and go to your slave girl. Indeed"," nursing is only the nursing of the young child.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15666","(15660) And ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A woman from the Anṣār went to her husband's slave girl and nursed her. When her husband came, she said, \This slave girl of yours has become your daughter.\"" The man went to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""I adjure you that when you return"," you should have intercourse with your slave girl and punish your wife's back.\""\n\nIn the narration of ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him): \""Indeed"," nursing is only the nursing of the young child.\"" [Good]"""
"15667","(15661) And Ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn ʿAffān informed us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from ʿUbaydullāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: \Nothing is made unlawful through nursing except that which occurs in childhood.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15668","(15662) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to say: \There is no nursing except for one who is nursed in childhood.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15669","(15663) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Rūq al-Hizzānī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Rūḥ narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: I heard ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \There is no nursing except within the two years"," in childhood.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15670","(15664) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, that Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding the nursing of an adult: \I do not see it except that it makes unlawful.\"" Ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Consider what you are issuing as verdicts to people.\"" Abū Mūsā said"," \""Then what do you say?\"" Ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""There is no nursing except that which occurs within the two years.\"" Abū Mūsā said: \""Do not ask me about anything as long as this scholar is in your midst.\""\n\nAlthough this is a mursal narration"," it has corroborating reports from Ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him). [Authentic]"""
"15671","(15665) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Mughīrah informed us, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAbdullāh, who said: \There is no breastfeeding (raḍāʿ) except that which occurs within the two-year period — that which strengthens the bone and grows the flesh.\""\n\nAnd with the same meaning"," Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated it from Ibn Masʿūd as a mursal narration regarding the two-year period. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15672","(15666) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, from Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbaydullāh, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: He used to say, \There is no breastfeeding after two complete years.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15673","(15667) ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Whatever occurs within the two years establishes prohibition (taḥrīm)"," even if it is only a single suckling; and whatever occurs after the two years is nothing.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15674","(15668) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \There is no breastfeeding except that which occurs within the two-year period.\"" This is the correct version"," and it is mawqūf (stopped at the Companion). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15675","(15669) And Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: I heard ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad al-Wakīl say: Abū al-Walīd ibn Burd al-Anṭākī narrated to us; al-Haytham ibn Jamīl narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Breastfeeding does not establish prohibition except that which occurs within the two-year period.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: This is known from al-Haytham ibn Jamīl from Ibn ʿUyaynah as a musnad narration"," and other than al-Haytham stop it at Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both).\n\nAnd we have narrated this specification of the two-year period from the Tābiʿīn: from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"," and al-Shaʿbī. [Munkar]"""
"15676","(15670) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated to us, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he used to say: \When a woman gives birth after nine months"," twenty-one months of breastfeeding suffices her; and when she gives birth after seven months"," twenty-three months of breastfeeding suffices her; and when she gives birth after six months"," twenty-four months of breastfeeding suffices her — just as Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15677","(15671) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥusayn narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated to us, from ʿUqbah ibn al-Ḥārith: A dark-skinned woman came and claimed that she had breastfed both of them — meaning ʿUqbah and his wife. He said: So he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him, and he turned away. The Prophet (ﷺ) smiled and said: \How can that be"," when it has been said?\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15678","(15672) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ, Ibn Manīʿ, Abū Kurayb, Yaʿqūb, and Dallūwayh said: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ayyūb narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from ʿUbayd ibn Abī Maryam, from ʿUqbah ibn al-Ḥārith — and he said: \I heard it from ʿUqbah"," but I have a better memory of ʿUbayd's narration\"" — who said: \""I married a woman"," and a dark-skinned woman came to us and said: 'I have breastfed both of you.' So I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'I married the daughter of so-and-so"," and a dark-skinned woman came to us and said: I have breastfed both of you — and she is a liar.' He turned away from me. I came to him from the direction of his face and said: 'She is a liar.' He said: 'How can that be"," when she claims that she has breastfed both of you? Leave her (i.e."," divorce her).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh from Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15679","(15673) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Tamīm al-Qanṭarī narrated to us; Abū Qilābah narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Ḥamdān narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah; ʿUqbah ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me — or I heard it from him — that he married Umm Yaḥyā bint Abī Ihāb, and a dark-skinned slave woman came and said: \I have breastfed both of you.\"" I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he turned away from me. I moved aside and then mentioned it to him. He said: \""How can that be"," when she claims that she has breastfed both of you?\"" So he forbade him from her.\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿĀṣim and from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh from Yaḥyā"," thus in an interpolated (mudraj) manner. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15680","(15674) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj; Ibn Abī Mulaykah informed me that ʿUqbah ibn al-Ḥārith informed him that he married Umm Yaḥyā bint Abī Ihāb, and a dark-skinned slave woman said: \I have breastfed both of you.\"" He said: \""So I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him"," and he turned away. I moved aside and mentioned that to him"," and he said to him: 'How can that be"," when she claims that she has breastfed both of you?'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: His (ﷺ) turning away suggests that he did not consider her testimony to be binding upon him"," and his statement — \""How can that be"," when she claims that she has breastfed both of you?\"" — suggests that he disliked for him to remain with her when it had been said to him that she was his sister through breastfeeding. And this is the meaning of what we said: that he should leave her out of piety (waraʿ)"," not as a legal ruling (ḥukm). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15681","(15675) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, Sufyān al-Jawharī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd informed us, Sufyān narrated on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam: that a man and his wife came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and a woman came and said: \I have suckled both of you.\"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) refused to accept her statement and said: \""Your wife is yours.\""\n\nThis is a mursal hadith"," and it has been narrated through another chain. [Weak]"""
"15682","(15676) Abū Ḥāziṃ al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Hushaym informed us, Ibn Abī Laylā and al-Ḥajjāj narrated on the authority of ʿIkrimah ibn Khālid al-Makhzūmī: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a case concerning a woman who testified against a man and his wife that she had suckled both of them. He said: \Not until two men or one man and two women testify.\""\n\nAbū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us"," Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us"," al-Rabīʿ informed us"," al-Shāfiʿī informed us"," Muslim narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj on the authority of ʿAṭāʾ who said: \""The testimony of fewer than four women is not accepted.\"" [Weak]"""
"15683","(15677) As for the hadith which Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī informed us, ʿAffān informed us, Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān informed us — and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān informed us — he said: I heard Muḥammad ibn ʿUthaym narrate from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī from his father from Abī ʿUbayd who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: \What testimony is accepted regarding breastfeeding?\"" He said: \""A man or a woman.\""\n\nThis is a weak chain of narration; a proof cannot be established by something like it. Muḥammad ibn ʿUthaym is accused of lying"," and Ibn al-Baylamānī is weak. There has also been disagreement regarding its text: it has been reported thus"," and it has been said: \""a man and a woman","\"" and it has been said: \""a man and two women.\"" And Allah knows best."""
"15684","(15678) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us from the original of his hearing, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr ibn Sābiq al-Khawlānī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, al-Layth ibn Saʿd, and Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Jumaḥī narrated on the authority of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj al-Aslamī from his father from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said:\n\nAnd Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated it to me from his father from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr from Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj al-Aslamī from his father that he said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what removes from me the reproach of breastfeeding?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""A fair-complexioned male slave or a fair-complexioned female slave.\""\n\nAnd Abū Muʿāwiyah and ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," except that they both said: \""a male slave or a female slave.\""\n\nAnd it has been reported from ʿUrwah from Ḥajjāj ibn Ḥajjāj ibn Mālik from the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and it has been reported from him from Ḥajjāj ibn Abī al-Ḥajjāj from his father. The correct version is Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj from his father"," as stated by al-Bukhārī. [Sound]"""
"15685","(15679) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us, Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāyinī informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Madīnī informed us, Sufyān — meaning Ibn ʿUyaynah — informed us, ʿUmar ibn Ḥabīb informed me on the authority of a man from Banī ʿUtwārah, and sometimes Sufyān said: from a man from Banī Kinānah — \Are you from Banī So-and-so?\"" I said: \""No"," but they suckled me.\"" He said: \""I heard ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: 'Indeed"," milk causes resemblance.'\"" [Weak]"""
"15686","(15680) He said: And ʿAlī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed us, Sufyān — al-Thawrī — narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān from Shuʿayb ibn Khālid al-Khathʿamī from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) who said: \Milk causes resemblance.\""\n\nAnd ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd al-ʿAdanī narrated it from al-Thawrī with this chain of narration"," saying: \""I sat with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar"," and he said: 'Is that your child?' I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: 'Indeed"," breastfeeding causes resemblance.'\"" [Weak]"""
"15687","(15681) And Abū al-Ḥasan informed us, Bishr informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Ḥaddāʾ informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed us, Sufyān narrated on the authority of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz who said: \Milk causes resemblance.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15688","(15682) A mursal hadith has been narrated concerning this: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us, Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ informed us, Isḥāq — the son of the daughter of Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind — informed us from the report of men on the authority of Hishām ibn Ismāʿīl al-Makkī from Ziyād al-Sahmī who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade having the foolish woman act as a wet nurse, for milk causes resemblance. This is mursal. [Very weak]"
"15689","(15683) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Abū Tawbah informed us, Muḥammad ibn Muhājir narrated on the authority of his father from Asmāʾ bint Yazīd ibn al-Sakan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: \Do not kill your children secretly"," for coitus interruptus (al-ghayl) overtakes the horseman and throws him from his horse.\"" [Sound]"""
"15690","(15684) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us — he said: I read to Mālik — on the authority of Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Nawfal from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) from Judhāmah bint Wahb al-Asadiyyah that she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: \I had intended to forbid coitus interruptus (al-ghīlah)"," until I remembered that the Romans and the Persians do it"," and it does not harm their children.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Authentic]"""
"15691","(15685) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd informed us — and Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Faqīh al-Fāmī in Baghdād informed us: Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ṣawwāf informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqrīʾ informed us: Ḥaywah informed me: ʿAyyāsh ibn ʿAbbās informed me from Abū al-Naḍr from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ that Usāmah ibn Zayd informed his father, Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, saying: \A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I practise ʿazl (coitus interruptus) with my wife.' He asked: 'Why?' The man replied: 'Out of concern for her children.' He said: 'If that were so"," it would not have harmed the Persians and the Romans.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Numayr and others from al-Muqrīʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15692","(15686) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān informed us: I heard al-Rukayn say: al-Qāsim ibn Ḥassān informed me from his paternal uncle, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥarmalah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ disliked ṣufrah (meaning khalūq, a yellowish perfume), plucking white hair, letting the garment drag, wearing gold rings, playing with dice, displaying adornment (tabarruj biʾl-zīnah), and corrupting a child other than one's maḥram.\n\nYūsuf said: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: al-Muʿtamir narrated to us with the same chain and the same meaning. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15693","(15687) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from al-Zuhrī from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Umm Qays bint Miḥṣan, who said: \I came to the Prophet ﷺ with my son upon whom I had applied a ligature for ʿudhrah (a throat ailment). He said: 'Why do you treat your children's ʿudhrah by strangling? You should use this Indian aloes-wood (al-ʿūd al-Hindī)"," for in it are seven remedies: it is administered as a snuff for ʿudhrah and as a suppository for dhāt al-janb (pleurisy).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others"," all from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah.\n\nYūnus ibn Yazīd narrated it from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī and added therein: \""Meaning al-kust (costus).\"" Some of them said: \""al-qust.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15694","(15688) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Abī Naṣr informed me: I heard Manṣūr ibn Ibrāhīm al-Thaqafī say: I heard Abū ʿUmar Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, the pupil of Thaʿlab, say: Thaʿlab said regarding the statement of al-Shāfiʿī on the verse {That is more likely that you will not transgress (an taʿūlū)} — meaning \that your dependents do not become numerous\"" — he said: \""This is the most excellent linguistically.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15695","(15689) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Ṭālib al-Ḥāfiẓ Aḥmad ibn Naṣr informed us: ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Ṣadafī informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth informed me: my father from his father from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hilāl from Zayd ibn Aslam, regarding the statement of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: {That is more likely that you will not transgress (an taʿūlū)}, he said: \That is more likely that those whom you support do not become numerous.\""\n\nThe hadith regarding the occasion of revelation of this verse has already been mentioned in the Book of Marriage. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15696","(15690) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-ʿAbdī informed us: Sufyān from Hishām from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Hind said to the Prophet ﷺ: \Abū Sufyān is a stingy man. Is there any sin upon me if I take from his property?\"" He said: \""Take what suffices you and your child in a fair manner.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15697","(15691) The Shaykh al-Imām Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Najīd ibn Aḥmad al-Sulamī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī informed us: Abū ʿĀṣim al-Nabīl from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ encouraged giving charity. A man came and said: \I have a dīnār.\"" — And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I have a dīnār.' He said: 'Spend it on yourself.' He said: 'I have another.' He said: 'Spend it on your child.' He said: 'I have another.' He said: 'Spend it on your family.' In the hadith of Abū ʿĀṣim: 'on your wife.' He said: 'I have another.' He said: 'Spend it on your servant.' He said: 'I have another.' He said: 'You know best.' In the hadith of Abū ʿĀṣim: 'You are more discerning.'\""\n\nSufyān added in his narration from Ibn ʿAjlān: Saʿīd said: Then Abū Hurayrah would say when narrating this hadith: \""Your child says: 'Spend on me — to whom will you entrust me?' Your wife says: 'Spend on me or divorce me.' Your servant says: 'To whom will you entrust me? Spend on me or sell me.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15698","(15692) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī informed us: Wakīʿ from al-Aʿmash from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The best charity is that given from surplus wealth"," and the upper hand is better than the lower hand"," and begin with those whom you support.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī extracted it"," no. 5355]"""
"15699","(15693) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Sulmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh in Baghdād informed us: It was recited to Muḥammad ibn Muslimah al-Wāsiṭī while I heard: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Bahz ibn Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Qushayrī informed me: my father from his father, who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," our wives — what may we approach of them and what should we forgo?' He said: 'Approach your field however you wish"," but do not strike the face"," do not revile"," and do not forsake except in the house. Feed them when you feed"," and clothe them when you clothe. How is it that some of you have intimate access to others?'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15700","(15694) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Shuʿbah from Abī Isḥāq said: I heard Wahb ibn Jābir say: \I was present with ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ (may Allah be pleased with them both) in Bayt al-Maqdis"," and a freed slave of his came to him and said: 'I wish to spend this month here in devotion' — meaning Ramaḍān. ʿAbd Allāh said to him: 'Have you left for your family what will sustain them?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then do not stay. Go back and leave for them what will sustain them"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""It is enough sin for a man that he neglect those whom he is obligated to feed.\""'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15701","(15695) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī in Ṭūs narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī in al-Baṣrah narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah informed me: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Anṣārī narrating from Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī. I asked, \From the Prophet (ﷺ)?\"" He replied"," \""From the Prophet (ﷺ)"," who said: 'When a Muslim spends upon his family while counting on the reward from it"," it is recorded as charity (ṣadaqah) for him.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and Muslim extracted it from two other routes from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"15702","(15696) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: al-Firyābī — and Sulaymān informed us: Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Ibn Kathīr — and Sulaymān informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym said: Sufyān narrated to us from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) came to visit me while I was in Makkah"," and he disliked that any of us should die in the land from which he had emigrated. He said: 'May Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," have mercy on Ibn ʿAfrā.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," shall I bequeath all of my wealth?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'Then half?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'Then a third?' He said: 'A third — and a third is much. Indeed"," that you leave your heirs wealthy is better than leaving them destitute"," stretching out their hands to people. And whatever you spend upon your family by way of expenditure"," it is charity — even the morsel that you raise to your wife's mouth. And it may be that Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," will benefit a people through you and harm others through you.'\"" He had no children on that day except a daughter.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym and Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," and Muslim extracted it from another route from Sufyān al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"15703","(15697) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb, Abū al-Muthannā, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar, and Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabbān said: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us: Sufyān — and ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Tamtām narrated to us: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Muzāḥim ibn Zufr from Mujāhid from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'A dinar you give to a poor person"," a dinar you give to free a slave's neck"," a dinār you give in the cause of Allah"," and a dinār you spend upon your family.' He said: 'The dinar you spend upon your family is the greatest in reward.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15704","(15698) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us by dictation: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, ʿĀrim, Abū al-Rabīʿ, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd, Musaddad, and Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated from Abū Qilābah from Abū Asmāʾ from Thawbān, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The best dinar a man spends is a dinar he spends upon his dependents (ʿiyāl); a dinar a man spends upon his mount in the cause of Allah; and a dinar a man spends upon his companions in the cause of Allah.'\""\n\nAbū Qilābah said: \""He began with the dependents. What man can be greater in reward than a man who spends upon young dependents"," whom Allah sustains and through whom He benefits them?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15705","(15699) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Lakhmī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: al-Firyābī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Hishām from his father from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā), who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'The best of you is the best of you to his family"," and I am the best of you to my family.' And Allah knows best.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15706","(15700) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad, that is Ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥāfiẓ, informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Khathʿamī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to me: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said: Sufyān al-Thawrī said to me, \What do you have regarding provisions (al-qūt)?\"" I said"," \""Nothing.\"" He said: \""Then I remembered afterwards a ḥadīth that Maʿmar narrated to us from al-Zuhrī from Mālik ibn Aws from ʿUmar (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu)"," that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to sell the palm trees of Banī al-Naḍīr and set aside provisions for his family for a year.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Salām from Wakīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"15707","(15701) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad Dalʿaj ibn Aḥmad al-Sijzī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Mālik ibn Aws ibn al-Ḥadathānī informed me — and he mentioned the ḥadīth in full — from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) regarding what Allah bestowed upon His Messenger. He said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to spend upon his family provisions for a year from this wealth"," and then take what remained and treat it as the wealth of Allah.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr and others"," and Muslim extracted it from the ḥadīth of Maʿmar and others."""
"15708","(15702) The Shaykh — meaning Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī — informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khurāsānī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, in the story of the Bedouin who had intercourse with his wife during Ramaḍān, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought a basket of dates. He said: 'Take this and give it as charity.' He mentioned it.\"" ʿAṭāʾ said: \""I asked Saʿīd"," 'How many ṣāʿ of dates were in that basket?' He said"," 'Between fifteen and twenty ṣāʿ.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15709","(15703) We have narrated from the ḥadīth of al-Awzāʿī from al-Zuhrī from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah, in the story of the one who had intercourse, in which it is stated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Feed sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""I cannot find (that much).\""\n\nHe said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought a basket containing fifteen ṣāʿ. He said: 'Take it and give it as charity.'\""\n\nAbū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed him: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-Kātib narrated to us: al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Hiql narrated from al-Awzāʿī"," who said: al-Zuhrī narrated to me"," and he mentioned it.\n\nThus did he narrate it from al-Awzāʿī"," incorporated (mudraj) within the ḥadīth of al-Zuhrī from Ḥumayd.\n\nIbn al-Mubārak narrated it from al-Awzāʿī"," and he made the specification of the basket's quantity in the narration of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"," and we have mentioned it elsewhere. Al-Shāfiʿī said regarding the expenditure of the well-to-do (al-mūsir): \""It is two mudd.\"" He said: \""I only made the most I have obligated two mudd and two mudd because the most the Prophet (ﷺ) set for the expiatory feeding (fidyah al-kaffārah) for the oath was two mudd per poor person.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15710","(15704) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Mālik ibn Anas narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī from Mujāhid ibn Jabr from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjarah, who said: \He was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the state of iḥrām"," and lice troubled him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered him to shave his head and said: 'Fast three days"," or feed six poor persons"," two mudd each"," or slaughter a sheep. Whichever of these you do will suffice you.'\""\n\nAl-Ḥusayn ibn al-Walīd also narrated it from Mālik with a sound chain"," and the two Shaykhs (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) extracted it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from other routes from ʿAbd al-Karīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"15711","(15705) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Bahr al-Attar narrated to us in al-Basrah; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Khalifah, from al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'ah, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that he fixed for a woman and her servant twelve dirhams: eight dirhams for the woman and four dirhams for the servant, and one dirham out of the eight was for cotton and linen. This is a weak chain of narration, and Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"15712","(15706) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us among the last narrators. They said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to the commanders of the military corps regarding men who had been absent from their wives. He commanded them to take hold of such men and instruct them either to provide maintenance or to divorce. If they divorced, they were to send the maintenance for the period they had withheld. [Sahih]"
"15713","(15707) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us among the last narrators. They said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, who said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about a man who does not find the means to provide maintenance for his wife. He said: Separation shall be effected between them. Abu al-Zinad said: I asked: Is this a Sunnah? Sa'id said: It is a Sunnah.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: What makes Sa'id's statement resemble a Sunnah is that it is a Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). [Sahih]"
"15714","(15708) Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Balawayh narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us. And Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; Uthman ibn Ahmad al-Sammak and Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' and Isma'il ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Awdi narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, regarding a man who does not find the means to provide maintenance for his wife. He said: Separation shall be effected between them. [Sahih]"
"15715","(15709) He said: And Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), with its like. [Sahih]"
"15716","(15710) Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya al-Zuhri al-Qadi narrated to us in Makkah; Abu Yahya ibn Abi Masrrah narrated to us. And Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Bazzaz informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Faki narrated to us in Makkah; Abu Yahya Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Masrrah al-Makki narrated to us; Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that he said: \The best charity is that which leaves one in sufficiency"," and the upper hand is better than the lower hand"," and begin with those whom you support.\"" He said: \""And whom do I support"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Your wife says: 'Feed me"," or else divorce me.' Your servant says: 'Feed me and employ me.' Your son says: 'To whom will you leave me?'\"" Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated it in this manner from Ibn Ajlan. And Ibn Uyaynah and others narrated it from Ibn Ajlan"," from al-Maqburi"," from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and they made its latter part the statement of Abu Hurairah. [Sahih]"""
"15717","(15711) Likewise, al-A'mash made it go back through Abu Salih from Abu Hurairah. Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Adib informed us; Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed me; al-Hasan, that is Ibn Sufyan, narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us. He said: And al-Hasan informed me; Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated to us. They said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," the best charity is that which leaves one in sufficiency"," and the upper hand is better than the lower hand"," and begin with those whom you support.\"" Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Your wife says: 'Feed me"," or else divorce me.' Your servant says: 'Feed me"," or else sell me.' Your son says: 'To whom will you entrust me?'\"" They said: \""O Abu Hurairah"," is this something you say from your own opinion"," or is it from the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?\"" He said: \""No"," rather this is from my own reasoning.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath"," from his father"," from al-A'mash. [Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"15718","(15712) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, the freed slave of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays, that Abu Amr ibn Hafs divorced her irrevocably while he was absent. He sent his agent to her with some barley, but she was displeased with it. She said: \By Allah"," you have nothing due from us.\"" She came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said to her: \""You have no maintenance due from him.\"" He commanded her to observe her waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik. Then he said: \""That woman is visited by my companions. Observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum"," for he is a blind man"," and you may leave your garments there. And when your waiting period ends"," inform me.\"" She said: \""When my waiting period ended"," I mentioned to him that Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm had proposed to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'As for Abu Jahm"," he does not lay his staff down from his shoulder"," and as for Mu'awiyah"," he is a destitute man with no wealth. Marry Usamah ibn Zayd.'\"" She said: \""I disliked him.\"" He said: \""Marry Usamah ibn Zayd.\"" So I married him"," and Allah placed goodness in him"," and I was filled with contentment.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," from Malik. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 1480.]"""
"15719","(15713) Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; Ibn Milhan narrated to us; Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us; Imran ibn Abi Anas narrated to us. And Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim al-Muzzi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abu Salamah, who said: I asked Fatimah bint Qays, and she informed me that her husband from Banu Makhzum had divorced her and refused to provide maintenance for her. She came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \You have no maintenance. Move and go to Ibn Umm Maktum and stay with him"," for he is a blind man"," and you may leave your garments with him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. [Sahih]"""
"15720","(15714) Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us verbally; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays, that her husband divorced her during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he had been providing her with a meagre maintenance. When she saw that, she said: \By Allah"," I shall certainly speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). If maintenance is due to me"," I shall take what is appropriate for me"," and if no maintenance is due to me"," I shall not take anything.\"" She said: \""I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and he said: 'You have no maintenance and no residence.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Qutaybah.\n\nAnd likewise Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated it from Abu Salamah regarding both residence and maintenance. [Sahih]"""
"15721","(15715) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from Abū Salamah, from Fāṭimah bint Qays, that she was married to a man from Banū Makhzūm, and he irrevocably divorced her (ṭalāqan al-battah). She sent to her family seeking maintenance (nafaqah), but they said: \You are not entitled to any maintenance from us.\"" She came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him"," and he said: \""You are not entitled to maintenance from him"," but you are obligated to observe the waiting period (ʿiddah). Move to the house of Umm Sharik.\"" Then he said: \""Umm Sharik is a woman whose brothers from the early Muhājirūn visit her. So move to Ibn Umm Maktūm"," for he is a blind man; if you lay aside your garment"," he will see nothing. And do not let us miss you.\"" She said: \""When she became ḓalāl (completed her waiting period)"," men mentioned her (in marriage proposals)"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'What about Usāmah?'\"" He said: \""It was as though her family disliked that.\"" She said: \""No"," by Allah"," I will not marry except the one he spoke of","\"" and she married him.\n\nMuḥammad ibn ʿAmr said: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to me that ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," used to say: \""O Fāṭimah"," fear Allah"," for you know from what matter this was.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and others"," without the statement of ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15722","(15716) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us; ʿUqayl ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me that Fāṭimah bint Qays — and she was the sister of al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Qays — informed him that she was married to Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥafs, and he divorced her with three divorces. His agent (wakīl) ordered maintenance for her, but she was disinclined toward it. His agent said to me: \She is not entitled to any maintenance from us.\"" She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that"," and he said to her: \""He spoke the truth.\"" And he transferred her to Ibn Umm Maktūm. The people disapproved of what she narrated about her leaving (her husband's house) before she became ḓalāl. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15723","(15717) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, and Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Faḍl said: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated — Isḥāq said \informed us","\"" and Ibn Rāfiʿ said \""narrated to us","\"" and the wording is his — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah"," that Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥafs ibn al-Mughīrah went out with ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," to Yemen"," and he sent to his wife Fāṭimah bint Qays the remaining divorce from her divorces. Al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām and ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah ordered maintenance for her. They said: \""By Allah"," you are not entitled to any maintenance unless you are pregnant.\"" She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned their statement to him"," and he said: \""You are not entitled to maintenance.\"" She asked his permission to relocate"," and he gave her permission. She said: \""Where (should I go)"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""To Ibn Umm Maktūm.\"" He was a blind man; she could lay aside her garments in his presence and he would not see her. When her waiting period expired"," the Prophet ﷺ married her to Usāmah ibn Zayd. Marwān sent Qabīṣh ibn Dhūʾayb to her to ask her about this hadith"," and she narrated it to him. Marwān said: \""We have not heard this hadith except from a woman. We will hold fast to the bond (ʿiṣmah) upon which we found the people.\"" When Fāṭimah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," learned of Marwān's statement"," she said: \""Between you and me is the Qur'an. Allah"," the Mighty and Sublime"," said: *'Do not turn them out of their houses"," nor should they leave"," unless they commit a clear immorality (fāḥishah mubayyinah)'* — until He reached: *'Perhaps Allah will bring about a new matter thereafter.'*\"" She said: \""This is for the one for whom there is a possibility of return (murājaʿah). What matter can occur after the three (divorces)? How can you say she is not entitled to maintenance if she is not pregnant? On what basis are you detaining her?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15724","(15718) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Khālid narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated, and he mentioned the chain of narration of the hadith, except that he said in the hadith: \I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'You are not entitled to maintenance unless you are pregnant.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15725","(15719) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm, who said: \I and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān went to Fāṭimah bint Qays"," and she had sent her sister's daughter out for purification (ṭuhr). We said to her: 'What compelled you to do this?' She said: 'My husband sent my divorce — three divorces — with ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah during the expedition of Najrān"," and he sent five ṣāʿ of barley and five ṣāʿ of dates.' She said: 'I said: Is there no maintenance for me except this?' She said: 'I gathered my garments and went to the Prophet ﷺ.' He said: 'How many times did he divorce you?' I said: 'Three.' He said: 'He spoke the truth. There is no maintenance for you. Observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm"," where you may lay aside your garments.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī and Abū ʿĀṣim"," from Sufyān. And Shuʿbah narrated it from Abū Bakr regarding both maintenance and lodging together. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15726","(15720) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī informed us; Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Sayyār, Ḥuṣayn, Mughīrah ibn Miqsam, Ashʿath, Mujālid, Dāwūd, and Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid — all of them — narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \I entered upon Fāṭimah bint Qays and asked her about the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning her. She said: 'Her husband irrevocably divorced her (ṭallaqahā al-battah).' She said: 'I contested the matter with him before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding lodging (suknā) and maintenance (nafaqah).' She said: 'He did not grant me lodging or maintenance"," and he commanded me to observe my waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb. Thus is the narration of the group from al-Shaʿbī.\n\nAnd in the narration of Mujālid from al-Shaʿbī"," the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \""Lodging and maintenance are only for the one for whom there is a possibility of return (murājaʿah).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15727","(15721) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed it to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Hushaym narrated, and he mentioned the hadith from the group as it has passed, and he added this addition from Mujālid. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15728","(15722) And in the narration of Firās from al-Shaʿbī, in the story of Fāṭimah bint Qays, he said: \The two of them contested the matter before the Prophet ﷺ.\"" A man said — or the man said: \""He has divorced her three times.\"" He said: \""Lodging and maintenance are only for the one upon whom there is a revocable divorce (rajʿah).\"" So he commanded her"," and she observed her waiting period at Ibn Umm Maktūm's. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15729","(15723) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed it to us; Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Shaybān narrated from Firās, from al-Shaʿbī, and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15730","(15724) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd informed me; Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from al-Suddī, from al-Bahīyy, from Fāṭimah bint Qays, who said: \My husband divorced me three times"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant me lodging or maintenance.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥulwānī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15731","(15725) It was narrated by someone other than Yaḥyā ibn Ādam, as Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Shādhān narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us, from al-Suddī, from al-Bahī, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to Fāṭimah bint Qays: \O Fāṭimah"," indeed residence and maintenance are only for one whose husband has the right of return (rajʿah) over her.\""\n\nAl-Aswad ibn ʀāmir"," i.e."," Shādhān"," brought it in this manner"," and the correct version is the first one.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The narration of the group from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Fāṭimah bint Qays pertains to the denial of maintenance but not residence. Similarly"," the narration of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah from Fāṭimah"," and in the narration of some of them from Abū Salamah"," and in the narration of al-Shaʿbī and al-Bahī"," both are denied together. There is disagreement regarding it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm from Fāṭimah. What is most consistent with the context of the hadith is that the Prophet (ﷺ) denied maintenance and permitted her to relocate due to a reason—perhaps she was too shy to mention it—and others have mentioned it"," as we have previously noted in the Kitāb al-ʿIddah. He did not intend the denial of residence at all. Do you not see that he (ﷺ) did not say to her"," \""Observe your ʿiddah wherever you wish","\"" but rather he placed her in a secure location of her choosing"," since her husband was absent and had no guardian to protect her.\n\nAs for his statement"," \""Indeed residence and maintenance are only for one over whom there is a right of return\""—this is not well-known in this hadith and has not been reported through any reliable chain. As for the criticism directed at Fāṭimah by those who criticized her"," it is only because she concealed the reason for her relocation. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15732","(15726) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn ibn Mihrān, from his father, who said: I came to Madīnah and asked about the most knowledgeable person among its inhabitants, and I was directed to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab. I asked him about the al-mabtūtah (irrevocably divorced woman), and she said: \She observes her ʿiddah in her husband's house.\"" I said: \""Then where is the hadith of Fāṭimah bint Qays?\"" He said—and it was described that he became angry—and said: \""Fāṭimah caused fitnah among the people. She had a sharp tongue and overstepped with her in-laws"," so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded her to observe her ʿiddah in the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm.\""\n\nAbū Muʿāwiya al-Ḍarīr likewise narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15733","(15727) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū ʿUtbah narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Ḥabīb ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād al-Makkī narrated to me, saying: I was sitting with Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) when a man asked him: \Does the woman divorced by three pronouncements (ṭalāq thalāth) have a right to maintenance?\"" I said: \""She has no maintenance.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""You have spoken correctly"," O my nephew"," I agree with you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15734","(15728) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, that Abū al-Zubayr informed him, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that he heard him say: \The maintenance of a divorced woman is due as long as she is not forbidden (i.e."," the divorce is revocable). But when she becomes irrevocably forbidden"," then it is a provision given in a fair manner (matāʿ bi-l-maʿrūf).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15735","(15729) ʿAbd al-Majīd also informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʿAṭāʾ said: \The irrevocably divorced woman (al-mabtūtah) is entitled to nothing except in the case of pregnancy—he must provide for her on account of the pregnancy. But if she is not pregnant"," then she has no maintenance"," and Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15736","(15730) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from al-Shaʿbī, from Fāṭimah bint Qays, that her husband divorced her irrevocably (three pronouncements), and the Prophet (ﷺ) did not grant her residence or maintenance. He (al-Shaʿbī) said: \I mentioned this to Ibrāhīm"," and Ibrāhīm said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'We will not abandon the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah of our Prophet for the statement of a woman—she has both residence and maintenance.'\"" The hadith of al-Shaʿbī was recorded by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān. The hadith of Ibrāhīm from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15737","(15731) It has also been narrated as a connected, stopped (mawqūf) narration. Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Aswad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), that when the statement of Fāṭimah bint Qays reached him, he said: \We will not abandon the Book of Allah for the statement of a woman—perhaps she has forgotten.\"" Likewise"," Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad narrated it from al-Aʿmash as a mawqūf narration. And Ashʿath narrated it from al-Ḥakam and Ḥammād"," from Ibrāhīm"," from al-Aswad"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and in it he added: \""and the Sunnah of our Prophet.\"" Ashʿath ibn Sawwār is weak (ḍaʿīf). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15738","(15732) It has also been narrated through another route from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) as a connected, musnad narration. Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf ibn Masʿadah narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿIṣām ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Asadī—who is Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī—narrated to us: ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, who said: I was sitting with al-Aswad ibn Yazīd in the Great Mosque, and al-Shaʿbī was with us. Al-Shaʿbī narrated the hadith of Fāṭimah bānt Qays, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not grant her residence or maintenance. Al-Aswad took a handful of pebbles and pelted him, then said: \Woe to you! Do you narrate such a thing?\"" He said: \""ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'We will not abandon the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of our Prophet (ﷺ) for the statement of a woman—we do not know whether she remembered or forgot. She has both residence and maintenance.' Allah"," the Most High"," said: {Do not expel them from their houses"," nor should they leave"," unless they commit a clear immorality (fāḥishah mubayyinah).} [al-Ṭalāq: 1]\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Jabalah"," from Abū Aḥmad. Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated it from ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq"," mentioning only the relocation (nuqlah) and not the maintenance"," and he did not include in it: \""and the Sunnah of our Prophet.\"" Its mention has already passed in the Kitāb al-ʿIddah.\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith said to me: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \""This narration is more authentic than the one before it"," because this wording is not established"," and Yaḥyā ibn Ādam is more precise and more reliable than Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī"," and Allah knows best.\"" Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah also followed him and narrated it from ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq in the same manner as Yaḥyā ibn Ādam. And al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmārah narrated it from Salamah ibn Kuhayl"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Khalīl"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and in it he said: \""and the Sunnah of our Prophet.\"" Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmārah is abandoned (matrūk). What is most consistent with what we have narrated from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and others in their criticism of Fāṭimah bint Qays is that she was criticized only for the relocation without a valid reason"," not for the maintenance"," and this is most consistent with the verse cited as evidence.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""We do not know of any mention of maintenance (nafaqah) in the Book of Allah; rather"," the Book of Allah mentions only residence (suknā)"," and Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15739","(15733) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Mihrān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that Hind said: \O Messenger of Allah"," Abū Sufyān is a stingy man. Is there any sin upon me if I take something from his wealth?\"" He said: \""Take what is sufficient for you and your child"," in a fair manner (bi-l-maʿrūf).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān al-Thawrī"," and Muslim recorded it through other routes from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15740","(15734) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamm ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī informed us: Abū Muslim al-Baṣrī narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAjlān, from al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) encouraged giving charity. A man came and said: \I have a dinar.\"" He said: \""Spend it on yourself.\"" He said: \""I have another.\"" He said: \""Spend it on your child.\"" He said: \""I have another.\"" He said: \""Spend it on your wife.\"" He said: \""I have another.\"" He said: \""Spend it on your servant.\"" He said: \""I have another.\"" He said: \""You are the most discerning (abṣar).\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15741","(15735) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū al-Yamān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Qurqūb al-Tammār in Hamadhān informed me — Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us — Abū al-Yamān informed me — Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī — ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr informed us that ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: A woman came to me with her two daughters, asking me for something, but I found nothing with me except a single date. So I gave it to her. She took it and split it between her two daughters and did not eat any of it herself. Then she stood up and left with her daughters. The Prophet ﷺ came to me, and I related her story to him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever is tested with daughters and treats them kindly"," they will be a shield for him from the Fire.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq"," from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15742","(15736) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū al-Walīd informed me — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Abū Kurayb narrated to us — Abū Usāmah narrated to us — Hishām narrated from his father — from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah — from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her. She said: I said, \O Messenger of Allah"," is there any reward for me in spending upon the children of Abī Salamah? I will not leave them like this and like that — they are after all my children.\"" He said: \""Yes"," there is reward for you in them for whatever you spend upon them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb"," and al-Bukhārī reported it through another chain from Hishām. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15743","(15737) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Ashʿath narrated from al-Shaʿbī and from one who narrated to him — from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding His statement {and upon the heir is the like of that}: He said: That he should not cause harm. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15744","(15738) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us — Ādam narrated to us — Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ — from Mujāhid regarding His statement {and the mothers shall nurse their children for two complete years}: He said: By \the mothers\"" are meant the divorced mothers. {No mother shall be harmed by her child}: He said: That she should not refuse to nurse him"," causing difficulty to his father. {Nor shall a father be harmed by his child}: He said: That the father should not cause harm to his child by preventing his mother from nursing him"," thereby causing her grief through that. {And upon the heir is the like of that}: He said: That is"," the guardian"," whomever he may be. {But if they desire weaning through mutual consent and consultation}: without either of them sinning against themselves or against their child before the two years. {And if you wish to seek nursing for your children}: out of fear of loss to the child. {There is no sin upon you when you hand over what you have given with kindness}: meaning"," according to the account of what the child has been nursed. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15745","(15739) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj — from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb — from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib: that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, compelled the paternal uncles of a child to spend upon him — the men rather than the women. And Layth ibn Abī Sulaym narrated from a man — from Ibn al-Musayyib: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, compelled an uncle to nurse his brother's son. And it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15746","(15740) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar — from al-Zuhrī: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, ordered three people — all of whom were heirs of the child — to pay the wage of his nursing. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15747","(15741) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Shaʿīrī informed us — Maḥmish ibn ʿIṣām narrated to us — Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to me — Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated — from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb — from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We went on the expedition of Tabūk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A vigorous young man passed by us, driving his small flock of sheep. We said: \If only this youth's vigor and energy were in the cause of Allah"," it would be better for him than this.\"" Our words reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \""What did you say?\"" We said: \""Such and such.\"" He said: \""If he strives to serve his parents"," or one of them"," then he is in the cause of Allah. And if he strives to provide for his dependents"," then he is in the cause of Allah. And if he strives to earn for himself"," then he is in the cause of Allah"," the Almighty"," the Glorious.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15748","(15742) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ, the judge in Kūfah, informed us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn Ḥakīm narrated to us — Sharīk narrated from Maghrāʾ al-ʿAbdī — from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man passed by them, and they were amazed at his physique. They said: \If only this were in the cause of Allah.\"" They came to the Prophet ﷺ"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: \""If he strives to serve his two elderly parents"," then he is in the cause of Allah. And if he strives to provide for his young children"," then he is in the cause of Allah. And if he strives to earn for himself to make himself independent"," then he is in the cause of Allah.\"" [Munkar]"""
"15749","(15743) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Sayyār narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us — Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr — from Ibrāhīm — from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr — from his paternal aunt: that she asked ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her: \I have an orphan in my care — may I eat from his property?\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""The purest thing a man eats is from his earnings"," and his child is from his earnings.\""\n\nAnd it has also been said: from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr"," from his mother"," from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15750","(15744) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam — from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr — from his mother — from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \A man's child is from his earnings — from the purest of his earnings. So eat from their properties.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15751","(15745) Imam Ahmad, may Allah have mercy on him, reported it, and Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman narrated it from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and he added in it: \If you are in need of it.\""\n\nAnd it is munkar [objectionable]"," as Abu Dawud al-Sijistani stated.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Hafiz in Marw narrated to us — Hammad ibn Ahmad al-Qadi narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us"," he said: I heard my father saying: Abu Hamzah narrated to us from Ibrahim al-Sa'igh"," from Hammad"," from Ibrahim"," from al-Aswad"," from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," she said: The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""Verily"," your children are a gift of Allah to you. {He grants females to whom He wills"," and He grants males to whom He wills} [al-Shura 49:49]. So they and their wealth are for you"," if you are in need of it.\"" [Munkar]"""
"15752","(15746) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Jarhi in Marw narrated to us — Yahya ibn Sasawayh narrated to us — 'Abd al-Karim al-Sukkari narrated to us — Wahb ibn Zam'ah informed us — Sufyan ibn 'Abd al-Malik said: I asked 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak about the hadith of 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: \And their wealth is for you"," if you are in need of it.\"" He said: Sufyan narrated it to me from Hammad"," from Ibrahim"," from al-Aswad"," from 'A'ishah. Sufyan said: This is a confusion [wahm] on the part of Hammad. 'Abd Allah said: I asked the companions of Sufyan about this hadith"," but they did not memorize it. 'Abd Allah said: And this is from his hadith from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr"," in which there is no mention of al-Aswad"," and in which there is no phrase \""if you are in need.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And it has been narrated from al-A'mash"," from Ibrahim"," from al-Aswad"," from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," without this wording [i.e."," \""if you are in need\""]"," and it is not preserved with this chain of narration. [Sahih]"""
"15753","(15747) Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Isfarayini informed us — Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Rizwayh narrated to us — Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Nasawi narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us — Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The purest thing a man eats is from his own earning"," and his child is from his own earning.\""\n\n(T) And similarly it was narrated by Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd from al-A'mash"," and Allah knows best. And it was narrated from Matar"," from al-Hakam"," from Ibrahim"," from Shurayh"," from 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," from the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," but it is not preserved. [Sahih]"""
"15754","(15748) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki informed us — Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Ishaq ibn al-Khurasani narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur narrated to us — Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Akhas narrated — from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \My father wants to seize my wealth.\"" He said: \""You and your father's wealth are for your father. The purest thing you eat is from your own earning"," so eat of it with pleasure.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15755","(15749) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us — Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us — Habib al-Mu'allim narrated — from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that a Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \I have wealth and children"," and my father wants to seize my wealth.\"" He said: \""You and your wealth are for your father. Your children are among the purest of your earnings.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15756","(15750) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us — Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated with his chain of narration, similar to it: that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have a child and wealth"," and my father wants to seize my wealth.\"" He said: \""You and your wealth are for your father. Your children are among the purest of your earnings"," so eat of the earnings of your children.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15757","(15751) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir: that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have wealth and dependents"," and my father has wealth and dependents"," and he wants to take my wealth to feed his dependents.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""You and your wealth are for your father.\""\n\nThis is munqati' [disconnected]"," and it has been narrated as musnad [connected] from other routes"," but its like is not established. [Da'if]"""
"15758","(15752) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Jamal narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh narrated to us — al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad narrated from his father, from Jabir: that a man said, \O Messenger of Allah…\"" and he mentioned it.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Whoever claims that the wealth of a child belongs to his father cites the apparent meaning of this hadith as evidence. And whoever claims that the father may take from his child's wealth what suffices him when he is in need of it"," and that when he is no longer in need of it"," the father has no right to anything from his child's wealth"," cites the reports that have been transmitted regarding the prohibition of consuming the wealth of others. And if the man dies and leaves a son"," the father receives only one-sixth of his wealth. And if the father were to own his son's wealth"," he would inherit all of it. [Da'if]"""
"15759","(15753) And it is reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \Every one of you has more right to his wealth than his father"," his children"," and all people combined.\"" Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us — Abu al-Hasan al-Karazi narrated to us — 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us — Abu 'Ubayd narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya narrated — from Hayyan ibn Abi Jabalah"," from the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," to that effect. [Da'if]"""
"15760","(15754) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsūs al-Sūsī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, al-Fayḍ ibn Wathīq informed us, from al-Mundhir ibn Ziyād al-Ṭāʾī, who said: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, who said:\n\nI was present with Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him), when a man said to him: \O Khalīfah of the Messenger of Allah"," this one intends to take all my wealth and consume it entirely.\"" Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""You are entitled to from his wealth only that which suffices you.\"" The man said: \""O Khalīfah of the Messenger of Allah"," did not the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'You and your wealth belong to your father'?\"" Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Be content with that which Allah has deemed good for you.\""\n\nAnother narrator transmitted it from al-Mundhir ibn Ziyād and said therein: \""He meant by that [only] maintenance (al-nafaqah).\"" And al-Mundhir ibn Ziyād is weak (ḍaʿīf). [Very weak]"""
"15761","(15755) Abū Muḥammad — Janāḥ ibn Nudhayr ibn Janāḥ in al-Kūfah — informed us: Abū Ja'far ibn Duḥaym — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn — informed us: Abū Ghassān — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah — from 'Abd Allāh ibn Shubrumah — from Abī Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarīr — from Abī Hurayrah: that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \O Messenger of Allah"," who among people is most deserving of my good companionship?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Your mother.\"" He asked: \""Then who?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Your mother.\"" He asked: \""Then who?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Your mother.\"" He asked: \""Then who?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Your father.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Ibn Shubrumah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15762","(15756) Abū al-Ḥasan — 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān — informed us: Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār — informed us: Abū Muslim — Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Kajjī — informed us: al-Anṣārī — informed us: Bahz ibn Ḥakīm — from his father — from his grandfather, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," who is most deserving of my kindness?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Your mother.\"" I said: \""Then who?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Your mother.\"" I said: \""Then who?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Your mother.\"" I said: \""Then who?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Your father"," then the nearest in kinship"," then the nearest.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"15763","(15757) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan — both said: Abū al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm — informed us: al-Rabī' — informed us: al-Shāfi'ī — informed us: Ibn 'Uyaynah — from Ziyād ibn Sa'd — Abū Muḥammad (I think) from Hilāl ibn Abī Maymūnah — from Abī Maymūnah — from Abī Hurayrah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī — informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī — informed us: Abū Ya'lā al-Mawṣilī — informed us: Hārūn ibn Ma'rūf — informed us: Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah — from Ziyād ibn Sa'd — from Hilāl ibn Abī Maymūnah — from his father — from Abī Hurayrah: that the Prophet ﷺ gave a young boy the choice between his father and his mother. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15764","(15758) And Abū al-Ḥusayn — 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad — informed us: Abū Ja'far — Muḥammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzāz — informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ja'far — informed us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk, meaning Ibn Makhlad — informed us: 'Āṣim.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī the jurist — informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah — informed us: Abū Dāwūd — informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī — informed us: 'Abd al-Razzāq and Abū 'Āṣim — from Ibn Jurayj — informed me: Ziyād — from Hilāl ibn Usāmah — that Abā Maymūnah Salīm, a freedman (mawlā) from the people of al-Madīnah and a trustworthy man, said: \While I was sitting with Abī Hurayrah"," a Persian woman came to him with her son"," and she claimed him as her own"," her husband having divorced her. She said: 'O Abā Hurayrah"," my husband — speaking in Persian — wants to take my son away.' Abū Hurayrah said: 'Cast lots between you two","' and he spoke to her in Persian. Then her husband came and said: 'Who will contest me regarding my son?' Abū Hurayrah said: 'O Allah"," I say this only because I heard a woman come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was sitting with him"," and she said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," my husband wants to take my son away"," though he has given me water from Abī 'Anabah's well and has been of benefit to me.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Cast lots between you two.\"" Her husband said: \""Who will contest me regarding my son?\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""This is your father and this is your mother; take the hand of whichever of the two you wish.\"" So he took the hand of his mother"," and she went away with him.\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Rūdhbārī's ḥadīth; the ḥadīth of Ibn Bishrān is shorter in wording"," though the meaning is the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ — previously mentioned]"""
"15765","(15759) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad — both said: Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — informed us: Sa'dān.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān — informed us: Abū Ja'far — Muḥammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzāz — informed us: Sa'dān ibn Naṣr — informed us: Wakī' ibn al-Jarrāḥ — informed us: 'Alī ibn al-Mubārak — from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr — from Abī Maymūnah — from Abī Hurayrah, who said: A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ, her husband having divorced her, and she wished to take her child. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Cast lots.\"" The man said: \""Who will stand between me and my child?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the child: \""Choose whichever of the two you wish.\"" He chose his mother"," and she went away with him."""
"15766","(15760) Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq — informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī ibn Ziyād — informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā — informed us: 'Īsā ibn Yūnus — informed us: 'Abd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ja'far — informed me: my father — informed me: Rāfi' ibn Sinān: that he had become Muslim while his wife refused to accept Islam. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \My daughter\"" — and she was a suckling infant — and Rāfi' said: \""My daughter.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said to Rāfi': \""Sit aside.\"" And he said to his wife: \""Sit aside.\"" He placed the girl between them and then said: \""Call her.\"" The girl inclined toward her mother"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: \""O Allah"," guide her.\"" Then she inclined toward her father"," and he took her.\n\nRāfi' ibn Sinān is the grandfather of 'Abd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ja'far. [Ṣaḥīḥ — previously mentioned]"""
"15767","(15761) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq — informed us: Abū al-'Abbās — Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb — informed us: al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān — informed us: al-Shāfi'ī — informed us: Ibn 'Uyaynah — from Yūnus ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Jurmī — from 'Umārah al-Jurmī, who said: 'Alī, may Allah be pleased with him, gave me the choice between my mother and my paternal uncle, and then said regarding a younger brother of mine: \Had he reached this age"," I would have given him the choice as well.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""
"15768","(15762) Al-Shāfi'ī said: Ibrāhīm related from Yūnus from 'Umārah from 'Alī, may Allah be pleased with him, something similar to that, and in the ḥadīth he said: \I was seven or eight years old.\"" And al-Shāfi'ī narrated in the older transmission — though this is not in what we heard — from Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah from Yazīd ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir from Ismā'īl ibn 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Abī al-Muhājir from 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm: that 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," gave a young boy the choice between his father and his mother. [Ḍa'īf — previously mentioned]"""
"15769","(15763) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Ubdūs al-'Anazī — informed us: 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī — informed us: Maḥmūd ibn Khāld al-Dimashqī — informed us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim — informed me: Abū 'Amr al-Awzā'ī — informed me: 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb — from his father — from his grandfather, 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Amr: that a woman said: \O Messenger of Allah"," this son of mine — my womb was his vessel"," my breast was his drink"," and my lap was his refuge. His father has divorced me and wishes to take him away from me.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \""You have more right to him so long as you do not remarry.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15770","(15764) Abū al-Ḥasan — 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffā' al-Baghdādī — informed us: Abū 'Amr — 'Uthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr — informed us: Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq — informed us: Ismā'īl ibn Abī Uways and 'Īsā ibn Mīnā — both said: 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād — from his father — from the leading jurists of al-Madīnah, whose word was authoritative, that they used to say: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with them both, ruled regarding the custody of his grandson 'Āṣim ibn 'Umar in favour of 'Āṣim's grandmother, that she should have custody of him until he reached maturity, while Umm 'Āṣim was at that time alive and married. [Ḍa'īf]"
"15771","(15765) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, who said: There was a woman from the Anṣār in the marriage of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and she bore him ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar. Then ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) separated from her. One day he rode towards Qubāʾ and found his son playing in the courtyard of the mosque. He took him by his upper arm and placed him before him on the mount. The boy's grandmother caught up with them and contested him for the child. They both came to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him). ʿUmar said, \He is my son.\"" The woman said"," \""He is my son.\"" Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," \""Leave him between her and him.\"" ʿUmar did not press the matter further. [Weak]"""
"15772","(15766) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Maḥmūdī al-Marwazī narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Mūsā narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Mujālid, from ʿĀmir, from Masrūq, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) divorced Umm ʿĀṣim, and the child was in the care of his grandmother. She took the matter to Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) for judgment. He ruled that the child should remain with his grandmother and that the maintenance would be upon ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said, \She has more right to him.\"" [Weak]"""
"15773","(15767) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd informed us, Ibn Shuʿayb informed us, Ibn Lahīʿah al-Ḥaḍramī informed us from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd Allāh, the client of Ufrah, that he informed him from Zayd ibn Isḥāq ibn Jāriyah al-Anṣārī, that he informed him: When ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) brought the dispute concerning his son to Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled in favor of the mother. Then he said, \I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Do not separate a mother from her child.'\"" [Weak]"""
"15774","(15768) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ʿUmrah in Dhū al-Qaʿdah. The people of Makkah refused to let him enter Makkah until he agreed with them to stay for only three days. When they wrote the treaty, they wrote: \This is what Muḥammad"," the Messenger of Allah"," has agreed to.\"" They said"," \""We do not accept this. Had we known that you were the Messenger of Allah"," we would not have prevented you from anything. But you are Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh.\"" He said"," \""I am the Messenger of Allah"," and I am Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh. O ʿAlī"," erase 'the Messenger of Allah.'\"" He said"," \""By Allah"," I will never erase you.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took the document — and he did not know how to write well — and wrote in place of \""the Messenger of Allah\"": \""This is what Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh has agreed to: that no arms shall be brought into Makkah except a sword in its sheath; that no one shall be taken from its people if he wishes to follow him; and that none of his Companions shall be prevented from staying there if he wishes.\"" When he entered Makkah and the time expired"," they came to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) and said"," \""Tell your companion to leave us"," for the time has expired.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed"," and the daughter of Ḥamzah followed him"," calling out"," \""O uncle! O uncle!\"" ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) took her by the hand and said to Fāṭimah (peace be upon her)"," \""Here"," take your cousin.\"" She carried her. Then ʿAlī"," Zayd"," and Jaʿfar (may Allah be pleased with them) disputed over her. ʿAlī said"," \""I took her"," and she is my cousin.\"" Jaʿfar said"," \""She is my cousin"," and her maternal aunt is under my care (i.e."," is my wife).\"" Zayd said"," \""She is my brother's daughter.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled in favor of her maternal aunt and said"," \""The maternal aunt is in the position of the mother.\"" He said to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," \""You are from me"," and I am from you.\"" He said to Jaʿfar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," \""You resemble me in creation and character.\"" He said to Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him)"," \""You are our brother and our freedman.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā.\n\nThus ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated it from Isrāʾīl"," incorporating the narrations together.\n\nIsmāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated the story of the daughter of Ḥamzah from Isrāʾīl"," from Abū Isḥāq"," from Hānīʾ ibn Hānīʾ and Hubayrah"," from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). And likewise ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated it on another occasion separately. [Authentic. Agreed upon.]"""
"15775","(15769) Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah and others narrated it from Abū Isḥāq, as Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād. Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, Asad ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us, my father and others narrated to me from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed in Makkah for three days during the ʿUmrah of Qaḍāʾ. When the third day arrived, they said to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), \This is the last day stipulated by your companion. Tell him to leave.\"" He conveyed this to the Prophet"," and he said"," \""Yes","\"" and he departed. [Authentic. Previously mentioned.]"""
"15776","(15770) Abū Isḥāq said: Hānīʾ ibn Hānīʾ and Hubayrah ibn Yarīm narrated to me from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The daughter of Ḥamzah followed them, calling out, \O uncle! O uncle!\"" ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) took her by the hand and said to Fāṭimah (peace be upon her)"," \""Here"," take your cousin.\"" She carried her. Then ʿAlī"," Zayd ibn Ḥārithah"," and Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with them) disputed over her. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," \""I took her"," and she is my cousin.\"" Jaʿfar said"," \""She is my cousin"," and her maternal aunt is under my care.\"" Zayd said"," \""She is my brother's daughter.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled in her favor for her maternal aunt and said"," \""The maternal aunt is in the position of the mother.\"" He said to Zayd"," \""You are our brother and our freedman.\"" He hopped back. He said to Jaʿfar"," \""You most resemble me in creation and character.\"" He hopped back behind Zayd's hop. Then he said to me"," \""You are from me"," and I am from you.\"" I hopped back behind Jaʿfar's hop. He said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," \""Will you not marry the daughter of Ḥamzah?\"" He said"," \""She is the daughter of my foster brother.\""\n\nIt is possible that the narration of Abū Isḥāq from al-Barāʾ regarding the story of the daughter of Ḥamzah is abridged"," as we have narrated"," and that he then narrated it from both of them from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) in a more complete form"," as we have narrated. The story of the hopping appears in their narration but not in the narration of al-Barāʾ. And Allah knows best.\n\nWe have also narrated this story from Muḥammad ibn Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjayr"," from his father"," from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him). [Authentic. Agreed upon.]"""
"15777","(15771) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal informed us, al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from Yazīd ibn al-Hād, from Muḥammad ibn Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjayr, from his father Nāfiʿ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), in the story of the daughter of Ḥamzah. He said: Jaʿfar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \I have more right to her"," for her maternal aunt is under my care.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""As for the girl"," I rule in favor of Jaʿfar"," for her maternal aunt is under his care"," and the maternal aunt is indeed a mother.\"" Thus he narrated it to us.\n\nAnd likewise Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī narrated it from Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah"," and likewise ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated it from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad. And it is in the Sunan of Abū Dāwūd"," from al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm"," from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAmr"," from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad"," from Yazīd ibn al-Hād"," from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm"," from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjayr"," from his father"," from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd what we hold is that the first narration is more authentic. And likewise al-Uwaysī narrated it from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad. [Authentic. Agreed upon.]"""
"15778","(15772) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Mihrān narrated to us, Abū al-Ṭāhir informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him from al-ʿAjlān, the client of Fāṭimah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that he said: \The slave is entitled to his food and his clothing"," and he shall not be burdened with work beyond his capacity.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir. [Authentic. Narrated by Muslim"," 1669.]"""
"15779","(15773) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ashajj, from ʿAjlān Abī Muḥammad, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The slave is entitled to his food and his clothing in a fair manner"," and he shall not be burdened with work beyond his capacity.\"" [Authentic. Narrated by Muslim"," 1669.]"""
"15780","(15774) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī al-Anṣārī narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Abī al-Ruṭayl narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd ibn Abjar narrated from his father. And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb al-Mukharramī narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Jarmī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd ibn Abjar narrated from his father, from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif, from Khaythamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: We were sitting with ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr when a steward of his came and entered. He said, \Have you given the slaves their provisions?\"" He said"," \""No.\"" He said"," \""Go and give them.\"" And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""It is enough sin for a believer to withhold the food of one whom he owns.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Jarmī. [Authentic. Muslim"," 996.]"""
"15781","(15775) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan al-'Amiri narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated from al-A'mash, from al-Ma'rur, who said: We met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadha. He was wearing a garment, and his slave boy was wearing a similar one. A man said to him: \O Abu Dharr"," if you were to take this garment from your slave boy and wear it"," it would form a complete set"," and you could clothe your slave boy with another garment.\"" He replied: \""Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'They are your brothers — Allah has placed them under your authority. So whoever has his brother under his authority"," let him feed him from what he himself eats"," and clothe him from what he himself wears"," and do not burden him with what overwhelms him. And if you do burden him with what overwhelms him"," then assist him.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim both recorded it in their Sahih collections from the hadith of al-A'mash. [Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15782","(15776) And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Khwarizmi in Baghdad informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad — he is Ibn Hamdan al-Naysaburi — narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Nadr al-Harashi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Yunus narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated from al-Ma'rur, who said: We arrived at al-Rabadha and came to Abu Dharr. He was wearing a complete set of garments (hullah), and his slave boy was wearing another. We said: \If you were to clothe your slave boy with something else and combine these two garments into one complete set…\"" He said: \""Let me narrate to you regarding this. I once insulted a man whose mother was a non-Arab"," and I disparaged her. The man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained about me. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'Did you insult so-and-so?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you mention his mother?' I said: 'Whoever insults men"," his father and mother are mentioned"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'You are a man in whom there remains jahiliyyah (ignorance).' I said: 'Even at the time of my old age?' He said: 'Yes. They are your brothers — Allah has placed them under your authority. So whoever has his brother under his authority"," let him feed him from his own food"," clothe him from his own clothing"," and not burden him with what overwhelms him. And if you burden him with what overwhelms him"," then assist him.'\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Yunus"," and al-Bukhari recorded it from another chain from al-A'mash. [Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15783","(15777) Abu 'Ali al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahmuyah al-'Askari in Basra informed us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi narrated to us: Abu Iyas narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Wasil al-Ahdab narrated to us. He said: I heard al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd saying: I saw Abu Dharr al-Ghifari — may Allah be pleased with him — wearing a complete set of garments (hullah), and his slave boy wearing a complete set. I asked him about that, and he said: \I insulted a man and he complained about me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Did you reproach him by mentioning his mother?' Then he said to me: 'Your brothers — Allah has placed them under your authority. So whoever has his brother under his authority"," let him feed him from what he eats"," clothe him from what he wears"," and do not burden them with what overwhelms them. And if you burden them with what overwhelms them"," then assist them.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in his Sahih from Adam"," and Muslim recorded it from another chain from Shu'bah. [Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15784","(15778) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razi narrated to us: Jarir narrated from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Muwarriq, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever finds his slave compliant"," let him feed him from what he eats and clothe him from what he wears. And whoever does not find them compliant"," let him sell them"," and do not torment the creation of Allah.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15785","(15779) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Ibrahim ibn Abi Khidash ibn 'Utban ibn Abi Lahb, that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying regarding slaves: \Feed them from what you eat"," and clothe them from what you wear.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: \""And if one does not do this"," then he is bound by what the Prophet ﷺ said: 'His maintenance and his clothing are a duty upon you bil-ma'ruf (in a reasonable manner).' And al-ma'ruf"," according to us"," is what is customary for someone of his standing in the land in which he resides.\"" [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""
"15786","(15780) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the servant of any one of you brings his food"," let him seat him with him. If he does not do so"," then let him hand him one or two morsels (uklah)"," for he has endured its heat and smoke.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in his Sahih from Hajjaj ibn Minhal and others"," from Shu'bah. [Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]\n\nAl-Shafi'i — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: \""And this indicates what we have described regarding the difference between the food of the slave and the food of his master.\"""""
"15787","(15781) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Farra' informed us: Abu Nu'aym al-Mala'i and Abd Allah ibn Maslamah both said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us: Musa ibn Yasar narrated from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \When the servant of any one of you prepares food for him and brings it"," having endured its heat and smoke"," let him seat him with him so that he may eat. If the food is scarce and limited"," let him place one or two morsels (uklah) in his hand.\""\n\nDawud ibn Qays said: \""Al-uklah means al-luqmah (a morsel).\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi. [Sahih — agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15788","(15782) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Sufyan narrated from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the servant of any one of you has prepared his food"," enduring its heat and smoke"," let him call him to sit with him. If he refuses"," then let him moisten a morsel for him and hand it to him or give it to him.\"" Or he said a word to that effect. [Sahih]"""
"15789","(15783) And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: 'Ubayd ibn Sharik informed us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Layth narrated from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, that al-'Ajlan Abu Muhammad narrated to him before his death, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The slave has the right to his food and his clothing"," and he shall not be burdened with work that he cannot bear.\"" [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""
"15790","(15784) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi all said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated from al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the earnings of a slave woman, unless she has a recognized occupation or a known means of earning.\n\nAnd 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated it from al-Zanj ibn Khalid, from Haram ibn 'Uthman, from Abu 'Atiq, from Jabir, in a marfu' (elevated) chain. [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"
"15791","(15785) Abū Jaʿfar — Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī — and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣibghī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us: Ibn Abī Uways informed us: Mālik —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us from his paternal uncle Abū Suhayl, from his father, that he heard ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) say in his sermon: \Do not impose earning upon a young child"," for if you impose earning upon him"," he will steal. And do not impose earning upon a slave woman who has no skill"," for if you impose earning upon her"," she will earn through her private parts.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Shāfiʿī. Ibn Abī Uways added in his narration: \""Be forgiving"," as Allah has been forgiving to you"," and feed them from what is wholesome of food.\"" Some of them raised it from ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) from the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī"," and its raising is weak. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15792","(15786) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Mālik ibn Anas and Sufyān ibn Saʿīd al-Thawrī informed us that Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated to them from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: Abū Ṭaybah cupped the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so he gave him two ṣāʿs or one ṣāʿ of dates, and he instructed his family to reduce his kharāj (tax/levy) for him.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from another route from Ḥumayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"
"15793","(15787) Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl al-Ṣayrafī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd informed us: My father informed me: al-Awzāʿī informed me: A man from among us, called Nuhayk ibn Yarīm, informed me: Mughīth ibn Sumayy informed me, saying: al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām (may Allah be pleased with him) had a thousand slaves who paid him kharāj, yet he would not bring any of their kharāj into his house. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15794","(15788) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najīd informed us: Abū Muslim informed us: Abū ʀāṣim narrated to us from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from Dirham, the mawlā of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: My master imposed upon me one dirham every day. So I came to Abū Hurayrah, and he said: \Fear Allah"," and fulfil the right of Allah and the right of your master.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15795","(15789) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Mālik ibn Anas and Yūnus ibn Yazīd and al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed us that Ibn Shihāb narrated to them from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that Abū Masʿūd ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade them from the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer — except that Yūnus said in the ḥadīth: \Three"," they are unlawful earnings (suḥt).\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15796","(15790) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Kāmil al-Jaḥdarī informed us: Abū ʿAwānah narrated to us from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Sufyān, from Jābir, who said: There were two slave girls of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy — one was called Musaykah and the other Umaymah — and he used to coerce them into prostitution. They complained of this to the Prophet (ﷺ), so Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution, if they desire chastity} [al-Nūr 33] up to His words: {Forgiving, Merciful.}\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kāmil. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15797","(15791) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from al-Aʿmash —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us from Abū ʿUbayd, who said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to me from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Sufyān, from Jābir, who said: There was a slave girl of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy, and he used to coerce her into fornication, so there was revealed: {And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution, if they desire chastity, seeking the transient goods of worldly life. And whoever compels them, then indeed, Allah, after their compulsion, is Forgiving, Merciful.} [al-Nūr 33] In the narration of Abū Muʿāwiyah, he said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl used to say to his slave girl: \Go and earn something for us","\"" so Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: {And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution} [al-Nūr 33] up to {Forgiving"," Merciful.} Abū ʿUbayd said: \""The forgiveness is for them"," not for the master.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15798","(15792) He said: And Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to me from ʿAwf, from al-Ḥasan, regarding this verse, he said: \For them"," by Allah"," for them"," by Allah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan]"""
"15799","(15793) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh informed us: Muʿtamir — he is Ibn Sulaymān al-Taymī — narrated to me from his father regarding the verse {And whoever compels them, then indeed, Allah, after their compulsion, is Forgiving, Merciful}: Saʿīd ibn Abī al-Ḥasan said: \Forgiving to those who were compelled.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15800","(15794) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Abū Kāmil informed us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us: al-Aʿmash narrated to us from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from his father, from Abū Masʿūd, who said: \I was striking my slave with a whip when I heard a voice from behind me: 'Know"," O Abū Masʿūd!' I did not understand the voice due to anger. Then he said: 'Know"," O Abū Masʿūd!' When he drew near to me"," behold"," it was the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: 'Know"," O Abū Masʿūd"," that Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has greater power over you than you have over this slave.' So I threw the whip from my hand and said: 'I will never strike a slave again after this day.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kāmil. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15801","(15795) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ and Ibn al-Muthannā both said: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from his father, from Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī, who said:\n\n\I was striking a slave boy of mine when I heard a voice from behind me: 'Know"," O Abū Masʿūd! Know"," O Abū Masʿūd! Know"," O Abū Masʿūd! Allah has greater power over you than you have over him.' I turned around and it was the Prophet ﷺ. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," he is free for the sake of Allah.' He said: 'Had you not done so"," the Fire would have scorched you"," or the Fire would have touched you.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ"," Abū Kurayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15802","(15796) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar and Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl both said: Musaddad narrated to us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us, from Firās, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Zādhān Abī ʿUmar, that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) freed a slave of his, then he picked up a stick from the ground and said: \I have no reward in this equal to that","\"" and then he said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever slaps his slave or strikes him a blow that he did not deserve"," his expiation is to free him.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kāmil"," from Abū ʿAwanah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15803","(15797) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī narrated to us; Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Fuḍayl ibn Ghazwān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Fuḍayl ibn Ghazwān narrated to us; Ibn Abī Nuʿm narrated to us; Abū Hurayrah narrated, saying: Abū al-Qāsim, the Prophet of Repentance ﷺ, narrated to me, saying:\n\n\Whoever accuses his slave of something he is innocent of"," the Ḥadd punishment will be carried out against him on the Day of Resurrection"," unless it is as he said.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," from Yaḥyā"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Fuḍayl.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15804","(15798) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī narrated to us; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrah narrated to us; al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated to me; Abū Hānīʾ narrated to me, from ʿAbbās al-Ḥajarī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," my servant behaves unjustly and oppresses.\"" He said: \""You should forgive him seventy times every day.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15805","(15799) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Hamdānī and Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Sarḥ narrated to us — and this is the ḥadīth of al-Hamdānī, and it is the more complete — both saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Abū Hānīʾ al-Khawlānī informed me, from al-ʿAbbās ibn Julayd al-Ḥajarī, who said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar say:\n\n\A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," how many times should we forgive the servant?' He repeated the question to him"," and he remained silent. When it was the third time"," he said: 'Forgive him seventy times every day.'\""\n\nAnd al-Aṣbagh said"," from Ibn Wahb"," with his chain: \""He heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ","\"" but Ibn ʿUmar is more correct. [Ḥasan]"""
"15806","(15800) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah both said: Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us, from Mughīrah, from Umm Mūsā, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\n\The last words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were: 'The prayer"," the prayer! Fear Allah regarding those whom your right hands possess (i.e."," your slaves).'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"15807","(15801) Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ṭūsī al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to me; al-Layth ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah, who said:\n\n\Jibrīl (peace be upon him) continued to enjoin upon me the rights of the neighbour to the point where I thought he would make him an heir. And he continued to enjoin upon me the rights of the slave to the point where I thought he would set a fixed term for him"," upon reaching which he would be freed.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15808","(15802) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥabbān al-Tammār al-Anṣārī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Ṣāliḥ ibn Ṣāliḥ, from al-Shaʿbī, from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Any man who has a female slave and disciplines her well"," giving her the best upbringing"," and teaches her well"," giving her the best education"," then frees her and marries her"," he shall have a double reward. And any slave who fulfils the right of Allah and the right of his masters"," he shall have a double reward.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," and Muslim narrated it from other routes from Ṣāliḥ.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15809","(15803) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated to us, from al-Suddī, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, who said:\n\n\ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon and said: 'O people"," carry out the prescribed punishments upon your slaves"," those among them who are married and those who are not married.' A female slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had committed adultery"," and he ordered me to flog her. I came to her and she was in a state of post-natal bleeding"," so I feared that if I flogged her she would die. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him"," and he said: 'You have done well.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Muqaddamī"," from Abū Dāwūd. The remainder of this chapter is in the Book of Ḥudūd."""
"15810","(15804) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir said to me: \What is your name?\"" I said: \""Shuʿbah.\"" He said: \""Abū Shuʿbah narrated to me — and he was a refined man — from Suwayd ibn Muqarrin (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said:\n\n\""A man struck his slave — or a person — with a slap. Suwayd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Do you not know that the face is sacred? I saw myself as the seventh of seven brothers during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We had only one servant"," and one of us slapped him"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to free him.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from two other routes from Shuʿbah. Some of them said in the ḥadīth: \""One of us struck his face.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15811","(15805) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us; al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us; Shuʿbah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawiyah narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us; Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us, he said: I heard Hilāl ibn Yasāf saying: We used to sell cloth in the house of Suwayd ibn Muqarrin — may Allah be pleased with him — when a slave-girl of his came out and said something to a man, and that man slapped her. So Suwayd ibn Muqarrin — may Allah be pleased with him — said to him: Did you slap her face? I myself was the seventh of seven, and we had no servant but this one, and one of us slapped her, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to set her free.\n\nThe wording is that of Ādam's narration. Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī ʿAdī from Shuʿbah."
"15812","(15806) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Muʿāwiyah ibn Suwayd, who said: I struck a slave of ours, then I fled before midday prayer and prayed behind my father. He called him and called me, then said: Take retribution from him. So he forgave him. Then he said: We, the Banū Muqarrin, were in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had only one servant. One of us slapped him, and that reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: Set her free. They said: They have no other servant. He said: Then let them employ her, and when they no longer need her, let them set her free. [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. And in this there is evidence that the command to manumit is a command of recommendation and encouragement, and Allah knows best."
"15813","(15807) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq and Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār both said: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us from Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū Mūsā Hārūn ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, he said: I read to Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When a slave is sincere toward his master and worships Allah well, he shall have his reward twice over.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī]"
"15814","(15808) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Burayd from Abū Burdah from Abū Mūsā from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: For the slave who worships his Lord well and fulfills toward his master the rights, sincerity, and obedience that are due from him, there are two rewards: the reward for his worship of his Lord and the reward for his fulfilling the rights due to his master.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"15815","(15809) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī informed us; Abū al-Muwajjah informed us; ʿAbdān informed us; ʿAbdullāh informed us; Yūnus narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: I heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab saying: Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The righteous slave shall have a double reward. By Him in whose hand is the soul of Abū Hurayrah, were it not for jihād in the path of Allah, Ḥajj, and kindness to my mother, I would love to die as a slave.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Bishr ibn Muḥammad from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak, and Muslim narrated it through two other routes from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15816","(15810) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When a slave fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters, he shall have two rewards. He said: So I narrated it to Kaʿb, and he said: There shall be no reckoning upon him, nor upon a believer who abstains from worldly excess.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Abū Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15817","(15811) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us — may Allah be pleased with him. And in the narration of al-Ramādī: that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: How excellent it is for a slave that Allah cause him to die while he worships his Lord well and obeys his master — how excellent for him, how excellent for him.\n\nAl-Ramādī added in his narration: He said: And ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — whenever he passed by a slave, would say: O so-and-so, give glad tidings of a double reward.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, without the statement of ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15818","(15812) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih from Abū Hurayrah, who said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Let none of you say: \Give your lord to drink","\"" \""Feed your lord","\"" or \""Perform wuḍūʾ for your lord.\"" And let none of you say: \""My lord","\"" but rather say: \""My master"," my patron.\"" And let none of you say: \""My slave"," my slave-girl","\"" but rather say: \""My young man"," my young woman"," my boy.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15819","(15813) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us; Abū al-Aḥraz Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd ibn Jamīl al-Azdī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm Danūqā narrated to us; al-Aḥwaṣ ibn Jawwāb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us; ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from ʿIkrimah from Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar from Abū Hurayrah — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever incites a servant against his family is not of us, and whoever corrupts a woman against her husband is not of us.\n\nZayd ibn al-Ḥubbāb followed him in narrating from ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15820","(15814) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us; Mahdī ibn Maymūn narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Yaʿqūb narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn Saʿd, the freed slave of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted me behind him one day and confided to me a narration that I would not relate to anyone among the people. And the most beloved place in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would take cover for his need was a raised mound or a cluster of date palms — meaning a garden wall. He said: So he entered a garden belonging to a man of the Anṣār, and there was a camel therein. When it saw the Prophet ﷺ, its eyes overflowed with tears. The Prophet ﷺ came to it and stroked from its chest to its hump and its ears, and it became calm. He said: Who is the lord of this camel? To whom does this camel belong? A young man of the Anṣār came and said: It is mine, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Will you not fear Allah regarding this beast over whom Allah has given you authority? For it complains to me that you starve it and exhaust it.\n\nMuslim narrated the beginning of this ḥadīth in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15821","(15815) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Miṣrī, narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb ibn Muslim al-Miṣrī narrated to us — Mālik ibn Anas informed me — from Nāfiʿ — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman was punished on account of a cat which she had confined until it died of hunger"," and she was made to enter the Fire because of it. It was said to her — and Allah knows best — 'You neither fed it nor gave it water when you confined it"," nor did you release it so that it could eat from the vermin of the earth until it died of hunger.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15822","(15816) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us — Ismāʿīl narrated from Mālik, mentioning it with his chain of narration, similar to the above, except that he did not mention at the end the words \until it died of hunger.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim transmitted it through another route from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15823","(15817) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar narrated — from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: \This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us","\"" and he said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""A woman entered the Fire on account of a cat of hers which she had tied up. She neither fed it nor released it to eat from the vermin of the earth until it died of emaciation.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15824","(15818) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us — Mālik ibn Anas informed me — from Sumayy, the freedman of Abū Bakr — from Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Sammān — from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \While a man was on a road"," he was overcome by thirst. He came upon a well"," descended into it"," and drank. Then he came out and found a dog licking the damp earth from thirst. The man descended into the well again"," filled his shoe with water"," held it in his mouth"," and gave the dog to drink. Allah thanked him and forgave him.\"" They said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," do we have reward in regard to beasts?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""In every moist liver (i.e."," every living creature) there is reward.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah"," both from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15825","(15819) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūh, i.e., al-Shaybānī, narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Abū al-Ṭāhir narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us — Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim informed me — from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī — from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn — from Abū Hurayrah, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A dog was circling a well"," almost dying of thirst"," when it was seen by a prostitute of the Children of Israel. She removed her shoe"," drew water for it"," and gave it to drink"," and she was forgiven because of that.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Talid from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15826","(15820) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Mukarram narrated to us — Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us — al-Murajjā ibn Rajāʾ al-Yashkurī narrated to us — Salm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I heard Sawādah ibn al-Rabīʿ say: \I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him"," and he gave me provisions for the journey and said"," 'When you return to your children"," command them to give good nourishment to their milk-animals"," and command them to trim their nails and not to wound the udders of their cattle when they milk them.'\"" Muḥammad ibn Ḥumrān narrated it from Salm al-Jarmī"," adding in it: \""And say to them"," 'Milk their young while they are lean"," before a year of drought afflicts them and they become emaciated.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"15827","(15821) Abū Muḥammad — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal — informed us — Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us — Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — al-Aʿmash narrated — from Yaʿqūb ibn Baḥīr — from Ḍirār ibn al-Azwār, who said: \I gifted a milch-camel to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he ordered me to milk it. I milked it and exerted myself in milking it"," and he said"," 'Leave the milk for the young one (i.e."," leave some milk for the calf).'\"" Ibn al-Mubārak and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dāwūd similarly narrated it from al-Aʿmash"," but Abū Muʿāwiyah differed from them"," narrating it from al-Aʿmash from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sinān from Yaʿqūb from Ḍirār"," and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated from Abū Muʿāwiyah in accordance with the narration of the majority. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15828","(15822) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḍabbī, may Allah have mercy on him — narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us — from al-Aʿmash — from Shaqīq — from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl — from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about the major sins. He said"," 'That you invoke a rival unto Allah"," though it is He who created you; that you kill your child out of fear that he would eat with you; and that you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbour.' Then he recited: {And those who do not invoke with Allah another deity"," nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden"," except by right"," nor commit adultery — and whoever does that will meet a penalty} [al-Furqān 68].\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim transmitted it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15829","(15823) And Abū Muḥammad — Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī — informed us — Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharzah narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Jarīr narrated — from al-Aʿmash — from Abū Wāʾil — from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: A man said, \O Messenger of Allah"," which sin is the greatest before Allah?\"" He said"," \""That you invoke a rival unto Allah"," though it is He who created you.\"" He said"," \""Then which?\"" He said"," \""That you kill your child out of fear that he would eat with you.\"" He said"," \""Then which?\"" He said"," \""That you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbour.\"" Then Allah revealed in confirmation of that: {And those who do not invoke with Allah another deity…} up to His words: {a penalty} [al-Furqān 68]. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah. Al-Shāfiʿī said — and Allah"," the Most High"," said: {And whoever kills a soul for other than a soul or corruption in the land"," it is as if he has killed mankind entirely; and whoever gives it life"," it is as if he has given life to mankind entirely} [al-Māʾidah 32] — and He said: {And recite to them the news of the two sons of Adam in truth"," when they both offered a sacrifice"," and it was accepted from one of them and not accepted from the other. He said"," \""I will surely kill you\""} up to His words: {and he became of the losers} [al-Māʾidah 27–31]."""
"15830","(15824) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — informed us — Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād al-Abīwardī narrated to us — Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash — [separate chain] and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūnus al-Ḍabbī narrated to us — Abū Badr narrated to us — Sulaymān al-Aʿmash narrated — [separate chain] and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Murrah — from Masrūq — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \No soul is unjustly killed except that a share of the burden of its blood falls upon the first son of Adam"," for he was the first to initiate killing.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Sufyān. In the narration of Abū Muʿāwiyah it reads: \""No soul is unjustly killed except that a share of its blood falls upon the first son of Adam"," for he was the first to initiate killing.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq ʿalayh] Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿUmar from Sufyān"," and from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Ibn Numayr from Abū Muʿāwiyah. And Allah"," the Most High"," said: {And whoever kills a believer intentionally"," his recompense is Hell"," wherein he will abide eternally"," and Allah has become angry with him and has cursed him and has prepared for him a great punishment} [al-Nisāʾ 93]."""
"15831","(15825) Abū ʿAlī — al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī — informed us; Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī — narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us; al-Mughīrah ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to us, saying: I heard Saʿīd ibn Jubayr say: The people of Kūfah differed regarding His statement — {And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein} — so I set out concerning it to Ibn ʿAbbās and asked him about it. He said: This verse — {his recompense is Hell} — was revealed among the last of what was revealed, and nothing abrogated it.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam, and Muslim narrated it through other routes from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"
"15832","(15826) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Maḥmūyah informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Ādam narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us; Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about His statement — {And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell} — and he said: There is no repentance for him. And I asked about His statement — {And those who do not invoke with Allah another deity} — up to His statement — {except for those who repent and believe} — and he said: This pertained to the Jāhiliyyah.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it from Ādam, and Muslim narrated it through another route from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"
"15833","(15827) Abū ʿAmr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb — informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-ʿAdl informed me; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; both said: Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr; Saʿīd ibn Jubayr — or al-Ḥakam narrated to me from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr — narrated to me, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā commanded me, saying: Ask Ibn ʿAbbās about these two verses — what is their import? The verse in Sūrat al-Furqān: {And those who do not invoke with Allah another deity…} up to His statement: {and do not commit adultery}; and the verse in Sūrat al-Nisāʾ: {And whoever kills a believer intentionally…} to the end of the verse. He said: So I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about that. He said: When the one in al-Furqān was revealed, the polytheists of the people of Makkah said: \We have killed the soul which Allah has forbidden"," and we have invoked with Allah another deity"," and we have committed abominations.\"" So Allah"," the Most High"," revealed: {Except for those who repent and believe and do righteous deeds — for those"," Allah will replace their evil deeds with good deeds.} So this is for those. As for the one in al-Nisāʾ — {And whoever kills a believer intentionally} — he recited up to His statement: {a great [punishment]} — he said: When a man knows Islam and learns the laws of Islam"," then kills a believer intentionally"," his recompense is Hell"," and there is no repentance for him. I mentioned that to Mujāhid"," and he said: \""Except for the one who repents.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah from Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15834","(15828) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq narrated from Abū al-Zinād from Mujāld ibn ʿAwf that Khārijah ibn Zayd said: I heard Zayd ibn Thābit say in this place: This verse — {And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein} — was revealed after the one in al-Furqān — {And those who do not invoke with Allah another deity and do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden, except by right} — by six months. The Shaykh said: Thus was the revelation of the two verses, but the interpretation of the last verse is what [has been stated]. [Munkar]"
"15835","(15829) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated from Abū Mijlaz regarding His statement — {And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein} — Abū Mijlaz said: That is his recompense, but if Allah wills to forgive him, He forgives him. [Ḥasan for other than the previous]"
"15836","(15830) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Abū Shiḥāb narrated from Sulaymān al-Taymī from Abū Mijlaz, and he mentioned it, except that he said: But if Allah wills to pardon his punishment, He does so. [Ḥasan]"
"15837","(15831) The Ustādh Abū Manṣūr — ʿAbd al-Qāhir ibn Ṭāhir ibn Muḥammad — and Abū al-Qāsim — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥamdān al-Fārisī — and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah — and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṣaffār — all said: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najayd al-Sulamī informed us; Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us; Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us, saying: We were in the company of Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, and we were speaking in his presence, when a man from the people stood and said: {Whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell} — until he completed the verse. Muḥammad became angry and said: \Where are you regarding this verse? {Indeed"," Allah does not forgive that partners should be associated with Him"," but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills.} Leave me! Depart from me!\"" So he was expelled. [Ḥasan]"""
"15838","(15832) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah al-Bashīrī informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḍabbī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said: The people of knowledge, when they were asked, would say: \There is no repentance for him.\"" But when a person was afflicted [with this sin]"," they would say to him: \""Repent!\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15839","(15833) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr informed us; Aḥmad narrated to us; Saʿīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated from Kardam from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A man came to him and said: \I filled my trough"," waiting for my beast to come to drink"," but I did not wake except to find a man who had broken the edge of the trough with his she-camel"," and the water had flowed out. So I rose in alarm and struck him with the sword and killed him.\"" He said: \""This is not like what he [Allah] said.\"" So he commanded him to repent. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15840","(15834) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar in Baghdād informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Mushajjar narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us. He said: I heard Abū Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī say: A man came to ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — and said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," I have killed — is there any repentance for me?\"" So ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — recited over him: {Ḥā Mīm. The revelation of the Book is from Allah"," the Almighty"," the All-Knowing"," the Forgiver of sin"," the Acceptor of repentance"," the Severe in punishment.} Then he said to him: \""Do righteous deeds and do not despair.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that which confirms the interpretation of Abū Mijlaz — may Allah have mercy on him. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15841","(15835) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, informing us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us that Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ḥajjāj al-Ṣawwāf from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir: that Ṭufayl ibn ʿAmr al-Dawsī came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \Do you have a fortified stronghold and a place of refuge?\"" He said: \""A fortress that belonged to [the tribe of] Daws during the Jāhiliyyah.\"" But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ refused that"," on account of what Allah had stored for the Anṣār. When the Prophet ﷺ emigrated to Madīnah"," Ṭufayl emigrated with him"," and a man from his people emigrated with him. They found Madīnah uncongenial"," and the man fell ill. He became distressed"," so he took arrowheads and severed his own finger-joints with them. His hands bled profusely"," and he died. Ṭufayl saw him in his dream in a fine appearance"," but saw him with his hands covered. He said to him: \""Why do I see you with your hands covered?\"" He said: \""It was said to me: 'We shall not mend of you that which you have corrupted.'\"" So Ṭufayl related his dream to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Allah"," forgive him even for his hands.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb."""
"15842","(15836) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Hāshimī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār, and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us. Isḥāq said: \He informed us","\"" and the other two said: \""He narrated to us.\"" Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us — and the wording is that of Ibn al-Muthannā — he said: My father narrated to me from Qatādah from Abī al-Ṣiddīq al-Nājī from Abī Saʿīd that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""There was among those before you a man who killed ninety-nine souls. He asked about the most learned person on earth and was directed to a monk. He went to him and said: 'I have killed ninety-nine souls — is there any repentance for me?' He said: 'No.' So he killed him"," thereby completing one hundred. Then he asked about the most learned person on earth and was directed to a scholar. He went to him and said: 'I have killed a hundred souls — is there any repentance for me?' He said: 'Yes. Who can stand between you and repentance? Go to such-and-such a land"," for therein are people who worship Allah. Worship with them"," and do not return to your land"," for it is an evil land.' So he set out"," and when he had reached halfway along the path"," death came to him. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed over him. The angels of mercy said: 'He came repentant"," turning his heart toward Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.' The angels of punishment said: 'He never did any good at all.' Then an angel came to them in the form of a human and they appointed him as arbiter between them. He said: 'Measure the distance between the two lands. Whichever one he is closer to"," that is his.' They measured and found him closer to the land he had intended. So the angels of mercy took him.\""\n\nQatādah said: Al-Ḥasan said: \""It has been mentioned to us that when death came to him"," he inclined with his chest [toward the land of righteousness].\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār."""
"15843","(15837) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us that Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Every prophet has a supplication that is answered. I have kept my supplication as intercession for my Ummah"," and it shall reach"," Allah willing"," whoever among them dies associating nothing with Allah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Kurayb and others from Abī Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15844","(15838) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation, informing us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from Thābit al-Bunānī from Anas ibn Mālik that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \My intercession is for the people of major sins among my Ummah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq.]"""
"15845","(15839) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Abī Muʿāwiyah ʿAmr al-Bajalī, who said: I heard Abū ʿAmr al-Shaybānī say: I heard Ibn Masʿud — may Allah be pleased with him — say: I asked the Prophet ﷺ: \Which of the major sins is the greatest?\"" He said: \""That you set up a rival to Allah"," when it is He who created you.\"" I said: \""Then which?\"" He said: \""That you kill your child for fear that he may eat with you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"15846","(15840) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī narrated to us by dictation, informing us that Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Imam Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Dharr Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Qāsim al-Mudhakkir, Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān from Manṣūr, al-Aʿmash, and Wāṣil al-Aḥdab from Abī Wāʾil from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl from ʿAbdullāh, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," which sin is the greatest?\"" He said: \""That you set up a rival to Allah"," when it is He who created you.\"" He said: \""Then what?\"" He said: \""That you kill your child for fear that he may eat with you.\"" He said: \""Then what?\"" He said: \""That you commit zinā with the wife of your neighbour.\""\n\nIn the narration of al-Dhuhlī: \""That you commit zinā with the wife of your neighbour.\""\n\nThe ḥadīth of Manṣūr and al-Aʿmash is connected (mawṣūl)"," while the ḥadīth of Wāṣil from Abī Wāʾil from ʿAbdullāh does not contain mention of ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15847","(15841) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Adīb informed us of the authenticity of that, and Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Dūrī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr and al-Aʿmash from Abī Wāʾil from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl from ʿAbdullāh, who said: A man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," which sin is the greatest?\"" He said: \""That you set up a rival to Allah"," when it is He who created you.\"" He said: \""Then which?\"" He said: \""Then that you kill your child lest he eat with you.\"" He said: \""Then which?\"" He said: \""Then that you commit zinā with the wife of your neighbour.\""\n\nAbū Ḥafṣ said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān once said: from Manṣūr"," al-Aʿmash"," and Wāṣil from Abī Wāʾil from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl from ʿAbdullāh from the Prophet ﷺ. So I said to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: \""Yaḥyā narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr and Sulaymān from Abī Wāʾil from Abī Mayzarah — and he is ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl — from ʿAbdullāh.\"" And Sufyān narrated to me: Wāṣil narrated to us from Abī Wāʾil from ʿAbdullāh. So ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \""Leave it","\"" and Wāṣil was not mentioned after that.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15848","(15842) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us that Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us that Abū al-Yamān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Muzanī — from what I read to him — and Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Harwī both said: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsá narrated to us that Abū al-Yamān narrated to us. He said: Shuʿayb informed me from al-Zuhrī. He said: Abī Idrīs ʿĀʾidhullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh informed me from ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — while a group of his Companions were around him: \Pledge allegiance to me that you shall not associate anything with Allah"," nor steal"," nor commit zinā"," nor kill your children"," nor bring forth a lie that you fabricate between your hands and your feet"," nor disobey me in what is right. Whoever among you fulfils it"," his reward is upon Allah. And whoever among you is afflicted by any of these and is punished for it in this world"," it shall be an expiation for him. And whoever among you is afflicted by any of these and then it is concealed"," his affair is with Allah: if He wills"," He will forgive him"," and if He wills"," He will punish him.\"" He said: \""So we pledged allegiance to him upon that.\""\n\nThe wording of both their narrations is the same"," except that in the narration of al-Qāḍī: from ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit"," who witnessed Badr and was one of the chiefs (nuqabāʾ) of the Night of al-ʿAqabah. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it from another chain from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15849","(15843) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak — may Allah have mercy on him — informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī from Abī Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf, who said: We were with ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — in the house while he was besieged. We used to enter through a passage from which we could hear the words of those in the palace. ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — entered and then came out, his colour changed. It was said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," what is the matter with you?\"" He said: \""They have just threatened me with killing"," and I had not been certain of that from them until today.\"" We said: \""Allah is sufficient for you"," O Commander of the Faithful.\"" He said: \""Why would they kill me"," when I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except in one of three cases: a man who disbelieves after his Islam"," or who commits zinā after [having been in a state of] iḥṣān"," or who kills a soul without [right of] retaliation.' By Allah"," I never committed zinā in the Jāhiliyyah nor in Islam"," ever"," and I never desired a replacement for my religion since Allah guided me"," and I never killed a soul. Why do these people want to kill me?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15850","(15844) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash from ʿAbdullāh ibn Murrah from Masrūq, who said: ʿAbdullāh said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The blood of a man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except in one of three cases: a life for a life"," the married person who commits zinā"," and the one who leaves his religion and separates from the community (jamāʿah).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr from his father"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another chain from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"15851","(15845) Abū Muḥammad — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Mu'mal — informed us; Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb Abū Aḥmad narrated to us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from Abū Sufyān, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh.\n\nAnd from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, both said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they say 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh.' When they say it"," they have protected from me their blood and their property"," except by its right"," and their reckoning is with Allah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through another chain from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15852","(15846) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAdī ibn al-Khiyār, from al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad, that he informed him that he said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and he fights me and strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off"," then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says"," 'I have submitted to Allah' — should I kill him"," O Messenger of Allah"," after he has said it?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Do not kill him.\"" He said: \""I said: O Messenger of Allah"," he has cut off my hand"," then he said that after he cut it off — should I kill him?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Do not kill him. For if you kill him"," then indeed he is in your position before you kill him"," and you are in his position before he says the word that he said.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through other routes from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15853","(15847) Abū Muḥammad — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Mu'mal al-Māsarjisī — narrated to us; Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from Abī Ẓabyān; Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us on a military expedition to al-Ḥuruqāt. They became aware of us and fled. We caught up with a man"," and when we overtook him"," he said"," 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh","' but we struck him until we killed him. Something of that troubled my soul"," so I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'Who will avail you of Lā ilāha illā Allāh on the Day of Resurrection?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," he only said it out of fear of the sword and being killed.' He said: 'Did you not split open his heart so that you might know whether he said it for that reason or not? Who will avail you of Lā ilāha illā Allāh on the Day of Resurrection?'\"" He said: \""He kept repeating it until I wished that I had not become Muslim until that day.\"" Abū Ẓabyān said: \""Saʿd said: 'By Allah"," I would not kill him until Dhū al-Buṭayn — meaning Usāmah — killed him.' A man said: 'Has Allah not said: \""Fight them until there is no more fitnah\"" [al-Baqarah:193]?' Saʿd said: 'We fought until there was no more fitnah"," but you and your companions want us to fight until there is fitnah.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash"," and both narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ḥuṣayn from Abī Ẓabyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15854","(15848) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated to us; Qurrah narrated — (ḥ) and Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān informed me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Qurrah narrated; Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah, and from a man who, in my estimation, was better than ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah, from Abī Bakrah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) addressed the people at Minā and said: \Do you know what day this is?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. Then he said: \""Is it not the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr)?\"" We said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""What land is this?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""Is it not the Sacred Land (al-Balad al-Ḥarām)?\"" We said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," your blood"," your properties"," your honours"," and your skins are sacred to one another"," like the sanctity of your day this"," in your month this. Have I conveyed?\"" We said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""O Allah"," bear witness. Let the one who is present convey to the one who is absent"," for often the one to whom it is conveyed remembers it better than the one who hears it directly.\"" And he said: \""Beware"," do not return to disbelief after me"," striking one another's necks.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Jabalah and others"," all from Abū ʿĀmir. Al-Bukhārī narrated it from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim"," both from Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15855","(15849) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; al-Ḥasan, who is Ibn Sufyān, narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Abī al-Khayr, from al-Ṣunābihī, from ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit, that he said: \I am among the chiefs (nuqabāʾ) who gave bayʿah to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). We pledged to him that we would not associate anything with Allah"," nor commit adultery"," nor steal"," nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right"," nor engage in plundering"," nor disobey. If we do any of that"," then the judgment of that rests with Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15856","(15850) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The greatest of major sins are: associating partners with Allah"," killing the soul"," disobeying one's parents"," and uttering falsehood\"" — or he said: \""bearing false witness.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn Marzūq. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15857","(15851) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Thawr, from Abī al-Mughīth, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Avoid the seven destructive sins.\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what are they?\"" He said: \""Associating partners with Allah"," sorcery"," killing the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right"," consuming ribā"," consuming the property of the orphan"," fleeing from the battlefield"," and accusing chaste"," unaware believing women.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd from Ibn Wahb"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from al-Uwaysī from Sulaymān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15858","(15852) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Tamtām Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us; ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us; Shuʿbah said: Manṣūr, Zubayd, and Sulaymān informed me that they heard Abū Wāʾil narrating from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Reviling a Muslim is fusūq (sinful transgression)"," and fighting him is kufr (disbelief).\"" Zubayd said: \""I said to Abū Wāʾil: 'Did you hear it from ʿAbd Allāh from the Prophet (ﷺ)?' He said: 'Yes.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"15859","(15853) He said: And Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Abū Muslim narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Manṣūr, who said: \I heard Abū Wāʾil narrating from ʿAbd Allāh from the Prophet (ﷺ) a similar ḥadīth.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Numayr from ʿAffān"," the ḥadīth of Sulaymān al-Aʿmash. Both narrated it from the ḥadīth of Zubayd through another route."""
"15860","(15854) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān al-Mawṣilī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Hishām ibn Ḥujayr, from Ṭāwūs, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \It is not the kufr to which you refer; it is not a kufr that removes one from the religion. 'And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed — it is they who are the disbelievers' [al-Māʾidah:44] — it is a kufr lesser than kufr.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15861","(15855) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzzi and Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Musa Amirka al-Naysaburi and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever takes up arms against us is not one of us.\"" He also said: Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated from 'Ubayd Allah"," from Nafi'"," from Ibn 'Umar"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," a similar statement. Both agreed on the hadith of Abu Musa from Abu Kurayb from Abu Usamah"," and Muslim recorded the hadith of Ibn 'Umar from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Abu Usamah. [Sahih. Agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15862","(15856) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \Lasta minna\"" — he does not mean that you are not among the people of Islam"," but rather he means that you are not like us. [Weak (da'if)]"""
"15863","(15857) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahyay al-Dhuhli narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Yahyay al-Kinani narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated from 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A person remains in the spaciousness of his religion so long as he does not shed unlawful blood.\"" [Sahih. Agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15864","(15858) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz also informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-A'la ibn Kanasah al-Asadi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Sa'id narrated from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \A person remains in the spaciousness of his religion so long as he does not shed unlawful blood.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in his Sahih from 'Ali ibn Abi Hashim"," from Ishaq ibn Sa'id ibn 'Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-'As. [Sahih. Agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15865","(15859) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nasawi informed me: Hammad ibn Shakir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ishaq, that is, ibn Sa'id, said: I heard my father narrating from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, who said: \Indeed"," among the perilous matters from which there is no escape for one who casts himself into them is the shedding of unlawful blood without right.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it thus. [Sahih]"""
"15866","(15860) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Khushaysh al-Muqri' in Kufah informed us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah al-Azdhi, known as Ibn Abi al-'Azaim, narrated to us —\n\nAND Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Husayn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mati al-Kufi in Baghdad narrated to us — they both said: Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharzah narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us: al-A'mash narrated from Shaqiq, from 'Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The first matter that will be judged between people regarding bloodshed — meaning on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in his Sahih from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa"," and Muslim recorded it through other chains from al-A'mash. [Sahih. Agreed upon (mutafaqqun 'alayh)]"""
"15867","(15861) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mubarak narrated to us: Sadaqah narrated to us: Khalid ibn Dihaqan narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Zakariyya said: I heard Umm al-Darda' saying: I heard Abu al-Darda' saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Every sin is such that Allah may forgive it"," except one who dies as a polytheist (mushrik) or who kills a believer deliberately.\"" [Sahih]\n\nSadaqah said: Khalid said: Hani' ibn Kalthum ibn Kanaz al-Kinani said: I heard Mahmud ibn Rabi' narrating that he heard 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," who said: \""Whoever kills a believer and then takes pride in his killing"," no compensatory (sarf) or expiatory ('adl) deed will be accepted from him.\""\n\nKhalid ibn Dihaqan then narrated from Ibn Abi Zakariyya"," from Umm al-Darda'"," from Abu al-Darda'"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAnd Hani' ibn Kalthum narrated from Mahmud ibn Rabi'"," from 'Ubadah"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: \""A believer continues to be righteous so long as he does not shed blood.\"" Khalid said: I asked Yahya al-Ghassani about his taking pride in his killing. He said: They are those who kill during tribulation (fitnah)"," then one of them kills and considers himself to be upon guidance"," and never seeks Allah's forgiveness for it."""
"15868","(15862) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Mu'ammal ibn al-Fadl al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated from Khalid ibn Dihaqan, who mentioned the three hadiths, except that in the third hadith he said: \A believer continues to be righteous so long as he does not shed unlawful blood. But when he sheds unlawful blood"," he is ruined (ballah).\"" And he did not mention the explanation of al-Ghassani. [Sahih]"""
"15869","(15863) Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: 'Amr ibn 'Asim narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated from Bishr ibn 'Asim al-Laythi, from 'Uqbah ibn Malik al-Laythi, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," has made it contemptible to me for anyone to kill a believer.\"" He said it three times. [Sahih]"""
"15870","(15864) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sabi'i in Kufah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghifari informed us: 'Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us: 'Ata' ibn Muslim narrated —\n\nAND Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Malini informed us: Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami, Sijadah, narrated to us: 'Ata' ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated from al-'Ala' ibn al-Musayyib, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a man was killed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was not known who had killed him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \A person has been killed while I am among you"," and it is not known who killed him. If the people of the heavens and the people of the earth were to participate in the killing of a believer"," Allah would punish them — unless He wills otherwise.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of al-Malini"," and the hadith of Abu 'Abd Allah is an abridgement: \""If the people of the heavens and the people of the earth were to gather upon the killing of a believing man"," Allah would punish them.\"" [Weak (da'if)]"""
"15871","(15865) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jurjānī in Naysābūr narrated to us; Maḥmūd ibn Khidāsh narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Fazārī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Ziyād al-Shāmī narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever assists in the killing of a Muslim by even half a word"," he will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with it written upon his forehead: 'Despairing of the mercy of Allah.'\"" [Mawḍūʿ]"""
"15872","(15866) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq al-Mu'addib narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Ziyād al-Shāmī narrated it with its chain, the same, except that he said: \On the day he meets Him.\"""""
"15873","(15867) And with this chain from the Prophet (ﷺ), he said: \By Allah"," this world and all that is in it are more insignificant to Allah than the killing of a believer without right.\"" Yazīd ibn Ziyād"," and it is said Ibn Abī Ziyād al-Shāmī"," is Munkar al-ḥadīth. [Mawḍūʿ]"""
"15874","(15868) And the first text has been narrated from another route from al-Zuhrī, as a mursal narration. Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us it; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Thābit al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk al-Bazzāz narrated to us; Nūḥ ibn al-Haytham, son-in-law of Ādam ibn Abī Iyās through his sister, in ʿAsqalān in the year two hundred and twenty, narrated to us; al-Faraj ibn Faḍālah narrated from al-Ḍaḥḥāk, from al-Zuhrī, who raised it (marfūʿan): \Whoever assists in the killing of a believer by even half a word"," he will meet Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," on the Day of Resurrection with it written between his eyes: 'Despairing of the mercy of Allah.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15875","(15869) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Imām informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Yaʿlā ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: \The killing of a believer is greater in the sight of Allah than the passing away of this world.\"" This is the preserved version"," as a mawqūf narration. [Ḥasan]"""
"15876","(15870) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān narrated to us; Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Aswad narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated to us; Shuʿbah, Sufyān, and Misʿar narrated from Yaʿlā ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The passing away of this world is more insignificant to Allah than the killing of a Muslim.\"" It was also narrated by Ibn Abī ʿAdī from Shuʿbah as marfūʿ"," and it was narrated by Ghundar and others from Shuʿbah as mawqūf. The mawqūf version is more authentic. [Munkar]"""
"15877","(15871) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictamation; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Ibn ʿAwn narrated from Muḥammad, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The angels curse any one of you who points with an iron instrument"," even if it be his brother—his father's and mother's son.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Yazīd ibn Hārūn. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15878","(15872) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let none of you point toward his brother with a weapon"," for he does not know—perhaps Satan may cause it to slip from his hand"," and he may fall into a pit of the Fire.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ—both from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15879","(15873) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Burayd ibn Abī Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \When any one of you passes through our mosque or our market carrying arrows"," let him hold onto their heads"," so that he does not harm any Muslim with injury.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ"," and Muslim narrated it from him and from others"," from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15880","(15874) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Sulaymān and ʿĀrim both narrated; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that a man passed through the mosque carrying arrows whose heads were exposed, and he was instructed to grasp their heads so that they would not wound a Muslim. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Nuʿmān ʿĀrim, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Abū al-Rabīʿ, from Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15881","(15875) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿAlī narrated to us — Sufyān said: I said to ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, \O Abū Muḥammad"," did you hear Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh saying: A man passed through the mosque carrying arrows"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Cover their heads [i.e."," their tips].' He said: 'Yes.'\"""""
"15882","(15876) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us — they said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Wahayb narrated to us — Ayyūb narrated from Abū Qilābah, from Thābit ibn al-Ḥaḥḥāk, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam"," lying"," then he is as he has said; and whoever kills himself with something"," he will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief"," it is as if he has killed him; and cursing a believer is akin to killing him.\"""""
"15883","(15877) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣāghānī narrated to us — Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — al-Aʿmash narrated from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever kills himself with a blade"," his blade will be in his hand"," with which he will stab his own belly in the Fire of Jahannam"," abiding therein forever; and whoever kills himself with poison"," his poison will be in his hand"," from which he will sip in the Fire of Jahannam"," abiding therein forever; and whoever throws himself from a mountain"," he will be throwing himself in Jahannam"," abiding therein forever.\"""""
"15884","(15878) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Salmah narrated to us — Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Jarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, mentioning it with its chain and its meaning, and adding: \…and whoever throws himself from a mountain and kills himself…\"""""
"15885","(15879) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb informed us — Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us — Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated from al-Ḥasan, who said: Jundab ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us in this mosque, and we have not forgotten it since it was narrated to us, nor is it conceivable that he would have lied upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There was a man among those before you who developed a boil"," and he became distressed because of it. So he took a knife and cut his hand with it"," and the blood did not stop until he died. Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," said: 'My servant has hastened to Me with his own life; I have forbidden Paradise for him.'\"""""
"15886","(15880) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — they said: Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿĪsā ibn Mātī in al-Kūfah informed us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah al-Ghifārī narrated to us — ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us — (ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us — ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from ʿAlī ibn Ṣāliḥ, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Qurayẓah and al-Naḍīr [tribes] existed, and al-Naḍīr was more noble than Qurayẓah. So if a man from Qurayẓah killed a man from al-Naḍīr, he would be killed in retaliation; but if a man from al-Naḍīr killed a man from Qurayẓah, one hundred wasqs of dates would be paid. When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, a man from al-Naḍīr killed a man from Qurayẓah, so they said: \Hand him over to us so we may kill him.\"" They [al-Naḍīr] said: \""Between us and you is the Prophet ﷺ.\"" So they came to him"," and [the verse] was revealed: \""And if you judge"," judge between them with justice\"" (al-Māʾidah 42) — justice meaning life for life. Then [the verse] was revealed: \""Do they seek the judgment of the Days of Ignorance?\"" (al-Māʾidah 50)."""
"15887","(15881) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn al-Faḍl al-ʿAsqalānī narrated to us — Ādam narrated to us — Abū Jaʿfar narrated from al-Rabīʿ ibn Unas, from Abū al-ʿĀliyah, concerning [the verse] \So whoever transgresses against you\"" and kills after taking the blood-money"," \""for him is a painful punishment. That is a lightening from your Lord and a mercy\"" — he says: When you have given the blood-money and it was not permissible for the People of the Torah"," it was only retaliation or pardon. And the People of the Gospel — it was only pardon"," nothing else. So for this nation"," retaliation"," blood-money"," and pardon were made permissible. \""And in retaliation there is life for you\"" — meaning"," Allah the Almighty and Majestic has made retaliation a life for you: a man who wishes to kill is prevented from it out of fear of being killed."""
"15888","(15882) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī and Abū Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us — they said: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us — Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf narrated from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān concerning [the verse] \And in retaliation there is life for you\"" — he says: In retaliation there is life for you"," in that some of you are restrained from the bloodshed of others"," lest blood be shed out of fear of being killed. \""That you may fear Allah\"" — meaning"," [that you may fear] the shedding of blood"," when one of you fears being killed for it."""
"15889","(15883) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us — Ḥumayd narrated from Anas: That al-Rubayyiʿ bint al-Naḍr broke the front tooth of a girl. They offered them blood-money, but they refused. They offered them pardon, but they refused. So they came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered retaliation. Then her brother, Anas ibn al-Naḍr, came and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," shall the front tooth of al-Rubayyiʿ be broken? By the One Who has sent you with the truth"," her front tooth shall not be broken!\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""O Anas"," the Book of Allah is retaliation.\"" He said: The people agreed and forgave. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Verily"," among the servants of Allah are those who"," if they were to swear upon Allah"," He would fulfill their oath.\"""""
"15890","(15884) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us — Saʿīd, who is ibn Sulaymān, narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Kathīr narrated to us — ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever is killed unintentionally — or by mistake — such as by a stone or a whip"," then upon him is the ʿaql [blood-money] of an error. And whoever is killed deliberately"," then retaliation is by his hand. And whoever comes between him and [retaliation]"," then upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind. No expiation [ṣarf] nor atonement [ʿadl] shall be accepted from him.\"""""
"15891","(15885) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Zakariyya — Yahya ibn Muhammad al-'Anbari — narrated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi — narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Musa — narrated to us: Yahya ibn Hamzah — from Sulayman ibn Dawud — from al-Zuhri — from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm — from his father — from his grandfather — from the Prophet ﷺ, that he wrote a letter to the people of Yemen, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: And in the letter it was written: \Whoever kills a believer deliberately upon clear evidence"," then he is to be retaliated against"," except if the heirs of the slain forgive.\"" It was also narrated by 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from the Prophet ﷺ as a mursal hadith. [Sahih]"""
"15892","(15886) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-'Abbas — he is al-Aṣamm — narrated to us: Harun ibn Sulayman — narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi — from Sufyan — from Khusaif — from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: \He shall kill two in exchange for one.\"" [Hasan]"""
"15893","And Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — he is al-Aṣamm — narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah — narrated to us: Sufyan — from Khusaif — from Sa'id ibn Jubayr — regarding the statement of Allah, {We have made for his heir an authority} [al-Isra' 33], he said: \A way against him.\"" {So do not exceed the limit in killing} [al-Isra' 33]"," he said: \""He shall not kill two in exchange for one.\"" Al-Shafi'i said"," and it was also said regarding His statement {So do not exceed the limit in killing}: \""He shall not kill anyone other than his killer","\"" and this resembles what was said. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""
"15894","(15888) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Harun ibn Sulayman — narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi — from Sufyan — from Mansur — from Talq ibn Habib, regarding {So do not exceed the limit in killing} [al-Isra' 33], he said: \He shall not kill anyone other than his killer"," nor shall he mutilate him.\"" [Sahih]"""
"15895","(15889) And Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan — and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr all said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr — narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb — informed me: Yazid ibn Iyyad and Hisham ibn Sa'd — from Zayd ibn Aslam, that the people in the pre-Islamic era (Jahiliyyah): if a man from a tribe was killed, they would not be satisfied until they killed a noble man in retaliation. If their killer was not noble, they would not kill their killer but would kill someone else instead. They were admonished regarding that by the statement of Allah, the Blessed and Exalted: {And do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden, except by right. And whoever is killed unjustly — We have made for his heir an authority, so do not exceed the limit in killing; indeed, he will be supported} [al-Isra' 33]. And Zayd ibn Aslam said: \Al-saraf (excess) means killing someone other than the killer.\"" Al-Shafi'i said: Allah"," the Blessed and Exalted"," said: {Prescribed for you is legal retribution for those killed} [al-Baqarah 178]. [Sahih]"""
"15896","(15890) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Dawud — narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad — narrated to us: Shayban — from Qatadah, regarding His statement: {O you who have believed, prescribed for you is legal retribution for those killed — the free for the free, the slave for the slave, and the female for the female} [al-Baqarah 178]. He said: \The people of the pre-Islamic era used to practice transgression and obedience to Satan. So it was that among them"," if they were numerous and well-equipped"," and a slave of theirs was killed by a slave of another people"," they would say: 'We will not kill for him except a free man","' seeking superiority and preference over others. And if a woman of theirs was killed by a woman"," they would say: 'We will not kill for her except a man.' So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed this verse"," informing them that the slave for the slave"," the free for the free"," and the female for the female"," and He forbade them from transgression. Then He revealed Surah al-Ma'idah and said: {And We prescribed for them in it that the life for the life"," the eye for the eye"," the nose for the nose"," the ear for the ear"," the tooth for the tooth"," and wounds — legal retribution} [al-Ma'idah 45].\"" [Hasan]"""
"15897","(15891) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-Hasan — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus — and Abu Muhammad — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Ka'bi — both said: Isma'il ibn Qutaybah — narrated to us: Yazid ibn Salih — narrated to us: Bukayr ibn Ma'ruf — from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, regarding His statement: {Prescribed for you is legal retribution for those killed} [al-Baqarah 178] — the verse. He said: \The origin of this was between two tribes of the Arabs who fought before Islam"," then they entered Islam"," yet among them there remained wounds and killings"," and they sought retribution in Islam. One of the two tribes had a superiority over the other"," so they swore by Allah that they would kill a male in retaliation for a female of theirs"," and a free man in retaliation for a slave of theirs. When this verse was revealed"," they were pleased and submitted.\"" [Hasan]"""
"15898","(15892) And Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — narrated to us: al-Shafi'i — informed us: Mu'adh ibn Musa — from Bukayr ibn Ma'ruf — from Muqatil ibn Hayyan. Muqatil said: \I derived this tafsir from a group whom Mu'adh preserved among them: Mujahid"," al-Dahhak"," and al-Hasan.\"" He mentioned its meaning"," except that he did not mention his statement: \""Among them there remained wounds and killings.\"" Al-Shafi'i said: \""What they said most closely resembles what they said"," because Allah"," the Exalted"," has only bound every sinner to his own sin and has not made the crime of one person fall upon another.\"" Then he continued his discourse until he said: \""And it has been reported from the Prophet ﷺ: 'The most hostile person to Allah is he who kills someone other than his killer.'\"" [Hasan]"""
"15899","(15893) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' — informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq — narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr — narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zurai' — narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq — narrated to us: al-Zuhri — from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi — from Abu Shuraykh al-Khuza'i, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The most hostile person to Allah is he who kills someone other than his killer"," or seeks blood vengeance in Islam for a blood debt from the pre-Islamic era"," or gouges out his eyes for that which they did not see.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15900","(15894) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq — informed us: Musa ibn al-Hasan — narrated to us: al-Qa'nabi — narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal — from Ja'far ibn Muhammad — from his father — from 'Ali ibn Husayn, who said: there was found —\n\n(And Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — informed us: al-Shafi'i — informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad — from Ja'far ibn Muhammad — from his father — from his grandfather, who said:) — there was found in the scabbard of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a writing: \The most hostile person to Allah…\"" And in the hadith of Sulayman: \""The most hostile person to Allah is the one who kills someone other than his killer"," the one who strikes someone other than his striker"," and whoever takes as a patron other than his rightful patrons has disbelieved in what Allah revealed upon Muhammad ﷺ.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15901","(15895) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who said: I said to Abū Jaʿfar, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī: \What was in the scroll that was in the sheath of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""In it was: 'May Allah curse the one who kills other than his killer"," and the one who strikes other than his striker"," and whoever turns away from the master of his blessing"," he has indeed disbelieved in what Allah revealed to Muḥammad (ﷺ).'\"" [Weak]"""
"15902","(15896) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sinān narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us: Ibn Mawhab narrated to us, saying: I heard Mālik from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \There were found in the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) two inscriptions: 'Indeed"," the most insolent of people is a man who strikes other than his striker"," and a man who kills other than his killer"," and a man who turns away from the people of his blessing; whoever does that has indeed disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger. Allah shall accept from him neither obligatory nor supererogatory acts.'\"" And he mentioned the hadith. He is Mālik ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Rijāl"," narrating from his father. [Weak]"""
"15903","(15897) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan — and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd ibn Abjar from Iyāḍ ibn Laqīṭ from Abū Rimthah, who said: \I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and my father saw what was on the back of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," so he said: 'Let me treat what is on your back"," for I am a physician.' He said: 'You are a companion (rafīq).' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Who is this with you?' He said: 'My son — I bear witness by him.' He said: 'Indeed"," he shall not wrong you"," nor shall you wrong him.'\"" [Authentic]"""
"15904","(15898) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Iyād narrated from his father from Abū Rimthah, who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with my father"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) met us on his path. My father said to me: 'O my son"," do you know who this one approaching is?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'This is the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' He said: 'So my hair stood on end when he said that"," because I thought he would not resemble people. But he was a human being"," with abundant hair upon him"," a trace of henna"," and upon him two green garments.' My father greeted him"," and he returned the greeting. Then he said: 'Is this your son?' He said: 'Yes"," by the Lord of the Kaʿbah.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) smiled at the firmness of my resemblance to my father and at my father's swearing an oath upon me. Then he said: 'Indeed"," he shall not wrong you"," nor shall you wrong him.' Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited: {And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another}.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15905","(15899) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Abū Aḥmad — Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās — narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Danūqā narrated to us: Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Shabīb ibn Gharaqadah from Sulaymān ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Aḥwaṣ from his father, who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'Which day is the most sacred?' They said: 'This day of ours"," or the Day of the Greater Pilgrimage.' He said: 'Indeed"," your blood"," your wealth"," and your honors are sacred"," like the sanctity of your day and your city. Beware! No wrongdoer shall commit wrong except against himself. A father shall not wrong his child"," nor shall a child wrong his father.'\"" [Authentic through other chains]"""
"15906","(15900) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ, who said: \I heard al-Aswad ibn Hilāl narrate from a man from Banū Thaʿlabah ibn Yarbūʿ: that some of them came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and Banū Thaʿlabah ibn Yarbūʿ had killed a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," these Banū Thaʿlabah ibn Yarbūʿ have killed so-and-so.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'No soul shall wrong another.'\"" Thus said Shuʿbah: \""from a man from Banū Thaʿlabah","\"" and al-Thawrī said: \""from Thaʿlabah ibn Zahdam.\"" [Authentic through other chains]"""
"15907","(15901) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn al-Mathannā narrated to me: My father — al-Mathannā ibn Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh ibn Naṣr ibn Ḥassān ibn al-Ḥurr ibn Mālik ibn al-Khashkhāsh al-ʿAnbarī — informed me: My father informed me: al-Ḥurr ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated to me: Naṣr ibn Ḥassān narrated from Ḥuṣayn ibn Abī al-Ḥurr that his father Mālik and his two paternal uncles Qays and ʿUbayd, the sons of al-Khashkhāsh, came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and complained to him about a raid by horsemen from their paternal uncle's clan against the people. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wrote for them: 'This is a document from Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah, for Mālik, Qays, and ʿUbayd, the sons of al-Khashkhāsh: You are secure and Muslim; your blood and your wealth are protected. You shall not be taken to account for the crime of others, and no wrong shall befall you except by your own hands.'\ [Weak]"""
"15908","(15902) Abū ʿAmr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb — informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd and Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān narrated from Shuʿayb from Ibn Abī Ḥusayn from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: 'The most hated of people to Allah is one who commits sacrilege in the Sacred Sanctuary, one who seeks to revive the practices of the Jāhiliyyah within Islam, and one who demands the blood of a person without right, in order to shed his blood.' al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Authentic. al-Bukhārī]"
"15909","(15903) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, said: {O you who believe, prescribed for you is legal retribution for those murdered} — the entire verse. Then He said: {And We ordained for them therein: a life for a life} — the entire verse. Ibn Shihāb said: \When this verse was revealed"," a woman was held accountable for a man"," and in cases of deliberate wounding.\"" He said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me: Mālik informed me that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab said: \""A man may be killed for a woman if he kills her"," for Allah the Mighty and Sublime said: {And We ordained for them therein: a life for a life}.\"" [Authentic]"""
"15910","(15904) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak — informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Khalīfah al-Khayyāṭ narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The blood of the believers is equivalent"," and they are as one hand against those other than them.\"" Likewise"," Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb. [Good]"""
"15911","(15905) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā al-Qanṭarī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated from Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he wrote a letter to the people of Yemen containing the obligatory acts, the Sunnah, and the blood-money compensations, and he sent it with ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm. Among its contents was: \Indeed"," a man may be killed in retribution for a woman.\"" [Ḥasan for other than its own chain]"""
"15912","(15906) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad and ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ both said: Saʿīd narrated to us from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, that a Jewish man killed a young girl by stoning her with stones, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed him with the same.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"15913","(15907) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Shaybān narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Muṭarrif, from al-Shaʿbī, from Abū Juḥayfah, who said: I asked ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) — and in the narration of Ibn Shaybān he said: I said to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) — \Do you have anything from the Prophet ﷺ other than the Qurʾān?\"" He said: \""No"," by the One who split the seed and created the soul"," except that Allah may grant a servant understanding of His Book"," and what is in the scroll.\"" I said: \""What is in the scroll?\"" He said: \""Blood-money (al-ʿaql)"," the freeing of captives"," and a Muslim shall not be killed for a disbeliever.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"15914","(15908) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū Yaʿlī narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Muṭarrif, who said: I heard al-Shaʿbī say: Abū Juḥayfah informed me, who said: I said to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) — and he mentioned it with the same meaning. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ṣadaqah ibn al-Faḍl, from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah."
"15915","(15909) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated from Muṭarrif, from ʿĀmir, from Abū Juḥayfah, who said: I said to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): \O Commander of the Faithful"," do you have anything from revelation?\"" He said: \""No"," by the One who split the seed and created the soul"," I know of nothing except the understanding that Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," grants to a man"," and what is in the scroll.\"" I said: \""What is the scroll?\"" He said: \""Blood-money (al-ʿaql)"," the freeing of captives"," and a believer shall not be killed for a polytheist.\""\n\nZuhayr said: I said to Muṭarrif: \""What is the freeing of captives (fakāku al-asīr)?\"" He said: \""That captives be ransomed from the enemy — this is established by the Sunnah.\"" And Muṭarrif said: \""Al-ʿaql refers to the blood-money that is binding (al-muʿaqqalah).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus"," from Zuhayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15916","(15910) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Qays ibn ʿUbād, who said: We came to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) — I and Jāriyah ibn Qudāmah al-Saʿdī — and we said: \Do you have any covenant from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He said: \""No"," except what is in the scabbard of my sword.\"" He then brought out a document for us and read it"," and in it was: \""The Muslims are equal in their blood; the responsibility of their protection is borne by the lowest among them"," and they are one hand against those besides them. Beware! A Muslim shall not be killed for a disbeliever"," nor shall one under a covenant be violated during his covenant. Beware! Whoever introduces an innovation or gives refuge to an innovator"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15917","(15911) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muslim ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Abī Ḥusayn, from ʿAṭāʾ and Ṭāwūs — I think he said — and Mujāhid and al-Ḥasan, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the Day of the Conquest: \A believer shall not be killed for a disbeliever.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is a general statement according to the people of military expeditions (ahl al-maghāzī)"," that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke it in his sermon on the Day of the Conquest"," and it is narrated as a musnad ḥadīth from the Prophet ﷺ through the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb and the ḥadīth of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn.\n\nThe Shaykh said: As for the ḥadīth of ʿAmr — [Weak. But it has many authentic supporting narrations.]"""
"15918","(15912) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us: Abū al-Azhar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us: my father — all of them — from Ibn Isḥāq: ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people on the year of the Conquest and said: \O people"," whatever alliance existed in the Age of Ignorance"," Islam has only added it in strength"," and there is no alliance in Islam. The Muslims are one hand against those besides them; the responsibility of their protection is borne by the lowest among them. The most distant among them shall return their spoils to those who remained behind. A believer shall not be killed for a disbeliever. The blood-money of a disbeliever is half the blood-money of a believer. There shall be no bringing (of livestock to the collector) and no driving (of livestock away from the collector)"," and their charitable alms shall not be taken except in their own dwellings.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Yūnus ibn Bukayr. [Ḥasan]"""
"15919","(15913) Abū ʿAlī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to me: Hushaym narrated to me, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Muslims are equal in their blood; the responsibility of their protection is borne by the lowest among them"," and the most distant among them may grant them protection. They are one hand against those besides them. The strong among them shall return what they have taken to the weak among them"," and the expeditions of their raiding parties shall be returned to those who remained behind. A believer shall not be killed for a disbeliever"," nor shall one under a covenant be violated during his covenant.\"""""
"15920","(15914) As for the ḥadīth of ʿImrān: Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yazīd ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated to me, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUbayd, from Khurayniq bint al-Ḥuṣayn, from her brother ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the Day of the Conquest: \Have you not seen what your companion Hilāl ibn Umayyah did? Had I killed a believer for a disbeliever"," I would have killed him — so pay his blood-money.\"" So we paid his blood-money"," and Banū Mudlij were with us"," so they brought brown sheep the likes of which I had never seen more beautiful in color. Banū Mudlij had been allies of Banū Kaʿb in the Age of Ignorance.\n\nAl-Wāqidī also narrated it from ʿUmar ibn ʿUthmān"," from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUbayd"," except that he said \""Khirāsh ibn Umayyah\"" instead of \""Hilāl ibn Umayyah","\"" and he did not mention the blood-money or what followed it. [Weak]"""
"15921","(15915) Abū Saʿīd — Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl al-Ṣayrafī — narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sinān — narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd — narrated to us: Ibn Mawhab — said: I heard Mālik, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said: Two documents were found in the scabbard of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He mentioned one of them, and in the other was written: \The believers are equal in their blood"," and the least among them may act on their behalf in securing their covenant. A Muslim shall not be killed for a disbeliever"," nor shall a person under covenant be killed while under his covenant. The people of two different religions shall not inherit from one another. A woman shall not be married simultaneously with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. There is no prayer after ʿAṣr until the sun sets. And a woman shall not travel for three nights except with a maḥram.\""\n\nIbn Mawhab is ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mawhab"," and Mālik is Ibn Abī al-Rijāl"," and Abū al-Rijāl is Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Anṣārī"," from whom his son Mālik narrated. [Weak]"""
"15922","(15916) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī — narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Sinān — narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd — narrated to us: Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ — from ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Abī al-Janūb — from al-Ḥasan — from Maʿqil ibn Yasār, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A believer shall not be killed for a disbeliever"," nor shall a person under covenant be killed while under his covenant. The Muslims are one hand against those other than them; their blood is equal.\"" [Authentic through other chains]"""
"15923","(15917) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh — narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Ruhāwī — narrated to us: My grandfather Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Ruhāwī — informed me that ʿAmmār ibn Maṭar narrated to them — narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Aslamī — from Rābiʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — from Ibn al-Baylamānī — from Ibn ʿUmar: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) killed a Muslim for a person under covenant and said: \I am the most honourable of those who fulfil his covenant.\""\n\nThis narration is erroneous in two respects: first"," its being connected with the mention of Ibn ʿUmar in it"," when in fact it is from Ibn al-Baylamānī from the Prophet (ﷺ) as a mursal narration; and second"," its narration from Ibrāhīm from Rābiʿah"," when in fact Ibrāhīm narrates it from Ibn al-Munkadir. The blame in this falls upon ʿAmmār ibn Maṭar al-Ruhāwī"," for he used to invert the chains of narration and steal hadiths"," and this became so frequent in his narrations that he fell below the standard of being used as evidence. [Denounced (Munkar)]"""
"15924","(15918) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān — narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam — narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā — from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī: that a man from among the Muslims killed a man from among the People of the Book, and the matter was raised to the Prophet (ﷺ), and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the most deserving of those who fulfil their covenant.\"" Then he ordered"," and the man was killed.\n\nThis is the fundamental narration on this subject"," but it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)"," and its narrator is not trustworthy. [Weak]"""
"15925","(15919) It has also been narrated from Rābiʿah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī, from the Prophet (ﷺ) as a mursal narration. Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah — narrated to us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruyah — narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah — narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad — informed me: Rābiʿah — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī: that a man from among the people of the covenant came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \We made a covenant with you and pledged allegiance to you upon such and such"," and one of our men has been killed.\"" He said: \""I am the most deserving of those who fulfil their covenant.\"" So he enabled him (the Muslim) to retaliate"," and his neck was struck. [Weak; Mursal]"""
"15926","(15920) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us: al-Ramādī — (ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī — narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm — both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us — from al-Thawrī — from Rābiʿah — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī, raising it (to the Prophet): that the Prophet (ﷺ) exacted retaliation upon a Muslim who killed a Jew. And al-Ramādī said: He exacted retaliation upon a Muslim for a person under covenant, and said: \I am the most deserving of those who fulfil my covenant.\"" It is said that Rābiʿah only took it from Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaḥyā"," and the hadith revolves around him. [Weak; Mursal]"""
"15927","(15921) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī — informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan — Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Kārizī — narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — said: Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Salām said: I heard Ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrate it from Ibn al-Munkadir, and I heard Abū Yūsuf narrate it from Rābiʿah al-Raʾy — both of them from Ibn al-Baylamānī. Then it reached me from Ibn Abī Yaḥyā that he said: \I am the one who narrated this hadith to Rābiʿah.\"" Thus"," the hadith revolves around Ibn Abī Yaḥyā"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī: that the Prophet (ﷺ) exacted retaliation upon a Muslim for a person under covenant"," and said: \""I am the most deserving of those who fulfil their covenant.\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: This is a hadith that is not musnad (fully connected)"," and one like it should not be taken as an authority by which the blood of Muslims is shed.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed me"," from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād"," who said: I said to Zufar: \""You have become a subject of ridicule and mockery among the people.\"" He said: \""What is that?\"" I said: \""You say regarding all matters: 'Avert the prescribed punishments in cases of doubt","' yet you have come to the greatest of doubts and have proceeded upon it.\"" He said: \""What is that?\"" I said: \""A Muslim is killed for a disbeliever.\"" He said: \""Then bear witness that I have retracted from that.\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: And this is also the position of the people of the Ḥijāz — they do not exact retaliation for it. As for his statement"," \""nor shall a person under covenant be killed while under his covenant\"" — the person under covenant is a man from the territory of war who enters among us under a guarantee of safety; his killing is forbidden upon the Muslims until he returns to his place of safety. The basis for this is in His statement (Exalted is He): \""And if any one of the polytheists seeks your protection"," then grant him protection so that he may hear the words of Allah. Then deliver him to his place of safety.\"" [At-Tawbah: 6] [Weak]"""
"15928","(15922) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us: Abū al-Faḍl — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us by dictation: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym — narrated to us: Abū Qudāmah — narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī — narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād, who said: I met Zufar and said to him: \You have become a hadith of ridicule among the people.\"" He said: \""What is that?\"" I said: \""You say regarding all things: 'Avert the prescribed punishments in cases of doubt","' yet you have come to the greatest of the prescribed punishments and have said it is to be carried out on the basis of doubt.\"" He said: \""What is that?\"" I said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'A believer shall not be killed for a disbeliever.' Yet you say he is killed for him.\"" He said: \""Then I bear witness before you at this moment that I have retracted from that.\"" [Authentic"," as a statement of ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād]"""
"15929","(15923) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād — informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar — narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān al-Fārisī — narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm — said: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: \The hadith of Ibn al-Baylamānī — that the Prophet (ﷺ) killed a Muslim for a person under covenant — this revolves only around Ibn Abī Yaḥyā. It has no basis as evidence; he merely took it from him.\"" [Authentic"," as a statement of Ibn al-Madīnī]"""
"15930","(15924) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Bukhārī — narrated to us: Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ — said: \The hadith of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī is munkar (denounced). And Rābiʿah narrated from him that the Prophet (ﷺ) killed a Muslim for a person under covenant"," and it is mursal and munkar.\"" [Authentic"," as a statement of Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad]"""
"15931","(15925) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Dāraquṭnī, the ḥāfiẓ, said: Ibn al-Baylamānī is weak (ḍaʿīf), and no proof (ḥujjah) can be established by him when he narrates a hadith with a connected chain—so how much more so when he narrates it with a broken chain (mursal)? And Allāh knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. From al-Dāraquṭnī]"
"15932","(15926) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim informed me that Qays ibn Saʿd narrated to him from Makhūl, that ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmiṭ (may Allāh be pleased with him) called a Nabataean to hold his mount for him near Bayt al-Maqdis, but the man refused. So ʿUbādah struck him and wounded his head. The matter was then brought before ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: \What led you to do what you did to this man?\"" He replied: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," I asked him to hold my mount"," but I am a man prone to anger"," so I became angry and struck him.\"" ʿUmar said: \""Sit down"," for retribution (qiṣāṣ) is due.\"" But Zayd ibn Thābit said: \""Will you exact retribution upon your brother for the sake of your slave?\"" So ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) abandoned qiṣāṣ and ruled that blood-money (diyah) be paid instead. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15933","(15927) Abū Saʿīd informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: Baḥr narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: al-Layth informed me that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to him that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) was brought a man from among his companions who had wounded a man from among the People of the Dhimmah. ʿUmar intended to exact retribution (qiṣāṣ) upon him, but the Muslims said: \This is not appropriate.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \""Then we shall increase the blood-money (ʿaql) upon him","\"" and he doubled it.\n\nSulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"," from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Ḥakīm"," that he heard ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz relating to the people that a man from among the People of the Dhimmah was killed deliberately in al-Shām"," and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) was in al-Shām at that time. When the news reached him"," ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \""You have transgressed against the People of the Dhimmah—I shall certainly kill [the murderer] in retaliation for him.\"" Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \""You do not have the authority to do that.\"" ʿUmar then prayed and afterward summoned Abū ʿUbaydah and said: \""Why did you claim that I should not kill him in retaliation?\"" Abū ʿUbaydah (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \""Tell me"," if a man had killed his own slave"," would you kill him in retaliation for that slave?\"" ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) fell silent and then ruled that one thousand dinars be paid as an increased penalty upon him. [Ḍaʿīf. Mursal from ʿUmar]"""
"15934","(15928) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū Ḥanīfah narrated to us from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, that a man from Banū Bakr ibn Wāʾil killed a man from the people of al-Ḥīrah. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) wrote concerning the matter that the killer be handed over to the heirs of the deceased; if they wished, they could execute him, and if they wished, they could pardon him. So the man was handed over to the guardian (walī) of the deceased—a man called Ḥunayn from the people of al-Ḥīrah—and he killed him. After that, ʿUmar wrote: \If the man has not yet been killed"," do not kill him.\"" They understood that ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) intended to reconcile them by offering blood-money (diyah).\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: \""What he reverted to is more deserving of being followed. Perhaps he intended to frighten him with execution but not actually to kill him.\"" He said: \""The one who spoke to him—it has been narrated to you from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār that ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) wrote concerning a Muslim who killed a Christian: 'If the killer is a habitual murderer"," then execute him; if he is not a habitual murderer"," then leave him and do not execute him.'\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""We have received this narration. Follow ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) as he said"," for you do not follow him in what he said.\"" He said: \""Has anything been established from ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) on this matter?\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""Not a single letter. And these hadiths are either munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)"," ḍaʿīf (weak)"," or combine both disconnection and weakness.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15935","(15929) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf said: Sufyān mentioned from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from a shaykh, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) wrote concerning a Muslim who killed a muʿāhid (a person under a covenant of protection): \If it was an outburst in anger"," then impose four thousand [dinars] upon him; and if he is a habitual criminal (liss ʿādī)"," then execute him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15936","(15930) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ al-Baghdādī narrated to us in Balkh, saying: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād narrated from ʿAmr, from al-Qāsim ibn Abī Bazza, that a Muslim man killed a man from among the People of the Dhimmah in al-Shām. The matter was raised to Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ (may Allāh be pleased with him), who wrote concerning it to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him). ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) wrote back: \If this is his habitual character"," then bring him forward and strike his neck; but if it was a sudden outburst that overcame him"," then impose his blood-money upon him—four thousand [dinars].\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15937","(15931) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī narrated to us, saying: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him), that a Muslim man deliberately killed a man from among the People of the Dhimmah. The matter was raised to ʿUthmān (may Allāh be pleased with him), but he did not execute him; rather, he increased the blood-money upon him to the same amount as the blood-money of a Muslim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq in his Muṣannaf]"
"15938","(15932) Abū Bakr al-Faqīh informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar informed us, saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, saying: Zaḥmawayh narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us, saying: Ibn Shihāb said: \ʿUthmān (may Allāh be pleased with him) and Muʿāwiyah would not execute a polytheist in retaliation for a Muslim.\"" The first narration is connected (mawṣūl)"," while this one is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15939","(15933) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Yazīd informed us, saying: Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn narrated from al-Zuhrī that Ibn Shās al-Judhāmī killed a man from the Nabataeans of al-Shām. The matter was raised to ʿUthmān (may Allāh be pleased with him), who ordered his execution. But al-Zubayr (may Allāh be pleased with him) and a number of the Companions of the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke to him and dissuaded him from killing him. So ʿUthmān set the blood-money at one thousand dinars.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \I said: This is from the hadith of one whose status is unknown. If it is not firmly established"," then abandon using it as evidence. And if it is firmly established"," then you claimed that he intended to kill him"," but a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) prevented him"," and he yielded to them. Thus ʿUthmān (may Allāh be pleased with him) and a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) were unanimously agreed that a Muslim should not be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever—so how can you oppose them?\"""""
"15940","(15934) In this there is also an indication of the weakness of what Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, saying: al-Rabīʿ informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Asadī informed us, saying: Abān ibn Taghlib narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn Maymūn, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, the mawlā of Banī Hāshim, from Abī al-Janūb al-Asadī, who said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allāh be pleased with him) was brought a Muslim man who had killed a man from among the People of the Dhimmah. The evidence was established against him, so ʿAlī ordered his execution. Then the brother of the killer came and said: \I have pardoned him.\"" ʿAlī said: \""Perhaps they intimidated you"," frightened you"," and coerced you.\"" He said: \""No. But killing him will not bring my brother back to me"," and they compensated me [with blood-money]"," so I was satisfied.\"" ʿAlī said: \""You know best. Whoever is under our covenant of protection—his blood is as our blood"," and his blood-money is as our blood-money.\"" Al-Ḥasan said it thus"," while others said: Ḥusayn ibn Maymūn. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15941","(15935) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Aṣbahānī informed us, he said: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī, the ḥāfiẓ, said: Abū al-Janūb is weak (ḍaʿīf) in ḥadīth. Al-Shāfiʿī said in his earlier works: \How is it possible regarding the ḥadīth of Abū Juḥayfah from ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) that ʿAlī narrates nothing from the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) yet acts contrary to it?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — as per al-Dāraquṭnī]"""
"15942","(15936) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar, the ḥāfiẓ, informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from Ḥajjāj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that Abū Bakr and ʿUmar (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) would not execute a free man for killing a slave. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15943","(15937) ʿAlī said, and Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Ṭabarī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from ʿUmar ibn ʿĀmir and al-Ḥajjāj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, a similar narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15944","(15938) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar, the ḥāfiẓ, informed us; Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Abū al-Sāʾib Salm ibn Junādah narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from Isrāʾīl, from Jābir, from ʿĀmir, who said: ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) said: \It is from the Sunnah that a free man shall not be killed for a slave.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15945","(15939) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar informed us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; al-Sarī ibn Sahl narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rushayd narrated to us; ʿUthmān al-Burrī narrated from Juwaybir, from al-Ḥaḥḥāk, from Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \A free man shall not be killed for a slave.\"" There is weakness (ḍaʿf) in this isnād. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15946","(15940) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from al-Ḥakam, from ʿAlī and ʿAbd Allāh (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) regarding a free man who kills a slave, they both said: \Blood-money (diyah) is due.\"" This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15947","(15941) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed me; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar, the ḥāfiẓ, informed us; Ibn al-Junayd narrated to us; Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn Mālik narrated to us; Layth narrated from al-Ḥakam, who said: ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā) said: \If a free man kills a slave deliberately"," then he is subject to retribution (qawād).\"" ʿAlī said: \""No proof is established with it"," for it is mursal.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15948","(15942) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, who said: \A free man shall not be subjected to retribution for killing a slave.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — as per al-Ḥasan]"""
"15949","(15943) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me; Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to me from Ibn Abī Jaʿfar, from Bukayr, that: \The Sunnah has been established that a free Muslim shall not be killed for a slave"," even if he kills him deliberately"," and blood-money (ʿaql) is upon him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15950","(15944) He said, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me; Ibn Abī Dhʾib and Mālik ibn Anas narrated to me from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \There is no retribution (qawad) between a free man and a slave in anything"," except that if a slave kills a free man deliberately"," he shall be killed for it.\"" Mālik said to me the same. And we have received from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ a similar narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as per al-Zuhrī]"""
"15951","(15945) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Hisham from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever kills his slave"," we shall kill him; whoever mutilates his slave"," we shall mutilate him; and whoever castrates his slave"," we shall castrate him.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15952","(15946) And Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Hafs al-Muqri' in Baghdad informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman al-Najjad narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari and Sa'id ibn Amir both said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever kills his slave"," we shall kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave"," we shall mutilate him.\"" Qatadah said: Then al-Hasan forgot this hadith and said: \""A free person shall not be killed for a slave.\"" The Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is possible that al-Hasan did not forget the hadith but rather abandoned it due to its weakness. And most of the scholars of hadith abandoned the narration of al-Hasan from Samurah"," and some of them held that he heard nothing from Samurah except the hadith of the 'Aqiqah. [Da'if]"""
"15953","(15947) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — I heard al-Abbas ibn Muhammad saying: I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in saying: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated from Shu'bah, who said: Al-Hasan did not hear from Samurah. He said: And I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in saying: Al-Hasan did not hear anything from Samurah; it is a book. Yahya said regarding the hadith of al-Hasan from Samurah — \Whoever kills his slave"," we shall kill him\"" — this is in the hearing of the Baghdadis"," and al-Hasan did not hear from Samurah. As for Ali ibn al-Madinī"," he affirmed that al-Hasan heard from Samurah. And Allah knows best."""
"15954","(15948) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih narrated to us: Uthman ibn Said al-Darimi and Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyib al-Sha'rani both said: Abu Salih al-Misri Abd Allah ibn Salih, the scribe of al-Layth, narrated to me: Al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me: Umar ibn Isa al-Qurashi, then al-Asadi: Ibn Jurayj: Ata' ibn Abi Rabah: Ibn Abbas, who said: A slave-girl came to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: \My master accused me and sat me upon the fire until my private parts burned.\"" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to her: \""Did he do that to you?\"" She said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Did you confess anything to him?\"" She said: \""No.\"" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Bring him to me.\"" When Umar saw the man"," he said: \""Do you torment with the torment of Allah?\"" The man said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," I accused her of adultery.\"" He said: \""Did you see that?\"" The man said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Did she confess it to you?\"" He said: \""No.\"" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'A slave shall not be retaliated against on behalf of his master"," nor a child on behalf of his father' — I would have retaliated against you for her.\"" Then he brought him out and struck him with a hundred lashes and said to the slave-girl: \""Go"," you are free for the sake of Allah"," and you are the mawla of Allah and His Messenger.\"" Abu Salih said"," and al-Layth said: \""And this ruling is acted upon.\"" [Da'if]"""
"15955","(15949) And Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us: Abu Ahmad ibn Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abdan and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Ramli both said: Abd al-Malik ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me: My father narrated to me: Al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me: Umar ibn Isa narrated to me, mentioning something similar to it. Abu Ahmad said: \And this hadith — I do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ibn Jurayj with this isnad other than Umar ibn Isa"," and from Umar other than al-Layth — and it is well-known with this chain. I heard ibn Hammad mentioning from al-Bukhari that it is munkar (objectionable).\"""""
"15956","(15950) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us from Yahya ibn Ayyub from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabah from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: Zinba' had a slave called Sandar or Ibn Sandar. He was found kissing one of his slave-girls, so he seized him, gelded him, and cut off his ears and his nose. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he sent for Zinba' and said: \Do not burden them with what they cannot bear; feed them from what you eat; clothe them from what you wear; and if you dislike them"," sell them; and if you are pleased with them"," keep them. And do not torment the creation of Allah.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Whoever is mutilated or burned with fire"," he is free"," and he is the mawla of Allah and His Messenger.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emancipated him. He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," bequeath something for me.\"" He said: \""I bequeath you to every Muslim.\"" Al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabah is da'if and is not used as evidence. And it has been narrated from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Amr in an abbreviated form"," and he is not used as evidence. And it has been narrated from Sawwar Abu Hamzah from Amr"," and he is not strong. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""
"15957","(15951) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Sabuni al-Antaki, the judge of the frontiers, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hakam al-Ramli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated from al-Awza'i from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather: A man deliberately killed his slave, so the Prophet ﷺ flogged him with a hundred lashes, banished him for a year, erased his share from the Muslims, and did not retaliate against him for the slave. And he ordered him to emancipate a slave. [Da'if]"
"15958","(15952) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Hunayn narrated to me from his father from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man who had deliberately killed his slave was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged him with a hundred lashes, banished him for a year, and erased his share from the Muslims, and did not retaliate against him for the slave. [Da'if]"
"15959","(15953) He said: And Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Abi Farwah from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to it."
"15960","(15954) And Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us: Hafs from Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shu'ayh that Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: \A believer shall not be killed for his slave; rather he shall be flogged"," his imprisonment shall be prolonged"," and his share shall be cut off.\"" The chains of these ahadith are da'if; none of them constitutes a valid proof. However"," most of the scholars hold the view that a man shall not be killed for his slave"," as we have narrated it from Sulayman ibn Yasar"," al-Sha'bi"," al-Zuhri"," and others. [Da'if]"""
"15961","(15955) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to me from Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah that Sulaymān al-Muzanī narrated to him: that he sought a legal opinion from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding a man who beat his slave severely, and the slave died, though he had not intended to kill him. Ibn ʿAbbās said to him: \Let him emancipate a slave"," or let him fast two consecutive months.\"" [Weak]"""
"15962","(15956) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muqrīʾ narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn al-ʿAbbās, meaning al-Ṭabarī, narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from al-Ḥajjāj from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding a free man who kills a slave: \The diyah (blood money) for it is his (the slave's) price.\"" [Weak]"""
"15963","(15957) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Nūḥ ibn Darrāj narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding a slave who is killed: \His diyah is his price"," whatever it may amount to.\"" [Weak]"""
"15964","(15958) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan and Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab regarding a slave who is killed by mistake, they both said: \His diyah is his price"," whatever it may amount to.\"" And we also narrated it from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad and Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh. [Authentic]"""
"15965","(15959) And that was narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm from ʿAlī, ʿAbdullāh, and Sharīḥ, who said: \His price (is taken)"," even if it exceeds the diyah of a free man.\"" Abū ʿAbdullāh informed me by way of ijāzah"," Abū al-Walīd narrated to us"," al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us"," Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us"," Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAbd al-Karīm"," and he mentioned it. And in it there is a disconnection (irsāl) between him and ʿAbd al-Karīm. [Weak]"""
"15966","(15960) Abū ʿAbdullāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd narrated to me from Yazīd al-Raqāshī, who narrated to me that Anas ibn Mālik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \That I sit with a people who remember Allah after the morning prayer (Ṣalāt al-Fajr) until the sun rises is dearer to me than that upon which the sun has risen"," and that I sit with a people who remember Allah after the afternoon prayer (al-ʿAṣr) until the sun sets is dearer to me than emancipating eight slaves from the children of Ismāʿīl"," the diyah of each of them being twelve thousand.\"" [Good]"""
"15967","(15961) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr narrated to us, Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When a slave kills a free man"," he is handed over to the heirs of the slain. If they wish"," they may execute him"," and if they wish"," they may spare his life.\"" The Sheikh said: \""If they wish to spare him and demand the diyah"," he is sold to pay the diyah of the slain. And Allah knows best.\"" [Weak]"""
"15968","(15962) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar that in a letter of ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, it was stated that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \A slave is executed in retaliation for (killing) a slave in every case of deliberate killing that reaches his life and what is below that.\"" [Weak]"""
"15969","(15963) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated among others, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb that a man from Banī Mudlij, whose name was Qatādah, threw a sword at his son and struck his leg. He bled from his wound and died. Surāqah ibn Juʿshum came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him. ʿUmar said: \Prepare for me one hundred and twenty camels at Qudayd until I come to you.\"" When ʿUmar arrived"," he took from those camels thirty hiqqahs"," thirty jadhaʿahs"," and forty khalifahs"," then he said: \""Where is the brother of the slain?\"" He said: \""Here I am.\"" He said: \""Take them"," for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'The killer gets nothing.'\"" Abū ʿAbdullāh added in his narration that al-Shāfiʿī said: \""I have preserved from a number of the people of knowledge whom I met that a father is not executed for (killing) his son"," and that is my opinion.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: This hadith is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ)"," and al-Shāfiʿī corroborated it by stating that a number of the people of knowledge hold this view"," and it has also been narrated in a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Weak]"""
"15970","(15964) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh informed us from his original copy, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn Wārah narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Sābiq narrated to me, ʿAmr, meaning Ibn Abī Qays, narrated from Manṣūr, meaning Ibn al-Muʿtamir, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: \I gave a slave girl as a gift to a man from Banī Mudlij"," and she bore him a son. He used to employ her (in service). When the boy grew up"," he called her one day and said: 'Do such and such.' She said: 'You will not have me — when will you stop employing my mother?' He became angry and threw his sword at him"," striking his leg. The boy bled and died. He set out with a group of his people to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: 'O enemy of yourself! You are the one who killed your son! Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""A father is not executed for (killing) his son","\"" I would have killed you. Bring his diyah.' He brought one hundred and twenty or one hundred and thirty camels. He selected one hundred from them and gave them to his heirs"," and left his father (with nothing).\""\n\nAnd Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: \""I was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when he ruled that a son is executed in retaliation for his father"," but a father is not executed in retaliation for his son.\"" [Weak]"""
"15971","(15965) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Zuhrī, the judge of Makkah, narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muslim narrated to us: Muṭarrif ibn Ṭarīf narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah from a man called ʿArfajah from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \There is no qiṣāṣ (retaliatory punishment) upon a father for (killing) his child.\"" [Weak]"""
"15972","(15966) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated to us. Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim informed us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The prescribed punishments (ḥudūd) are not to be carried out in the mosques"," and a father is not to be executed for (killing) his child.\""\n\nIsmāʿīl ibn Muslim al-Makkī — there is weakness in him. [Hasan due to other reports. It has many supporting narrations; see al-Arwāʾ 2214]"""
"15973","(15967) It has also been narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnbarī from ʿAmr — and Allah knows best. Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us orally: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Shabīb al-Maʿmarī narrated to us: ʿUqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: Abū Ḥafṣ al-Tammār narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnbarī narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The prescribed punishments (ḥudūd) are not to be carried out in the mosques"," and a father is not to be killed for (killing) his child.\""\n\nAbū Ḥafṣ al-Tammār is Abū Tamām ʿUmar ibn ʿĀmir al-Saʿdī"," who lived among Banī Rifāʿah. It was also narrated by Saʿīd ibn Bashīr from Qatādah from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," with a connected chain. [Hasan due to other reports. It has many supporting narrations; see al-Arwāʾ 2214]"""
"15974","(15968) As for the ḥadīth of the sister of al-Rubayyiʿ, Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated to us: Thābit narrated from Anas, and he mentioned it. This will be presented in its complete form in its proper place, if Allah wills. Ḥumayd contradicted him from Anas, saying: \Al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwadh struck a slave girl and broke her front tooth.\"" Thābit is more precise (aḥfaẓ)"," and it is possible that they are two separate incidents"," and this is the more apparent view. It has also been narrated in this regard from Ibn ʿAbbās and Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with them both). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (by al-Bukhārī and Muslim)]"""
"15975","(15969) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His statement (Exalted is He): \A free person for a free person"," a slave for a slave"," and a female for a female\"" [al-Baqarah 178]. He said: \""They used not to kill a man for a woman"," but they would kill a man for a man and a woman for a woman. So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: 'A soul for a soul' [al-Māʾidah 45.\"" He said: \""Thus He made the free persons equal in qiṣāṣ among them in cases of deliberate killing — their men and their women — in matters of the soul and what is less than the soul. And He made the slaves equal among them in cases of deliberate killing — their men and their women — in matters of the soul and what is less than the soul.\"" [Weak]"""
"15976","(15970) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibn Lahīʿah informed me from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj: \The established practice (sunnah)"," according to what reached him"," was that if both were free — meaning the man and the woman — then if he gouged out her eye"," his eye would be gouged out.\"" He said: \""And it has reached me from Zayd ibn Thābit the same"," that he (the man) would be killed for her and qiṣāṣ would be taken from him.\"" [Weak]"""
"15977","(15971) As for the narration from the Tābiʿīn in this regard, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffāʾ al-Baghdādī informed us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Maynāʾ both said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, who said: \Among the jurists (fuqahāʾ) whom I encountered — whose word was considered authoritative — were Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"," al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad"," Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit"," ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah"," and Sulaymān ibn Yasār"," along with other eminent scholars of their calibre"," people of jurisprudence and virtue. They would sometimes differ on a matter"," and we would adopt the view of the majority among them or the one with the strongest opinion. What I have preserved from them regarding this issue is that they used to say: 'Qiṣāṣ is taken from a man for (injuring) a woman — an eye for an eye"," an ear for an ear"," and all wounds are subject to this. And if he kills her"," he is killed for her.'\"" We have also narrated it from al-Zuhrī and others.\n\nSufyān al-Thawrī narrated from al-Mughīrah from Ibrāhīm"," who said: \""Qiṣāṣ applies between a man and a woman in cases of deliberate killing.\"" And from Jābir from al-Shaʿbī is something similar. [Weak]"""
"15978","(15972) From Jaʿfar ibn Burqān from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz is something similar. Abū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us: Sufyān al-Jawharī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān narrated it.\n\nAnd we have narrated from al-Shaʿbī and Ibrāhīm a contrary view regarding matters less than the soul."
"15979","(15973) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) killed five or seven men for one man whom they had killed by treachery (ghīlah). He said: \Had the people of Ṣanʿāʾ all conspired together against him"," I would have killed them all.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15980","(15974) Al-Bukhārī said in the heading of the chapter: Ibn Bashshār told me: Yaḥyā narrated from ʿUbaydullāh from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that a young boy was killed by treachery (ghīlah), and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Had the people of Ṣanʿāʾ all participated in it"," I would have killed them.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us from Abī ʿUbayd: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to me"," and he mentioned it"," except that he said: \""A young boy was killed in Ṣanʿāʾ by treachery (ghīlah)"," so ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) killed seven men for him and said: 'Had the people of Ṣanʿāʾ all participated in it"," I would have killed them.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15981","(15975) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) executed seven men from the people of Ṣanʿāʾ who had participated in the killing of a boy, and he said: \Had the people of Ṣanʿāʾ all colluded in it"," I would have executed them all.\"" The Sheikh said: This is Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī"," whereas the first one is Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān. Al-Bukhārī said: And Mughīra ibn Ḥakīm reported from his father that four persons killed a boy"," and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15982","(15976) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim informed us that al-Mughīra ibn Ḥakīm al-Ṣanʿānī informed him from his father: that a woman in Ṣanʿāʾ whose husband had gone away, and she had in her care a boy from another man, called Uṣayl, took a companion after her husband. She said to her companion: \This boy will expose us; kill him.\"" He refused and withheld himself from it"," so she threatened to end their relationship"," and he yielded. The man"," another man"," the woman"," and her servant all gathered to kill him. They killed him"," then dismembered his limbs"," placed them in a leather pouch"," and threw it into a well on the outskirts of the village that contained no water. Then the woman cried out"," and the people gathered and went out searching for the boy. A man passed by the well in which the boy was"," and green flies emerged from it. He said: \""By Allah"," there is a corpse in this.\"" Her companion was with us"," and he was seized with trembling. We took him and detained him"," and sent a man who retrieved the boy. We took the man"," and he confessed and told us the account. The woman"," the other man"," and her servant also confessed. Yaʿlā"," who was the governor at that time"," wrote concerning their matter"," and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to him to execute them all"," and he said: \""By Allah"," had the people of Ṣanʿāʾ participated in his killing"," I would have executed them all.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī from Saʿīd ibn Wahb"," who said: A group of people set out"," and a man joined them. They arrived"," but he was not with them"," so his family accused them. Shurayḥ said: \""Your testimony is that they killed your companion; otherwise"," let them swear by Allah that they did not kill him.\"" They were brought to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). Saʿīd said: I was present with him. He separated them"," and they confessed. He said: I heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \""I am Abū al-Ḥasan al-Qarm.\"" ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered that they be executed. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15983","(15977) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us from Muṭarrif from ʿĀmir, meaning al-Shaʿbī.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī said, from Sufyān from Muṭarrif from al-Shaʿbī: that two men came to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) and testified against a man that he had stolen. So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) cut off his hand. Then they came to him with another man and said: \This is the one who stole"," and we were mistaken regarding the first.\"" He did not accept their testimony against the other"," and he held them liable for the blood-money of the first man's hand"," and he said: \""Had I known that you did it deliberately"," I would have cut off your hands.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī cited it under the heading of the chapter. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15984","(15978) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq and Abū Muḥammad ibn Mūsā said: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī and Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us from Ḥammād from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad from ʿĀʿishah from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: \The pen is lifted from three: from the boy until he reaches puberty"," from the insane person until he regains his senses"," and from the sleeper until he awakens.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""
"15985","(15979) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānjānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us, saying: Mālik said; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed me: that Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam wrote to Muʿāwiya ibn Abī Sufyān that a madman who had a killed a man was brought before him. Muʿāwiya wrote to him: \Take the blood-money from him and do not exact retaliation against him"," for there is no retaliation against a madman.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Mālik]"""
"15986","(15980) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus informed me from Abī al-Zinād. And Ibn Wahb informed us; Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd: that Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam wrote to Muʿāwiya, mentioning that a drunkard who had killed a man was brought before him. Muʿāwiya wrote to him: \Execute retaliation against him for it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Mālik]"""
"15987","(15981) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū Umayyah informed us; Abū Nuʿaym informed us; Sufyān informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us by dictation and recitation; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us; Sakhtawayh ibn Māziyār informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Sadūsī informed us; Shuʿbah and Sufyān informed us from Jābir from Abī ʿĀzib from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Everything involves error except the sword"," and for every error there is compensation.\"" This is the wording of the Ḥadīth of al-ʿAlawī. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15988","(15982) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Tamtām informed us; Abū Ḥudhayfah informed us; Sufyān informed us from Jābir from a man from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr: that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Indeed"," everything involves error except the sword\""—meaning the blade—\""and for every error there is compensation.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15989","(15983) Abū Saʿd ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī ʿUthmān al-Zāhid and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah said: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; ʿUqbah ibn Mukram informed us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr informed us; Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ informed us from Abī Ḥuṣayn from Ibrāhīm, the son of the daughter of al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Everything other than the blade involves error"," and for every error there is compensation.\""\n\nThe chain of this Ḥadīth revolves around Jābir al-Juʿfī and Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ"," and they are not used as evidence. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15990","(15984) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Shuʿbah informed us from Hishām ibn Zayd from Anas ibn Mālik: that a young girl went out wearing her ornaments, and a Jew seized her, crushed her head with a stone, and took what she was wearing. She was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while she still had some life in her. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: \Who killed you? Was it so-and-so?\"" She indicated with her head: \""No.\"" They said: \""The Jew?\"" She indicated with her head: \""Yes.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) seized him and crushed his head between two stones. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim reported it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the Ḥadīth of Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"15991","(15985) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Abū ʿUmar and Abū Salamah both said: Ḥammām narrated to us from Qatādah from Anas: that a young girl was found with her head crushed between two stones. She was asked, \Who did this to you? Was it so-and-so? Was it so-and-so?\"" — until the name of the Jew was mentioned"," whereupon she indicated with her head (in affirmation). He was brought and confessed. The Prophet ﷺ ordered"," and his head was crushed with stones. Abū Salamah said: \""Between two stones.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Salamah"," and Muslim narrated it from Haddāb ibn Khālid from Ḥammām. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15992","(15986) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAṭṭār in Baghdād informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās: that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the people about the (case of a) foetus. Ḥimāl ibn Mālik ibn al-Nābiqah stood up and said: \I was between two of my wives; one of them struck the other with a tent pole"," and she was pregnant"," so she killed her (the foetus).\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed regarding the foetus that a ghurrah (a slave or a female slave) be given as blood-money"," and he decreed that the woman be killed for the woman.\n\nThis is a sound isnād. Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī mentioned in Kitāb al-ʿIlal: \""I asked Muḥammad"," meaning al-Bukhārī"," about this hadith"," and he said: 'This is a sound hadith.' It was narrated by Ibn Jurayj from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and Ibn Jurayj is a ḥāfiẓ.\"" The Shaykh said: It is as al-Bukhārī stated regarding the continuity of the hadith with the mention of Ibn ʿAbbās in it"," except that in his wording there is an addition that I have not found in any of the routes of this hadith"," namely: \""the killing of the woman for the woman.\"" And there is the hadith of ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās as a connected narration"," and the hadith of Ibn Ṭāwūs from his father as a mursal narration"," and the hadith of Jābir and Abū Hurayrah as a firmly established connected narration: that he decreed that its blood-money be paid by the ʿāqilah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15993","(15987) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Yazīd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed me that he heard Ṭāwūs narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās, and he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner, and said in it: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed regarding her foetus that a ghurrah be given"," and that she be killed for it.\"" He said: \""I said to ʿAmr ibn Dīnār: 'Ibn Ṭāwūs informed me from his father that he decreed the blood-money and a ghurrah for her foetus.' He said: 'You have cast doubt in me.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15994","(15988) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bazzāz narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Muslim narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr al-Bursānī narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed me, and he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner, except that he said: \I said to ʿAmr: 'Did Ibn Ṭāwūs not inform me from his father such-and-such?' He said: 'You have cast doubt in me.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"15995","(15989) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr and others besides them informed us: they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj from ʿUbaydah ibn Musāfiʿ from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was distributing something, a man came and lunged at him. He (the Prophet ﷺ) struck him with a palm branch that he had with him, and the man was wounded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Come"," take your retaliation.\"" He said: \""Rather"," I have forgiven"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"15996","(15990) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us: al-Ḥajjāj informed us from Ziyād ibn ʿAlāqah: our shaykhs who met the Prophet ﷺ informed us: that a man struck a man with a stone, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ exacted retaliation from him for it. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15997","(15991) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Abū Khalīfah narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Jābir from Ziyād ibn ʿAlāqah from Mirdās: that a man threw a stone at another man and killed him. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he exacted retaliation from him for it. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15998","(15992) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us: ʿAbdān narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us: al-Walīd ibn Abī Thawr narrated to us from Ziyād ibn ʿAlāqah from Mirdās ibn ʿUrwah, who said: A man from the tribe struck his brother and killed him, and he fled. We found him with Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, and we took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he exacted retaliation from him for us. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"15999","(15993) It has been narrated to us from Bishr ibn Ḥāzim from ʿImrān ibn Yazīd ibn al-Barāʾ from his father from his grandfather: that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever kills (by a certain method)"," we will kill him (by the same method); whoever burns"," we will burn him; and whoever drowns"," we will drown him.\""\n\nAnd this is in what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Hārūn ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī: Bishr narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16000","(15994) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us from Abū ʿUbayd: Yazīd narrated to us from Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh from Zayd ibn Jubayr from Jarwah ibn Ḥumayl from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \One of you will strike his brother with something like a flesh-eating (weapon)"," and then he will see that I will not exact retaliation from him. By Allah"," I will certainly exact retaliation from him for it.\""\n\nIsrāʾīl corroborated it from Zayd ibn Jubayr from Jarwah from his father from ʿUmar. Abū ʿUbayd said: Yazīd said: al-Ḥajjāj said: \""Ākilat al-laḥm (flesh-eater) means a sharpened staff.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: \""In this hadith there is the ruling that he (ʿUmar) considered qiṣāṣ (retaliation) to be applicable in killing with something other than a blade"," provided that the like of it (the instrument) causes death.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16001","(15995) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to me from Ibn Jurayj that ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated to him that he heard ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr al-Laythī say: A man of standing would go to a man and beat him with a staff until he killed him, then he would say, \It was not deliberate!\"" And what act of deliberation could be more deliberate than that?\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"16002","(15996) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," in the case of quasi-deliberate killing (shibh al-ʿamd) by means of a whip or a staff"," there is a blood-money of one hundred camels made severe (mughtaẓah)"," of which forty are pregnant she-camels in whose wombs are their young.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16003","(15997) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sukkarī say: I heard Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah say: I was present one day in the gathering of al-Muzanī, and a questioner from among the Iraqis asked him about quasi-deliberate killing (shibh al-ʿamd). The questioner said: \Indeed"," Allah"," Blessed and Exalted"," described killing in His Book with two descriptions: deliberate (ʿamd) and accidental (khaṭaʾ). So why do you say it is of three categories"," and why do you say 'quasi-deliberate' (shibh al-ʿamd)?\"" Al-Muzanī then cited this hadith as evidence. His opponent in the debate said to him: \""Do you cite ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān as evidence?\"" Al-Muzanī fell silent. So I said to his opponent: \""Others besides ʿAlī ibn Zayd have narrated this report.\"" He said: \""Who narrated it other than ʿAlī?\"" I said: \""Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī and Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ.\"" He said to me: \""Who is ʿUqbah ibn Aws?\"" I said: \""ʿUqbah ibn Aws is a man from the people of Baṣrah"," and Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated from him despite his eminence.\"" The opponent then said to al-Muzanī: \""Are you the one debating"," or is this one?\"" Al-Muzanī replied: \""When the hadith comes"," he is the one who debates"," for he is more knowledgeable of hadith than I. Then I shall speak.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: As for the hadith of Ayyūb…\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16004","(15998) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Abī Khalaf al-Ṣūfī al-Isfarāʾīnī informed us there that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Yazdād ibn Masʿūd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Abū ʿUmar narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us from Ayyūb from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr from the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: \Accidental killing that is quasi-deliberate (shibh al-ʿamd) by means of a whip or a staff: therein is one hundred camels"," of which forty are in their wombs their young.\"" This is what Ayyūb said"," narrating from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16005","(15999) As for the hadith of Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ: Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that al-Thaqafī narrated to us from Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah from ʿUqbah ibn Aws from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on the day of the Conquest of Makkah: \Indeed"," in the case of accidental killing that is quasi-deliberate (shibh al-ʿamd)—killing by means of a whip or a staff—there is a severe blood-money (diyah mughtaẓah)"," of which forty are pregnant she-camels in whose wombs are their young.\""\n\nA group also narrated it from Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ.\n\nAnd Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it from Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ and he corrected its chain of narration.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16006","(16000) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed it, that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and Musaddad said: Ḥammād narrated to us from Khālid from al-Qāsim ibn Rabīʿah from ʿUqbah ibn Aws from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon on the day of the Conquest in Makkah and mentioned the hadith, then said: \Indeed"," the blood-money of accidental killing that is quasi-deliberate (shibh al-ʿamd)"," when it is by means of a whip or a staff"," is one hundred camels"," of which forty are in their wombs their young.\""\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by Wuhib from Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ. And it has been narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding deliberate killing"," quasi-deliberate killing"," and accidental killing"," and that will appear"," if Allah wills"," in the Book of Blood-Moneys (Kitāb al-Diyāt).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16007","(16001) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \Whoever is killed in a state of blind confusion (ʿimmīyah)—that is"," a shooting among them with stones"," or a lashing with a whip"," or a blow with a staff—then it is accidental (khaṭaʾ)"," and its blood-money is the blood-money of accidental killing. And whoever is killed deliberately (ʿamd)"," then it is a matter of retribution (qiṣāṣ) by his hand. So whoever stands in the way of that"," upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath; no expiation (ṣarf) nor ransom (ʿadl) shall be accepted from him.\""\n\nThis is a mursal hadith.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf — Mursal]"""
"16008","(16002) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Kathīr narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is killed in a state of blind confusion (ʿimmīyah) or a shooting (rimmīyah) among them with a stone or a staff"," its blood-money is the blood-money of accidental killing. And whoever is killed deliberately"," then it is a matter of retribution by his two hands. So whoever stands between him and that"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind; no expiation (ṣarf) nor ransom (ʿadl) shall be accepted from him.\""\n\nHis statement \""its blood-money is the blood-money of accidental killing\""—he means by it"," and Allah knows best"," quasi-accidental killing (shibh al-khaṭaʾ)"," which is quasi-deliberate killing (shibh al-ʿamd). And his statement \""then it is accidental (khaṭaʾ)\""—he means by it quasi-accidental killing"," so that retribution (qiṣāṣ) does not become obligatory by it. And it is also possible that what is meant by it is pure accidental killing (al-khaṭaʾ al-maḥḍ)"," which is that a person shoots at something and hits something else"," and thus its blood-money is the blood-money of accidental killing. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf — Munkar]"""
"16009","(16003) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Dārakī narrated to us that Abū Ḥātim narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Makhzūmī narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \And quasi-deliberate killing (shibh al-ʿamd) involves a severe blood-money"," and the one responsible shall not be killed in retribution for it. That is when Satan incites enmity between tribes"," and there occurs among them a shooting with stones in a state of blind confusion"," without any prior rancour and without the bearing of weapons.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16010","(16004) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us that ʿImrān narrated to us from Qatādah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaqīq from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever strikes with a whip unjustly"," retribution shall be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16011","(16005) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed me; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Hisham ibn Zayd from Anas: that a Jewish woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with a poisoned sheep, and he ate from it. She was then brought to him and it was said, \Shall we not kill him?\"" He said"," \""No.\"" He said"," \""I continued to recognize its effect in the throat of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" [Sahih — Agreed upon]"""
"16012","(16006) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr, and Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us. Ibn al-Nadr said, \informed us","\"" and the other two said"," \""narrated to us\""; Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us"," and he mentioned it with the same chain of narration"," except that he said: \""She was then brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he asked her about that. She said"," 'I intended to kill you.' He said"," 'Allah would never give you power over that' — or he said"," 'over me.' They said"," 'Shall we not kill her?' He said"," 'No.' Then he mentioned the remainder of the hadith.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from al-Hajabi"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi. [Sahih]"""
"16013","(16007) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us; 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated. And Harun ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us; 'Abbad narrated from Sufyan ibn Husayn from al-Zuhri from Sa'id and Abu Salamah. Harun said: from Abu Hurayrah: that a Jewish woman presented the Prophet (ﷺ) with a poisoned sheep. He said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) did not take any action against her.\"" [Sahih]"""
"16014","(16008) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Yunus informed me from Ibn Shihab. He said: Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah used to relate that a Jewish woman from the people of Khaybar poisoned a roasted sheep and then presented it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took the foreleg and ate from it, and a group of his Companions ate with him. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to them, \Raise your hands.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent for the Jewish woman and summoned her. He said to her"," \""Did you poison this sheep?\"" The Jewish woman said"," \""Who told you?\"" He said"," \""This one in my hand\"" — meaning the foreleg — informed me. She said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""What did you intend by that?\"" She said"," \""I said"," if he is a prophet"," it will not harm him"," and if he is not a prophet"," we would be relieved of him.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pardoned her and did not punish her. Some of his Companions who had eaten from the sheep passed away. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had cupping performed on his shoulder on account of what he had eaten from the sheep. Abu Hind performed the cupping with a horn and a razor"," and he was a freedman of Banu Bayadah from the Ansar. [Da'if]"""
"16015","(16009) And Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us; Khalid narrated from Muhammad ibn 'Amr from Abu Salamah: that a Jewish woman in Khaybar presented the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a roasted sheep — similar to the hadith of Jabir. He said: \Bishr ibn al-Bara' ibn Ma'rur died"," so he sent for the Jewish woman"," 'What compelled you to do what you did?'\"" And he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Jabir. He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered regarding her"," and she was killed.\"" He did not mention the matter of cupping. [Da'if]"""
"16016","(16010) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us; al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Laythi from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah: that a Jewish woman invited the Prophet (ﷺ) and some of his Companions to a roasted sheep. When they sat down to eat, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took a morsel and placed it in his mouth, then said to them, \Hold back! This sheep is poisoned.\"" He said to the Jewish woman"," \""Woe to me! Why did you poison me?\"" She said"," \""I wished to know: if you are a prophet"," it will not harm you"," and if you are not"," that I might relieve the people of you.\"" Bishr ibn al-Bara' ate from it and died. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) killed her. [Da'if]"""
"16017","(16011) Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi narrated to us; Abu Hamam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us; 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated from Muhammad ibn 'Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (ﷺ) killed her — meaning the one who had poisoned him. [Da'if]"
"16018","(16012) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Bahlul narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated from Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah from his grandfather: that on the day of Khaybar, a poisoned roasted sheep was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), which a Jewish woman had presented to him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and Bishr ibn al-Bara' ate from it, and they both fell severely ill because of it. Then Bishr passed away. When Bishr died, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent for the Jewish woman and she was brought to him. He said, \Woe to you! What did you feed us?\"" She said"," \""I fed you poison. I knew that if you are a prophet"," it would not harm you"," and that Allah would accomplish His decree concerning you. And if you are not that"," I wished to relieve the people of you.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered regarding her"," and she was crucified. [Da'if]"""
"16019","(16013) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Battah al-Isbahani narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn al-Jahm narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn al-Faraj narrated to us; al-Waqidi narrated to us; Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Labibah narrated from his grandfather Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered regarding her, and she was crucified after being killed. [Da'if]\n\nAl-Waqidi said: \The established position with us is that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) killed her and ordered the meat of the sheep to be burned.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""The narrations differ regarding her killing. The narration of Anas ibn Malik is the most authentic of them. It is possible that he (ﷺ) initially did not punish her when none of his Companions had died from what they had eaten. Then when Bishr ibn al-Bara' died"," he ordered her killing. Each narrator reported what he witnessed. And Allah knows best.\"""""
"16020","(16014) Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Abu 'Awanah narrated from Husayn from 'Amr ibn Maymun. He said: \I saw 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," a few days before he was struck"," in Madinah. He stood before Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and 'Uthman ibn Hunayf and said"," 'How have you acted? Do you fear that you have burdened the land with what it cannot bear?' They said"," 'We burdened it with a matter it can bear.' Hudhayfah said"," 'Had I burdened it"," I would have weakened it.' And 'Uthman ibn Hunayf said"," 'I burdened it with a matter it can bear"," in which there is no great merit.' He said"," 'Beware that you do not burden the land with what it cannot bear.' They said"," 'No.' So 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said"," 'If Allah grants me safety"," I will leave the widows of Iraq in such a state that they will not need any man after me.' He said"," 'Only four days passed before he was struck.' He said"," 'There was nothing between me and him except 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas on the morning he was struck. When he passed between the two rows"," he would stand. If he saw a gap"," he would say"," \""Straighten up!\"" until he saw no gap among them"," then he would step forward and say the takbir. He would sometimes recite Surah Yusuf or al-Nahl or something similar in the first rak'ah until the people gathered.' He said"," 'He had barely said the takbir when I heard him say"," \""The dog has killed me\"" — or \""The dog has devoured me\"" — when he stabbed him. The barbarian fled with a double-edged knife"," and he did not pass anyone to his right or left without stabbing him"," until he stabbed thirteen men"," nine of whom died. When a Muslim man saw that"," he threw a cloak over him. When the barbarian believed he was caught"," he killed himself. Then 'Umar took the hand of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," and put him forward. Those who were behind 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," saw what he saw. As for the sides of the mosque"," they did not know"," except that they lost the voice of 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and they were saying"," 'Subhan Allah! Subhan Allah!' So 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf"," may Allah be pleased with him"," led them in a brief prayer. When he finished"," he said"," 'O Ibn 'Abbas"," see who killed me.' He went out for a while"," then came and said"," 'The slave of al-Mughirah.' He said"," 'The craftsman?' He said"," 'Yes.' He said"," 'May Allah fight him! I had indeed enjoined good treatment of him.' Then he said"," 'All praise is due to Allah"," who did not make my death at the hands of a man who claims Islam.' He said"," 'You and your father used to love that the non-Muslim slaves increase in Madinah.' He said"," 'Al-'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," had the most slaves.' He said"," 'If you wish"," we will do it' — meaning"," 'If you wish"," we will kill them.' He said"," 'You lie! After they have spoken your language"," prayed toward your qibla"," and performed your Hajj.' He was then carried to his house"," and we went with him. It was as if the people had never been afflicted with a calamity before that day. One person would say"," 'It is nothing","' and another would say"," 'We fear for him.' He was brought nabidh and he drank it"," and it came out of his wound. Then he was brought milk and he drank it"," and it came out of his wound"," so they knew that he was dying. And he mentioned the hadith regarding his will and the matter of the Shura.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il."""
"16021","(16015) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Ya'qub al-Thaqafi and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh both said: Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Shabib al-Ma'mari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', who said: Abu Lu'lu'ah was a slave of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. He mentioned his story and said: He fashioned for himself a double-bladed dagger. He said: He sharpened it and poisoned it. He said: And 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, pronounced the takbir, and he would not pronounce the takbir when the prayer was established until he spoke and said: \Straighten your rows.\"" So he came and stood in the sandal's position adjacent to 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in the morning prayer. When he pronounced the takbir"," he came upon him at his shoulder and at another place"," and in his flank. So 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," fell"," and thirteen men were struck along with him. He dispersed seven of them"," and six died. 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was carried away and taken"," and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then he called for a drink to examine the extent of his wound. He was brought nabidh and he drank it"," and it came out"," and it was not known whether it was blood or nabidh. Then he called for milk and was brought it"," and he drank it"," and it came out of his wound. They said: \""There is no harm upon you"," O Commander of the Faithful.\"" He said: \""If killing is harmful"," then I have been killed.\"" [Sahih]"""
"16022","(16016) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Jallab narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us: Zā'idah narrated from Layth, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, lived for three days after being stabbed, then he passed away. He was washed and shrouded."
"16023","(16017) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: 'Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us: Abu Salih, meaning Mahbub ibn Musa, narrated to us: Al-Fazari, meaning Abu Ishaq, narrated from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Firas, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said in his sermon: \Behold"," I have not sent over you my governors to strike your skins or to take your wealth. Rather"," I have sent them to teach you your religion and your sunnahs. So whoever is done to other than that"," let him raise it to me"," that I may exact retribution from him.\"" So 'Amr ibn al-'As"," may Allah be pleased with him"," stood and said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," if a man disciplines some of your subjects"," would you exact retribution from him?\"" He said: \""Yes"," by Whose Hand is my soul"," I shall exact retribution from him. For I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ exact retribution from himself.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16024","(16018) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq recited to them both, and Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Sarraj dictated, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed me: 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from 'Ubaydah ibn Musafi', from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was distributing something, a man came and bent over him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck him with a palm stalk that was with him, and the man was wounded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Come and take retribution.\"" He said: \""Rather I have forgiven"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16025","(16019) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Malik informed me, and others informed him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man perfumed with saffron, so he struck him with a stick that was in his hand. Then he said: \Did I not forbid you from this?\"" The man said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," indeed Allah has sent you with the truth"," and you have wounded me.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the stick to him and said: \""Take retribution.\"" The man said: \""You struck me while I had no shirt upon me"," and you have a shirt upon you.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ exposed his belly for him"," and the man bent over him and kissed it. This is a disconnected narration"," though it has been reported in a connected form. [Da'if]"""
"16026","(16020) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yunus narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from al-Hasan, who said: Sawwad ibn 'Amr narrated to me, saying: I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was perfumed with khaluq perfume. When he saw me, he said: \O Sawwad ibn 'Amr"," is this khaluq of wars? Did I not forbid you from khaluq?\"" And he prodded me with a stick in his hand in my belly"," causing me pain. I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," retribution!\"" He said: \""Retribution!\"" So he exposed his belly for me"," and I began to kiss it. Then I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," will you leave intercession for me on the Day of Resurrection?\"" (T) 'Umar ibn Sulayt followed him in narrating from al-Hasan"," from Sawwad ibn 'Amr. [Sahih]"""
"16027","(16021) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to me: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Saydalani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: Yahya ibn al-Mughirah al-Sa'di narrated to us: Jarir narrated from Husayn, from 'Abd Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father, who said: Usayd ibn Hudayr was a man of good cheer and pleasant countenance. While he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, talking to the people and making them laugh, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck him with his finger in his flank and said: \You have pained me.\"" He said: \""Take retribution.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you have a shirt upon you"," and I have no shirt upon me.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his shirt"," embraced him"," and began to kiss his flank"," saying: \""By my father and my mother"," O Messenger of Allah"," this is what I desired.\"" [Sahih]"""
"16028","(16022) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sufyan informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet ﷺ sent Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah as a collector of zakah. A man resisted him regarding his zakah, so Abu Jahm struck him and wounded him. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \Retribution"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""You have such and such.\"" They were not pleased. He said: \""You have such and such.\"" They were not pleased. He said: \""You have such and such.\"" They were pleased. The Prophet ﷺ said: \""I shall address the people this evening and inform them of your pleasure.\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people and said: \""Indeed"," these Laythis came to me seeking retribution. I offered them such and such"," and they were pleased. Have you been pleased?\"" They said: \""No.\"" So the Muhajirun were enraged at them"," but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to restrain themselves"," and they restrained themselves. Then he called them and increased the offer"," and said: \""Have you been pleased?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I shall address the people and inform them of your pleasure.\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people and said: \""Have you been pleased?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" [Sahih]"""
"16029","(16023) Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli differed from him, narrating it as follows: Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed me: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: It reached us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Abu Jahm over zakah. He struck a man from Banu Layth and severely wounded him, cutting both thick muscles. They asked for retribution, so he satisfied them but did not exact retribution from him. [Da'if]"
"16030","(16024) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Farisi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: There was a black man who would come to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and he would bring him near and teach him the Qur'an, until he sent a raiding party — or he said a detachment — and said: \Send me with them.\"" He said: \""Rather"," remain with us.\"" But he refused"," so he sent him with them and enjoined goodness upon him. He had been absent only a short while when he came with his hand cut off. When Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," saw him"," his eyes overflowed with tears and he said: \""What has befallen you?\"" He said: \""I did not increase beyond the fact that he had appointed me over some of his work"," and I betrayed him in a single obligatory prayer"," so he cut off my hand.\"" Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Do you find the one who cut this betraying more than twenty obligatory prayers? By Allah"," if you are truthful"," I shall exact retribution from you for it.\"" Then he brought him near"," and his status with him did not change. The man would stand at night and recite"," and when Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," heard his voice"," he would say: \""Woe to the night of the one whose hand has been cut off.\"" She said: \""It was only a short while before the family of Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," lost their ornaments and possessions.\"" Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""The tribe was raided during the night.\"" The man with the severed hand stood"," faced the qibla"," raised his sound hand and the one that had been cut off"," and said: \""O Allah"," manifest upon the one who stole them\"" — or something to that effect. Ma'mar would sometimes say: \""O Allah"," manifest upon the one who stole the people of this righteous household.\"" She said: \""The day had not yet reached midday when the possessions were found in his possession.\"" Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to him: \""Woe to you! You have little knowledge of Allah.\"" So he commanded"," and his foot was cut off. [Sahih]\n\nMa'mar said: And Ayyub informed me from Nafi'"," from Ibn 'Umar"," similarly to that"," except that he said: When Abu Bakr heard his voice"," he would say: \""What a night for a thief!\"" The point of evidence in these narrations rests upon his statement: \""By Allah"," if you are truthful"," I shall exact retribution from you for it.\"""""
"16031","(16025) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzaki, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, and I heard Huyayy ibn 'Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri saying: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to me from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, stood on a Friday and said: \In the morning"," bring the charitable camels so that they may be distributed"," and let no one enter upon us without permission.\"" A woman said to her husband: \""Take this nose-rope"," perhaps Allah will grant us a camel.\"" But the man refused. Then he found that Abu Bakr and 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," had entered among the camels"," so he entered with them. Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," turned and said: \""What has brought you to us?\"" Then he took the nose-rope from him and struck him. When Abu Bakr finished distributing the camels"," he called for the man and gave him the nose-rope and said: \""Take your retribution.\"" 'Umar said to him: \""By Allah"," he will not take retribution — do not make this a Sunnah.\"" Abu Bakr said: \""Then who will protect me before Allah on the Day of Resurrection?\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Satisfy him.\"" So Abu Bakr al-Siddiq"," may Allah be pleased with him"," ordered his servant to bring his mount and its saddle"," a velvet garment"," and five dinars"," and he satisfied him with these. [Da'if]"""
"16032","(16026) Abu Sa'id narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Bahr narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to me from Ibn Shihab that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, and 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with them, offered themselves for retribution (qawad), but retribution was not taken from them while they were in authority (salatin). [Da'if — Mursal, from al-Zuhri]"
"16033","(16027) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan narrated to us: Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us: Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us: 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us from Abu Zur'ah from 'Amr ibn Jarir from Jarir that a man who had a powerful voice and struck fear into the enemy was with Abu Musa. They obtained a war-gain, and Abu Musa gave him his share but did not give him his full due. The man refused to accept it unless he received the full amount. So Abu Musa struck him twenty lashes and shaved his head. The man gathered his hair and went with it to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. Jarir said: \I was the closest of people to him\"" — and Hammad said: \""I was the closest of the people to him.\"" The man took some hair from his pocket and struck it against the chest of 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and said: \""What is the matter with you?\"" He recounted his story. So 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," wrote to Abu Musa: \""Peace be upon you. To proceed: So-and-so son of so-and-so has informed me of such-and-such. I adjure you by Allah: if you did what you did in the presence of people"," then sit before him in the presence of people and let him take retribution from you; and if you did what you did in private"," then sit before him in private and let him take retribution from you.\"" The people said to the man: \""Forgive him.\"" He said: \""No"," by Allah"," I will not leave him for anyone among the people.\"" When the letter was delivered to Abu Musa"," he sat for the retribution. The man raised his head toward the heavens and said: \""I have forgiven him for the sake of Allah.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16034","(16028) Abu Sa'id narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: al-Rabi' said: al-Shafi'i said: Hammad narrated to us from Qatadah from Khilas from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \If a man orders his slave to kill a person"," the slave is merely like his sword or his whip. The master (mawla) is to be killed"," and the slave is to be imprisoned.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16035","(16029) Abu Mansur Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Damaghani narrated to us in Bayhaq: Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us: Ahmad and Ibrahim, the sons of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ja'far al-Sayrafiyyan, narrated to us: 'Abadah ibn 'Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Hafri narrated to us: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Umayyah from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \If a man holds a man and the other kills him"," the one who killed is to be killed"," and the one who held him is to be imprisoned.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: This is not preserved (ghayr mahfuz). It has also been narrated from Isma'il ibn Umayyah from Sa'id al-Musayyab from the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him. [Munkar]"""
"16036","(16030) The correct narration is what Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Ubayd narrated to us: Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," judged regarding a man who held a man and the other killed him: the killer is to be killed"," and the one who held him is to be imprisoned.\""\n\nAnd from Sufyan from Jabir from 'Amir from 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he judged according to that. [Da'if]"""
"16037","(16031) Similarly, Ma'mar narrated it from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, raising it (yarfa'uhu), saying: \Kill the killer"," and imprison the one who held him.\""\n\nAbu 'Abd al-Rahman narrated it to us: Abu al-Hasan al-Karizi narrated to us: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us from Abu 'Ubayd"," who said: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrate it from Ma'mar from Isma'il ibn Umayyah"," raising it.\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: His words \""imprison the one who held him\"" (isbiru al-sabir) mean: confine the one who detained him. [Da'if]"""
"16038","(16032) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzaki narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Musa narrated to us from Bukayr ibn Ma'ruf from Muqatil ibn Hayyan. Muqatil said: I learned this tafsir from a group of scholars, among whom Mu'adh preserved the narrations of Mujahid, al-Hasan, and al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, regarding His words — exalted is He — {So whoever is pardoned anything by his brother, then let there be a follow-up with fair payment} [al-Baqarah 178]. He said: It was prescribed for the People of the Torah that whoever killed a soul without it being for a soul, it was his right to be executed for it, and he could not be pardoned, and blood-money (diyah) would not be accepted from him. And it was prescribed for the People of the Gospel that he be pardoned and not killed. And the Ummah of Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, was given the choice: if they wished, they could kill; if they wished, they could take the blood-money; and if they wished, they could pardon. That is His words — exalted is He — {That is a lightening from your Lord and a mercy} [al-Baqarah 178]. He says: The blood-money is a lightening from Allah, since He made the blood-money permissible and did not require killing. Then He said — exalted is He — {But whoever transgresses after that, for him is a painful punishment} [al-Baqarah 178]. He says: Whoever kills after having taken the blood-money, for him is a painful punishment. And regarding His words — exalted is He — {And in retribution (qisas) there is life for you} [al-Baqarah 179], He says: In retribution there is life for you, by which some of you will be deterred from others, out of fear of being killed. [Hasan]"
"16039","(16033) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydus and Abu Muhammad al-Ka'bi narrated to us, both saying: Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Salih narrated to us from Bukayr ibn Ma'ruf from Muqatil ibn Hayyan regarding His words — exalted is He — {So whoever is pardoned anything by his brother} [al-Baqarah 178]. He says: When a man kills intentionally and the guardian of the slain pardons him and does not take retribution from him, and accepts the blood-money, {then let there be a follow-up with fair payment} [al-Baqarah 178] — meaning: let the claim be made in a good manner. Then he turned to the one from whom payment is due and said: {and payment to him with good conduct} [al-Baqarah 178] — meaning: let the one from whom payment is due pay the blood-money to the claimant with good conduct. He said: It was prescribed for the People of the Torah — and he mentioned it in a manner similar to the narration of al-Shafi'i. And regarding His words — exalted is He — {But whoever transgresses after that, for him is a painful punishment} [al-Baqarah 178], he says: Whoever accepts the blood-money and then kills — {for him is a painful punishment} [al-Baqarah 178] — meaning: a painful one. That is because when a man's close relative was killed, the killer would go into hiding. The guardian of the slain would say: \I will accept the blood-money.\"" He would accept it until the killer returned"," and then the guardian of the slain would kill him"," having already accepted the blood-money. He would say: \""I only accepted the blood-money so that the killer would return and I would kill him when he appeared.\"" Allah — mighty and majestic is He — says: {But whoever transgresses} and kills after having taken it"," {for him is a painful punishment} [al-Baqarah 178]. [Hasan]"""
"16040","(16034) Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Muzaki narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Mujahid say: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: \Among the Children of Israel there was retribution (qisas) and there was no blood-money (diyah) among them. So Allah — mighty and majestic is He — said to this Ummah: {Prescribed for you is retribution for the slain: the free for the free"," the slave for the slave"," and the female for the female. But whoever is pardoned anything by his brother} [al-Baqarah 178].\"" He said: Pardoning means accepting the blood-money in the case of intentional killing. {Then let there be a follow-up with fair payment and payment to him with good conduct. That is a lightening from your Lord} [al-Baqarah 178] — from what was prescribed for those who came before you. {But whoever transgresses after that"," for him is a painful punishment} [al-Baqarah 178]. [Sahih — al-Bukhari 4498]"""
"16041","(16025) And 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allāh narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from 'Amr ibn Dīnār — he said: Mujāhid narrated to me from Ibn 'Abbās, and he mentioned it with a similar narration.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Qutaybah, from Sufyān."
"16042","(16036) And Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us — they both said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us — Abū 'Āmir narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from 'Amr ibn Dīnār from Jābir ibn Zayd from Ibn 'Abbās regarding the verse: *\Legal retribution is prescribed for you in cases of murder: the free for the free"," the slave for the slave\""* [al-Baqarah 178] — he said: Legal retribution was prescribed upon the Children of Israel"," and you were granted concession regarding the blood-money. *\""But whoever is pardoned by his brother for anything"," then there should be a follow-up with fairness and payment to him with good conduct\""* [al-Baqarah 178] — he said: It refers to intentional murder where the victim's family is pleased with the blood-money"," so the claimant follows up with fairness"," and the one from whom it is due pays with good conduct. *\""That is an alleviation from your Lord and a mercy\""* [al-Baqarah 178] — he said: [It is an alleviation] from what had been prescribed upon the Children of Israel.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ from other than this chain.]"""
"16043","(16027) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us — Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfi'ī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ismā'il ibn Abī Fudayk narrated from Ibn Abī Dhi'b from Sa'īd al-Maqburī from Abū Shurayḥ al-Ka'bī that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Verily"," Allah has sanctified Makkah — not the people. It is not permissible for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood therein or to cut down its tree. If anyone claims an exemption and says: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was granted permission","' then know that Allah made it permissible for me"," and He did not make it permissible for the people. It was made permissible for me only for a single hour of the day"," after which it is sacred as it was before. O Khuzā'ah! You have killed this man from Hudhayl"," and by Allah"," I shall pay his blood-money. Whoever kills another after that — his family shall have the choice: if they wish"," they may execute [retaliation]"," and if they wish"," they may accept the blood-money.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"16044","(16038) Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us — they both said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — Abū Zur'ah al-Dimashqī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated from al-Ḥārith ibn al-Fuḍayl from Sufyān ibn Abī al-'Awjā' al-Sulamī from Abū Shurayḥ al-Khuzā'ī, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Whoever suffers a killing or a wounding has the choice among three options. If he desires a fourth"," then seize his hand. He may choose to exact retaliation"," or to pardon"," or to accept the blood-money. If he accepts any of that and then transgresses thereafter"," he shall have the Fire.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"16045","(16029) Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw narrated to us — Sa'īd ibn Mas'ūd narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Mūsá narrated to us — Shaybān narrated from Yaḥyá ibn Abī Kathīr — Abū Salamah informed me that Abū Hurayrah informed him: that the Khuzā'ah killed a man from Banī Layth during the year of the Conquest of Makkah in retaliation for one of their own whom they had killed. When this reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he mounted his riding animal and addressed the people, saying: \Verily"," Allah withheld the elephant from Makkah and empowered over it His Messenger and the believers. Know that it was not made lawful for anyone before me"," and it shall not be made lawful for anyone after me. Know that it was made permissible for me only for a single hour of the day. Know that at this very hour it is sacred — its thorns are not to be broken"," its trees are not to be cut"," and its fallen property is not to be picked up except by one who publicly announces it. And for whoever a killing has been committed"," he has the better of two options: either he may be given the blood-money"," or the family of the slain may be executed.\"" Then a man from the people of Yemen"," Abū Shāh"," came and said: \""Write it down for me"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Write it down for Abū Shāh.\"" A man from Quraysh said: \""Except the idhkhir grass"," O Messenger of Allah"," for we use it in our homes and our graves.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Except the idhkhir.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Abū Nu'aym from Shaybān"," except that he said: \""Either he may be paid [the blood-money] or the family of the slain may be executed.\"" And he also said: 'Ubayd Allāh said: \""Either the family of the slain may be executed.\"" And Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr from 'Ubayd Allāh.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"16046","(16040) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn 'Abdān informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Hishām ibn 'Alī narrated to us — Ibn Rajā' narrated to us — Ḥarb ibn Shaddād narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us — Abū Salamah narrated to us — Abū Hurayrah narrated: that during the year of the Conquest of Makkah, the Khuzā'ah killed a man from Banī Layth in retaliation for one of theirs whom they had killed in the Jāhiliyyah. He mentioned the hadith with a similar narration, except that he said: \And for whoever a killing has been committed"," he has the better of two options: either he may be paid [the blood-money] or the family of the slain may be executed.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: And 'Abd Allāh ibn Rajā' narrated to us — Ḥarb narrated.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq 'alayh).]"""
"16047","(16041) And Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū 'Abd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī and Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — al-'Abbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd informed us — my father narrated to us — al-Awzā'ī narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to me — Abū Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān said: Abū Hurayrah narrated to me, saying: \When Makkah was conquered"," the Hudhayl killed a man from Banī Layth in retaliation for one killed in the Jāhiliyyah. This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He mentioned the hadith with a similar narration"," except that he said: \""And for whoever a killing has been committed"," he has the better of two options: either the family of the slain may be executed"," or he may be ransomed.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq 'alayh).]"""
"16048","(16042) And Abū 'Amr al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismā'īlī narrated to us — Abū Ya'lá narrated to us — Hārūn ibn Ma'rūf narrated to us — al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from al-Awzā'ī. He mentioned it with a similar narration, except that he said: \Either he may be ransomed or he may be killed.\""\n\nBoth [al-Bukhārī and Muslim] recorded it in their *Ṣaḥīḥ* from the hadith of al-Walīd ibn Muslim."""
"16049","(16043) Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us — Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsá from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever kills intentionally shall be handed over to the heirs of the slain. If they wish"," they may execute him"," and if they wish"," they may accept the blood-money.\"" And in the hadith of Wā'il ibn Ḥujr from the Prophet ﷺ: when the killer was brought to him bound in a leather strap"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the guardian of the slain: \""Will you pardon?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Will you accept the blood-money?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Will you kill him?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then take him.\""\n\nAnd this is mentioned in the chapter on pardon (al-'afw) with its chain of narration.\n\n[Ḥasan.]"""
"16050","(16044) Abū al-Ḥusayn 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Bishrān the 'Adl in Baghdad informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Dāwūd al-Makkī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Kathīr narrated from 'Amr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs from Ibn 'Abbās, who raised it [to the Prophet], saying: \Whoever is killed by a stone"," a whip"," or a staff — his blood-money is the blood-money of an accidental killing. And whoever is killed intentionally — he is subject to retaliation. And whoever comes between him and his victim [i.e."," kills through an intermediary or in an ambiguous manner] — upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all the people. No expiation (ṣarf) and no compensation ('adl) shall be accepted from him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ from other than this chain.]"""
"16051","(16045) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd — he is Ibn Abī ʿArūbah — from Maṭar, from al-Ḥasan, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I shall not grant pardon to a man who kills after having received the blood-money.\""\n\nThis narration is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)"," though it has also been narrated in a connected (mawṣūl) form. [Weak — disconnected"," mursal]"""
"16052","(16046) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ḥammād informed us: Maṭar al-Warrāq said — and I think he said — from al-Ḥasan, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I shall not grant pardon to one who kills after having received the blood-money.\"" [Weak]"""
"16053","(16047) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated from Shuʿbah, from Qays, from Ṭāriq, that ʿAbd Allāh said regarding His statement {"
"16054","(16048) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from Qays, from Ṭāriq, from al-Haytham ibn al-Aswad, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, regarding His statement {"
"16055","(16049) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Maymūnah, who said — I do not know it except from Anas ibn Mālik — who said: \No case of legal retribution (qiṣāṣ) was ever raised to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) except that he commanded therein forgiveness.\""\n\nHe said: \""I said to ʿAffān: 'Who has doubt about it?' He said: 'ʿAbd Allāh said: I used to say \""from Anas","\"" and they said to me: \""Do not have doubt about it.\"" So I said: \""I do not know it","\"" and he was a man of great caution and intelligence.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"16056","(16050) And Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq narrated to us: Abū Salamah al-Minqarī narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Maymūnah, from Anas, who said: \I never saw the Prophet (ﷺ) have anything of legal retribution (qiṣāṣ) raised to him except that he commanded therein forgiveness.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"16057","(16051) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Tamīm ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Abū Yūnus narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, that ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil narrated to him that his father narrated to him, saying:\n\n\I was sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) when a man came"," leading another by a strap (nisʿah). He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," this man killed my brother.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Did you kill him?' He said: 'Had he not confessed"," I would have established proof against him.' He said: 'Yes"," I killed him.' He said: 'How did you kill him?' He said: 'He and I were gathering leaves from a tree"," and he insulted me"," which angered me"," so I struck him with the axe on his head and killed him.' The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: 'Do you have anything with which to free yourself?' He said: 'I have no wealth except my cloak.' He said: 'Do you think your people would ransom you?' He said: 'I am more insignificant to my people than that.' So he (the Prophet ﷺ) threw the strap to him and said: 'Take your companion.' The man departed with him. When he turned away"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'If he kills him"," he will be like him.' A man from the people came to him and said: 'Woe to you! The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) says: \""If he kills him"," he will be like him.\""' So he returned and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I have been told that you said: \""If he kills him"," he will be like him","\"" and I only took him by your command.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Do you not wish that he bear your sin and the sin of your companion?' He said: 'Yes"," O Prophet of Allah.' He said: 'Then that is how it is.' So he threw the strap and let him go.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAnbarī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim]"""
"16058","(16052) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us in Kūfah: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunay narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me: Abū ʿAlī Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad Jazarah narrated to us. Both said: Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us. He said: Ibn Abī al-Ḥunay — Saʿdawayh — narrated to us: Hushaym ibn Bashīr narrated to us, sixty years ago. He said: Ismāʿīl ibn Sālim narrated to me: ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil narrated to me from his father, who said:\n\n\The Prophet (ﷺ) was brought a man who had killed another man — meaning"," so he granted the guardian of the slain man authority over him (for retribution). He departed with him"," a strap (nisʿah) around his neck"," dragging it. When he turned away"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The killer and the killed are both in the Fire.' A man came to the man and conveyed to him the words of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," so he let him go.\""\n\nIsmāʿīl said: \""I mentioned that to Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit"," and he said: 'Ibn Ashwaʿ narrated to me that the Prophet (ﷺ) asked him to forgive"," but he refused to forgive.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim from Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān. Thus narrated Hushaym. And Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Ismāʿīl"," and he said in it: \""I mentioned that to Ibn Ashwaʿ"," and Ibn Ashwaʿ said: 'I mentioned that to Ḥabīb"," and Ḥabīb said: The Prophet (ﷺ) had commanded him to forgive.'\""\n\nIt was narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from the Prophet (ﷺ) in this hadith in a mursal form"," that he said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," my brother was killed"," so he is in the Fire. If I kill him"," am I like him?\"" He said: \""Your brother was killed"," so he is in the Fire. And I commanded you"," but you disobeyed me"," so you are in the Fire if you disobey me.\""\n\nAnd it was said that he said that because the killer had said: \""By Allah"," I did not intend to kill him\"" — and that is in the hadith of Abū Hurayrah. If he was truthful"," and you killed him knowing his truthfulness"," then you are like him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16059","(16053) As for what Ḥabīb or Ibn Ashwaʿ said, it is clarified in what Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Fāmī al-Faqīh informed us in Baghdād: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAlī — he is Ibn al-Madīnī — narrated to us: Yaḥyā — he is Ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān — narrated to us: Jāmiʿ ibn Maṭar narrated to me: ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil narrated to me that his father informed him, saying:\n\n\While I was with the Prophet (ﷺ)"," a man was brought to him with a strap (nisʿah) around his neck. When he came to him"," he said: 'This man and my brother were digging a well"," and he raised the pickaxe and struck my brother's head with it"," killing him.' He said: 'Forgive him.' He refused. He said: 'Take the blood-money.' He said: 'I do not want the blood-money.' He repeated the hadith and said: 'Forgive him.' He refused. He said: 'Take the blood-money.' He refused. He repeated the hadith and said: 'Forgive him.' He refused. He said: 'Take the blood-money.' He refused. When he insisted on nothing but killing him"," he said: 'Know that if you kill him"," you will be like him.' He said: 'Then what shall I do?' He said: 'Forgive him.' He said: 'I saw him dragging his strap until he disappeared from us.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16060","(16054) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn al-Jahm ibn Hārūn al-Simmārī narrated to us: Hawdhah ibn Khalīfah al-Bakrāwī narrated to us: ʿAwf narrated from Ḥamzah Abī ʿUmar al-ʿāʾidhī, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil al-Ḥaḍramī, from his father, who said:\n\n\I was present with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when the killer was brought"," being led by a strap (nisʿah). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to the guardian of the slain man: 'Will you forgive?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you take the blood-money?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you kill him?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Go with him.' When he went with him and turned away from him"," he said to him: 'Come here. Will you forgive?' — like his first statement. So the guardian of the slain man said like his first statement"," three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on the fourth occasion: 'Know that if you forgive"," he shall bear your sin and the sin of your companion.' So he let him go. I saw him dragging his strap.\""\n\nAnd Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān said in it"," from ʿAwf: \""He shall bear his sin and the sin of your companion.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"16061","(16055) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad al-Bayrutiyy informed us: Ibn Shu'ayb informed us: Shayban ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq al-Hamdani, that he narrated to them from Abu al-Safar, that a man from Quraysh broke the tooth of a man from the Ansar. The latter sought redress from Mu'awiyah, saying, \This man has broken my tooth.\"" Mu'awiyah replied"," \""No indeed—we shall satisfy you.\"" The Ansarite persisted and pressed his claim against Mu'awiyah until he compelled him. Mu'awiyah then said"," \""Do as you wish with your companion.\"" Now Abu al-Darda' was sitting with Mu'awiyah"," and he said"," \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'No Muslim is afflicted with any bodily harm and then forgives it"," except that Allah"," the Almighty and Exalted"," raises him thereby in rank and expiates thereby some of his sins.'\""\n\nThe Ansarite then said to Abu al-Darda'"," \""Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He replied"," \""Yes—my ears heard it and my heart retained it.\"" The Ansarite then said"," \""I leave it for the sake of Allah.\"" Mu'awiyah said"," \""By no means! By Allah"," you shall not be disappointed","\"" and ordered that he be given compensation. [Hasan]"""
"16062","(16056) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Yunus ibn Habib informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Muhammad ibn Aban informed us: 'Alqamah ibn Marthad informed us: from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit said in the presence of Mu'awiyah, \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever is afflicted in his body to the extent of half his diyah and then forgives"," half his sins shall be expiated; and if it be a third or a quarter"," then accordingly.'\"" A man then said"," \""By Allah"," did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" 'Ubadah replied"," \""By Allah"," I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" Both chains are munqati' (disconnected). [Da'if — Munqati']"""
"16063","(16057) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi informed us: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways informed me: my father, Abi Uways, informed me: Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'idah, may Allah be pleased with her, in the hadith of al-Ifk, she said: Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal struck Hassan ibn Thabit with his sword, delivering a blow. Hassan ibn Thabit cried out and called upon the people against Safwan. Safwan fled, and Hassan came to the Prophet ﷺ and sought redress against Safwan for his blow. The Prophet ﷺ asked him to grant the blow of Safwan to him, and so he granted it to the Prophet ﷺ. In compensation, the Prophet ﷺ gave him a large palm-tree wall, a Roman slave-girl—also said to be a Coptic one. [Da'if]"
"16064","(16058) Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Khaliq ibn 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq al-Mu'addhin informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Khanb informed us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Tirmidhi informed us: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal informed me: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi 'Atiq and Musa ibn 'Uqbah, both of whom said: Ibn Shihab was asked about a man who strikes another with his sword in a fit of anger—what is to be done with him? He replied: \Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal struck Hassan ibn Thabit"," who was wounded"," yet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not amputate his hand.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16065","(16059) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us: Bahr informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed me: Anas ibn Iyyad informed me: Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, that 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, used to go out at dawn with his staff in his hand, waking the people with it. Then Ibn Muljam struck him. 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Feed him"," give him drink"," and treat him well in his captivity. If I live"," I am the authority over my own blood—I may forgive if I wish"," or I may exact retribution if I wish.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16066","(16060) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan informed us: Abu Hanifah informed us: from Hammad, from Ibrahim, who said: \Whoever forgives a person of standing (dhi sahm)"," his forgiveness is a valid pardon.\"" 'Umar and Ibn Mas'ud"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," permitted forgiveness in the case of a person of standing"," and they did not ask whether it was a case of treacherous murder (ghilah) or otherwise.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: \""And some of our companions have said regarding a man who kills another without rancour—the matter rests with the ruler; he need not await the wali of the slain.\"" And those who are familiar with their positions have cited in support the affair of Majdhar ibn Ziyad—though were his hadith established"," we would rule by it. But it has not been established to me up to this day. And if it is not established"," then every slain person killed by one other than a combatant—the matter of his killing rests with the wali of the slain"," because Allah"," the Most High"," says: *'And whoever is killed wrongfully"," We have given his heir authority'* [17:33]"," and He says: *'But if anything is remitted to him by his brother"," then let the pursuing be reasonable'* [2:178].\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""The story of Majdhar ibn Ziyad has reached us only through the hadith of al-Waqidi"," as a munqati' narration"," and it is da'if.\"" [Sahih — the statement of Ibrahim only]"""
"16067","(16061) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Battah informed us: al-Hasan ibn al-Jahm informed us: al-Husayn ibn al-Faraj informed us: al-Waqidi, in his mention of those slain at Uhud among the Muslims, said: \And Majdhar ibn Ziyad—al-Harith ibn Suwayd killed him treacherously.\""\n\nThe story of Majdhar ibn Ziyad is that he killed Suwayd ibn al-Samit during the Jahiliyyah. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah"," al-Harith ibn Suwayd ibn al-Samit and Majdhar ibn Ziyad both embraced Islam and witnessed Badr together. Al-Harith began seeking Majdhar in order to kill him for his father"," but could not overpower him that day. Then"," on the day of Uhud"," when the Muslims were routed"," al-Harith came upon him from behind and struck his neck. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to Madinah"," then set out towards Hamra' al-Asad. Upon his return"," Jibril"," peace be upon him"," came to him and informed him that al-Harith ibn Suwayd had killed Majdhar ibn Ziyad treacherously"," and commanded him to kill him.\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode to Quba'"," and when he saw him"," he called upon 'Uwaymir ibn Sa'idah and said: \""Al-Harith ibn Suwayd has come to the door of the mosque—strike his neck in retribution for Majdhar ibn Ziyad"," for he killed him treacherously on the day of Uhud.\"" So 'Uwaymir seized him. Al-Harith said"," \""Let me speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" But 'Uwaymir refused. Al-Harith struggled"," seeking to address the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Prophet ﷺ rose"," intending to mount. Al-Harith kept saying"," \""By Allah"," I have indeed killed him"," O Messenger of Allah! And by Allah"," my killing him was not out of apostasy from Islam nor doubt in it—rather"," it was the fury of Satan and a matter entrusted to myself. I repent to Allah"," the Almighty and Exalted"," and to the Messenger of Allah. I shall pay his diyah"," fast two consecutive months"," free a slave"," and feed sixty poor persons. I repent to Allah.\"" And he grasped the stirrup of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Banu Majdhar were present"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said nothing to them. When Al-Harith had finished speaking"," the Prophet ﷺ said"," \""Bring him forward"," O 'Uwaymir"," and strike his neck.\"" So he struck his neck. [Very Da'if]"""
"16068","(16062) Abu Muhammad al-Sukariyy in Baghdad informed us: Abu Bakr al-Shafi'i informed us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Azhar informed us: al-Mufaddal ibn Ghassan al-Ghallabiyy, who mentions among those known for hypocrisy during the time of the Prophet ﷺ: \And al-Harith ibn Suwayd ibn al-Samit"," of Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf"," witnessed Badr—and he is the one who killed Majdhar treacherously on the day of Uhud"," and so the Prophet of Allah ﷺ killed him in retribution.\"" [Da'if]"""
"16069","(16063) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Musaddad informed us: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed me: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id said: I heard Abu Shurayh al-Ka'bi saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Beware! O company of Khuza'ah"," you have killed this man of Hudhayl"," and I shall pay his diyah on his behalf. So whoever has a killing done after my statement"," his people shall have the choice between taking the blood-wit (al-'aql) or killing the killer.\"" [Sahih]"""
"16070","(16064) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us: Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri informed us: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Yahya ibn Malik informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Asim, from Sufyan—\n\nAnd Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Ahmad ibn Salih informed us: Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: \The diyah belongs to the 'aqilah (the extended family/tribal group); a woman shall not inherit from her husband's diyah\""—until al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan said to him: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to me that I should give the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabiyy a share from her husband's diyah.\"" So 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," retracted his position.\n\nAhmad ibn Salih narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq"," with this hadith"," from Ma'mar"," from al-Zuhri"," from Sa'id"," and in it he said: \""The Prophet ﷺ had appointed him over the Bedouins.\"" This is the wording of al-Rudhbari's hadith. [Sahih]"""
"16071","(16065) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us: Shaybān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd said: I found in my book from Shaybān: Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated to us: Sulaymān, i.e. ibn Mūsā, narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," the blood-money (al-ʿaql) is inherited among the heirs of the slain according to their degrees of kinship"," and whatever remains goes to the paternal relatives (al-ʿaṣabah).\"" He said: \""And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) decreed that the blood-money of a woman is distributed among her paternal relatives (ʿaṣabah)"," those who do not inherit anything from her except what remains after her designated heirs have received their shares. And if she is killed"," her blood-money belongs to her heirs"," and they are the ones who shall kill her killer.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"16072","(16066) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ḥabīb ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Ḥarim, from Jābir ibn Zayd, who said: \The blood-money of a free man is inherited among his heirs; it is divided among them according to their fixed shares (farāʾiḍ)"," just as they divide his inheritance. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) decreed this. And the blood-money of a free woman is inherited among her heirs; it is divided among them just as her inheritance is divided"," and her paternal relatives (ʿaṣabah) pay blood-money on her behalf if she kills a person or wounds someone. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) decreed this.\""\n\nAnd from ʿAmr ibn Ḥarim"," who said: Jābir ibn Zayd was asked about the maternal brother—does he inherit from the blood-money if there is no father? He said: \""Yes. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," and Sharīḥ made him an heir. And ʿUmar used to say: 'His blood-money is in the status of his inheritance.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"16073","(16067) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd informed us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from one who informed him, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: \He has indeed wronged who does not make the maternal brothers inherit anything from the blood-money.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16074","(16068) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī narrated to us: Mālik ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Sālim, from ʿĀmir, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The blood-money is divided according to the fixed shares (farāʾiḍ) of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," and every heir inherits from it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"16075","(16069) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-Qārīʾ narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed me: Khālid ibn Yazīd informed me, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hilāl, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Abū Sinān al-Duʾalī narrated to him: that he visited ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding a complaint he had made. He said: \We have been fearful for you"," O Commander of the Faithful"," regarding this complaint of yours.\"" He said: \""But by Allah"," I have not feared for myself regarding it"," because I heard the truthful and confirmed Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'You will be struck a blow here and a blow here'—and he pointed to his temples—'and their blood will flow until it dyes your beard"," and its bearer will be the most wretched of them"," just as the slayer of the she-camel was the most wretched of Thamūd.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
